entidades","Validar con datos de ejemplo","Crear un esquema por cada archivo","Reutilizar grupos estándar","Duplicar campos"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Estándares y pruebas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices improve XDM model quality? (Choose 2)","options":["Avoid identities","Validate with sample data","One schema per file","Reuse standard groups","Duplicate fields"],"explanation":"Standards and testing."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un esquema con la etiqueta Profile habilitado y sin datos?","options":["Que está roto","Está listo para recibir datos que alimentarán Profile","Que no se puede usar","Que el esquema está mal configurado y debe recrearse"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se puede asociar a datasets.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Profile-enabled schema with no data mean?","options":["It's broken","It's ready to receive data feeding Profile","It's unusable","The schema is misconfigured and must be recreated"],"explanation":"It can be tied to datasets."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa la identidad en un esquema de catálogo de productos?","options":["Un email","El ECID del último visitante que vio el producto","Un ECID","El SKU o ID de producto para relaciones"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Necesaria para lookups.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does identity represent in a product catalog schema?","options":["An email","The ECID of the last visitor who viewed the product","An ECID","The SKU or product ID for relationships"],"explanation":"Needed for lookups."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un campo con el prefijo _tenantId en una consulta de Query Service?","options":["Que es estándar de Adobe","Que es un campo estándar de Adobe reservado","Que es un campo personalizado de la organización","Que es una identidad"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los personalizados se anidan bajo el tenant.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a _tenantId-prefixed field in Query Service mean?","options":["It's Adobe standard","It's a reserved Adobe standard field","It's an org custom field","It's an identity"],"explanation":"Custom fields nest under the tenant."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene si los datos de origen tienen estructura muy distinta del modelo XDM?","options":["Cambiar el modelo XDM para que copie la estructura de origen","Ingerir sin mapear","Cambiar el modelo XDM por el de origen","Usar Data Prep para mapear y transformar al ingerir"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Data Prep transforma en ingesta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What if source data structure differs greatly from XDM?","options":["Change the XDM model to copy the source structure","Ingest unmapped","Change XDM to the source model","Use Data Prep to map and transform on ingestion"],"explanation":"Data Prep transforms on ingestion."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de campo permite valores sugeridos en lugar de restringidos?","options":["Campo booleano","Enum estricto","Campo de identidad","Campo string con valores sugeridos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Suggested values no validan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which field type allows suggested rather than restricted values?","options":["A boolean field","A strict enum","An identity field","A string field with suggested values"],"explanation":"Suggested values don't validate."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos se deben revisar al planificar el modelo para segmentación? (Elige 2)","options":["Qué atributos y eventos usarán los segmentos","El nombre del sandbox","Cómo se relacionan con las identidades","El color de la interfaz","Los usuarios de Analytics"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"El modelo sirve a los casos de uso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two items should be reviewed when planning the model for segmentation? (Choose 2)","options":["Which attributes and events segments will use","Sandbox name","How they relate to identities","UI color","Analytics users"],"explanation":"The model serves use cases."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con esquemas obsoletos que no se usan?","options":["Habilitarlos para Profile","Borrarlos sin revisar porque no afectan a nada","Borrarlos sin revisar","Revisar dependencias antes de retirarlos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Pueden tener datasets o segmentos asociados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What to do with unused obsolete schemas?","options":["Enable for Profile","Delete them unreviewed since they affect nothing","Delete without review","Review dependencies before retiring them"],"explanation":"They may have related datasets or segments."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el término \"time-series\" en una clase?","options":["Cada registro es un evento en un momento concreto","Cada registro es un atributo fijo","Que no tiene campos","Cada registro es un atributo que se sobrescribe"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Eventos inmutables con fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does time-series mean for a class?","options":["Each record is an event at a specific time","Each record is a fixed attribute","It has no fields","Each record is an attribute that gets overwritten"],"explanation":"Immutable dated events."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de esquema se usa para datos de fidelización como nivel y puntos?","options":["Producto","Business Account","Individual Profile con el grupo de campos de Loyalty","ExperienceEvent sin identidad"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Atributos de perfil.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which schema holds loyalty data like tier and points?","options":["Product","Business Account","Individual Profile with the Loyalty field group","ExperienceEvent without identity"],"explanation":"Profile attributes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar tipos de datos estándar como Phone Number?","options":["Menor tamaño de los datos","Cifrado automático","Cifrado automático de los números de teléfono","Consistencia y compatibilidad con servicios de Adobe"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Estándares facilitan integración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of standard data types like Phone Number?","options":["Smaller data","Automatic encryption","Automatic phone number encryption","Consistency and compatibility with Adobe services"],"explanation":"Standards ease integration."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene si un dataset recibe datos de varios orígenes con calidades distintas?","options":["Borrar los de peor calidad sin revisar","Mezclarlos en un único dataset y dejar que Profile decida","Mezclarlos todos en uno","Separarlos en datasets diferentes para controlar precedencia"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Permite políticas de fusión por dataset.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What if one dataset gets data from several sources of different quality?","options":["Delete the worse ones unreviewed","Mix them in one dataset and let Profile decide","Mix them all in one","Split into separate datasets to control precedence"],"explanation":"It enables per-dataset merge policies."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un error de validación \"required field missing\" en ingesta?","options":["Que el sandbox ha superado su cuota de almacenamiento","Falta un campo obligatorio del esquema","El destino falló","El sandbox está lleno"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Validación XDM.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"required field missing\" ingestion error indicate?","options":["The sandbox exceeded its storage quota","A required schema field is missing","The destination failed","The sandbox is full"],"explanation":"XDM validation."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas de Platform permiten crear datasets? (Elige 2)","options":["Segment Builder","La API de Catalog","Destinations","Identity graph viewer","La interfaz de Datasets"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"UI y API.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Platform tools create datasets? (Choose 2)","options":["Segment Builder","The Catalog API","Destinations","Identity graph viewer","The Datasets UI"],"explanation":"UI and API."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la arquitectura de Real-Time CDP respecto a Experience Platform?","options":["RT-CDP es un producto independiente que no usa Platform","RT-CDP se construye sobre los servicios de Experience Platform","RT-CDP es un producto independiente sin Platform","Platform es parte de Analytics"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Usa XDM, identidades, Profile, segmentación y destinos de Platform.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How does Real-Time CDP architecture relate to Experience Platform?","options":["RT-CDP is a standalone product not using Platform","RT-CDP is built on Experience Platform services","RT-CDP is standalone without Platform","Platform is part of Analytics"],"explanation":"It uses Platform's XDM, identities, Profile, segmentation and destinations."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para datos que solo se usarán en análisis SQL y no en personalización?","options":["Habilitarlo para Profile por si se necesita más adelante","Exportarlo a un destino","Habilitarlo para Profile igualmente","Dataset sin Profile consultable con Query Service"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Ahorro de capacidad de Profile.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for data used only for SQL analysis, not personalization?","options":["Enable it for Profile in case it's needed later","Export to a destination","Enable it for Profile anyway","A non-Profile dataset queried via Query Service"],"explanation":"It saves Profile capacity."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre al deshabilitar Profile en un dataset que ya tenía datos en perfiles?","options":["No se puede deshabilitar nunca","Se borran de inmediato todos los perfiles del sandbox","Hay que eliminar sus datos de Profile por separado si se desea","Se borran todos los perfiles"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Profile conserva datos hasta limpiarlos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens disabling Profile on a dataset with data already in profiles?","options":["It can never be disabled","Every sandbox profile is deleted immediately","Its Profile data must be removed separately if desired","All profiles are deleted"],"explanation":"Profile keeps data until cleaned."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que un campo de evento enlace con un perfil?","options":["Que el campo tenga el mismo nombre en ambos esquemas","Que esté en el mismo sandbox solamente","Que el evento contenga una identidad del perfil","Que tenga el mismo nombre de campo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Identidades unen eventos y perfiles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What links an event field to a profile?","options":["The field has the same name in both schemas","Same sandbox only","The event containing a profile identity","Same field name"],"explanation":"Identities join events and profiles."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer si un campo de un esquema de Profile se creó con un tipo equivocado y aún no tiene datos en producción?","options":["Ingerir los datos igualmente y convertir el tipo más adelante con una consulta de Query Service","Corregirlo antes de ingerir","Etiquetar el campo como sensible para que Profile lo descarte automáticamente","Crear un segmento que ignore ese campo y dejar el esquema como está para siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios estructurales son más fáciles antes de tener datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done if a Profile schema field was created with the wrong type and has no production data yet?","options":["Ingest anyway and convert the type later with a Query Service query","Fix it before ingesting","Label the field sensitive so Profile discards it automatically","Build a segment ignoring that field and leave the schema forever"],"explanation":"Structural changes are easier before data exists."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere segmentar por la categoría del último producto visto, que está en un catálogo aparte. ¿Qué modelo lo permite?","options":["Copiar a mano el nombre de la categoría en cada evento web antes de ingerirlo","Crear una clase de evento nueva por cada categoría del catálogo","Habilitar el catálogo como dataset de destino para que Profile lo lea","Una relación con el esquema de producto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las relaciones permiten usar atributos de lookup.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants to segment by the category of the last viewed product, kept in a separate catalog. Which model enables it?","options":["Hand-copy the category name into every web event before ingestion","Create a new event class per catalog category","Enable the catalog as a destination dataset so Profile reads it","A relationship to the product schema"],"explanation":"Relationships enable lookup attributes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos campos de un evento web enviado con Web SDK suelen identificar al visitante? (Elige 2)","options":["La resolución de pantalla del dispositivo","El nombre del navegador que usa el visitante","ECID en identityMap","Un ID autenticado como email con hash","El título de la página que se está visitando"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"ECID anónimo y una identidad autenticada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two web event fields sent with Web SDK typically identify the visitor? (Choose 2)","options":["The device's screen resolution","The name of the visitor's browser","ECID in identityMap","An authenticated ID like hashed email","The title of the page being visited"],"explanation":"Anonymous ECID and an authenticated identity."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un esquema de eventos no tiene ningún campo de identidad y se habilita para Profile?","options":["Se habilita y los eventos se asocian al último perfil actualizado del sandbox","No se puede habilitar","Se convierte automáticamente en un esquema de registro","Se habilita y Adobe genera una identidad aleatoria para cada evento ingerido"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Profile necesita identidad para asociar los datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if an event schema with no identity field is enabled for Profile?","options":["It's enabled and events attach to the sandbox's last updated profile","It can't be enabled","It automatically becomes a record schema","It's enabled and Adobe generates a random identity per ingested event"],"explanation":"Profile needs identity to associate data."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que los campos de varios orígenes con nombres distintos (por ejemplo, mail y email) acaben en el mismo campo XDM?","options":["Renombrar los campos en el esquema de unión a mano","Crear dos campos XDM distintos y dejar que Profile los combine por similitud de nombre","Ingerir solo una de las fuentes y descartar la otra sin analizarla","Mapear ambos al mismo campo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El mapeo en ingesta armoniza.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What makes fields named differently in several sources (e.g. mail and email) land in the same XDM field?","options":["Rename fields by hand in the union schema","Create two XDM fields and let Profile combine them by name similarity","Ingest only one source and discard the other unanalyzed","Map both to the same field"],"explanation":"Ingestion mapping harmonizes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta muestra el linaje y los lotes ingeridos en un dataset?","options":["La actividad del dataset","El visor del gráfico de identidades de un perfil concreto","La lista de destinos activos con su programación","El editor de segmentos con la vista de estimaciones de audiencia por dataset"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Dataset activity muestra lotes y errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which tool shows lineage and batches ingested into a dataset?","options":["Dataset activity","The identity graph viewer for a specific profile","The active destinations list with schedules","The segment editor with audience estimates per dataset"],"explanation":"Dataset activity shows batches and errors."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene separar en datasets distintos los datos de CRM y los de comercio electrónico?","options":["Que se reduce el número de esquemas a uno solo","Controlar la precedencia y el gobierno por fuente","Que los perfiles se crean dos veces y así hay más datos disponibles para segmentar","Que los datos de CRM dejan de necesitar identidad principal"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Datasets separados permiten políticas de fusión y etiquetas por fuente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of separate datasets for CRM and e-commerce data?","options":["The number of schemas drops to one","Controlling precedence and governance per source","Profiles are created twice so there's more data to segment","CRM data no longer needs a primary identity"],"explanation":"Separate datasets allow per-source merge policies and labels."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el Real-Time Customer Profile?","options":["Una vista unificada de cada cliente","Un destino que envía perfiles a plataformas publicitarias","Un informe diario con el resumen de las visitas web de cada cliente por canal","Un dataset de eventos sin identidades usado solo para análisis"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Combina fragmentos de perfil de varias fuentes en tiempo real.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Real-Time Customer Profile?","options":["A unified view of each customer","A destination sending profiles to ad platforms","A daily report summarizing each customer's web visits by channel","An identity-less event dataset used only for analysis"],"explanation":"It combines profile fragments from many sources in real time."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un fragmento de perfil?","options":["Un segmento que contiene menos de cien perfiles","Una parte del perfil que se exporta a un destino de archivos","Una etiqueta de gobierno aplicada a un campo","Los datos de un perfil procedentes de un dataset"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Profile une fragmentos por identidades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a profile fragment?","options":["A segment containing fewer than a hundred profiles","A part of the profile exported to a file destination","A governance label on a field","A profile's data from one dataset"],"explanation":"Profile joins fragments via identities."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué determina qué fragmentos se combinan y qué valor prevalece al leer un perfil?","options":["El orden alfabético de los nombres de los datasets","La programación del destino","La etiqueta de gobierno del dataset más reciente que se haya ingerido","La política de fusión"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Merge policy: precedencia y unión de identidades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What determines which fragments merge and which value wins when reading a profile?","options":["The alphabetical order of dataset names","The destination schedule","The governance label of the most recently ingested dataset","The merge policy"],"explanation":"Merge policy: precedence and identity stitching."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos métodos de fusión de atributos ofrece una política de fusión? (Elige 2)","options":["Por el número de caracteres del valor más largo","Por orden alfabético del valor del atributo en cada fragmento","Por marca de tiempo","Por el país del perfil","Por precedencia de dataset"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Timestamp ordered y dataset precedence.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two attribute merge methods does a merge policy offer? (Choose 2)","options":["The character count of the longest value","Alphabetical order of the attribute value in each fragment","Timestamp ordered","The profile's country","Dataset precedence"],"explanation":"Timestamp ordered and dataset precedence."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Con la fusión por marca de tiempo, ¿qué valor gana si dos datasets tienen distinto email?","options":["El del dataset creado primero en el sandbox, independientemente de la fecha del dato","El que coincida con el ECID","El que tenga más caracteres","El actualizado más recientemente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Timestamp ordered usa la fecha de ingesta o la indicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"With timestamp ordered merge, which value wins if two datasets have different emails?","options":["The one from the first dataset created in the sandbox, regardless of data date","The one matching the ECID","The longest one","The most recently updated"],"explanation":"Timestamp ordered uses ingestion or supplied time."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuándo conviene la fusión por precedencia de dataset?","options":["Cuando una fuente es más fiable","Cuando solo hay un dataset de perfil en el sandbox","Cuando no hay identidades en los datos de origen","Cuando todas las fuentes tienen la misma calidad y se quiere el dato más reciente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Se ordenan datasets por prioridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When is dataset precedence merging advisable?","options":["When one source is more reliable","When there's only one profile dataset in the sandbox","When source data has no identities","When all sources share quality and the newest data is wanted"],"explanation":"Datasets are ordered by priority."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la opción de unión de identidades (ID stitching) \"Private Graph\" o gráfico de identidades en la política de fusión?","options":["Que se crea un gráfico nuevo para cada segmento","Que se usa el gráfico para unir fragmentos","Que los perfiles solo se unen si comparten el mismo email exacto","Que no se une ningún fragmento y cada identidad forma un perfil independiente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Con \"None\" no se unen identidades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the merge policy's identity stitching option (identity graph) indicate?","options":["A new graph is created per segment","The graph is used to join fragments","Profiles join only if they share the exact same email","No fragments join and each identity forms its own profile"],"explanation":"With \"None\" identities aren't stitched."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuántas políticas de fusión predeterminadas puede haber por clase y sandbox?","options":["Una","Dos, una para atributos y otra para eventos de la misma clase","Ninguna obligatoriamente","Tantas como datasets de perfil haya habilitados en el sandbox"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Una default por esquema/clase.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How many default merge policies can exist per class and sandbox?","options":["One","Two, one for attributes and one for same-class events","Mandatorily none","As many as Profile-enabled datasets in the sandbox"],"explanation":"One default per schema/class."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la política de fusión activa en el edge (Active-On-Edge)?","options":["Una política que solo se aplica a exportaciones de archivos por lotes","La que se usa para segmentación en el edge","Una política para datos B2B","Una política que fusiona datos de Analytics con Target sin identidades"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Solo una política puede estar activa en el edge.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is the Active-On-Edge merge policy?","options":["A policy applied only to batch file exports","The one used for edge segmentation","A B2B data policy","A policy merging Analytics and Target data without identities"],"explanation":"Only one policy can be active on edge."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el Identity Service?","options":["Un servicio que verifica la identidad legal de los clientes con documentos oficiales","El servicio que construye gráficos de identidades","Un servicio de autenticación de usuarios internos de Platform","Un destino de identidades publicitarias"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Une identidades entre dispositivos y canales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Identity Service?","options":["A service verifying customers' legal identity with official documents","The service building identity graphs","An authentication service for internal Platform users","An ad identity destination"],"explanation":"It links identities across devices and channels."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un namespace de identidad?","options":["El nombre del dataset en el que se guarda una identidad concreta","Una etiqueta de gobierno de identidad","El contexto o tipo de una identidad","El sandbox donde se creó el perfil por primera vez"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Ej.: Email, ECID, CRM ID.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an identity namespace?","options":["The dataset name storing a specific identity","An identity governance label","An identity's context or type","The sandbox where the profile was first created"],"explanation":"E.g. Email, ECID, CRM ID."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos namespaces de identidad son estándar en Experience Platform? (Elige 2)","options":["Email","LoyaltyNumber, que Adobe proporciona con el valor del programa de cada cliente","StoreCode","ECID","CRM_ID de la empresa, creado automáticamente por Adobe para cada organización"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Los IDs propios requieren namespaces personalizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two identity namespaces are standard in Experience Platform? (Choose 2)","options":["Email","LoyaltyNumber, provided by Adobe with each customer's program value","StoreCode","ECID","The company's CRM_ID, auto-created by Adobe for each org"],"explanation":"Own IDs need custom namespaces."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene crear para un identificador propio de la empresa, como el número de cliente?","options":["Guardarlo en un campo sin marcarlo como identidad","Reutilizar el namespace Email con el número de cliente como valor","Usar