":"The PO decides; the analyst facilitates."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se puede asociar a una historia para facilitar las pruebas?","options":["Casos de prueba derivados de los criterios","El código compilado de la aplicación en producción","Nada","Contraseñas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los casos de prueba se derivan de los criterios de aceptación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What can be linked to a story to ease testing?","options":["Test cases derived from the criteria","The compiled production app code","Nothing","Passwords"],"explanation":"Test cases are derived from acceptance criteria."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos indican que una historia es demasiado grande? (Elige 2)","options":["Tiene un solo criterio","El equipo no puede estimarla con confianza","Se entiende bien","No cabe en un sprint","Es de un solo rol"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Tamaño excesivo e incertidumbre indican que debe dividirse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two signs indicate a story is too large? (Choose 2)","options":["It has one criterion","The team can't estimate it confidently","It's well understood","It doesn't fit in a sprint","It's for one role"],"explanation":"Excessive size and uncertainty indicate splitting."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué historia describe una necesidad de integración?","options":["Como agente, quiero ver los datos del cliente del CRM al abrir un caso","CRM","Conector","Integrar con el CRM usando una llamada REST en el nodo 3 del proceso"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La historia describe la necesidad, no la implementación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which story describes an integration need?","options":["As an agent, I want to see CRM customer data when opening a case","CRM","Connector","Integrate with the CRM using a REST call at process node 3"],"explanation":"The story describes the need, not the implementation."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué estado tiene una historia lista para que el equipo la seleccione?","options":["Draft, porque todavía puede cambiar durante el sprint","Defined","Cancelada","Done"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Defined indica que está lista para planificarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What status does a story ready for the team to pick have?","options":["Draft, because it may still change during the sprint","Defined","Cancelled","Done"],"explanation":"Defined means it's ready to plan."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una épica \"Gestión de reclamaciones\" es demasiado amplia. ¿Cuál es el siguiente paso?","options":["Asignarla completa al sprint actual para avanzar rápido","Descomponerla en historias de usuario","Convertirla en defecto","Archivarla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las épicas se descomponen en historias entregables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A \"Claims management\" epic is too broad. What's the next step?","options":["Assign it whole to the current sprint to move fast","Break it into user stories","Turn it into a defect","Archive it"],"explanation":"Epics are broken into deliverable stories."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos de una historia ayudan a priorizar? (Elige 2)","options":["La longitud del título","El color","La estimación de esfuerzo","El autor","El beneficio de negocio"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Valor y esfuerzo guían la prioridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two story elements help prioritize? (Choose 2)","options":["Title length","Color","Effort estimate","Author","Business benefit"],"explanation":"Value and effort guide priority."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué historia está escrita con un rol demasiado genérico?","options":["Como usuario, quiero ver cosas","Como auditor, quiero exportar el historial","Como técnico de campo, quiero ver mis visitas del día","Como gestor de cuentas, quiero ver mis clientes"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"\"Usuario\" y \"ver cosas\" no aportan contexto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which story uses a role that's too generic?","options":["As a user, I want to see things","As an auditor, I want to export history","As a field technician, I want to see my visits for the day","As an account manager, I want to see my customers"],"explanation":"\"User\" and \"see things\" give no context."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se hace con una historia que ya no aporta valor tras cambiar las prioridades del negocio?","options":["Convertirla en épica","Desarrollarla igualmente porque ya estaba escrita","Eliminarla o archivarla del backlog","Moverla al sprint actual"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El backlog debe reflejar solo trabajo con valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's done with a story that no longer adds value after business priorities change?","options":["Turn it into an epic","Build it anyway because it was already written","Remove or archive it from the backlog","Move it to the current sprint"],"explanation":"The backlog should hold only valuable work."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es BPMN?","options":["Un lenguaje de programación propio de Appian para escribir reglas","Una notación estándar para modelar procesos","Una base de datos","Un tipo de integración"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"BPMN (Business Process Model and Notation) es el estándar de modelado de procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is BPMN?","options":["An Appian-specific programming language for writing rules","A standard notation for modeling processes","A database","An integration type"],"explanation":"BPMN (Business Process Model and Notation) is the process modeling standard."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En BPMN, ¿qué representa un círculo de borde fino?","options":["Evento de inicio","Evento de fin, que termina todos los flujos del proceso","Una pasarela","Una tarea"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El inicio se representa con un círculo de borde fino.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In BPMN, what does a thin-bordered circle represent?","options":["Start event","End event, which terminates every process flow","A gateway","A task"],"explanation":"The start is a thin-bordered circle."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En BPMN, ¿qué representa un círculo de borde grueso?","options":["Evento de fin","Un subproceso","Evento de inicio programado que lanza el proceso cada día","Una tarea de usuario"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El fin se representa con un círculo de borde grueso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In BPMN, what does a thick-bordered circle represent?","options":["End event","A subprocess","A scheduled start event launching the process daily","A user task"],"explanation":"The end is a thick-bordered circle."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En BPMN, ¿qué forma tiene una pasarela (gateway)?","options":["Un rectángulo con esquinas redondeadas y un icono de persona","Una flecha","Un círculo","Un rombo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las pasarelas se representan con rombos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In BPMN, what shape is a gateway?","options":["A rounded rectangle with a person icon","An arrow","A circle","A diamond"],"explanation":"Gateways are diamonds."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En BPMN, ¿qué representa un rectángulo con esquinas redondeadas?","options":["Un evento intermedio que espera un mensaje","Una pasarela","Un carril","Una actividad o tarea"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las actividades se representan con rectángulos redondeados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In BPMN, what does a rounded rectangle represent?","options":["An intermediate event waiting for a message","A gateway","A lane","An activity or task"],"explanation":"Activities are rounded rectangles."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué elemento BPMN representa a un rol o departamento dentro del proceso?","options":["Pasarela exclusiva que decide quién hace cada tarea","Carril (swimlane)","Evento","Artefacto"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los carriles organizan actividades por responsable.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN element represents a role or department within the process?","options":["An exclusive gateway deciding who does each task","Lane (swimlane)","Event","Artifact"],"explanation":"Lanes organize activities by owner."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué pasarela sigue solo un camino según una condición?","options":["Exclusiva (XOR)","Paralela (AND), que activa todos los caminos a la vez","Inclusiva (OR)","Compleja"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La pasarela exclusiva elige un único camino.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which gateway follows only one path based on a condition?","options":["Exclusive (XOR)","Parallel (AND), activating every path at once","Inclusive (OR)","Complex"],"explanation":"The exclusive gateway picks a single path."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué pasarela activa todos los caminos a la vez sin evaluar condiciones?","options":["Inclusiva (OR)","Paralela (AND)","Exclusiva (XOR), que evalúa condiciones y elige uno","Basada en eventos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La pasarela paralela divide el flujo en todos los caminos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which gateway activates every path at once without evaluating conditions?","options":["Inclusive (OR)","Parallel (AND)","Exclusive (XOR), which evaluates conditions and picks one","Event-based"],"explanation":"The parallel gateway splits the flow into every path."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué pasarela activa uno o varios caminos cuyas condiciones se cumplan?","options":["Paralela (AND)","Inclusiva (OR)","Ninguna","Exclusiva (XOR), que activa exactamente un camino"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La pasarela inclusiva permite varios caminos según condiciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which gateway activates one or more paths whose conditions are met?","options":["Parallel (AND)","Inclusive (OR)","None","Exclusive (XOR), which activates exactly one path"],"explanation":"The inclusive gateway allows several paths based on conditions."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una solicitud debe ser revisada a la vez por Legal y por Finanzas antes de continuar. ¿Qué pasarela se usa?","options":["Exclusiva (XOR), eligiendo Legal o Finanzas según el importe","Inclusiva sin condiciones","Paralela (AND)","Ninguna"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Ambas revisiones ocurren simultáneamente: pasarela paralela.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A request must be reviewed by both Legal and Finance before continuing. Which gateway is used?","options":["Exclusive (XOR), picking Legal or Finance by amount","Inclusive with no conditions","Parallel (AND)","None"],"explanation":"Both reviews happen simultaneously: parallel gateway."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Si la solicitud se aprueba, continúa; si se rechaza, se notifica al solicitante. ¿Qué pasarela modela esto?","options":["Inclusiva","Exclusiva (XOR)","Basada en eventos","Paralela (AND), que envía la solicitud por ambos caminos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Aprobado o rechazado son caminos mutuamente excluyentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"If the request is approved, it continues; if rejected, the requester is notified. Which gateway models this?","options":["Inclusive","Exclusive (XOR)","Event-based","Parallel (AND), sending the request down both paths"],"explanation":"Approved or rejected are mutually exclusive paths."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos BPMN son eventos? (Elige 2)","options":["Fin","Carril","Inicio","Tarea","Pasarela"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Inicio, fin e intermedios son eventos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two BPMN elements are events? (Choose 2)","options":["End","Lane","Start","Task","Gateway"],"explanation":"Start, end and intermediate are events."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un evento intermedio de temporizador en BPMN?","options":["Un fin de proceso","Una pasarela","Una espera hasta una fecha o durante un tiempo","Una tarea que un usuario debe completar antes de una fecha límite"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El temporizador pausa el flujo durante un tiempo o hasta una fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an intermediate timer event represent in BPMN?","options":["A process end","A gateway","Waiting until a date or for a period","A task a user must complete before a deadline"],"explanation":"The timer pauses the flow for a period or until a date."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa la línea continua con flecha en BPMN?","options":["Una asociación con un documento","Un carril","Flujo de secuencia","Flujo de mensajes entre organizaciones distintas"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El flujo de secuencia indica el orden de las actividades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a solid line with an arrow represent in BPMN?","options":["An association with a document","A lane","Sequence flow","Message flow between different organizations"],"explanation":"Sequence flow shows the order of activities."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa una línea discontinua con un círculo y flecha en BPMN?","options":["Un evento de fin","Flujo de secuencia dentro del mismo carril","Una pasarela","Flujo de mensajes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El flujo de mensajes conecta participantes distintos (pools).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a dashed line with a circle and arrow represent in BPMN?","options":["An end event","Sequence flow within the same lane","A gateway","Message flow"],"explanation":"Message flow connects different participants (pools)."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un pool en BPMN?","options":["Una tarea automatizada ejecutada por el sistema","Un evento","Una pasarela","Un participante del proceso (p. ej. una organización)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Un pool representa un participante; los carriles lo subdividen.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a pool in BPMN?","options":["An automated task run by the system","An event","A gateway","A process participant (e.g. an organization)"],"explanation":"A pool represents a participant; lanes subdivide it."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian corresponde a una tarea BPMN realizada por una persona?","options":["Evento de inicio","Tarea de usuario (User Input Task)","Pasarela XOR","Script task, que ejecuta lógica sin intervención humana"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las tareas de usuario asignan trabajo a personas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node maps to a BPMN task done by a person?","options":["Start event","User Input Task","XOR gateway","Script task, which runs logic without human input"],"explanation":"User tasks assign work to people."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian corresponde a una tarea automática que calcula o transforma datos?","options":["Script task","Carril","Tarea de usuario asignada a un grupo de sistemas","Evento de fin"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El script task ejecuta expresiones sin interacción humana.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node maps to an automated task that computes or transforms data?","options":["Script task","Lane","A user task assigned to a systems group","End event"],"explanation":"The script task runs expressions without human interaction."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian se usa para invocar un servicio externo en el proceso?","options":["Tarea de usuario que pide a alguien llamar al servicio","Temporizador","Pasarela AND","Nodo de integración (Call Integration)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El nodo Call Integration ejecuta integraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node is used to call an external service in the process?","options":["A user task asking someone to call the service","Timer","AND gateway","Call Integration node"],"explanation":"The Call Integration node runs integrations."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian se usa para guardar datos en la base de datos desde un proceso?","options":["Pasarela XOR","Write Records / Write to Data Store Entity","Send E-Mail","Script task que muestra los datos en pantalla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los nodos de escritura persisten datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node saves data to the database from a process?","options":["XOR gateway","Write Records / Write to Data Store Entity","Send E-Mail","A script task that shows data on screen"],"explanation":"Write nodes persist data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian llama a otro modelo de proceso reutilizable?","options":["Evento de fin","Script task que copia los nodos del otro modelo","Subproceso (Start Process / Sub-Process)","Temporizador"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El subproceso reutiliza lógica de otros modelos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node calls another reusable process model?","options":["End event","A script task copying the other model's nodes","Sub-Process / Start Process","Timer"],"explanation":"The subprocess reuses other models' logic."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos de Appian son de comunicación? (Elige 2)","options":["Write Records","Pasarela AND","Send E-Mail","Script task","Send Push Notification"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Correo y notificaciones push comunican con usuarios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian nodes are communication nodes? (Choose 2)","options":["Write Records","AND gateway","Send E-Mail","Script task","Send Push Notification"],"explanation":"Email and push notifications communicate with users."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de integración intercambia datos JSON sobre HTTP?","options":["SOAP, que usa JSON sobre colas de mensajes","Correo","FTP","REST (JSON)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las APIs REST suelen intercambiar JSON por HTTP.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which integration type exchanges JSON over HTTP?","options":["SOAP, which uses JSON over message queues","Email","FTP","REST (JSON)"],"explanation":"REST APIs typically exchange JSON over HTTP."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de integración usa XML y un contrato WSDL?","options":["REST con JSON y documentación OpenAPI","Correo electrónico","Ninguna","SOAP"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los servicios SOAP se describen con WSDL y usan XML.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which integration type uses XML and a WSDL contract?","options":["REST with JSON and OpenAPI documentation","Email","None","SOAP"],"explanation":"SOAP services are described by WSDL and use XML."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un Connected System en Appian?","options":["Un informe","Un objeto que centraliza conexión y autenticación con un sistema externo","Un usuario que conecta Appian a internet","Un proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El connected system guarda URL base y credenciales reutilizables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Connected System in Appian?","options":["A report","An object centralizing connection and auth to an external system","A user connecting Appian to the internet","A process"],"explanation":"The connected system stores base URL and reusable credentials."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene un Connected System frente a configurar credenciales en cada integración?","options":["Permite que cada integración use una contraseña distinta sin control","Ninguna","Es más lento","Se configura una vez y se reutiliza"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Centralizar credenciales simplifica mantenimiento y despliegues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a Connected System over configuring credentials in each integration?","options":["It lets each integration use a different uncontrolled password","None","It's slower","It's set once and reused"],"explanation":"Centralizing credentials simplifies maintenance and deployments."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se define en un diagrama de proceso qué rol realiza cada tarea?","options":["Escribiendo el rol en el título del proceso","Con colores aleatorios","No se define","Colocando las tareas en el carril del rol correspondiente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los carriles indican el responsable de cada actividad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How does a process diagram define which role performs each task?","options":["Writing the role in the process title","With random colors","It doesn't","Placing tasks in the corresponding role's lane"],"explanation":"Lanes indicate each activity's owner."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene representar en un diagrama de proceso futuro (to-be)? (Elige 2)","options":["Contraseñas","Detalles de CSS","Roles en carriles","Decisiones con sus condiciones","Nombres de servidores"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Roles y decisiones son claves para entender el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should a future-state (to-be) process diagram show? (Choose 2)","options":["Passwords","CSS details","Roles in lanes","Decisions with their conditions","Server names"],"explanation":"Roles and decisions are key to understanding the process."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué beneficio tiene diseñar el modelo futuro (to-be) junto con expertos de negocio (SMEs)?","options":["Reducir la necesidad de pruebas porque los SMEs ya conocen el proceso","Evitar el trabajo del analista","Ninguno","Validar el diseño y lograr su apoyo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La colaboración con SMEs mejora la calidad y la adopción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of designing the to-be model with business SMEs?","options":["Reducing testing because SMEs already know the process","Avoiding the analyst's work","None","Validating the design and gaining buy-in"],"explanation":"Collaborating with SMEs improves quality and adoption."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una oportunidad de automatización en un proceso?","options":["Tareas repetitivas basadas en reglas","Reuniones","Decisiones complejas que requieren juicio humano experto","Negociaciones"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las tareas repetitivas y basadas en reglas son buenas candidatas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What indicates an automation opportunity in a process?","options":["Repetitive, rule-based tasks","Meetings","Complex decisions needing expert human judgment","Negotiations"],"explanation":"Repetitive, rule-based tasks are good candidates."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características hacen buena candidata a automatizar una tarea? (Elige 2)","options":["Requiere empatía","Cada caso es único","Implica negociación","Reglas claras y estables","Alto volumen"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Volumen y reglas estables maximizan el beneficio de automatizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two traits make a task a good automation candidate? (Choose 2)","options":["Needs empathy","Every case is unique","Involves negotiation","Clear, stable rules","High volume"],"explanation":"Volume and stable rules maximize automation benefit."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En el diagrama actual, un empleado copia datos de un correo a una hoja de cálculo. ¿Qué propone el analista?","options":["Capturar los datos con un formulario o integración","Nada","Contratar a otro empleado para repartir el trabajo de copiar","Imprimir los correos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Eliminar la transcripción manual reduce errores y tiempo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In the as-is diagram, an employee copies data from an email into a spreadsheet. What does the analyst propose?","options":["Capture data with a form or integration","Nothing","Hire another employee to share the copying","Print the emails"],"explanation":"Removing manual transcription reduces errors and time."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evento BPMN inicia un proceso al recibir un mensaje?","options":["Evento de inicio de mensaje","Tarea de usuario","Evento de fin de mensaje que envía una respuesta","Pasarela paralela"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un inicio de mensaje arranca el proceso al recibir un mensaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN event starts a process on receiving a message?","options":["Message start event","User task","Message end event that sends a reply","Parallel gateway"],"explanation":"A message start triggers the process on message receipt."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evento BPMN inicia un proceso en una fecha o periodicidad?","options":["Evento de fin","Evento de inicio de temporizador","Pasarela","Evento de inicio de mensaje que espera un correo cada día"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El inicio temporizado arranca procesos programados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN event starts a process on a date or schedule?","options":["End event","Timer start event","Gateway","A message start event waiting for an email each day"],"explanation":"The timer start launches scheduled processes."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué elemento BPMN agrupa varias actividades en una sola caja expandible?","options":["Subproceso","Carril","Pasarela inclusiva que agrupa caminos","Evento de fin"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El subproceso encapsula un conjunto de actividades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN element groups several activities into a single expandable box?","options":["Subprocess","Lane","An inclusive gateway grouping paths","End event"],"explanation":"The subprocess encapsulates a set of activities."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un evento de borde (boundary event) de temporizador sobre una tarea?","options":["Una acción si la tarea no se completa a tiempo","Un carril","El fin del proceso","El tiempo que tarda el usuario en abrir la tarea por primera vez"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El evento de borde temporizado modela escalados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a timer boundary event on a task represent?","options":["An action if the task isn't done in time","A lane","The process end","How long the user takes to first open the task"],"explanation":"The timer boundary event models escalations."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se implementa en Appian un escalado de una tarea no completada?","options":["Configurando un escalado/temporizador en la tarea","Con un informe","Pidiendo al gestor que revise manualmente la lista cada mañana","No se puede"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las tareas admiten escalados automáticos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is an uncompleted-task escalation implemented in Appian?","options":["Configuring an escalation/timer on the task","With a report","Asking the manager to manually check the list each morning","It can't be"],"explanation":"Tasks support automatic escalations."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos de Appian corresponden a pasarelas BPMN? (Elige 2)","options":["Send E-Mail","XOR","Script task","User Input Task","AND"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Appian ofrece pasarelas XOR, AND, OR y compleja.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian nodes map to BPMN gateways? (Choose 2)","options":["Send E-Mail","XOR","Script task","User Input Task","AND"],"explanation":"Appian offers XOR, AND, OR and complex gateways."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Tras una pasarela paralela, ¿qué hace falta para esperar a que terminen todos los caminos?","options":["Un evento de fin en cada camino","Una pasarela de unión que sincronice los caminos","Nada, porque el proceso continúa en cuanto termina el primer camino","Un temporizador"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La unión (join) espera a todos los flujos antes de continuar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After a parallel gateway, what's needed to wait for every path to finish?","options":["An end event on each path","A joining gateway that syncs the paths","Nothing, since the process continues when the first path ends","A timer"],"explanation":"The join waits for every flow before continuing."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un evento de fin de terminación en BPMN?","options":["Termina todo el proceso, incluidos los caminos activos","Inicia el proceso","Es una pasarela","Termina solo el camino actual dejando los demás en marcha"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La terminación detiene todos los flujos del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a terminate end event represent in BPMN?","options":["Ends the whole process, including active paths","Starts the process","It's a gateway","Ends only the current path, leaving others running"],"explanation":"Termination stops every process flow."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un analista dibuja un proceso en el que una tarea \"Revisar\" puede repetirse hasta que se corrija. ¿Cómo se modela?","options":["Copiando la tarea \"Revisar\" diez veces en secuencia","No se puede modelar","Un bucle de vuelta con pasarela XOR","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Una pasarela que devuelve el flujo modela el ciclo de corrección.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An analyst draws a process where a \"Review\" task can repeat until corrected. How is it modeled?","options":["Copying the \"Review\" task ten times in sequence","It can't be modeled","A loop back with an XOR gateway","An end event"],"explanation":"A gateway looping the flow back models the correction cycle."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué artefacto BPMN representa un documento usado en una actividad?","options":["Un evento de inicio","Objeto de datos (data object)","Un carril dedicado a documentos","Una pasarela"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los objetos de datos representan información usada o generada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN artifact represents a document used in an activity?","options":["A start event","Data object","A lane dedicated to documents","A gateway"],"explanation":"Data objects represent information used or produced."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué artefacto BPMN añade explicaciones al diagrama sin afectar al flujo?","options":["Una tarea de usuario que el lector debe completar","Una pasarela","Un evento","Anotación de texto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las anotaciones aclaran sin cambiar el comportamiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN artifact adds explanations to the diagram without affecting the flow?","options":["A user task the reader must complete","A gateway","An event","Text annotation"],"explanation":"Annotations clarify without changing behavior."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué beneficio tiene el process modeler de Appian para el analista?","options":["Escribir código Java para cada nodo","Diseñar visualmente con notación similar a BPMN","Ninguno","Gestionar servidores"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El modelador visual permite al analista colaborar en el diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What benefit does Appian's process modeler give the analyst?","options":["Writing Java code for each node","Designing visually with BPMN-like notation","None","Managing servers"],"explanation":"The visual modeler lets the analyst collaborate on design."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una tarea debe asignarse a quien tenga menos trabajo dentro de un grupo. ¿Qué indica al equipo el analista?","options":["Nada","Un requisito de reglas de asignación","Que la tarea se asigne siempre al primer usuario del grupo","Un plug-in de correo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las reglas de asignación deben documentarse como requisito.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A task must go to whoever has the least work within a group. What does the analyst tell the team?","options":["Nothing","It's an assignment-rules requirement","Always assign the task to the group's first user","An email plug-in"],"explanation":"Assignment rules must be documented as a requirement."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene usar subprocesos en Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Más nodos en el modelo principal","Ocultar errores","Eliminar la necesidad de pruebas","Reutilizar lógica común","Diagramas más simples y legibles"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Los subprocesos favorecen reutilización y claridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages come from using subprocesses in Appian? (Choose 2)","options":["More nodes in the main model","Hiding errors","Eliminating testing","Reusing common logic","Simpler, more readable diagrams"],"explanation":"Subprocesses favor reuse and clarity."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un subproceso síncrono y uno asíncrono en Appian?","options":["El síncrono no se ejecuta","No hay diferencia","El asíncrono espera a que termine y el síncrono continúa de inmediato","El síncrono espera a que termine; el asíncrono no"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El síncrono bloquea el proceso padre hasta completarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a synchronous and asynchronous subprocess in Appian?","options":["Sync doesn't run","No difference","Async waits for completion and sync continues immediately","Synchronous waits for completion; async doesn't"],"explanation":"Synchronous blocks the parent until it completes."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de integración se usaría para conectar con un servicio web antiguo con XML y WSDL?","options":["RPA siempre","REST con JSON","SOAP","Una hoja de cálculo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los servicios con WSDL se integran vía SOAP.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which integration type would connect to an old web service with XML and WSDL?","options":["Always RPA","REST with JSON","SOAP","A spreadsheet"],"explanation":"WSDL services are integrated via SOAP."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un servicio expone operaciones GET y POST que devuelven JSON. ¿Qué tipo de integración aplica?","options":["REST / HTTP","Base de datos directa","SOAP con contrato WSDL obligatorio","Correo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"GET/POST con JSON indica una API REST.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A service exposes GET and POST operations returning JSON. Which integration type applies?","options":["REST / HTTP","Direct database","SOAP with mandatory WSDL contract","Email"],"explanation":"GET/POST with JSON indicates a REST API."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa en el diagrama una integración que solo consulta datos?","options":["Un fin","Una lectura que no modifica el sistema externo","Una escritura que actualiza el sistema externo","Una tarea humana"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las integraciones de consulta no cambian datos externos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an integration that only queries data represent in the diagram?","options":["An end","A read that doesn't modify the external system","A write that updates the external system","A human task"],"explanation":"Query integrations don't change external data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe aclarar el analista para cada integración del proceso? (Elige 2)","options":["Qué datos se envían y reciben","El nombre del desarrollador","El tamaño de la pantalla","El color del icono","Qué pasa si el sistema externo falla"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Datos y manejo de errores son esenciales en integraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things must the analyst clarify for each process integration? (Choose 2)","options":["What data is sent and received","Developer name","Screen size","Icon color","What happens if the external system fails"],"explanation":"Data and error handling are essential for integrations."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian permite que un proceso espere a un evento externo (p. ej. un mensaje)?","options":["Un script task que comprueba cada segundo si ha llegado el mensaje","Send E-Mail","Un evento de fin","Un evento intermedio de recepción de mensaje"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los eventos de recepción pausan el flujo hasta el mensaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian node lets a process wait for an external event (e.g. a message)?","options":["A script task checking every second whether the message arrived","Send E-Mail","End event","An intermediate receive message event"],"explanation":"Receive events pause the flow until the message."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que un proceso tenga muchos traspasos entre departamentos?","options":["Nada","Que el proceso es muy eficiente y no necesita mejoras","Que hay pocos usuarios","Posibles retrasos y oportunidades de simplificación"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los traspasos suelen generar esperas y errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What do many handoffs between departments in a process indicate?","options":["Nothing","The process is very efficient and needs no improvement","Few users","Possible delays and simplification opportunities"],"explanation":"Handoffs often cause waits and errors."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un cuello de botella en un proceso?","options":["Una notificación","Un evento de fin","Un punto donde se acumula trabajo y se ralentiza el flujo","Una pasarela paralela que acelera el proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cuellos de botella limitan el rendimiento del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a process bottleneck?","options":["A notification","An end event","A point where work piles up and slows the flow","A parallel gateway that speeds the process up"],"explanation":"Bottlenecks limit process throughput."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué capacidad de Appian ayuda a descubrir cuellos de botella con datos reales?","options":["Un grupo","Process mining / Process HQ","Un desplegable","Encuestas anuales a los empleados"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La minería de procesos analiza eventos reales para encontrar ineficiencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian capability helps find bottlenecks with real data?","options":["A group","Process mining / Process HQ","A dropdown","Annual employee surveys"],"explanation":"Process mining analyzes real events to find inefficiencies."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos BPMN/Appian sirven para tomar decisiones automáticas? (Elige 2)","options":["Pasarela XOR con condiciones","Evento de fin","Tarea de usuario","Send E-Mail","Regla de decisión invocada desde el proceso"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Las pasarelas y reglas de decisión automatizan decisiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two BPMN/Appian elements make automatic decisions? (Choose 2)","options":["XOR gateway with conditions","End event","User task","Send E-Mail","Decision rule invoked from the process"],"explanation":"Gateways and decision rules automate decisions."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de Appian representa una tabla de decisión con reglas de negocio?","options":["Decision (decisión)","Grupo","Interfaz con una cuadrícula editable","Carpeta"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El objeto Decision modela tablas de reglas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian object represents a decision table with business rules?","options":["Decision","Group","An interface with an editable grid","Folder"],"explanation":"The Decision object models rule tables."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene modelar reglas de negocio en una tabla de decisión?","options":["Son más lentas","Las reglas son visibles y fáciles de mantener","Las reglas quedan ocultas en el código para que nadie las cambie","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las tablas de decisión hacen las reglas transparentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of modeling business rules in a decision table?","options":["They're slower","Rules are visible and easy to maintain","Rules are hidden in code so nobody changes them","None"],"explanation":"Decision tables make rules transparent."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de tarea BPMN representa enviar un mensaje a otro participante?","options":["Pasarela","Evento de inicio","Tarea de usuario que recibe el mensaje","Tarea de envío (send task)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La tarea de envío comunica con otro participante.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN task type represents sending a message to another participant?","options":["Gateway","Start event","A user task receiving the message","Send task"],"explanation":"The send task communicates with another participant."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de tarea BPMN la ejecuta un sistema sin intervención humana?","options":["Tarea manual realizada fuera del sistema","Ninguna","Tarea de servicio / script","Tarea de usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las tareas de servicio o script son automáticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN task type is executed by a system without human input?","options":["Manual task done outside the system","None","Service / script task","User task"],"explanation":"Service or script tasks are automated."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de tarea BPMN representa trabajo físico fuera del sistema (p. ej. archivar papel)?","options":["Evento","Tarea de script","Tarea de servicio ejecutada automáticamente por Appian","Tarea manual"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La tarea manual ocurre fuera de cualquier sistema.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN task type represents physical work outside the system (e.g. filing paper)?","options":["Event","Script task","A service task automatically run by Appian","Manual task"],"explanation":"The manual task happens outside any system."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Al modelar el proceso futuro, el analista elimina un paso de aprobación que no aporta valor. ¿Qué beneficio busca?","options":["Ninguno","Reducir tiempo y esfuerzo sin perder control","Aumentar el número de pasos para tener más trazabilidad","Cambiar el diseño"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Eliminar pasos sin valor optimiza el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When modeling the future process, the analyst removes an approval step that adds no value. What benefit is sought?","options":["None","Cutting time and effort without losing control","Adding more steps for more traceability","Changing the design"],"explanation":"Removing valueless steps optimizes the process."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos métricas ayudan a evaluar el proceso actual? (Elige 2)","options":["Edad de los usuarios","Tiempo de ciclo","Tamaño de la oficina","Volumen de casos","Número de colores"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Tiempo y volumen describen el rendimiento del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two metrics help evaluate the current process? (Choose 2)","options":["User age","Cycle time","Office size","Case volume","Number of colors"],"explanation":"Time and volume describe process performance."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el tiempo de ciclo de un proceso?","options":["Tiempo que tarda el servidor en arrancar","Tiempo desde que empieza un caso hasta que termina","El tiempo de despliegue","El tiempo de una reunión"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El tiempo de ciclo mide la duración total del caso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a process's cycle time?","options":["Time the server takes to boot","Time from a case's start to its end","Deployment time","A meeting's length"],"explanation":"Cycle time measures total case duration."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un carril \"Sistema\" en un diagrama de procesos de Appian?","options":["Las actividades automatizadas por Appian","Las tareas del equipo de TI que gestiona los servidores","El cliente","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Es común separar actividades automáticas en su propio carril.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"System\" lane in an Appian process diagram represent?","options":["Activities automated by Appian","Tasks for the IT team managing servers","The customer","Nothing"],"explanation":"Automated activities are often separated into their own lane."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evento modela que un caso se cancele si el cliente lo solicita mientras está en curso?","options":["Un evento de inicio","Una pasarela AND","Una tarea de usuario al final del proceso que pregunta si cancelar","Un evento de mensaje/señal que interrumpe el proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los eventos interruptores modelan cancelaciones en cualquier momento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which event models a case being cancelled if the customer asks mid-way?","options":["A start event","An AND gateway","A user task at the end asking whether to cancel","A message/signal event interrupting the process"],"explanation":"Interrupting events model cancellations at any time."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos tipos de datos de proceso conviene identificar al modelar? (Elige 2)","options":["Ninguno","Contraseñas de usuarios","Datos personales irrelevantes","Datos que se generan en cada paso","Datos de entrada del caso"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Entradas y datos generados definen variables y registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two kinds of process data should be identified while modeling? (Choose 2)","options":["None","User passwords","Irrelevant personal data","Data produced at each step","Case input data"],"explanation":"Inputs and produced data define variables and records."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué son las variables de proceso (pv) en Appian?","options":["Grupos","Las variables de entorno del servidor de Appian","Datos que el proceso guarda durante su ejecución","Constantes globales"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las pv almacenan datos de la instancia del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are process variables (pv) in Appian?","options":["Groups","Environment variables of the Appian server","Data the process holds while running","Global constants"],"explanation":"pvs store the process instance's data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos de inicio puede tener un proceso Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Inicio por formulario/acción","Inicio por carril","Inicio por temporizador o mensaje","Inicio por evento de fin","Inicio por pasarela"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Los procesos pueden iniciarse por acción de usuario, temporizador o mensaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two kinds of start can an Appian process have? (Choose 2)","options":["Form/action start","Lane start","Timer or message start","End-event start","Gateway start"],"explanation":"Processes start via user action, timer or message."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una solicitud de vacaciones superior a 10 días requiere aprobación de RR. HH. además del jefe. ¿Cómo se modela?","options":["XOR tras la aprobación del jefe que evalúa los días","No se modela","Pasarela paralela que siempre envía a RR. HH. y al jefe","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La condición determina si hay paso adicional.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A vacation request over 10 days needs HR approval besides the manager. How is it modeled?","options":["XOR after the manager approval evaluating the days","It isn't modeled","A parallel gateway always sending to HR and manager","An end event"],"explanation":"The condition determines whether there's an extra step."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el término \"camino feliz\" (happy path) en un proceso?","options":["El camino más largo","El camino que más les gusta a los usuarios","El de error","El flujo principal sin excepciones"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El camino feliz es el flujo esperado sin incidencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does \"happy path\" mean in a process?","options":["The longest path","The path users like the most","The error path","The main flow with no exceptions"],"explanation":"The happy path is the expected flow with no issues."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos excepciones debe considerar el analista al modelar una integración? (Elige 2)","options":["Los datos devueltos son inválidos","Llueve","El usuario cambia de navegador","El logo cambia","El servicio no responde"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Errores de disponibilidad y de datos deben manejarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two exceptions must the analyst consider when modeling an integration? (Choose 2)","options":["Returned data is invalid","It rains","The user switches browsers","The logo changes","The service doesn't respond"],"explanation":"Availability and data errors must be handled."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué capacidad de Appian permite exponer un proceso a otros sistemas?","options":["Una Web API","Un grupo","Una carpeta","Un informe con gráficos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las Web APIs exponen endpoints que pueden iniciar procesos o devolver datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian capability exposes a process to other systems?","options":["A Web API","A group","A folder","A report with charts"],"explanation":"Web APIs expose endpoints that can start processes or return data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuál es la diferencia entre una integración y una Web API en Appian?","options":["Ninguna existe","La Web API llama a sistemas externos y la integración recibe llamadas","Son idénticas","La integración llama hacia fuera; la Web API recibe llamadas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Integración = saliente; Web API = entrante.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between an integration and a Web API in Appian?","options":["Neither exists","A Web API calls external systems and an integration receives calls","They're identical","An integration calls out; a Web API receives calls"],"explanation":"Integration = outbound; Web API = inbound."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un analista identifica que un empleado valida manualmente si un NIF tiene formato correcto. ¿Qué propone?","options":["Nada","Formar al empleado para que revise más despacio","Un informe","Una validación automática en el formulario"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las validaciones automáticas evitan errores y esfuerzo manual.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An analyst finds an employee manually checks whether a tax ID is well formed. What do they propose?","options":["Nothing","Training the employee to check more slowly","A report","An automatic validation on the form"],"explanation":"Automatic validations avoid errors and manual effort."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de Appian permite pedir varias aprobaciones a la vez, una por cada miembro de una lista?","options":["Un evento de fin","Instancias múltiples del nodo (MNI)","Send E-Mail","Una pasarela XOR por cada aprobador"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Multiple Node Instances ejecuta un nodo para cada elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian feature asks for several approvals at once, one per list member?","options":["An end event","Multiple Node Instances (MNI)","Send E-Mail","An XOR gateway per approver"],"explanation":"Multiple Node Instances runs a node for each item."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un evento de error en BPMN?","options":["Una tarea completada correctamente","Un inicio","Una decisión","Un fallo que desvía el flujo a un manejo de errores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los eventos de error modelan el manejo de fallos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an error event represent in BPMN?","options":["A successfully completed task","A start","A decision","A failure diverting flow to error handling"],"explanation":"Error events model failure handling."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a que un diagrama de proceso sea legible para negocio? (Elige 2)","options":["Carriles por rol","Cientos de nodos en un solo nivel","Siglas sin explicar","Detalles técnicos de cada expresión","Nombres de tareas con verbo + objeto"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Nombres claros y carriles facilitan la lectura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a process diagram readable for the business? (Choose 2)","options":["Lanes by role","Hundreds of nodes on one level","Unexplained acronyms","Technical details of every expression","Task names as verb + object"],"explanation":"Clear names and lanes ease reading."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nombre de tarea sigue mejor la convención verbo + objeto?","options":["Revisar solicitud","Tarea de Juan","Revisión","Paso 3"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Verbo + objeto describe claramente la actividad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which task name best follows the verb + object convention?","options":["Review request","John's task","Review","Step 3"],"explanation":"Verb + object clearly describes the activity."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un proceso con muchas tareas de \"revisar\" consecutivas por distintas personas?","options":["Nada","Posible redundancia de controles","Que el proceso tiene la calidad máxima posible","Que faltan revisiones"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Revisiones repetidas pueden ser redundantes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a process with many consecutive \"review\" tasks by different people indicate?","options":["Nothing","Possible redundant controls","The process has the highest possible quality","Missing reviews"],"explanation":"Repeated reviews may be redundant."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evento BPMN espera a que se cumpla una condición de negocio?","options":["Tarea","Evento condicional","Evento de fin condicional que termina el proceso si se cumple","Pasarela paralela"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El evento condicional se activa cuando la condición es verdadera.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which BPMN event waits for a business condition to be met?","options":["Task","Conditional event","A conditional end event ending the process if met","Parallel gateway"],"explanation":"The conditional event fires when the condition is true."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos actores suelen modelarse como carriles en un proceso de compras? (Elige 2)","options":["Departamento de compras","Solicitante","Base de datos","Servidor web","Navegador"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Los carriles representan roles de negocio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actors are usually modeled as lanes in a purchasing process? (Choose 2)","options":["Purchasing department","Requester","Database","Web server","Browser"],"explanation":"Lanes represent business roles."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un analista detecta que la mitad de las solicitudes vuelven al solicitante por falta de datos. ¿Qué mejora propone?","options":["Nada","Eliminar el formulario","Añadir un revisor más que devuelva aún más solicitudes","Validaciones y campos obligatorios en el formulario inicial"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Capturar datos completos desde el inicio reduce retrabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An analyst finds half the requests go back to the requester for missing data. What improvement do they propose?","options":["Nothing","Removing the form","Adding another reviewer to send even more back","Validations and required fields on the initial form"],"explanation":"Capturing complete data upfront reduces rework."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evento de Appian puede iniciar un proceso cuando cambia un registro?","options":["Una carpeta","Un temporizador que comprueba cada minuto todas las tablas","Un proceso iniciado al guardar el registro (acción o automatización)","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las acciones de registro o automatizaciones lanzan procesos al cambiar datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian mechanism can start a process when a record changes?","options":["A folder","A timer checking every table every minute","A process started on record save (action or automation)","An end event"],"explanation":"Record actions or automations launch processes on data change."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa en BPMN un pequeño símbolo \"+\" en una actividad?","options":["Nada","Una suma de datos","Una pasarela paralela incrustada en la tarea","Un subproceso colapsado"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El \"+\" indica que la actividad contiene un subproceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a small \"+\" on an activity mean in BPMN?","options":["Nothing","A data sum","A parallel gateway embedded in the task","A collapsed subprocess"],"explanation":"The \"+\" indicates the activity contains a subprocess."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa en BPMN un símbolo de bucle en una actividad?","options":["Un evento","La actividad se ejecuta una sola vez al final del proceso","La actividad se repite mientras se cumpla una condición","Un carril"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El marcador de bucle indica repetición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a loop marker on an activity mean in BPMN?","options":["An event","The activity runs once at the process end","The activity repeats while a condition holds","A lane"],"explanation":"The loop marker indicates repetition."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa en BPMN el marcador de tres líneas paralelas en una actividad?","options":["Instancias múltiples","Un subproceso","Una actividad que se ejecuta tres veces exactamente","Un error"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las tres líneas indican instancias múltiples (paralelas o secuenciales).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the three-parallel-lines marker on an activity mean in BPMN?","options":["Multiple instances","A subprocess","An activity that runs exactly three times","An error"],"explanation":"The three lines indicate multiple instances (parallel or sequential)."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos beneficios aporta modelar el proceso antes de construirlo en Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Entendimiento compartido","Eliminar la necesidad de pruebas","Detección temprana de problemas","Evitar el feedback","Garantizar cero defectos"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Modelar antes alinea al equipo y revela problemas pronto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two benefits come from modeling the process before building it in Appian? (Choose 2)","options":["Shared understanding","Eliminating testing","Early problem detection","Avoiding feedback","Guaranteeing zero defects"],"explanation":"Modeling first aligns the team and surfaces issues early."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que un proceso tenga un paso donde alguien \"espera la llamada\" del cliente?","options":["Que el proceso está totalmente automatizado","Un fin","Nada","Una dependencia externa que podría modelarse como evento"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las esperas externas se modelan como eventos de recepción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a step where someone \"waits for the customer's call\" indicate?","options":["The process is fully automated","An end","Nothing","An external dependency to model as an event"],"explanation":"External waits are modeled as receive events."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas de Appian ayudan a analizar el rendimiento de los procesos en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Process HQ / minería de procesos","El selector de color","Una carpeta de documentos","El editor de expresiones","Informes de procesos"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Los informes y la minería de procesos analizan datos reales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian tools help analyze process performance in production? (Choose 2)","options":["Process HQ / process mining","The color picker","A document folder","The expression editor","Process reports"],"explanation":"Reports and process mining analyze real data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de integración permite el Connected System de tipo HTTP?","options":["Solo envío de correos electrónicos","Ninguna","Llamadas a APIs REST/HTTP","Solo bases de datos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El connected system HTTP sirve para APIs REST.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which integration type does an HTTP Connected System enable?","options":["Only sending emails","None","Calls to REST/HTTP APIs","Only databases"],"explanation":"The HTTP connected system is for REST APIs."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tienen los connected systems preconstruidos (p. ej. para Salesforce o Google)?","options":["Eliminan la necesidad de autenticarse con el sistema externo","Ninguna","Simplifican la integración con plantillas listas","Son obligatorios"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los conectores preconstruidos aceleran la integración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of prebuilt connected systems (e.g. for Salesforce or Google)?","options":["They remove the need to authenticate with the external system","None","They simplify integration with ready templates","They're mandatory"],"explanation":"Prebuilt connectors speed up integration."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un diagrama donde una tarea no tiene flujo de salida?","options":["Que es una pasarela","Nada","Un error de modelado","Que la tarea es el final correcto del proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las actividades deben conectar con otra actividad o un evento de fin.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a diagram where a task has no outgoing flow indicate?","options":["It's a gateway","Nothing","A modeling error","The task is the process's correct end"],"explanation":"Activities must connect to another activity or an end event."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa el nivel de detalle adecuado en un diagrama para negocio?","options":["Cada clic del usuario y cada consulta a la base de datos","Solo el inicio y el fin","Los pasos y decisiones relevantes, sin detalles técnicos","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El diagrama de negocio debe ser comprensible y relevante.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the right level of detail in a diagram for the business?","options":["Every user click and every database query","Only start and end","Relevant steps and decisions, without technical details","Nothing"],"explanation":"The business diagram should be understandable and relevant."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso tiene una aprobación que solo ocurre en el 2% de los casos. ¿Cómo se modela?","options":["Una rama condicional desde una pasarela XOR","En el flujo principal para todos los casos","Con un evento de fin","No se modela"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los casos poco frecuentes se modelan como ramas condicionales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process has an approval occurring in only 2% of cases. How is it modeled?","options":["A conditional branch from an XOR gateway","In the main flow for every case","With an end event","Not modeled"],"explanation":"Rare cases are modeled as conditional branches."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones ayudan a validar un modelo to-be con SMEs? (Elige 2)","options":["Evitar preguntas","Pedir que identifiquen excepciones que faltan","Recorrer casos reales sobre el diagrama","Enviarlo sin explicación","Aprobarlo sin revisarlo"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Recorrer casos reales revela huecos del modelo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions help validate a to-be model with SMEs? (Choose 2)","options":["Avoiding questions","Asking them to spot missing exceptions","Walking real cases through the diagram","Sending it with no explanation","Approving it unreviewed"],"explanation":"Walking real cases reveals model gaps."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre una pasarela de división y una de unión?","options":["La división abre caminos; la unión los junta","Ninguna existe","Son lo mismo","La unión abre caminos y la división los junta de nuevo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Split divide el flujo; join lo sincroniza o fusiona.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a split gateway and a join gateway?","options":["A split opens paths; a join merges them","Neither exists","They're the same","A join opens paths and a split merges them back"],"explanation":"A split divides the flow; a join syncs or merges it."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa un carril que contiene solo tareas de un cliente externo?","options":["Un sistema automático gestionado por Appian","El papel del cliente en el proceso","Un error de diseño","Un evento"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los clientes pueden tener su carril o pool para mostrar sus interacciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lane containing only an external customer's tasks represent?","options":["An automated system managed by Appian","The customer's part in the process","A design error","An event"],"explanation":"Customers can have their lane or pool to show their interactions."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué capacidad de Appian permite que un cliente externo complete su tarea en el proceso?","options":["Un grupo interno","Una tarea de usuario asignada a una cuenta compartida de empleados","Un informe","Un portal o formulario externo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Portals permiten la participación de usuarios externos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian capability lets an external customer complete their task in the process?","options":["An internal group","A user task assigned to a shared employee account","A report","A portal or external form"],"explanation":"Portals enable external user participation."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene un modelo de proceso demasiado complejo en un solo nivel? (Elige 2)","options":["Difícil de entender","Más fácil de validar","Difícil de mantener","Menos errores","Mejor rendimiento siempre"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Los subprocesos reducen la complejidad visual y de mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from an overly complex single-level process model? (Choose 2)","options":["Hard to understand","Easier to validate","Hard to maintain","Fewer errors","Always better performance"],"explanation":"Subprocesses reduce visual and maintenance complexity."}}}]}$exam$::jsonb);

-- appian-associate-developer.json: 500 preguntas
select public.import_exam_unchecked($exam${"slug":"appian-associate-developer","name":"Appian Certified Associate Developer","vendor":"Appian","code":"ACD101","language":"es","description":"Preguntas de práctica escritas a partir de los objetivos oficiales publicados por Appian (blueprint de octubre de 2023). No son preguntas del examen real.","exam":{"questions":60,"minutes":60,"passing":"73%","mini":{"questions":20,"minutes":20}},"domains":[{"code":"D1","name":"Introduction to the Appian platform","weight":14,"docs":[{"title":"Appian Designer","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/welcome-app-designer.html"},{"title":"Application building tutorial","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Application_Building_Tutorial.html"}]},{"code":"D2","name":"General Appian principles","weight":9,"docs":[{"title":"Object security","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/object-security.html"},{"title":"Appian design guidance","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/appian-recommendations.html"},{"title":"Recommended object names","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Standard_Object_Names.html"}]},{"code":"D3","name":"Data persistence","weight":13,"docs":[{"title":"Custom data types","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Custom_Data_Types.html"},{"title":"Data stores","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Data_Stores.html"},{"title":"CDT design guidance","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/cdt_design_guidance.html"}]},{"code":"D4","name":"Appian development: Process models","weight":17,"docs":[{"title":"Process model object","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/process-model-object.html"},{"title":"Configuring the user input task","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Configuring_the_User_Input_Task.html"},{"title":"Process model recipes","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Process_Model_Recipes.html"}]},{"code":"D5","name":"Appian development: Interface design","weight":19,"docs":[{"title":"Interface object","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/interface_object.html"},{"title":"Local variables","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Local_Variables.html"},{"title":"Interface recipes","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/SAIL_Recipes.html"}]},{"code":"D6","name":"Appian development: Records","weight":13,"docs":[{"title":"About record types","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Record_Type_Object.html"},{"title":"Record type relationships","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/record-type-relationships.html"},{"title":"Record actions","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/record-actions.html"}]},{"code":"D7","name":"Appian development: Expression rules","weight":15,"docs":[{"title":"Expression rules","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Expression_Rules.html"},{"title":"Expressions","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Expressions.html"},{"title":"Appian functions","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Appian_Functions.html"}]}],"questions":[{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador recibe un error desconocido al desplegar y quiere saber si es un problema conocido con solución documentada por el soporte de Appian. ¿Qué recurso consulta primero?","options":["La base de conocimiento (Knowledge Base) de Appian","Las notas de su equipo","El Appian AppMarket, donde se publican los parches de cada versión de la plataforma","Un foro de otro fabricante"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La base de conocimiento recoge artículos de soporte sobre errores conocidos y sus soluciones o workarounds.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer gets an unknown error while deploying and wants to know if it's a known issue with a documented fix from Appian Support. Which resource do they check first?","options":["The Appian Knowledge Base","Their team's notes","The Appian AppMarket, where patches for each platform version are published","Another vendor's forum"],"explanation":"The Knowledge Base collects support articles about known errors and their fixes or workarounds."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador necesita la sintaxis exacta y los parámetros de la función a!queryRecordType para la versión de Appian que usa. ¿Qué recurso es el más fiable?","options":["Una respuesta antigua en un foro","La documentación oficial de Appian para su versión","Un vídeo de un curso de hace tres años sobre una versión anterior de la plataforma","Probar parámetros al azar"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La documentación oficial (docs.appian.com) es la referencia de funciones y está versionada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer needs the exact syntax and parameters of a!queryRecordType for their Appian version. Which resource is most reliable?","options":["An old forum answer","The official Appian documentation for their version","A three-year-old course video about an earlier platform version","Trying random parameters"],"explanation":"The official documentation (docs.appian.com) is the function reference and is versioned."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo busca un plug-in ya existente para generar códigos QR en Appian en lugar de desarrollarlo. ¿Dónde debe buscar?","options":["En la base de conocimiento, que incluye los plug-ins descargables de la comunidad","En el diseñador de procesos","En el AppMarket de Appian","En la consola de administración"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El AppMarket ofrece plug-ins, plantillas de connected systems y aplicaciones reutilizables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team is looking for an existing plug-in to generate QR codes in Appian instead of building one. Where should it look?","options":["The Knowledge Base, which includes downloadable community plug-ins","The process modeler","The Appian AppMarket","The Admin Console"],"explanation":"The AppMarket offers plug-ins, connected system templates and reusable applications."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador junior quiere aprender buenas prácticas de diseño de Appian con guías y contenidos curados por Appian. ¿Qué recurso encaja?","options":["Los logs del servidor","La consola de administración, que incluye una sección de tutoriales interactivos para cada objeto","El registro de auditoría del entorno","Appian Max y Appian Academy"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian Max y Appian Academy concentran contenidos de aprendizaje y buenas prácticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A junior developer wants to learn Appian design best practices from guides and content curated by Appian. Which resource fits?","options":["Server logs","The Admin Console, which includes interactive tutorials for each object","The environment's audit log","Appian Max and Appian Academy"],"explanation":"Appian Max and Appian Academy concentrate learning content and best practices."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador tiene una duda de diseño poco común y quiere conocer la experiencia de otros desarrolladores. ¿Qué recurso es adecuado?","options":["El Health Check del entorno, que analiza los diseños de otros clientes","El AppMarket","La documentación de una función","Los foros de la comunidad de Appian"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La comunidad de Appian permite consultar y preguntar a otros desarrolladores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer has an uncommon design question and wants to learn from other developers' experience. Which resource fits?","options":["The environment's Health Check, which analyzes other customers' designs","The AppMarket","A function's documentation","The Appian Community forums"],"explanation":"The Appian Community lets you browse and ask other developers."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuál es la función principal del objeto aplicación en Appian?","options":["Ejecutar la lógica de negocio de la solución y almacenar sus datos en la base de datos","Agrupar los objetos de diseño de una solución para organizarlos y desplegarlos","Sustituir a las carpetas","Definir la seguridad de los usuarios finales"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La aplicación agrupa objetos para organizarlos, exportarlos y desplegarlos; no ejecuta lógica ni guarda datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the main purpose of the application object in Appian?","options":["Run the solution's business logic and store its data in the database","Group a solution's design objects to organize and deploy them","Replace folders","Define end-user security"],"explanation":"The application groups objects to organize, export and deploy them; it doesn't run logic or store data."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo crea una aplicación nueva de gestión de vacaciones. ¿Qué práctica de nomenclatura recomienda Appian para sus objetos?","options":["Usar un prefijo corto de aplicación en los nombres de los objetos","Nombrar cada objeto con el nombre completo del desarrollador y la fecha de creación","Usar nombres genéricos como \"regla1\"","No usar convenciones"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un prefijo común identifica a qué aplicación pertenece cada objeto y evita colisiones de nombres.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team creates a new vacation management application. Which naming practice does Appian recommend for its objects?","options":["Use a short application prefix in object names","Name each object with the developer's full name and creation date","Use generic names like \"rule1\"","Use no conventions"],"explanation":"A common prefix shows which application each object belongs to and avoids name collisions."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Al crear una aplicación, ¿qué grupos suelen configurarse como base para la seguridad?","options":["Un grupo de administradores de la aplicación y un grupo de usuarios","Ningún grupo","Un único grupo con todos los usuarios del entorno, que simplifica la configuración","Un grupo por cada objeto"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los grupos de administradores y usuarios de la aplicación sirven de base para la seguridad de objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When creating an application, which groups are typically set up as the basis for security?","options":["An application administrators group and a users group","No groups","A single group with every user in the environment, which simplifies configuration","One group per object"],"explanation":"Application administrator and user groups form the basis of object security."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere organizar las reglas de expresión de una aplicación para que otros las encuentren y para heredar seguridad. ¿Qué objeto usa?","options":["Un grupo","Un sitio","Un objeto aplicación adicional solo para las reglas de expresión","Una carpeta de reglas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las carpetas de reglas organizan reglas, constantes e interfaces y permiten heredar seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to organize an application's expression rules so others can find them and inherit security. Which object do they use?","options":["A group","A site","An additional application object just for expression rules","A rule folder"],"explanation":"Rule folders organize rules, constants and interfaces and allow inherited security."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un objeto de diseño se añade a dos aplicaciones distintas?","options":["Se crea una copia independiente del objeto en cada aplicación","El objeto es el mismo y se comparte entre ambas aplicaciones","Appian lo impide","Se elimina de la primera"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un objeto puede pertenecer a varias aplicaciones; no se duplica, y un cambio afecta a ambas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if a design object is added to two different applications?","options":["An independent copy of the object is created in each application","It's the same object, shared by both applications","Appian prevents it","It's removed from the first"],"explanation":"An object can belong to several applications; it isn't duplicated, and a change affects both."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere almacenar los documentos que suben los usuarios de su aplicación con permisos propios. ¿Qué estructura de Appian utiliza?","options":["Un grupo","Una constante","Una carpeta de documentos dentro de una knowledge center","Una carpeta de reglas, que admite documentos de usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los documentos se guardan en carpetas de documentos dentro de knowledge centers, con su propia seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants to store documents uploaded by its application's users with their own permissions. Which Appian structure does it use?","options":["A group","A constant","A document folder inside a knowledge center","A rule folder, which accepts user documents"],"explanation":"Documents are stored in document folders inside knowledge centers, with their own security."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una empresa quiere entender cómo se ejecutan realmente sus procesos (tiempos, desviaciones, cuellos de botella) a partir de los registros de sus sistemas. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian encaja?","options":["Una constante","RPA, porque los robots registran cada paso de los procesos existentes","Un interface","Process Mining"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Process Mining analiza los registros de eventos para descubrir cómo funcionan los procesos reales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A company wants to understand how its processes actually run (times, deviations, bottlenecks) from its systems' event logs. Which Appian capability fits?","options":["A constant","RPA, because robots record every step of existing processes","An interface","Process Mining"],"explanation":"Process Mining analyzes event logs to discover how real processes work."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso requiere introducir datos en una aplicación de escritorio antigua sin API. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian permite automatizarlo?","options":["Process Mining, que ejecuta las tareas que descubre en los registros","Un record type","Un sitio","RPA (automatización robótica de procesos)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"RPA automatiza la interacción con interfaces de sistemas sin API.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process requires entering data into an old desktop application with no API. Which Appian capability can automate it?","options":["Process Mining, which runs the tasks it discovers in logs","A record type","A site","RPA (robotic process automation)"],"explanation":"RPA automates interaction with the user interfaces of systems without an API."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una aseguradora recibe miles de formularios escaneados y quiere extraer sus campos automáticamente para iniciar procesos. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian encaja?","options":["Un grupo","Un portal","Procesamiento inteligente de documentos (IDP) o AI skills de extracción","Una regla de expresión que lee el texto de las imágenes con funciones de cadena"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las capacidades de IDP y AI skills extraen y clasifican información de documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An insurer receives thousands of scanned forms and wants to extract their fields automatically to start processes. Which Appian capability fits?","options":["A group","A portal","Intelligent document processing (IDP) or extraction AI skills","An expression rule reading text from images with string functions"],"explanation":"IDP and AI skills extract and classify information from documents."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una organización tiene datos de clientes en tres sistemas distintos y quiere verlos y relacionarlos en Appian sin migrarlos. ¿Qué capacidad encaja?","options":["Copiar los tres sistemas a la base de datos de Appian todas las noches con un proceso","RPA","Process Mining","Data fabric mediante record types"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El data fabric de Appian unifica datos de distintas fuentes mediante record types y relaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An organization has customer data in three different systems and wants to view and relate it in Appian without migrating it. Which capability fits?","options":["Copy all three systems to the Appian database nightly with a process","RPA","Process Mining","Data fabric via record types"],"explanation":"Appian's data fabric unifies data from different sources through record types and relationships."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de problema de negocio es un buen caso de uso para Appian?","options":["Un firmware de dispositivos","Un sistema de edición de vídeo","Un videojuego en 3D con gráficos en tiempo real y alta tasa de refresco","Un proceso con tareas humanas, reglas y datos de varios sistemas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian destaca en la automatización de procesos que combinan personas, sistemas, reglas y datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which kind of business problem is a good use case for Appian?","options":["Device firmware","A video editing system","A 3D video game with real-time graphics and a high refresh rate","A process with human tasks, rules and data from several systems"],"explanation":"Appian excels at automating processes that combine people, systems, rules and data."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos recursos son oficiales de Appian para resolver dudas técnicas? (Elige 2)","options":["Un PDF de preguntas filtradas","La documentación de Appian","Un repositorio personal de un desarrollador desconocido","La comunidad de Appian","Un chat de otro producto"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"La documentación y la comunidad son recursos oficiales; los materiales filtrados no son fiables ni legítimos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two are official Appian resources for technical questions? (Choose 2)","options":["A PDF of leaked questions","Appian documentation","An unknown developer's personal repository","Appian Community","Another product's chat"],"explanation":"Documentation and Community are official resources; leaked material is neither reliable nor legitimate."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere exportar todos los objetos de una aplicación para desplegarlos en otro entorno. ¿Qué le facilita tener los objetos asociados a la aplicación?","options":["Nada","Exportar la aplicación como un paquete con sus objetos","Ejecutar los procesos más rápido","Que los objetos se sincronicen solos con el otro entorno sin necesidad de exportar"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Asociar los objetos a la aplicación permite exportarlos o desplegarlos juntos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to export all of an application's objects to deploy them to another environment. What does having the objects associated with the application make easier?","options":["Nothing","Exporting the application as a package with its objects","Running processes faster","Objects syncing automatically to the other environment without exporting"],"explanation":"Associating objects with the application lets you export or deploy them together."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirven las constantes en una aplicación de Appian?","options":["Almacenar los datos de negocio que introducen los usuarios en los formularios","Guardar valores reutilizables (p. ej. un grupo o un texto) referenciados desde otros objetos","Iniciar procesos","Definir pantallas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las constantes guardan valores fijos o referencias a objetos que se reutilizan en reglas, procesos e interfaces.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are constants used for in an Appian application?","options":["Storing business data users enter in forms","Storing reusable values (e.g. a group or a text) referenced from other objects","Starting processes","Defining screens"],"explanation":"Constants hold fixed values or object references reused across rules, processes and interfaces."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador debe comprobar en qué versiones de Appian está disponible una funcionalidad antes de usarla. ¿Dónde lo consulta?","options":["En las notas de la versión (release notes) de la documentación","En los logs del servidor de su entorno de desarrollo","En los grupos","En el AppMarket"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las release notes describen qué funcionalidades llegan en cada versión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer must check which Appian versions include a feature before using it. Where do they look?","options":["The release notes in the documentation","Their development environment's server logs","Groups","The AppMarket"],"explanation":"Release notes describe which features arrive in each version."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario de negocio quiere acceder en una sola página a las acciones, registros e informes de su departamento. ¿Qué objeto de Appian ofrece esa experiencia?","options":["Un sitio (site)","Un grupo","Un process model","Una regla de expresión que devuelve una lista de enlaces a cada objeto"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los sitios agrupan páginas (registros, acciones, informes, interfaces) en una experiencia de usuario enfocada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A business user wants one place for their department's actions, records and reports. Which Appian object provides that experience?","options":["A site","A group","A process model","An expression rule returning a list of links to each object"],"explanation":"Sites group pages (records, actions, reports, interfaces) into a focused user experience."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una organización quiere que clientes externos sin cuenta de Appian rellenen un formulario público. ¿Qué capacidad encaja?","options":["Process Mining","Un portal de Appian","Un sitio interno","Crear una cuenta de usuario básico para cada cliente externo que lo necesite"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los portales ofrecen interfaces públicas a usuarios sin cuenta de Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An organization wants external customers without Appian accounts to fill in a public form. Which capability fits?","options":["Process Mining","An Appian portal","An internal site","Create a basic user account for every external customer who needs it"],"explanation":"Portals provide public interfaces to users without Appian accounts."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene definir al crear la estructura de una aplicación nueva? (Elige 2)","options":["El color de cada botón","Las contraseñas de los usuarios","Los datos de producción de prueba","Grupos de seguridad de la aplicación","Prefijo de la aplicación y estructura de carpetas"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Prefijo, carpetas y grupos forman la estructura básica sobre la que se organiza y asegura la aplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should be defined when setting up a new application's structure? (Choose 2)","options":["Each button's color","User passwords","Test production data","Application security groups","Application prefix and folder structure"],"explanation":"Prefix, folders and groups form the basic structure for organizing and securing the application."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un analista quiere saber dónde se pierde más tiempo en el proceso de compras, que se ejecuta en un ERP externo. ¿Qué paso es el primero con Process Mining?","options":["Reconstruir el proceso de compras en Appian antes de analizar nada","Obtener el registro de eventos del ERP (caso, actividad, fecha)","Contratar RPA","Crear un record type de compras"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Process Mining necesita un registro de eventos con identificador de caso, actividad y marca de tiempo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An analyst wants to know where the most time is lost in the purchasing process, which runs in an external ERP. What's the first step with Process Mining?","options":["Rebuild the purchasing process in Appian before analyzing anything","Get the ERP's event log (case, activity, timestamp)","Buy RPA","Create a purchasing record type"],"explanation":"Process Mining needs an event log with case ID, activity and timestamp."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo necesita integrar un servicio externo con un conector ya preparado. ¿Qué recurso consulta antes de construir la integración desde cero?","options":["Los grupos del sistema","La consola de procesos","La base de conocimiento, que publica las credenciales de los servicios externos","El AppMarket, por si existe una plantilla de connected system"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El AppMarket incluye plantillas de connected systems y plug-ins de integración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team needs to integrate an external service with a ready-made connector. Which resource does it check before building from scratch?","options":["System groups","The process console","The Knowledge Base, which publishes external services' credentials","The AppMarket, for an existing connected system template"],"explanation":"The AppMarket includes connected system templates and integration plug-ins."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una aplicación de Appian combina tareas humanas, una integración con un CRM, reglas de negocio y un robot que actualiza un sistema legado. ¿Qué describe mejor este enfoque?","options":["Un CMS","Desarrollo de software tradicional sin plataforma, con código a medida en cada componente","Un data warehouse","Automatización de procesos que orquesta personas, sistemas y bots"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian orquesta personas, sistemas, reglas y robots dentro de un mismo proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An Appian application combines human tasks, a CRM integration, business rules and a bot updating a legacy system. What best describes this approach?","options":["A CMS","Traditional platform-less software development, with custom code in every component","A data warehouse","Process automation orchestrating people, systems and bots"],"explanation":"Appian orchestrates people, systems, rules and robots within one process."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Al revisar una aplicación heredada, un desarrollador encuentra objetos sin prefijo, en carpetas sueltas y sin asociar a ninguna aplicación. ¿Qué riesgo principal tiene?","options":["Que los objetos se ejecutan más despacio por no tener prefijo","Que los usuarios no pueden iniciar sesión","Ninguno","Es difícil saber a qué solución pertenecen y desplegarlos de forma completa"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Sin estructura, se pierde trazabilidad y se corre el riesgo de olvidar objetos en los despliegues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Reviewing a legacy application, a developer finds objects with no prefix, in loose folders and not associated with any application. What's the main risk?","options":["Objects run slower for lacking a prefix","Users can't log in","None","It's hard to know which solution they belong to and deploy them completely"],"explanation":"Without structure, traceability is lost and objects risk being left out of deployments."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recurso de Appian conviene para seguir un itinerario formativo estructurado antes de la certificación?","options":["La consola de administración del entorno de producción","El AppMarket","Los logs de despliegue","Appian Academy (cursos y rutas de aprendizaje)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian Academy ofrece cursos y rutas de aprendizaje oficiales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian resource fits for following a structured learning path before certification?","options":["The production environment's Admin Console","The AppMarket","Deployment logs","Appian Academy (courses and learning paths)"],"explanation":"Appian Academy offers official courses and learning paths."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso de aprobación de facturas tarda días porque los aprobadores no saben qué tienen pendiente. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian ayuda más directamente?","options":["Tareas asignadas en una lista de tareas (task list) con notificaciones","Process Mining","Un informe mensual que muestre cuántas facturas se aprobaron el mes anterior","RPA"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las tareas asignadas y su lista de pendientes hacen visible el trabajo y aceleran las aprobaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An invoice approval process takes days because approvers don't know what's pending. Which Appian capability helps most directly?","options":["Tasks assigned in a task list with notifications","Process Mining","A monthly report showing how many invoices were approved last month","RPA"],"explanation":"Assigned tasks and a pending list make work visible and speed up approvals."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un nuevo miembro del equipo quiere entender rápidamente qué contiene una aplicación (procesos, registros, interfaces). ¿Dónde lo consulta?","options":["En la consola de administración, en la sección de usuarios","En la vista de la aplicación en Appian Designer","En el AppMarket","En los logs"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Appian Designer muestra los objetos de la aplicación, filtrables por tipo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A new team member wants to quickly understand what an application contains (processes, records, interfaces). Where do they look?","options":["In the Admin Console users section","In the application view in Appian Designer","In the AppMarket","In logs"],"explanation":"Appian Designer shows the application's objects, filterable by type."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja aporta el enfoque low-code de Appian frente al desarrollo tradicional en un proyecto de automatización?","options":["No necesitar datos","Eliminar por completo la necesidad de probar y desplegar las aplicaciones","Construir y modificar aplicaciones más rápido con componentes visuales y reutilizables","No necesitar usuarios"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El low-code acelera la construcción y el cambio, pero no elimina las pruebas ni el ciclo de despliegue.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What advantage does Appian's low-code approach bring over traditional development in an automation project?","options":["Needing no data","Eliminating the need to test and deploy applications entirely","Building and changing applications faster with visual, reusable components","Needing no users"],"explanation":"Low-code speeds building and change, but doesn't remove testing or the deployment cycle."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un responsable pregunta si Appian puede asignar tareas a un grupo para que cualquiera de sus miembros las acepte. ¿Qué respuesta es correcta?","options":["Solo con RPA","Sí: se asignan a un grupo y un miembro puede aceptarlas","Solo en portales","No: cada tarea solo puede asignarse a un usuario concreto definido al diseñar el proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las tareas pueden asignarse a grupos; un miembro acepta la tarea para trabajarla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A manager asks whether Appian can assign tasks to a group so any member can accept them. Which answer is right?","options":["Only with RPA","Yes: they're assigned to a group and a member can accept them","Only in portals","No: each task can only be assigned to a specific user defined at design time"],"explanation":"Tasks can be assigned to groups; a member accepts the task to work on it."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere reutilizar en varias aplicaciones una misma regla que calcula festivos. ¿Qué estructura es adecuada?","options":["No reutilizarla","Escribirla en cada interfaz","Copiar la regla en cada aplicación con un nombre distinto para evitar dependencias","Una aplicación común compartida con objetos reutilizables"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los objetos reutilizables suelen agruparse en una aplicación común para mantenerlos en un solo sitio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants to reuse the same holiday-calculating rule across several applications. Which structure fits?","options":["Don't reuse it","Write it in every interface","Copy the rule into each application with a different name to avoid dependencies","A shared common application with reusable objects"],"explanation":"Reusable objects are usually grouped in a common application to maintain them in one place."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos capacidades de Appian ayudan a automatizar trabajo que hoy hacen personas manualmente? (Elige 2)","options":["Las notas de la versión","El tema de colores del sitio","La lista de usuarios","Extracción de documentos con IA","RPA para tareas repetitivas en interfaces"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"RPA e IDP/AI skills automatizan trabajo manual repetitivo con interfaces y documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian capabilities help automate work people currently do by hand? (Choose 2)","options":["Release notes","The site color theme","The user list","AI document extraction","RPA for repetitive UI tasks"],"explanation":"RPA and IDP/AI skills automate repetitive manual work with interfaces and documents."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar en su aplicación un componente de interfaz que vio en un ejemplo y no sabe qué parámetros admite. ¿Dónde encuentra ejemplos y parámetros de los componentes?","options":["En la documentación de componentes de interfaz de Appian","En la consola de administración, en el apartado de componentes instalados","En el AppMarket","En los logs del servidor"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La documentación describe cada componente, sus parámetros y ejemplos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to try an interface component they saw in an example and doesn't know its parameters. Where do they find component examples and parameters?","options":["In Appian's interface component documentation","In the Admin Console, under installed components","In the AppMarket","In server logs"],"explanation":"The documentation describes each component, its parameters and examples."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una aplicación nueva necesita objetos de seguridad, carpetas y grupos básicos. ¿Qué herramienta de Appian Designer facilita crearlos de forma consistente al iniciar la aplicación?","options":["Un proceso de RPA","Las opciones de creación de aplicación que generan grupos y carpetas iniciales","Una regla de expresión que crea los grupos al ejecutarse por primera vez","Process Mining"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Al crear una aplicación, Appian Designer puede generar grupos y carpetas base con el prefijo de la aplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A new application needs security objects, folders and basic groups. Which Appian Designer feature helps create them consistently when starting the application?","options":["An RPA process","The application creation options that generate initial groups and folders","An expression rule creating the groups the first time it runs","Process Mining"],"explanation":"When creating an application, Appian Designer can generate base groups and folders with the application prefix."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características describen bien el objeto aplicación? (Elige 2)","options":["Ejecuta la lógica de negocio","Guarda los datos de los usuarios","Puede exportarse como paquete para despliegue","Sus objetos pueden compartirse con otras aplicaciones","Sustituye a los grupos de seguridad"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"La aplicación es un contenedor organizativo y de despliegue; los objetos pueden estar en varias aplicaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two characteristics describe the application object well? (Choose 2)","options":["It runs business logic","It stores user data","It can be exported as a package for deployment","Its objects can be shared with other applications","It replaces security groups"],"explanation":"The application is an organizational and deployment container; objects can be in several applications."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una empresa quiere reducir el tiempo de alta de clientes, que hoy implica correos, hojas de cálculo y tres sistemas. ¿Qué propuesta con Appian encaja mejor?","options":["Un informe","Un único formulario sin proceso","Una hoja de cálculo compartida más grande con macros para las tres aplicaciones","Un proceso que orquesta tareas, reglas e integraciones con un registro de clientes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian sustituye flujos manuales dispersos por un proceso orquestado con datos e integraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A company wants to cut customer onboarding time, which now involves emails, spreadsheets and three systems. Which Appian proposal fits best?","options":["A report","A single form with no process","A bigger shared spreadsheet with macros for the three applications","A process orchestrating tasks, rules and integrations with a customer record"],"explanation":"Appian replaces scattered manual flows with an orchestrated process with data and integrations."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recurso consulta un desarrollador para conocer las limitaciones conocidas y los cambios que pueden romper compatibilidad al actualizar la versión de Appian?","options":["El AppMarket","Las notas de la versión y avisos de deprecación","La lista de grupos","Los informes de rendimiento del entorno de desarrollo del último mes"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las release notes incluyen cambios de comportamiento y funcionalidades deprecadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which resource does a developer check to learn known limitations and breaking changes when upgrading Appian?","options":["The AppMarket","Release notes and deprecation notices","The group list","The development environment's performance reports from last month"],"explanation":"Release notes include behavior changes and deprecated features."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador crea objetos para una aplicación pero olvida añadirlos a ella. Al exportar la aplicación para desplegar, ¿qué ocurre?","options":["El despliegue falla siempre","Appian los añade automáticamente porque detecta que pertenecen a la aplicación","Esos objetos no se incluyen en el paquete","Se duplican"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Solo se exportan los objetos asociados a la aplicación (o al paquete); hay que revisar dependencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer creates objects for an application but forgets to add them to it. When exporting the application to deploy, what happens?","options":["The deployment always fails","Appian adds them automatically because it detects they belong to the application","Those objects aren't included in the package","They're duplicated"],"explanation":"Only objects associated with the application (or package) are exported; dependencies must be checked."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere identificar en qué partes de un proceso conviene automatizar con robots y en cuáles con IA. ¿Qué capacidad le ayuda a priorizar con datos reales?","options":["Un record type con los datos actuales de los clientes","Un grupo","Process Mining","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Process Mining revela pasos repetitivos, tiempos y variantes que orientan dónde automatizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants to identify which parts of a process to automate with bots and which with AI. Which capability helps it prioritize with real data?","options":["A record type with current customer data","A group","Process Mining","A constant"],"explanation":"Process Mining reveals repetitive steps, times and variants that guide where to automate."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene organizar los objetos en carpetas con seguridad definida a nivel de carpeta?","options":["Evita los despliegues","Las carpetas aceleran la ejecución de los procesos que contienen","Permite omitir los grupos","Los objetos heredan la seguridad de la carpeta"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La herencia de seguridad de carpetas simplifica gestionar permisos de muchos objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What advantage does organizing objects in folders with folder-level security have?","options":["It avoids deployments","Folders speed up execution of the processes they contain","It lets you skip groups","Objects inherit the folder's security"],"explanation":"Folder security inheritance simplifies managing permissions for many objects."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador encuentra en internet un \"volcado\" con supuestas preguntas reales del examen de Appian. ¿Qué debe hacer?","options":["Compartirlo con el equipo","No usarlo y preparar el examen con recursos oficiales","Usarlo como recurso principal, ya que contiene las preguntas que aparecerán","Venderlo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Usar contenido filtrado vulnera las políticas de certificación y no garantiza el aprendizaje real.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer finds online a \"dump\" with supposed real Appian exam questions. What should they do?","options":["Share it with the team","Not use it, and prepare with official resources","Use it as the main resource, since it contains the questions that will appear","Sell it"],"explanation":"Using leaked content breaches certification policies and doesn't ensure real learning."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de Appian representa un conjunto de usuarios para asignar permisos y tareas?","options":["Un record type que contiene la lista de usuarios de la aplicación","Una carpeta","Un grupo","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los grupos agrupan usuarios para asignar seguridad y trabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian object represents a set of users for assigning permissions and tasks?","options":["A record type containing the application's user list","A folder","A group","A constant"],"explanation":"Groups collect users to assign security and work."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere que una aplicación de Appian conozca a qué departamento pertenece cada usuario para asignar tareas. ¿Qué estructura usa?","options":["Una constante por usuario","Grupos (o una jerarquía de grupos) por departamento","Un campo de texto libre en cada formulario donde el usuario escribe su departamento","Una carpeta por departamento"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los grupos por departamento permiten asignar tareas y permisos de forma mantenible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants an Appian application to know each user's department to assign tasks. Which structure does it use?","options":["A constant per user","Groups (or a group hierarchy) by department","A free-text field on every form where users type their department","A folder per department"],"explanation":"Department groups allow maintainable task and permission assignment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué describe mejor el papel de Appian en un proyecto de automatización inteligente?","options":["Solo un motor de base de datos relacional para guardar los datos de negocio","Solo un editor de formularios","Plataforma que unifica procesos, datos, IA, RPA e integraciones","Solo un servidor de correo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Appian combina orquestación de procesos, datos, IA, RPA e integraciones en una plataforma.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What best describes Appian's role in an intelligent automation project?","options":["Only a relational database engine for business data","Only a form editor","A platform unifying processes, data, AI, RPA and integrations","Only a mail server"],"explanation":"Appian combines process orchestration, data, AI, RPA and integrations in one platform."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador tiene problemas para conectar con un servicio externo y sospecha de un fallo de la plataforma. Ha revisado documentación y comunidad sin éxito. ¿Qué canal oficial usa a continuación?","options":["Abrir un caso con el soporte de Appian","Esperar a la siguiente versión","Publicar las credenciales del servicio en la comunidad para que otros prueben","Reinstalar el entorno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El soporte de Appian atiende posibles fallos de la plataforma tras agotar los recursos de autoservicio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer can't connect to an external service and suspects a platform bug. They've checked documentation and community without luck. Which official channel do they use next?","options":["Open a case with Appian Support","Wait for the next version","Post the service credentials in the community so others can test","Reinstall the environment"],"explanation":"Appian Support handles possible platform issues after self-service resources are exhausted."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo de RR. HH. quiere un cuadro de mando con el estado de las solicitudes y acceso directo a crear nuevas. ¿Qué combinación de objetos encaja?","options":["Una constante","Un grupo","Un único process model que muestra el cuadro de mando al iniciarse","Un sitio con una página de informe y una página de acciones"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los sitios combinan páginas de informes, registros y acciones para un perfil de usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An HR team wants a dashboard with request status and direct access to create new ones. Which object combination fits?","options":["A constant","A group","A single process model showing the dashboard when started","A site with a report page and an actions page"],"explanation":"Sites combine report, record and action pages for a user profile."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas facilitan el mantenimiento de una aplicación a largo plazo? (Elige 2)","options":["Reutilizar reglas e interfaces en lugar de duplicarlas","Duplicar la lógica en cada interfaz","Nombres con prefijo y descripciones en los objetos","No documentar","Guardar todo en una sola carpeta sin estructura"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Nomenclatura clara, descripciones y reutilización reducen el coste de mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices make an application easier to maintain long term? (Choose 2)","options":["Reusing rules and interfaces instead of duplicating them","Duplicating logic in every interface","Prefixed names and descriptions on objects","Not documenting","Keeping everything in one unstructured folder"],"explanation":"Clear naming, descriptions and reuse reduce maintenance cost."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una empresa quiere usar IA para clasificar automáticamente correos entrantes por tipo de solicitud y lanzar el proceso correspondiente. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian encaja?","options":["Una AI skill de clasificación integrada en un proceso","Un portal","Process Mining, que clasifica los correos a partir de los registros de eventos","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las AI skills de clasificación permiten etiquetar contenido y enrutar procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A company wants to use AI to automatically classify incoming emails by request type and start the matching process. Which Appian capability fits?","options":["A classification AI skill integrated into a process","A portal","Process Mining, which classifies emails from event logs","A group"],"explanation":"Classification AI skills label content and route processes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Al planificar una aplicación, el equipo decide qué datos guardar, qué procesos automatizar y qué pantallas necesita cada perfil. ¿Qué objetos de Appian se corresponden con esas tres necesidades?","options":["Record types (datos), process models (procesos) e interfaces/sitios (pantallas)","Solo interfaces","Constantes (datos), grupos (procesos) y carpetas (pantallas)","Solo reglas de expresión"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Records, procesos e interfaces/sitios cubren datos, automatización y experiencia de usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When planning an application, the team decides what data to store, which processes to automate and which screens each profile needs. Which Appian objects match those three needs?","options":["Record types (data), process models (processes) and interfaces/sites (screens)","Only interfaces","Constants (data), groups (processes) and folders (screens)","Only expression rules"],"explanation":"Records, processes and interfaces/sites cover data, automation and user experience."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es Appian Designer?","options":["Un plug-in","El entorno donde los desarrolladores crean y gestionan aplicaciones y objetos","La interfaz donde los usuarios finales completan sus tareas diarias","El motor de base de datos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Appian Designer es el entorno de desarrollo de aplicaciones y objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Appian Designer?","options":["A plug-in","The environment where developers build and manage applications and objects","The interface where end users complete their daily tasks","The database engine"],"explanation":"Appian Designer is the development environment for applications and objects."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere ver ejemplos de patrones de interfaz recomendados (p. ej. formularios por pasos, tarjetas) para copiarlos como punto de partida. ¿Qué recurso integrado le ayuda?","options":["La lista de grupos","Los logs de auditoría de diseño","Los patrones del diseñador de interfaces","El monitor de procesos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El diseñador de interfaces incluye patrones prediseñados basados en buenas prácticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants examples of recommended interface patterns (e.g. wizards, cards) to copy as a starting point. Which built-in resource helps?","options":["The group list","Design audit logs","The interface designer's patterns","The process monitor"],"explanation":"The interface designer includes prebuilt patterns based on best practices."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un responsable quiere saber si Appian sirve para un proceso que necesita a la vez decisiones humanas y respuestas automáticas en segundos. ¿Qué respuesta es adecuada?","options":["Solo con RPA","Solo con portales","Sí: combina tareas humanas con nodos automáticos e integraciones","No: Appian solo gestiona tareas humanas y no puede automatizar pasos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los procesos de Appian combinan nodos humanos y automatizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A manager wants to know whether Appian suits a process needing both human decisions and automated responses within seconds. Which answer fits?","options":["Only with RPA","Only with portals","Yes: it combines human tasks with automated nodes and integrations","No: Appian only manages human tasks and can't automate steps"],"explanation":"Appian processes combine human and automated nodes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué estructura facilita que un equipo grande trabaje en varias aplicaciones sin pisarse?","options":["Un grupo por objeto","Aplicaciones con prefijos distintos y objetos comunes en una aplicación compartida","Sin aplicaciones","Una única aplicación gigante con todos los objetos de todos los equipos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Separar aplicaciones con prefijos y centralizar lo común reduce conflictos y dependencias ocultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which structure helps a large team work on several applications without stepping on each other?","options":["A group per object","Applications with distinct prefixes and common objects in a shared application","No applications","A single giant application with every team's objects"],"explanation":"Separating applications with prefixes and centralizing common items reduces conflicts and hidden dependencies."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un analista de negocio pregunta qué ventaja tiene modelar el proceso en Appian frente a documentarlo en un diagrama estático. ¿Qué respuesta es correcta?","options":["Que se imprime mejor","Que no necesita pruebas","El modelo de proceso es ejecutable: el diagrama es la propia automatización","Ninguna, porque el modelo de Appian solo sirve como documentación del proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"En Appian, el process model se ejecuta; diseño y automatización coinciden.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A business analyst asks what advantage modeling the process in Appian has over documenting it in a static diagram. Which answer is right?","options":["It prints better","It needs no testing","The process model is executable: the diagram is the automation itself","None, because Appian's model only documents the process"],"explanation":"In Appian, the process model runs; design and automation coincide."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos casos de uso encajan con las capacidades de Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Renderizado de vídeo en 4K","Gestión de expedientes con tareas, documentos y plazos","Desarrollo de sistemas operativos","Entrenamiento de modelos de IA desde cero","Automatización de aprobaciones con reglas e integraciones"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Appian se orienta a gestión de casos y automatización de procesos de negocio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two use cases fit Appian's capabilities? (Choose 2)","options":["4K video rendering","Case management with tasks, documents and deadlines","Operating system development","Training AI models from scratch","Approval automation with rules and integrations"],"explanation":"Appian targets case management and business process automation."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere saber qué objetos dependen de una regla antes de modificarla. ¿Qué herramienta de Appian Designer usa?","options":["El monitor de procesos, que lista las reglas que han fallado recientemente","El AppMarket","La vista de dependencias (dependents/precedents) del objeto","Los logs del servidor"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Appian Designer muestra qué objetos usan un objeto (dependientes) y cuáles usa (precedentes).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to know which objects depend on a rule before changing it. Which Appian Designer tool do they use?","options":["The process monitor, which lists rules that failed recently","The AppMarket","The object's dependency view (dependents/precedents)","Server logs"],"explanation":"Appian Designer shows which objects use an object (dependents) and which it uses (precedents)."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una aplicación debe enviar un correo cuando se aprueba una solicitud. ¿Qué elemento de Appian lo realiza dentro del proceso?","options":["Un grupo","El smart service Send E-Mail","Un record type","Una regla de expresión con la función de envío de correo dentro de una interfaz"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los smart services como Send E-Mail ejecutan acciones dentro de los procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An application must send an email when a request is approved. Which Appian element does it within the process?","options":["A group","The Send E-Mail smart service","A record type","An expression rule with an email-sending function inside an interface"],"explanation":"Smart services like Send E-Mail perform actions within processes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere saber si un nombre de objeto ya está en uso en el entorno antes de crearlo. ¿Qué ocurre si intenta crear dos reglas con el mismo nombre?","options":["Se sobrescribe la primera sin avisar","Se crea en otra aplicación","Appian no lo permite: los nombres de reglas son únicos en el entorno","Appian crea ambas y elige una al azar al ejecutarse"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los nombres de reglas y muchos otros objetos deben ser únicos; el prefijo ayuda a evitar colisiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to know if an object name is already in use before creating it. What happens if they try to create two rules with the same name?","options":["The first is silently overwritten","It's created in another application","Appian doesn't allow it: rule names are unique in the environment","Appian creates both and picks one at random at runtime"],"explanation":"Rule names and many other object names must be unique; the prefix helps avoid collisions."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un cliente pregunta cómo Appian ayuda a reducir errores en la entrada de datos manual en un proceso de alta. ¿Qué capacidades se mencionan?","options":["Más campos de texto libre para que el usuario escriba toda la información con detalle","Eliminar el formulario","Process Mining","Validaciones en interfaces y extracción automática de documentos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las validaciones y la extracción automática reducen errores de entrada manual.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A customer asks how Appian helps reduce manual data entry errors in an onboarding process. Which capabilities apply?","options":["More free-text fields so users type all information in detail","Removing the form","Process Mining","Interface validations and automatic document extraction"],"explanation":"Validations and automatic extraction reduce manual entry errors."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador hereda una aplicación y quiere saber qué cambios se hicieron en una interfaz y quién los hizo. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian Designer usa?","options":["El historial de versiones del objeto","La lista de grupos","El monitor de procesos","El AppMarket"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los objetos de diseño mantienen un historial de versiones con autor y fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer inherits an application and wants to know what changes were made to an interface and by whom. Which Appian Designer capability do they use?","options":["The object's version history","The group list","The process monitor","The AppMarket"],"explanation":"Design objects keep a version history with author and date."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recurso de Appian ofrece aplicaciones de ejemplo y soluciones preconstruidas que pueden instalarse y adaptarse?","options":["La documentación de funciones","Los logs del servidor","El diseñador de procesos","El AppMarket"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El AppMarket incluye aplicaciones y soluciones que se pueden instalar y adaptar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian resource offers sample applications and prebuilt solutions that can be installed and adapted?","options":["The function documentation","Server logs","The process designer","The AppMarket"],"explanation":"The AppMarket includes applications and solutions that can be installed and adapted."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario final pregunta dónde ve las tareas que tiene asignadas en una aplicación construida con sitios. ¿Qué respuesta es adecuada?","options":["En Appian Designer, en la lista de objetos de la aplicación","En una página de tareas del sitio (o en la lista de tareas)","En el AppMarket","En la consola de administración"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los usuarios finales trabajan desde sitios o la lista de tareas, no desde Appian Designer.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An end user asks where to see their assigned tasks in an application built with sites. Which answer fits?","options":["In Appian Designer, in the application's object list","On a site tasks page (or the task list)","In the AppMarket","In the Admin Console"],"explanation":"End users work from sites or the task list, not from Appian Designer."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos recursos ayudan a un desarrollador a seguir las buenas prácticas recomendadas por Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Las guías de buenas prácticas de la documentación y Appian Max","Las recomendaciones de Health Check","Los volcados de exámenes","Copiar aplicaciones de otros clientes","Los logs de errores de otros entornos"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Las guías oficiales y el Health Check orientan sobre buenas prácticas y riesgos de diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two resources help a developer follow Appian's recommended best practices? (Choose 2)","options":["Best practice guides in the documentation and Appian Max","Health Check recommendations","Exam dumps","Copying other customers' applications","Error logs from other environments"],"explanation":"Official guides and Health Check point to best practices and design risks."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo duda si crear una aplicación nueva o añadir objetos a una existente para una funcionalidad pequeña del mismo proceso de negocio. ¿Qué criterio aplica?","options":["Crearla en una aplicación al azar","Crear siempre una aplicación nueva para cada funcionalidad, por pequeña que sea","Si pertenece a la misma solución, añadirla a la aplicación existente","No asociarla a ninguna aplicación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las aplicaciones agrupan soluciones coherentes; dividir en exceso complica el mantenimiento y los despliegues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team weighs creating a new application or adding objects to an existing one for a small feature in the same business process. Which criterion applies?","options":["Put it in a random application","Always create a new application for each feature, however small","If it belongs to the same solution, add it to the existing application","Don't associate it with any application"],"explanation":"Applications group coherent solutions; over-splitting complicates maintenance and deployments."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una entidad pública quiere digitalizar solicitudes ciudadanas con formularios, revisión interna y notificaciones. ¿Qué combinación de capacidades de Appian encaja?","options":["Solo RPA","Portal para el ciudadano, proceso con tareas internas y notificaciones","Solo Process Mining sobre las solicitudes en papel de años anteriores","Solo un informe"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El portal recoge la solicitud, el proceso gestiona la revisión y las notificaciones informan al ciudadano.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A public agency wants to digitize citizen requests with forms, internal review and notifications. Which combination of Appian capabilities fits?","options":["Only RPA","A portal for citizens, a process with internal tasks, and notifications","Only Process Mining over previous years' paper requests","Only a report"],"explanation":"The portal collects the request, the process handles review and notifications keep the citizen informed."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la sección de dependencias faltantes al preparar un paquete de despliegue de una aplicación?","options":["Procesos activos","Usuarios que no tienen permisos sobre la aplicación en el entorno de destino","Objetos que usa la aplicación pero que no están incluidos en el paquete","Errores de sintaxis"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Revisar dependencias evita desplegar objetos que referencian otros ausentes en el destino.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the missing dependencies section indicate when preparing an application's deployment package?","options":["Active processes","Users lacking permissions on the application in the target environment","Objects the application uses that aren't included in the package","Syntax errors"],"explanation":"Checking dependencies avoids deploying objects that reference others missing in the target."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere añadir una descripción clara a cada regla para que el equipo entienda su propósito. ¿Por qué es recomendable?","options":["Hace que la regla se ejecute más rápido en producción","Es obligatoria para desplegar","Evita los tests","Facilita encontrar, entender y reutilizar el objeto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las descripciones mejoran la mantenibilidad y la reutilización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to add a clear description to every rule so the team understands its purpose. Why is that recommended?","options":["It makes the rule run faster in production","It's mandatory for deployment","It avoids tests","It makes the object easier to find, understand and reuse"],"explanation":"Descriptions improve maintainability and reuse."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos objetos usan los usuarios finales (no los desarrolladores) para trabajar en una aplicación? (Elige 2)","options":["Sitios","Tareas asignadas","Carpetas de reglas","Objetos aplicación","Constantes"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Los usuarios finales trabajan con sitios y tareas; carpetas, constantes y aplicaciones son objetos de diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two objects do end users (not developers) use to work in an application? (Choose 2)","options":["Sites","Assigned tasks","Rule folders","Application objects","Constants"],"explanation":"End users work with sites and tasks; folders, constants and applications are design objects."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un grupo de usuarios debe poder ver una regla de expresión pero no modificarla. ¿Qué nivel de permiso se asigna?","options":["Deny","Administrator","Viewer","Editor, ya que permite ver y es más flexible si luego necesitan cambiar algo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Viewer permite ver y usar el objeto sin modificarlo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user group must be able to view an expression rule but not change it. Which permission level is assigned?","options":["Deny","Administrator","Viewer","Editor, since it allows viewing and is more flexible if they need changes later"],"explanation":"Viewer allows viewing and using the object without changing it."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre el permiso Editor y Administrator en un objeto de Appian?","options":["Editor solo puede ver","Editor puede cambiar la seguridad del objeto y Administrator solo puede editarlo","Administrator además puede cambiar la seguridad y eliminar el objeto","Ninguna"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Administrator incluye gestionar la seguridad y eliminar; Editor permite modificar el objeto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between Editor and Administrator permissions on an Appian object?","options":["Editor can only view","Editor can change the object's security and Administrator can only edit it","Administrator can also change security and delete the object","None"],"explanation":"Administrator includes managing security and deleting; Editor allows changing the object."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un grupo pertenece a otro grupo con permiso Viewer sobre un objeto, pero el objeto le asigna directamente Deny. ¿Qué permiso efectivo tiene?","options":["Deny","Viewer, porque la pertenencia a un grupo padre siempre prevalece","Ninguno definido","Editor"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Deny prevalece sobre otros permisos asignados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A group belongs to another group with Viewer on an object, but the object assigns it Deny directly. What's its effective permission?","options":["Deny","Viewer, because parent group membership always prevails","Undefined","Editor"],"explanation":"Deny takes precedence over other assigned permissions."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere que la seguridad de las aplicaciones se gestione asignando permisos a grupos y no a usuarios individuales. ¿Qué ventaja aporta?","options":["Mejora el rendimiento de las consultas","Evita los despliegues","Basta con cambiar la pertenencia al grupo cuando cambian las personas","Los usuarios individuales no pueden recibir permisos en Appian"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La seguridad basada en roles (grupos) es más mantenible que asignar permisos a usuarios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants application security managed by assigning permissions to groups rather than individual users. What advantage does this bring?","options":["It improves query performance","It avoids deployments","Only group membership changes when people change","Individual users can't receive permissions in Appian"],"explanation":"Role-based (group) security is more maintainable than assigning permissions to users."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permiso de un process model permite a un usuario iniciar el proceso pero no ver ni modificar su diseño?","options":["Editor","Administrator","Viewer, que permite iniciar y además ver el diseño del modelo","Initiator"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Initiator permite iniciar el proceso sin acceso al diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process model permission lets a user start the process but not view or change its design?","options":["Editor","Administrator","Viewer, which allows starting and also viewing the model design","Initiator"],"explanation":"Initiator allows starting the process without design access."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un administrador de negocio necesita gestionar instancias en curso de un proceso (reasignar tareas, ver el estado) sin cambiar el diseño del modelo. ¿Qué rol de process model encaja?","options":["Editor, porque es necesario poder modificar el modelo para reasignar","Initiator","Viewer","Manager"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Manager permite gestionar instancias en curso sin editar el diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A business admin needs to manage running process instances (reassign tasks, view status) without changing the model design. Which process model role fits?","options":["Editor, since modifying the model is needed to reassign","Initiator","Viewer","Manager"],"explanation":"Manager allows managing running instances without editing the design."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de usuario de Appian tiene acceso completo para administrar el entorno, incluidos todos los objetos?","options":["Viewer","Basic user, si pertenece al grupo de administradores de una aplicación","Initiator","System administrator"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los administradores del sistema tienen acceso total; los usuarios básicos dependen de los permisos asignados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian user type has full access to administer the environment, including all objects?","options":["Viewer","Basic user, if they belong to an application's administrators group","Initiator","System administrator"],"explanation":"System administrators have full access; basic users depend on assigned permissions."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere evitar que todos los usuarios del entorno vean una regla con lógica sensible. ¿Qué configuración revisa?","options":["La carpeta de documentos","El nombre de la regla, para que sea menos evidente su contenido","El process model","El permiso por defecto para todos los demás usuarios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El permiso por defecto define qué pueden hacer los usuarios no incluidos explícitamente en la seguridad del objeto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to stop every user in the environment from viewing a rule with sensitive logic. Which setting do they review?","options":["The document folder","The rule's name, so its content is less obvious","The process model","The default permission for all other users"],"explanation":"The default permission defines what users not explicitly listed in the object's security can do."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño se usa para mostrar y recoger información del usuario en una pantalla?","options":["Constante","Interfaz","Regla de expresión, que es el objeto específico para formularios de usuario","Grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las interfaces definen las pantallas; las reglas de expresión devuelven valores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object is used to display and collect user information on a screen?","options":["Constant","Interface","Expression rule, the object specific to user forms","Group"],"explanation":"Interfaces define screens; expression rules return values."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño define la secuencia de pasos, tareas y decisiones de un flujo de trabajo?","options":["Record type, que contiene el flujo de trabajo de cada registro","Constante","Interfaz","Process model"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El process model define el flujo de trabajo ejecutable.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object defines the sequence of steps, tasks and decisions in a workflow?","options":["Record type, which contains each record's workflow","Constant","Interface","Process model"],"explanation":"The process model defines the executable workflow."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño encapsula lógica reutilizable que devuelve un valor a partir de entradas?","options":["Regla de expresión","Grupo","Process model, que siempre devuelve un valor al terminar","Sitio"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las reglas de expresión reciben rule inputs y devuelven un resultado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object encapsulates reusable logic that returns a value from inputs?","options":["Expression rule","Group","Process model, which always returns a value when finished","Site"],"explanation":"Expression rules take rule inputs and return a result."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño representa una entidad de negocio (p. ej. Cliente) con sus datos, vistas, acciones y relaciones?","options":["Constante","Custom data type (CDT), que incluye vistas y acciones de usuario","Carpeta","Record type"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El record type reúne datos, vistas, acciones y relaciones de una entidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object represents a business entity (e.g. Customer) with its data, views, actions and relationships?","options":["Constant","Custom data type (CDT), which includes user views and actions","Folder","Record type"],"explanation":"The record type brings together an entity's data, views, actions and relationships."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño define la estructura de datos (campos y tipos) usada en procesos e interfaces y que puede mapearse a una tabla?","options":["Grupo","Custom data type (CDT)","Sitio, que define la estructura de datos de la aplicación","Constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El CDT define una estructura de datos con campos tipados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object defines the data structure (fields and types) used in processes and interfaces and can map to a table?","options":["Group","Custom data type (CDT)","Site, which defines the application's data structure","Constant"],"explanation":"The CDT defines a data structure with typed fields."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué se usa un decision object en Appian?","options":["Almacenar los documentos aprobados por los usuarios","Definir grupos","Definir reglas de decisión en forma de tabla (entradas y salidas)","Iniciar procesos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las decisiones modelan lógica de negocio tabular con entradas y salidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a decision object used for in Appian?","options":["Storing documents approved by users","Defining groups","Defining decision rules as a table (inputs and outputs)","Starting processes"],"explanation":"Decisions model tabular business logic with inputs and outputs."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de diseño almacena la configuración de conexión y autenticación con un sistema externo?","options":["Grupo","Constante","Connected system","Integration, que guarda también las credenciales en su propia definición"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El connected system guarda la URL base y la autenticación; las integraciones lo usan para llamar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object stores the connection and authentication settings for an external system?","options":["Group","Constant","Connected system","Integration, which also stores credentials in its own definition"],"explanation":"The connected system holds the base URL and authentication; integrations use it to make calls."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto expone un endpoint HTTP para que sistemas externos llamen a Appian?","options":["Web API","Integration, que recibe llamadas de sistemas externos","Sitio","Connected system"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las Web APIs exponen endpoints; las integraciones llaman hacia fuera.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object exposes an HTTP endpoint for external systems to call Appian?","options":["Web API","Integration, which receives calls from external systems","Site","Connected system"],"explanation":"Web APIs expose endpoints; integrations call outward."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos objetos de diseño se usan para la lógica reutilizable sin interfaz de usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["Decisiones","Sitios","Interfaces","Portales","Reglas de expresión"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Reglas de expresión y decisiones encapsulan lógica; sitios, interfaces y portales son experiencia de usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two design objects are used for reusable logic without a user interface? (Choose 2)","options":["Decisions","Sites","Interfaces","Portals","Expression rules"],"explanation":"Expression rules and decisions encapsulate logic; sites, interfaces and portals are user experience."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué se usa normalmente el entorno de desarrollo en Appian?","options":["Ejecutar los procesos reales de negocio con los usuarios finales","Construir y probar cambios antes de promoverlos","Hacer las pruebas de aceptación de usuario finales","Guardar copias de seguridad"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"En desarrollo se construyen y prueban cambios; después se despliegan a test y producción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is the development environment normally used for in Appian?","options":["Running real business processes with end users","Building and testing changes before promoting them","Final user acceptance testing","Storing backups"],"explanation":"Development is where changes are built and tested; then they're deployed to test and production."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve un entorno de pruebas (test/QA) en el ciclo de Appian?","options":["Almacenar documentos de usuario","Validar los cambios desplegados con pruebas funcionales y de aceptación","Ejecutar el negocio real","Desarrollar nuevas funcionalidades directamente con los datos de producción"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El entorno de test valida los paquetes antes de llegar a producción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a test (QA) environment for in the Appian lifecycle?","options":["Storing user documents","Validating deployed changes with functional and acceptance testing","Running the real business","Building new features directly against production data"],"explanation":"The test environment validates packages before they reach production."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere corregir un error urgente editando una interfaz directamente en producción. ¿Qué práctica recomienda Appian?","options":["Reiniciar el servidor","Corregir en desarrollo, probar y desplegar a producción","Editar en producción para ahorrar tiempo y replicar el cambio en desarrollo más tarde","No corregir"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios siguen el flujo dev → test → prod para mantener los entornos coherentes y controlados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to fix an urgent bug by editing an interface directly in production. Which practice does Appian recommend?","options":["Restart the server","Fix in development, test and deploy to production","Edit in production to save time and replicate the change in development later","Don't fix it"],"explanation":"Changes follow dev → test → prod to keep environments consistent and controlled."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué entorno usan los usuarios finales para su trabajo diario?","options":["Producción","Test","Desarrollo, porque siempre tiene la versión más reciente de la aplicación","Cualquiera"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Producción es el entorno del negocio real; desarrollo y test son para construir y validar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which environment do end users use for their daily work?","options":["Production","Test","Development, because it always has the latest version of the application","Any"],"explanation":"Production is the real business environment; development and test are for building and validating."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un grupo de usuarios necesita poder editar el diseño de un process model y gestionar sus instancias, pero no cambiar su seguridad. ¿Qué rol encaja?","options":["Editor","Initiator","Viewer","Administrator, que es el único que permite editar el diseño"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Editor permite modificar el diseño (y gestionar); Administrator añade cambiar la seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user group needs to edit a process model's design and manage its instances, but not change its security. Which role fits?","options":["Editor","Initiator","Viewer","Administrator, the only one allowing design edits"],"explanation":"Editor allows changing the design (and managing); Administrator adds changing security."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type contiene datos de clientes. Algunos usuarios solo deben ver los clientes de su región. ¿Qué mecanismo aplica?","options":["Crear un record type distinto para cada región con los mismos campos","Ocultar los campos en la interfaz","Seguridad a nivel de registro (record-level security)","Un grupo por cliente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La seguridad a nivel de registro filtra qué filas ve cada usuario según reglas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type holds customer data. Some users should only see customers in their region. Which mechanism applies?","options":["Create a separate record type per region with the same fields","Hide fields in the interface","Record-level security","One group per customer"],"explanation":"Record-level security filters which rows each user sees based on rules."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre la seguridad de un record type (quién lo ve) y la seguridad a nivel de registro?","options":["La primera no existe","La primera controla el acceso al objeto; la segunda, qué registros ve cada usuario","Son la misma configuración con dos nombres distintos en Appian Designer","La segunda solo afecta a los administradores"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad del objeto define quién accede al tipo; la de registro filtra filas concretas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a record type's security (who sees it) and record-level security?","options":["The former doesn't exist","The former controls object access; the latter, which records each user sees","They're the same setting with two names in Appian Designer","The latter only affects administrators"],"explanation":"Object security defines who can access the type; record-level security filters specific rows."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas de seguridad recomienda Appian para las aplicaciones? (Elige 2)","options":["Compartir cuentas entre usuarios","Dejar el permiso por defecto en Editor para todos","Dar a los usuarios finales solo los permisos que necesitan","Hacer a todos los usuarios administradores del sistema","Asignar permisos a grupos, no a usuarios"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Seguridad por grupos y mínimo privilegio son las prácticas básicas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two security practices does Appian recommend for applications? (Choose 2)","options":["Share accounts between users","Set the default permission to Editor for everyone","Give end users only the permissions they need","Make every user a system administrator","Assign permissions to groups, not users"],"explanation":"Group-based security and least privilege are the basic practices."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador debe elegir entre una regla de expresión y una interfaz para calcular el importe con IVA que se mostrará en varias pantallas. ¿Qué elige y por qué?","options":["Un process model","Una constante con el resultado","Una regla de expresión reutilizable desde las interfaces","Una interfaz, porque el cálculo se muestra en pantalla"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La lógica reutilizable va en reglas de expresión; las interfaces la invocan para mostrar el resultado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer must choose between an expression rule and an interface to compute an amount with VAT shown on several screens. Which and why?","options":["A process model","A constant holding the result","A reusable expression rule called from the interfaces","An interface, because the result is shown on screen"],"explanation":"Reusable logic goes in expression rules; interfaces call them to display the result."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto se usa para enviar a usuarios notificaciones con un formato reutilizable o para generar documentos a partir de plantillas?","options":["Una carpeta de reglas","Un sitio","Un grupo con el texto de la notificación en su descripción","Plantillas de documento (p. ej. con smart services de generación) o reglas de texto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las plantillas y reglas permiten reutilizar contenidos de notificaciones y documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object is used to send users notifications with reusable formatting or generate documents from templates?","options":["A rule folder","A site","A group holding the notification text in its description","Document templates (e.g. with generation smart services) or text rules"],"explanation":"Templates and rules allow reusing notification and document content."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere que los cambios lleguen a producción de forma controlada y trazable. ¿Qué mecanismo de Appian usa?","options":["Exportar a Excel","Copiar y pegar el código de cada objeto entre entornos a mano","Despliegues (compare and deploy o paquetes) entre entornos","Editar en producción"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los despliegues entre entornos llevan los paquetes de forma controlada y con historial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants changes to reach production in a controlled, traceable way. Which Appian mechanism does it use?","options":["Exporting to Excel","Manually copying and pasting each object's code between environments","Deployments (compare and deploy or packages) between environments","Editing in production"],"explanation":"Cross-environment deployments move packages in a controlled way, with history."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario de negocio se queja de que no puede ver un informe en un sitio, aunque otros compañeros sí. ¿Qué es lo primero que revisa el desarrollador?","options":["Que el usuario tenga el navegador actualizado a la última versión disponible","Los logs de base de datos","El process model","La pertenencia del usuario a los grupos con permiso sobre el informe y el sitio"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los problemas de visibilidad suelen deberse a permisos o a pertenencia a grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A business user complains they can't see a report on a site, though colleagues can. What does the developer check first?","options":["That the user's browser is updated to the latest version","Database logs","The process model","The user's membership in groups with permission on the report and site"],"explanation":"Visibility issues usually come from permissions or group membership."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características distinguen un process model de una regla de expresión? (Elige 2)","options":["No hay diferencia","La regla de expresión puede asignar tareas a usuarios","El process model se ejecuta como una instancia con estado","El process model puede incluir tareas humanas y esperar en el tiempo","La regla de expresión se ejecuta durante días"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Los procesos tienen instancias con estado, tareas y temporizadores; las reglas evalúan y devuelven un valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two characteristics distinguish a process model from an expression rule? (Choose 2)","options":["There's no difference","An expression rule can assign tasks to users","A process model runs as a stateful instance","A process model can include human tasks and wait over time","An expression rule runs for days"],"explanation":"Processes have stateful instances, tasks and timers; rules evaluate and return a value."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador necesita un valor de configuración que cambia entre entornos (p. ej. la URL de un servicio en test y producción). ¿Qué práctica es adecuada?","options":["Una constante cuyo valor se ajusta por entorno (p. ej. con un fichero de personalización de importación)","Escribir la URL directamente en cada integración y cambiarla a mano en cada despliegue","Una interfaz","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los valores dependientes del entorno se gestionan con constantes ajustables en el despliegue.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer needs a configuration value that differs between environments (e.g. a service URL in test and production). Which practice fits?","options":["A constant whose value is set per environment (e.g. via an import customization file)","Hard-code the URL in every integration and change it by hand on each deployment","An interface","A group"],"explanation":"Environment-dependent values are managed with constants adjusted at deployment."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario puede ver los documentos de una carpeta pero recibe un error al intentar subir uno nuevo. ¿Qué es lo más probable?","options":["Que el process model está mal","Su rol en la carpeta solo permite ver, no crear contenido","Que falta una constante","Que el documento es demasiado pequeño para guardarse en una carpeta de Appian"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Subir documentos requiere un rol de la carpeta que permita crear contenido, no solo verlo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user can view a folder's documents but gets an error trying to upload a new one. What's most likely?","options":["The process model is wrong","Their folder role only allows viewing, not creating content","A constant is missing","The document is too small to store in an Appian folder"],"explanation":"Uploading documents requires a folder role that allows creating content, not just viewing."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador ve que una tarea asignada a un grupo no aparece a un usuario. Comprueba que el usuario es miembro del grupo. ¿Qué más puede revisar?","options":["Si otro miembro ya aceptó la tarea","El AppMarket","La constante del entorno","El nombre del process model, que debe coincidir con el del grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Cuando un miembro acepta una tarea de grupo, deja de estar disponible para los demás.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer sees a task assigned to a group isn't showing for a user. They confirm the user is a group member. What else can they check?","options":["Whether another member already accepted the task","The AppMarket","The environment constant","The process model name, which must match the group name"],"explanation":"When a member accepts a group task, it's no longer available to the others."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué se usan los grupos de tipo equipo y los tipos de grupo personalizados?","options":["Definir el aspecto visual de los sitios de cada departamento","Organizar usuarios y, con tipos personalizados, añadir atributos al grupo","Iniciar procesos","Guardar datos de negocio"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los grupos organizan usuarios; los tipos personalizados permiten atributos adicionales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are team groups and custom group types used for?","options":["Defining the look of each department's sites","Organizing users and, with custom types, adding attributes to the group","Starting processes","Storing business data"],"explanation":"Groups organize users; custom types allow extra attributes."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que solo los miembros de un grupo puedan ver una página concreta de un sitio. ¿Qué configura?","options":["La visibilidad de la página para ese grupo","Un process model","Una constante","Un mensaje en la página pidiendo que otros usuarios no la usen"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las páginas de un sitio pueden mostrarse solo a determinados grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants only members of a group to see a specific site page. What do they configure?","options":["The page's visibility for that group","A process model","A constant","A message on the page asking other users not to use it"],"explanation":"Site pages can be shown only to specific groups."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos objetos de diseño se usan para integrar Appian con sistemas externos? (Elige 2)","options":["Connected systems","Integrations y Web APIs","Grupos","Sitios","Carpetas de documentos"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Connected systems, integrations y Web APIs gestionan la comunicación con sistemas externos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two design objects are used to integrate Appian with external systems? (Choose 2)","options":["Connected systems","Integrations and Web APIs","Groups","Sites","Document folders"],"explanation":"Connected systems, integrations and Web APIs handle communication with external systems."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario de pruebas tiene permisos de administrador del sistema y nunca detecta problemas de permisos. En producción, los usuarios reales sí los tienen. ¿Qué cambio en las pruebas ayuda?","options":["Probar con usuarios básicos con los grupos reales","No probar","Eliminar la seguridad","Dar permisos de administrador a todos los usuarios de producción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las pruebas deben hacerse con perfiles equivalentes a los usuarios reales para detectar fallos de permisos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A test user has system administrator rights and never detects permission issues. In production, real users do. Which testing change helps?","options":["Test with basic users in the real groups","Don't test","Remove security","Give administrator rights to every production user"],"explanation":"Testing must use profiles equivalent to real users to catch permission failures."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué entorno es el más adecuado para que los usuarios de negocio validen una nueva funcionalidad antes de su lanzamiento (UAT)?","options":["Cualquiera","Producción, porque los datos son reales y la validación será más fiable","Test/UAT","Desarrollo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las pruebas de aceptación se hacen en un entorno de test, no en producción ni en desarrollo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which environment is best for business users to validate a new feature before launch (UAT)?","options":["Any","Production, since data is real and validation is more reliable","Test/UAT","Development"],"explanation":"Acceptance testing happens in a test environment, not in production or development."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto conviene usar para guardar el ID de un grupo que se usa en muchas reglas y procesos?","options":["Una constante","Escribir el ID del grupo directamente en cada regla y proceso","Un sitio","Un CDT"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las constantes centralizan referencias reutilizables y evitan valores codificados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object type should store the ID of a group used in many rules and processes?","options":["A constant","Write the group ID directly into each rule and process","A site","A CDT"],"explanation":"Constants centralize reusable references and avoid hard-coded values."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un process model se ha publicado con una seguridad que solo incluye al grupo de administradores de la aplicación. Los usuarios del grupo de usuarios no pueden iniciarlo desde una acción de un sitio. ¿Qué falta?","options":["Que los usuarios sean administradores del sistema para poder iniciar cualquier proceso","Un CDT","El permiso Initiator (o superior) para ese grupo","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Para iniciar un proceso, el grupo necesita al menos el rol Initiator sobre el process model.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process model is published with security that only includes the application administrators group. Members of the users group can't start it from a site action. What's missing?","options":["Users being system administrators so they can start any process","A CDT","Initiator permission (or higher) for that group","A constant"],"explanation":"To start a process, the group needs at least the Initiator role on the process model."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar un cambio en una regla sin afectar a los usuarios que ya están usando la aplicación en producción. ¿Dónde lo prueba?","options":["En desarrollo y después en test","No lo prueba","En producción, con un usuario de pruebas, para ver el efecto con datos reales","En cualquier entorno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los cambios se prueban en entornos no productivos antes de desplegarlos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to test a rule change without affecting users already working in production. Where do they test it?","options":["In development and then in test","They don't test it","In production, with a test user, to see the effect on real data","In any environment"],"explanation":"Changes are tested in non-production environments before deployment."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto de diseño define una experiencia de navegación con varias páginas para un perfil de usuario?","options":["Grupo","Interfaz, que admite varias páginas con menú de navegación propio","Sitio","Regla de expresión"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los sitios definen páginas y navegación para perfiles de usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design object type defines a multi-page navigation experience for a user profile?","options":["Group","Interface, which supports several pages with its own navigation menu","Site","Expression rule"],"explanation":"Sites define pages and navigation for user profiles."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un grupo de auditores debe ver los registros de una aplicación pero no realizar acciones sobre ellos. ¿Qué configuración es adecuada?","options":["Darles acceso a Appian Designer","Hacerlos administradores del sistema","Acceso de visualización al record type sin visibilidad de las acciones","Permiso de administrador sobre el record type para que puedan ver todo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Se concede visualización y se restringe la visibilidad de las acciones a otros grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An auditors group must view an application's records but not perform actions on them. Which configuration fits?","options":["Give them Appian Designer access","Make them system administrators","View access to the record type without action visibility","Administrator permission on the record type so they can see everything"],"explanation":"Grant viewing and restrict action visibility to other groups."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos afirmaciones sobre los entornos de Appian son correctas? (Elige 2)","options":["Los cambios se construyen en desarrollo y se despliegan hacia test y producción","Test y producción deben compartir base de datos","Producción es el lugar adecuado para desarrollar","No es necesario desplegar entre entornos","Los usuarios finales trabajan en producción"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"El flujo habitual es dev → test → prod y los usuarios trabajan en producción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two statements about Appian environments are correct? (Choose 2)","options":["Changes are built in development and deployed to test and production","Test and production should share a database","Production is the right place to develop","Deploying between environments isn't necessary","End users work in production"],"explanation":"The usual flow is dev → test → prod and users work in production."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador debe dar a un grupo de soporte acceso para ver el estado de las instancias de proceso en curso, sin poder modificarlas. ¿Qué rol de process model es el mínimo adecuado?","options":["Viewer","Administrator, que es el único rol que permite ver las instancias","Ninguno","Editor"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Viewer permite consultar el modelo y sus instancias sin gestionarlas ni editarlas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer must give a support group access to view running process instance status without modifying them. Which process model role is the minimum fit?","options":["Viewer","Administrator, the only role that allows viewing instances","None","Editor"],"explanation":"Viewer allows inspecting the model and its instances without managing or editing them."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"En una base de datos relacional, ¿qué es una clave primaria?","options":["Un índice opcional","Un campo (o conjunto) que identifica de forma única cada fila","El nombre de la tabla","Un campo que enlaza siempre con otra tabla y puede repetirse en varias filas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La clave primaria identifica de forma única cada fila de la tabla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In a relational database, what is a primary key?","options":["An optional index","A field (or set) that uniquely identifies each row","The table name","A field that always links to another table and can repeat across rows"],"explanation":"The primary key uniquely identifies each row in the table."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una solicitud puede tener muchos comentarios, y cada comentario pertenece a una sola solicitud. ¿Cómo se modela en la base de datos?","options":["Una sola tabla con 100 columnas de comentario","Tabla de comentarios con una clave foránea a la tabla de solicitudes","Un campo de texto en la tabla de solicitudes que concatena todos los comentarios","Una tabla por comentario"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Una relación uno a muchos se modela con una clave foránea en la tabla del lado \"muchos\".","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A request can have many comments, and each comment belongs to one request. How is this modeled in the database?","options":["A single table with 100 comment columns","A comments table with a foreign key to the requests table","A text field in the requests table concatenating every comment","One table per comment"],"explanation":"A one-to-many relationship is modeled with a foreign key in the \"many\" side's table."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un estudiante puede matricularse en muchos cursos y cada curso tiene muchos estudiantes. ¿Cómo se modela correctamente?","options":["Una sola tabla","Una columna en la tabla de estudiantes con la lista de cursos separados por comas","Duplicar los estudiantes en cada curso","Una tabla intermedia con las claves de estudiante y curso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las relaciones muchos a muchos se resuelven con una tabla intermedia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A student can enroll in many courses and each course has many students. How is this modeled correctly?","options":["A single table","A column in the students table with the course list comma-separated","Duplicate students in each course","A join table with the student and course keys"],"explanation":"Many-to-many relationships are resolved with a join table."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un custom data type (CDT) en Appian?","options":["Un proceso","Una estructura de datos con campos tipados que puede mapearse a una tabla","Un tipo de usuario","Una tabla de la base de datos creada automáticamente por cada interfaz"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El CDT define una estructura de datos; puede asociarse a una tabla mediante un data store.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a custom data type (CDT) in Appian?","options":["A process","A data structure with typed fields that can map to a table","A user type","A database table created automatically for each interface"],"explanation":"A CDT defines a data structure; it can be associated with a table via a data store."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué objeto de Appian conecta los CDT con una fuente de datos para poder leerlos y escribirlos?","options":["Data store","Grupo","Connected system, que es el objeto que mapea CDT a tablas","Sitio"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El data store define las entidades que mapean CDT a tablas de una fuente de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian object connects CDTs to a data source so they can be read and written?","options":["Data store","Group","Connected system, the object mapping CDTs to tables","Site"],"explanation":"The data store defines entities mapping CDTs to tables in a data source."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función se usa para consultar datos de una entidad de un data store desde una regla de expresión?","options":["a!save","a!queryProcessAnalytics, que consulta cualquier tabla de la base de datos","a!localVariables","a!queryEntity"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!queryEntity consulta entidades de data stores con filtros, selección y paginación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function queries a data store entity from an expression rule?","options":["a!save","a!queryProcessAnalytics, which queries any database table","a!localVariables","a!queryEntity"],"explanation":"a!queryEntity queries data store entities with filters, selection and paging."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función se usa para consultar datos de un record type, incluidas agregaciones?","options":["a!map","a!forEach","a!queryRecordType","a!queryEntity, que es la única que admite agregaciones"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!queryRecordType consulta record types y admite filtros, campos relacionados y agregaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function queries a record type's data, including aggregations?","options":["a!map","a!forEach","a!queryRecordType","a!queryEntity, the only one supporting aggregations"],"explanation":"a!queryRecordType queries record types and supports filters, related fields and aggregations."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe guardar en la base de datos los datos de una solicitud almacenados en un CDT mapeado a una entidad. ¿Qué smart service usa?","options":["Send E-Mail, que guarda una copia de los datos en la base de datos","Write to Data Store Entity","Start Process","Script Task"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Write to Data Store Entity inserta o actualiza datos de CDT en la entidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must save to the database the request data held in a CDT mapped to an entity. Which smart service does it use?","options":["Send E-Mail, which saves a copy of the data to the database","Write to Data Store Entity","Start Process","Script Task"],"explanation":"Write to Data Store Entity inserts or updates CDT data in the entity."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe crear o actualizar registros de un record type con sincronización de datos. ¿Qué smart service es el recomendado?","options":["Write Records","Delete from Data Store Entities","Write to Data Store Entity, que es el único que escribe en tablas de records","Send E-Mail"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Write Records escribe en la fuente del record type y mantiene sincronizados los datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must create or update records of a data-synced record type. Which smart service is recommended?","options":["Write Records","Delete from Data Store Entities","Write to Data Store Entity, the only one writing to record tables","Send E-Mail"],"explanation":"Write Records writes to the record type's source and keeps data synced."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe guardar datos al pulsar un botón, sin iniciar un proceso. ¿Qué función se usa en el saveInto del botón?","options":["a!queryEntity, que guarda los datos al ejecutarse","a!writeRecords o a!writeToDataStoreEntity","a!forEach","a!localVariables"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las funciones de escritura (smart service functions) pueden ejecutarse en un saveInto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must save data when a button is clicked, without starting a process. Which function goes in the button's saveInto?","options":["a!queryEntity, which saves data when it runs","a!writeRecords or a!writeToDataStoreEntity","a!forEach","a!localVariables"],"explanation":"Write functions (smart service functions) can run in a saveInto."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta con a!queryEntity devuelve demasiadas filas y la interfaz se vuelve lenta. ¿Qué parámetro ayuda a limitar los resultados?","options":["fetchTotalCount: true, que limita las filas devueltas","pagingInfo con un batchSize adecuado","Quitar los filtros","Aumentar el timeout"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La paginación limita las filas devueltas; los filtros también reducen el volumen.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An a!queryEntity query returns too many rows and the interface becomes slow. Which parameter helps limit results?","options":["fetchTotalCount: true, which limits returned rows","pagingInfo with an appropriate batchSize","Removing filters","Raising the timeout"],"explanation":"Paging limits returned rows; filters also reduce volume."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador solo necesita el nombre y el estado de las solicitudes, pero la consulta devuelve las 40 columnas. ¿Qué mejora aplica?","options":["Cachear la tabla completa","Recuperar todas las columnas y ocultar las que no se usan en la interfaz","Usar una constante","Seleccionar solo los campos necesarios en la consulta"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Seleccionar solo los campos necesarios reduce la carga de la consulta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer only needs the requests' name and status, but the query returns all 40 columns. Which improvement applies?","options":["Cache the whole table","Fetch every column and hide unused ones in the interface","Use a constant","Select only the needed fields in the query"],"explanation":"Selecting only needed fields reduces query load."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere contar cuántas solicitudes hay por estado directamente en la consulta. ¿Qué capacidad de a!queryRecordType usa?","options":["Una constante","Un grupo","Recuperar todos los registros y contarlos con a!forEach en la interfaz","Agregación (agrupar por estado y contar)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las agregaciones en la consulta delegan el cálculo a la fuente de datos y son más eficientes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to count requests by status directly in the query. Which a!queryRecordType capability do they use?","options":["A constant","A group","Fetch every record and count them with a!forEach in the interface","Aggregation (group by status and count)"],"explanation":"Aggregations in the query delegate computation to the data source and are more efficient."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función combina varios filtros de consulta con lógica AND u OR?","options":["a!save","a!queryLogicalExpression","a!queryFilter, que admite varios operadores lógicos en una sola llamada","a!match"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!queryLogicalExpression combina filtros con operadores AND u OR.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function combines several query filters with AND or OR logic?","options":["a!save","a!queryLogicalExpression","a!queryFilter, which supports several logical operators in one call","a!match"],"explanation":"a!queryLogicalExpression combines filters with AND or OR operators."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Se añade una columna nueva a la tabla que respalda un record type con sincronización de datos. ¿Qué pasos son necesarios para usarla en Appian?","options":["Reiniciar el servidor","Añadir el campo al record type y volver a sincronizar","Nada: el record type detecta y muestra la columna nueva al instante sin cambios","Crear un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El campo debe añadirse al record type y los datos sincronizarse para estar disponibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A new column is added to the table backing a data-synced record type. What steps are needed to use it in Appian?","options":["Restart the server","Add the field to the record type and resync","Nothing: the record type detects and shows the new column instantly with no changes","Create a group"],"explanation":"The field must be added to the record type and the data synced to be available."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Se añade un campo a un CDT mapeado a una entidad de un data store. ¿Qué paso es necesario para que la base de datos y Appian queden alineados?","options":["Cambiar el nombre del CDT","Reiniciar los procesos","Solo guardar el CDT, porque Appian crea la columna sin más pasos en cualquier caso","Actualizar la tabla y verificar y publicar el data store"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Tras cambiar un CDT, hay que alinear la tabla y verificar y publicar el data store.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A field is added to a CDT mapped to a data store entity. What step is needed to keep the database and Appian aligned?","options":["Rename the CDT","Restart processes","Just save the CDT, because Appian always creates the column with no further steps","Update the table and verify and publish the data store"],"explanation":"After changing a CDT, align the table and verify and publish the data store."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene el codeless data modeling al crear un record type?","options":["Crea interfaces automáticamente para cualquier caso","Sustituye a los procesos","Elimina la necesidad de una base de datos para guardar los datos del record type","Appian crea las tablas y relaciones desde el record type sin escribir SQL"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El modelado sin código crea la estructura de datos en la base de datos de Appian desde el record type.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What advantage does codeless data modeling have when creating a record type?","options":["It auto-creates interfaces for any case","It replaces processes","It removes the need for a database to store the record type's data","Appian creates tables and relationships from the record type without writing SQL"],"explanation":"Codeless modeling creates the data structure in Appian's database from the record type."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos funciones se usan para leer datos en Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["a!save","a!queryRecordType","a!queryEntity","a!startProcess","a!writeRecords"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Las funciones de consulta leen datos; las de escritura y a!save modifican.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two functions are used to read data in Appian? (Choose 2)","options":["a!save","a!queryRecordType","a!queryEntity","a!startProcess","a!writeRecords"],"explanation":"Query functions read data; write functions and a!save modify."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador guarda en una tabla la misma dirección del cliente en cada pedido, y al cambiar la dirección hay que actualizar cientos de filas. ¿Qué principio de modelado se incumple?","options":["El uso de constantes","La seguridad de registros","La normalización (evitar duplicar datos)","La paginación de consultas"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La normalización evita duplicar datos y las anomalías de actualización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer stores the same customer address on every order in a table, and changing the address means updating hundreds of rows. Which modeling principle is broken?","options":["Use of constants","Record security","Normalization (avoid duplicating data)","Query paging"],"explanation":"Normalization avoids duplicate data and update anomalies."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta con a!queryRecordType debe devolver las solicitudes creadas en los últimos 30 días. ¿Qué elemento se usa?","options":["Una constante","Una agregación de suma","Un filtro sobre el campo de fecha","Recuperar todas las solicitudes y filtrar en la interfaz con una regla"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Filtrar en la consulta reduce los datos que viajan a Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An a!queryRecordType query must return requests created in the last 30 days. Which element is used?","options":["A constant","A sum aggregation","A filter on the date field","Fetch every request and filter in the interface with a rule"],"explanation":"Filtering in the query reduces the data sent to Appian."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una clave foránea?","options":["Un campo que identifica de forma única cada fila de su propia tabla","Un campo que referencia la clave primaria de otra tabla","Un usuario","Un índice de texto completo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La clave foránea enlaza una fila con otra tabla mediante su clave primaria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a foreign key?","options":["A field uniquely identifying each row in its own table","A field referencing another table's primary key","A user","A full-text index"],"explanation":"A foreign key links a row to another table through its primary key."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type usa sincronización de datos y la tabla de origen se modifica directamente con SQL fuera de Appian. ¿Qué hay que tener en cuenta?","options":["No se puede modificar la tabla","Hay que resincronizar para que Appian refleje los cambios","Appian siempre detecta los cambios externos al instante sin ninguna acción","Se borra el record type"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios hechos fuera de Appian no se reflejan en los datos sincronizados hasta resincronizar (o según la sincronización programada).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type uses data sync and its source table is modified directly with SQL outside Appian. What must be considered?","options":["The table can't be modified","A resync is needed for Appian to reflect the changes","Appian always detects external changes instantly with no action","The record type is deleted"],"explanation":"Changes made outside Appian aren't reflected in synced data until a resync (or scheduled sync)."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene escribir datos con Write Records en vez de modificar la tabla directamente fuera de Appian para un record type sincronizado?","options":["No requiere permisos","Mantiene los datos sincronizados del record type actualizados","Es más rápido porque no escribe en la base de datos","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Escribir a través de Appian actualiza la fuente y los datos sincronizados a la vez.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What advantage does writing data with Write Records have over modifying the table directly outside Appian for a synced record type?","options":["It needs no permissions","It keeps the record type's synced data up to date","It's faster because it doesn't write to the database","None"],"explanation":"Writing through Appian updates the source and the synced data together."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla devuelve los pedidos de un cliente con a!queryRecordType. ¿Cómo debe recibir el identificador del cliente para ser reutilizable?","options":["Con el identificador escrito directamente en el filtro de la regla","Con una variable global","Como rule input usado en el filtro","Con una constante distinta por cliente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los rule inputs parametrizan la consulta y la hacen reutilizable.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule returns a customer's orders with a!queryRecordType. How should it receive the customer ID to be reusable?","options":["With the ID written directly into the rule's filter","With a global variable","As a rule input used in the filter","With a different constant per customer"],"explanation":"Rule inputs parameterize the query and make it reusable."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de relación de record type se usa cuando un cliente tiene muchos pedidos?","options":["Ninguna","Uno a uno","Muchos a uno, desde el cliente hacia los pedidos","Uno a muchos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Desde Cliente hacia Pedido es uno a muchos; desde Pedido hacia Cliente, muchos a uno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record type relationship is used when a customer has many orders?","options":["None","One-to-one","Many-to-one, from customer to orders","One-to-many"],"explanation":"From Customer to Order it's one-to-many; from Order to Customer, many-to-one."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta debe devolver los pedidos junto con el nombre de su cliente sin hacer una segunda consulta. ¿Qué permite hacerlo con records?","options":["Hacer una consulta por cada pedido para obtener el nombre del cliente","Duplicar el nombre del cliente en cada pedido","Usar una constante","Consultar campos relacionados mediante la relación entre record types"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las relaciones permiten recuperar campos relacionados en una sola consulta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A query must return orders along with their customer's name without a second query. What enables this with records?","options":["Running one query per order to get the customer name","Duplicating the customer name on each order","Using a constant","Querying related fields through the record type relationship"],"explanation":"Relationships allow retrieving related fields in a single query."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son buenas prácticas al consultar datos? (Elige 2)","options":["Ignorar la paginación","Filtrar en la consulta","Consultar dentro de un bucle por cada fila","Seleccionar solo los campos necesarios","Traer todos los datos y filtrar en la interfaz"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Filtrar y seleccionar en la fuente reduce volumen y mejora el rendimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are good practices when querying data? (Choose 2)","options":["Ignore paging","Filter in the query","Query inside a loop for each row","Select only the needed fields","Fetch all data and filter in the interface"],"explanation":"Filtering and selecting at the source reduces volume and improves performance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador ejecuta una consulta dentro de a!forEach para cada una de 500 filas de una tabla. La interfaz tarda mucho. ¿Qué mejora es adecuada?","options":["Cachear cada consulta individual en una variable local","Añadir más memoria al servidor","Una sola consulta con filtro \"in\" sobre todos los identificadores","Usar una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Consultar en bucle multiplica las llamadas; una consulta con varios valores es mucho más eficiente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer runs a query inside a!forEach for each of 500 table rows. The interface is very slow. Which improvement fits?","options":["Cache each individual query in a local variable","Add more server memory","A single query with an \"in\" filter on all IDs","Use a constant"],"explanation":"Querying in a loop multiplies calls; one query with many values is far more efficient."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de dato conviene usar para guardar importes monetarios en una tabla?","options":["Booleano","Decimal con precisión fija","Texto, para conservar el formato con símbolo de moneda","Entero sin decimales"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los importes se guardan como decimales numéricos; el formato se aplica al mostrar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which data type should store monetary amounts in a table?","options":["Boolean","Fixed-precision decimal","Text, to keep the currency-symbol formatting","Integer with no decimals"],"explanation":"Amounts are stored as numeric decimals; formatting is applied when displaying."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador necesita eliminar registros de una entidad de un data store desde un proceso. ¿Qué smart service usa?","options":["Write to Data Store Entity con los campos vacíos","Send E-Mail","Start Process","Delete from Data Store Entities"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Delete from Data Store Entities elimina filas de entidades indicadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer needs to delete rows from a data store entity in a process. Which smart service do they use?","options":["Write to Data Store Entity with empty fields","Send E-Mail","Start Process","Delete from Data Store Entities"],"explanation":"Delete from Data Store Entities removes rows from the given entities."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el parámetro fetchTotalCount en una consulta paginada?","options":["El número máximo de filas que devuelve la consulta en cada página","El orden de los resultados","El filtro","Si se devuelve el número total de resultados además de la página"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"fetchTotalCount pide el total de resultados para, por ejemplo, mostrar la paginación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the fetchTotalCount parameter indicate in a paged query?","options":["The maximum rows the query returns per page","Result order","The filter","Whether the total result count is returned besides the page"],"explanation":"fetchTotalCount requests the total result count, e.g. to show paging."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una tabla de solicitudes necesita registrar quién la creó y cuándo. ¿Qué campos conviene añadir?","options":["Solo un campo de texto libre con un comentario sobre la creación","Un campo booleano","Usuario creador y fecha y hora de creación","Ninguno; Appian lo guarda en la interfaz"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los campos de auditoría (creador, fecha) son una práctica habitual de modelado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A requests table needs to record who created each request and when. Which fields should be added?","options":["Just a free-text field with a comment about creation","A boolean field","Creator user and creation date-time","None; Appian stores it in the interface"],"explanation":"Audit fields (creator, date) are a common modeling practice."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador elige entre un record type con sincronización de datos y consultar directamente la fuente sin sincronizar para una tabla de 2.000 filas que se consulta mucho. ¿Qué ventaja ofrece la sincronización?","options":["Que no requiere base de datos","Consultas rápidas y capacidades como relaciones y campos calculados","Ninguna","Que los datos nunca necesitan actualizarse porque se copian una vez"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La sincronización almacena los datos en Appian para consultas rápidas y funcionalidades avanzadas de records.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer chooses between a data-synced record type and querying the source directly without sync for a frequently queried 2,000-row table. What does sync offer?","options":["No database needed","Fast queries and features like relationships and custom fields","Nothing","Data never needing updates because it's copied once"],"explanation":"Sync stores data in Appian for fast queries and advanced record features."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos smart services escriben datos en Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Send E-Mail","Write to Data Store Entity","Query Entity","Write Records","User Input Task"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Write Records y Write to Data Store Entity escriben datos; Query Entity lee.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two smart services write data in Appian? (Choose 2)","options":["Send E-Mail","Write to Data Store Entity","Query Entity","Write Records","User Input Task"],"explanation":"Write Records and Write to Data Store Entity write data; Query Entity reads."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere ordenar los resultados de una consulta por fecha de creación descendente. ¿Qué configura?","options":["El sort de la paginación (campo y orden descendente)","Un filtro por fecha de creación con el operador \"mayor que\"","Una constante","Una agregación"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El orden se define en la configuración de ordenación de la paginación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to sort a query's results by creation date descending. What do they configure?","options":["The paging sort (field and descending order)","A filter on creation date with the \"greater than\" operator","A constant","An aggregation"],"explanation":"Order is defined in the paging sort configuration."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta con filtros devuelve resultados vacíos cuando el rule input del filtro es nulo, aunque se espera que entonces devuelva todo. ¿Qué parámetro del filtro ayuda?","options":["fetchTotalCount: true para forzar que se devuelvan todos los resultados","Quitar la paginación","ignoreFiltersWithEmptyValues (o aplicar el filtro solo si hay valor)","Usar a!save"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Ignorar filtros con valor vacío permite consultas con filtros opcionales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A filtered query returns empty results when the filter's rule input is null, though it should then return everything. Which filter parameter helps?","options":["fetchTotalCount: true to force returning all results","Remove paging","ignoreFiltersWithEmptyValues (or apply the filter only when there's a value)","Use a!save"],"explanation":"Ignoring filters with empty values enables queries with optional filters."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa una entidad dentro de un data store?","options":["La asociación entre un CDT y una tabla o vista","Un usuario con acceso a la base de datos","Un tipo de interfaz","Un proceso que escribe en la base de datos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Cada entidad del data store vincula un CDT a una tabla o vista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an entity in a data store represent?","options":["The association between a CDT and a table or view","A user with database access","An interface type","A process writing to the database"],"explanation":"Each data store entity links a CDT to a table or view."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo necesita mostrar datos combinados de tres tablas con una lógica de cálculo compleja que se reutiliza en varios informes. ¿Qué opción de base de datos puede simplificar la consulta desde Appian?","options":["Tres consultas separadas en cada interfaz combinadas con a!forEach","Una vista de base de datos que se consulta como fuente","Copiar los datos a un CDT","Una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las vistas encapsulan combinaciones y cálculos en la base de datos y pueden servir de fuente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team needs to display data combined from three tables with complex calculation logic reused across several reports. Which database option can simplify querying from Appian?","options":["Three separate queries in each interface combined with a!forEach","A database view queried as a source","Copy the data into a CDT","A constant"],"explanation":"Views encapsulate joins and calculations in the database and can act as a source."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos pasos son necesarios cuando se cambia el tipo de un campo en la tabla que respalda un record type sincronizado? (Elige 2)","options":["Volver a sincronizar los datos","Reiniciar todos los procesos","Actualizar el tipo del campo en el record type","Borrar la aplicación","Cambiar el nombre del record type"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Los cambios de esquema deben reflejarse en el record type y los datos resincronizarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two steps are needed when changing a field's type in the table backing a synced record type? (Choose 2)","options":["Resync the data","Restart every process","Update the field's type in the record type","Delete the application","Rename the record type"],"explanation":"Schema changes must be reflected in the record type and data resynced."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que el identificador de cada nueva solicitud lo genere la base de datos automáticamente. ¿Cómo se configura la clave primaria?","options":["Sin clave primaria","Como clave autoincremental o generada por la base de datos","Escribiendo el identificador a mano en el formulario de alta","Con una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las claves generadas por la base de datos evitan conflictos y duplicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants the database to generate each new request's ID automatically. How is the primary key configured?","options":["No primary key","As auto-increment or database-generated","Typed by hand in the creation form","With a constant"],"explanation":"Database-generated keys avoid conflicts and duplicates."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Tras escribir una solicitud nueva con Write to Data Store Entity, el proceso necesita su identificador generado. ¿Dónde lo obtiene?","options":["Haciendo una consulta por fecha para buscar la última solicitud creada","No se puede obtener","En la salida del smart service, que devuelve los datos guardados","Con una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El smart service devuelve los datos almacenados, incluido el identificador generado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After writing a new request with Write to Data Store Entity, the process needs its generated ID. Where does it get it?","options":["By querying by date to find the most recently created request","It can't be obtained","From the smart service output, which returns the stored data","With a constant"],"explanation":"The smart service returns the stored data, including the generated ID."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué limitación tiene usar campos de texto muy largos para guardar listas de valores (por ejemplo, \"rojo;azul;verde\") en una sola columna?","options":["Ninguna, porque es la forma recomendada de guardar listas en una base de datos relacional","Ocupa menos espacio","Dificulta filtrar, validar y relacionar esos valores","Mejora el rendimiento"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Guardar listas en una columna rompe la normalización y complica consultas y validaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the drawback of using very long text fields to store lists of values (e.g. \"red;blue;green\") in a single column?","options":["None, since it's the recommended way to store lists in a relational database","It takes less space","It makes filtering, validating and relating those values harder","It improves performance"],"explanation":"Storing lists in a column breaks normalization and complicates queries and validation."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type necesita mostrar el total de pedidos de cada cliente como un campo. ¿Qué capacidad de records lo permite sin guardar el valor en la tabla?","options":["Una constante","Añadir una columna \"total\" que se actualice a mano cada vez que cambien los pedidos","Un campo calculado (custom record field) de agregación","Un grupo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los campos de registro personalizados calculan valores (p. ej. agregaciones) a partir de datos relacionados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type needs to show each customer's total orders as a field. Which records capability allows this without storing the value in the table?","options":["A constant","Add a \"total\" column updated by hand whenever orders change","A calculated (custom record field) aggregation","A group"],"explanation":"Custom record fields compute values (e.g. aggregations) from related data."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de dato de Appian conviene usar para una fecha de vencimiento sin hora?","options":["Text, con la fecha en formato dd/mm/aaaa","Integer","Date","Boolean"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Usar el tipo Date permite comparaciones y cálculos correctos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian data type should be used for a due date without time?","options":["Text, with the date as dd/mm/yyyy","Integer","Date","Boolean"],"explanation":"Using the Date type allows correct comparisons and calculations."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario guarda los datos con a!writeRecords en el saveInto de un botón. ¿Qué conviene hacer tras escribir para que la interfaz muestre los datos actualizados?","options":["Refrescar las variables que consultan esos datos","Nada","Reiniciar el proceso","Recargar la página completa del navegador del usuario"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las variables locales con consulta deben refrescarse tras escribir (p. ej. con refreshOnVarChange ligado a un contador).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form saves data with a!writeRecords in a button's saveInto. What should be done after writing so the interface shows updated data?","options":["Refresh the variables querying that data","Nothing","Restart the process","Reload the user's whole browser page"],"explanation":"Local variables holding queries should be refreshed after writing (e.g. refreshOnVarChange tied to a counter)."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos definen un CDT? (Elige 2)","options":["Sus campos con tipo","Su color","Su nombre y espacio de nombres","Los usuarios que lo pueden ver en producción","Los procesos que lo usan"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Un CDT se define por su nombre/namespace y sus campos tipados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements define a CDT? (Choose 2)","options":["Its typed fields","Its color","Its name and namespace","The users who can see it in production","The processes using it"],"explanation":"A CDT is defined by its name/namespace and its typed fields."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere relacionar el record type Pedido con Cliente para mostrar datos del cliente en la vista del pedido. ¿Qué tipo de relación crea desde Pedido?","options":["Muchos a uno","Uno a muchos, desde el pedido hacia los clientes","Muchos a muchos sin tabla intermedia","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Muchos pedidos apuntan a un cliente: desde Pedido es muchos a uno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to relate the Order record type to Customer to show customer data in the order view. Which relationship do they create from Order?","options":["Many-to-one","One-to-many, from order to customers","Many-to-many without a join table","None"],"explanation":"Many orders point to one customer: from Order it's many-to-one."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Al consultar un record type con a!queryRecordType, ¿cómo se hace referencia a los campos de forma segura frente a cambios de nombre?","options":["Con el índice de la columna","Escribiendo el nombre de la columna de la tabla como texto entre comillas","Con constantes","Con las referencias de campo del record type (recordType!...)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las referencias de campo del record type se actualizan con el objeto y evitan errores de texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When querying a record type with a!queryRecordType, how are fields referenced safely against renames?","options":["With the column index","Typing the table column name as quoted text","With constants","With the record type field references (recordType!...)"],"explanation":"Record type field references stay in sync with the object and avoid text errors."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador necesita actualizar el estado de una solicitud existente con Write Records. ¿Qué debe incluir el registro que envía?","options":["Solo el nuevo estado; Appian deducirá qué registro actualizar","Una constante","La clave primaria de la solicitud y el nuevo estado","Todos los registros de la tabla"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Con clave primaria, la escritura actualiza el registro existente; sin ella, crea uno nuevo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer needs to update an existing request's status with Write Records. What must the record sent include?","options":["Only the new status; Appian will infer which record to update","A constant","The request's primary key and the new status","Every record in the table"],"explanation":"With a primary key the write updates the existing record; without it, it creates a new one."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consecuencia tiene escribir un registro sin clave primaria con Write Records?","options":["Falla siempre","Se borran los registros","Se actualiza el último registro modificado de la tabla","Se crea un registro nuevo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Sin identificador, la escritura se trata como alta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens when writing a record without a primary key using Write Records?","options":["It always fails","Records are deleted","The table's most recently modified record is updated","A new record is created"],"explanation":"Without an identifier, the write is treated as an insert."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo quiere guardar el historial de cambios de estado de cada solicitud para auditoría. ¿Qué modelo de datos es adecuado?","options":["Sobrescribir el campo de estado en cada cambio y guardar el anterior en un comentario","Una constante","Un campo de texto con todo el historial concatenado","Una tabla de historial relacionada con la solicitud (una fila por cambio)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Una tabla de historial uno a muchos permite consultar y auditar los cambios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team wants to keep each request's status change history for audit. Which data model fits?","options":["Overwrite the status field on each change and keep the previous one in a comment","A constant","A text field with the whole history concatenated","A history table related to the request (one row per change)"],"explanation":"A one-to-many history table allows querying and auditing changes."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos afirmaciones sobre la sincronización de datos de un record type son correctas? (Elige 2)","options":["Elimina la necesidad de una fuente de datos","Las escrituras con Write Records se reflejan en los datos sincronizados","Permite consultas rápidas sobre los datos sincronizados","Detecta al instante cualquier cambio hecho fuera de Appian","Solo funciona con hojas de cálculo"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"La sincronización acelera las consultas y se mantiene al escribir vía Appian; los cambios externos requieren resincronizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two statements about record type data sync are correct? (Choose 2)","options":["It removes the need for a data source","Writes via Write Records are reflected in synced data","It enables fast queries over synced data","It instantly detects any change made outside Appian","It only works with spreadsheets"],"explanation":"Sync speeds up queries and is maintained when writing via Appian; external changes need a resync."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe devolver solo el número de solicitudes abiertas, no las filas. ¿Qué enfoque es más eficiente?","options":["Una consulta con agregación de recuento o que pida solo el total","Un grupo","Recuperar todas las solicitudes abiertas y contar la longitud de la lista","Una constante"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Pedir solo el recuento evita transferir filas innecesarias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must return only the number of open requests, not the rows. Which approach is most efficient?","options":["A query with a count aggregation or asking only for the total","A group","Fetch every open request and count the list length","A constant"],"explanation":"Asking only for the count avoids transferring unnecessary rows."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador modifica un CDT anidado (un CDT dentro de otro) y algunos procesos en curso que lo usan dan errores. ¿Qué tener en cuenta al cambiar el modelo de datos?","options":["Que hay que borrar los procesos","El impacto en objetos e instancias que ya usan el tipo","Nada: los cambios de CDT no afectan a los procesos en ejecución en ningún caso","Que hay que cambiar el nombre del CDT siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios de modelo deben planificarse considerando objetos dependientes e instancias activas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer modifies a nested CDT (a CDT within another) and some running processes using it error out. What must be considered when changing the data model?","options":["Processes must be deleted","The impact on objects and instances already using the type","Nothing: CDT changes never affect running processes","The CDT must always be renamed"],"explanation":"Data model changes must be planned considering dependent objects and active instances."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un error de restricción de clave foránea al guardar un pedido?","options":["El cliente referenciado no existe en la tabla relacionada","Que el usuario no tiene permisos en Appian","Que el pedido es demasiado largo","Que la tabla de pedidos está llena y no admite más filas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La clave foránea exige que exista la fila referenciada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a foreign key constraint error when saving an order indicate?","options":["The referenced customer doesn't exist in the related table","The user lacks Appian permissions","The order is too long","The orders table is full and accepts no more rows"],"explanation":"A foreign key requires the referenced row to exist."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una consulta devuelva solo los clientes activos de España. ¿Cómo combina los filtros?","options":["Una agregación","Ordenación por país","Dos filtros con lógica OR, que devuelve los que cumplen ambas condiciones","Dos filtros con lógica AND"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"AND exige que se cumplan ambas condiciones; OR basta con una.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a query to return only active customers in Spain. How do they combine the filters?","options":["An aggregation","Sort by country","Two filters with OR logic, which returns those meeting both conditions","Two filters with AND logic"],"explanation":"AND requires both conditions; OR needs only one."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de dato de Appian se usa para guardar un identificador de usuario o grupo?","options":["User / Group (o User or Group)","Text con el nombre completo de la persona para que sea legible","Integer con la posición en la lista","Boolean"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los tipos User y Group referencian usuarios y grupos de forma fiable.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian data type is used to store a user or group reference?","options":["User / Group (or User or Group)","Text with the person's full name so it's readable","Integer with the list position","Boolean"],"explanation":"User and Group types reference users and groups reliably."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta de a!queryRecordType devuelve como máximo un lote de resultados. Un desarrollador necesita procesar 50.000 registros en un proceso nocturno. ¿Qué enfoque es adecuado?","options":["Procesarlos por lotes con paginación","No procesarlos","Aumentar el batchSize a 50.000 en una sola consulta desde una interfaz","Mostrar los 50.000 en una cuadrícula"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los volúmenes grandes se procesan por lotes paginados para respetar límites y memoria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An a!queryRecordType query returns at most a batch of results. A developer needs to process 50,000 records in a nightly process. Which approach fits?","options":["Process them in paged batches","Don't process them","Raise batchSize to 50,000 in a single query from an interface","Show all 50,000 in a grid"],"explanation":"Large volumes are processed in paged batches to respect limits and memory."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué conviene que la base de datos aplique restricciones como NOT NULL o claves foráneas además de las validaciones de la interfaz?","options":["Aceleran las interfaces","Hacen innecesarias las validaciones de interfaz para los usuarios","No aportan nada","Protegen la integridad aunque los datos lleguen por otra vía"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las restricciones de base de datos garantizan integridad con independencia del canal de escritura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why should the database enforce constraints like NOT NULL or foreign keys in addition to interface validations?","options":["They speed up interfaces","They make interface validations unnecessary for users","They add nothing","They protect integrity even when data arrives another way"],"explanation":"Database constraints guarantee integrity regardless of the write channel."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere mostrar en una cuadrícula los pedidos de un cliente con paginación en la propia cuadrícula. ¿Qué fuente de datos es más directa con records?","options":["Una constante","Una consulta sin paginación guardada en una variable local","Un CDT vacío","El record type como fuente de la cuadrícula con un filtro por cliente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las cuadrículas de solo lectura pueden usar un record type como fuente y paginan automáticamente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to show a customer's orders in a grid with in-grid paging. Which data source is most direct with records?","options":["A constant","An unpaged query stored in a local variable","An empty CDT","The record type as the grid source with a customer filter"],"explanation":"Read-only grids can use a record type as source and page automatically."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene modificar directamente la base de datos de producción sin pasar por el proceso de despliegue? (Elige 2)","options":["Perder trazabilidad de los cambios","Facilitar las auditorías","Reducir los errores","Mejorar el rendimiento","Desalinear el modelo con los objetos de Appian"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Los cambios fuera del proceso controlado generan inconsistencias y pérdida de trazabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from modifying the production database directly outside the deployment process? (Choose 2)","options":["Losing change traceability","Easing audits","Reducing errors","Improving performance","Misaligning the model with Appian objects"],"explanation":"Changes outside the controlled process create inconsistencies and lose traceability."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador debe guardar a la vez una solicitud y sus líneas de detalle relacionadas. ¿Qué ventaja tiene usar Write Records con los registros relacionados?","options":["Puede escribir el registro y sus relacionados en una misma operación","Que no necesita definir relaciones entre los record types","Ninguna","Que no requiere claves primarias"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Write Records puede escribir registros relacionados juntos, gestionando las claves.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer must save a request and its related detail lines together. What advantage does Write Records with related records offer?","options":["It can write the record and its related records in one operation","It doesn't need relationships defined between record types","None","It needs no primary keys"],"explanation":"Write Records can write related records together, managing keys."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un campo de tipo Boolean en una tabla?","options":["Un valor verdadero o falso","Un texto con formato","Una lista","Una fecha"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Boolean representa valores verdadero/falso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Boolean field in a table represent?","options":["A true or false value","Formatted text","A list","A date"],"explanation":"Boolean represents true/false values."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere evitar que dos usuarios creen clientes con el mismo correo. ¿Qué medida es más fiable?","options":["Una constante","Una restricción de unicidad en la base de datos, además de validar en la interfaz","Pedir a los usuarios que lo comprueben","Solo una validación en la interfaz que consulta si el correo ya existe"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La restricción de unicidad protege frente a condiciones de carrera que una validación de interfaz no evita.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to stop two users creating customers with the same email. Which measure is most reliable?","options":["A constant","A unique constraint in the database, plus interface validation","Asking users to check","Only an interface validation querying whether the email exists"],"explanation":"A unique constraint protects against race conditions an interface validation can't prevent."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a que una aplicación lea datos de forma eficiente desde un record type? (Elige 2)","options":["Desactivar la sincronización sin motivo","Filtros y selección de campos en la consulta","Consultas dentro de bucles","Traer todos los campos siempre","Paginación adecuada"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Filtrar, seleccionar y paginar son la base de una lectura eficiente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements help an application read data efficiently from a record type? (Choose 2)","options":["Disabling sync for no reason","Filters and field selection in the query","Queries inside loops","Always fetching every field","Appropriate paging"],"explanation":"Filtering, selecting and paging are the basis of efficient reads."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario debe iniciar un proceso de solicitud de vacaciones desde un sitio rellenando un formulario. ¿Qué forma de inicio es la habitual?","options":["Un temporizador que inicia el proceso cada día para todos los usuarios","Una acción (record action o acción de sitio) que inicia el proceso con un formulario de inicio","Una Web API","Un correo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las acciones inician procesos con formulario desde sitios o registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user must start a vacation request process from a site by filling in a form. Which start method is typical?","options":["A timer starting the process daily for every user","An action (record action or site action) starting the process with a start form","A Web API","An email"],"explanation":"Actions start processes with a form from sites or records."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso de recordatorio debe ejecutarse automáticamente cada lunes a las 8:00. ¿Cómo se inicia?","options":["Con un sub-proceso","Con una acción de sitio que un usuario pulsa cada lunes","Con una Web API","Con un evento de inicio con temporizador (programado)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los eventos de inicio programados lanzan procesos en fechas y horas definidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A reminder process must run automatically every Monday at 8:00. How is it started?","options":["With a sub-process","With a site action a user clicks every Monday","With a Web API","With a timer (scheduled) start event"],"explanation":"Scheduled start events launch processes at defined dates and times."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un sistema externo debe iniciar un proceso de Appian cuando registra un pedido. ¿Qué mecanismo es adecuado?","options":["Una tarea de usuario asignada al sistema externo","Un grupo","Un temporizador cada minuto que pregunte al sistema","Una Web API que llama a a!startProcess"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Una Web API puede iniciar procesos al recibir una llamada de un sistema externo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An external system must start an Appian process when it records an order. Which mechanism fits?","options":["A user task assigned to the external system","A group","A timer every minute polling the system","A Web API calling a!startProcess"],"explanation":"A Web API can start processes when called by an external system."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un botón de una interfaz debe iniciar un proceso en segundo plano sin que el usuario abandone la pantalla. ¿Qué función se usa en el saveInto?","options":["a!forEach","a!queryEntity, que inicia el proceso asociado a la entidad","a!localVariables","a!startProcess"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!startProcess inicia un proceso desde un saveInto o una Web API.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface button must start a process in the background without the user leaving the screen. Which function goes in the saveInto?","options":["a!forEach","a!queryEntity, which starts the entity's associated process","a!localVariables","a!startProcess"],"explanation":"a!startProcess starts a process from a saveInto or Web API."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Dentro de un proceso, se necesita lanzar otro proceso independiente que no debe esperar a que termine. ¿Qué opción encaja?","options":["Un gateway XOR","Start Process smart service (o sub-proceso asíncrono)","Un sub-proceso síncrono, que continúa sin esperar a que termine el hijo","Un temporizador"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El inicio asíncrono continúa el flujo padre sin esperar; el sub-proceso síncrono espera.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Within a process, another independent process must be launched without waiting for it to finish. Which option fits?","options":["An XOR gateway","Start Process smart service (or asynchronous sub-process)","A synchronous sub-process, which continues without waiting for the child","A timer"],"explanation":"Asynchronous start continues the parent flow without waiting; a synchronous sub-process waits."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un sub-proceso síncrono y uno asíncrono?","options":["El síncrono espera a que el hijo termine y puede devolver datos; el asíncrono no espera","El asíncrono espera a que termine el hijo y el síncrono no","Ninguna","El síncrono no admite parámetros"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El sub-proceso síncrono bloquea el padre hasta terminar y permite mapear salidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a synchronous and an asynchronous sub-process?","options":["Synchronous waits for the child to finish and can return data; asynchronous doesn't wait","Asynchronous waits for the child and synchronous doesn't","None","Synchronous accepts no parameters"],"explanation":"A synchronous sub-process blocks the parent until done and allows mapping outputs."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué pasos son necesarios para que los cambios en un process model se usen en las nuevas instancias?","options":["Solo guardar el modelo; las instancias nuevas usan siempre la última versión guardada","Borrar las instancias anteriores","Guardar y publicar una nueva versión del modelo","Reiniciar el servidor"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las nuevas instancias usan la versión publicada; guardar sin publicar no las afecta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What steps are needed for changes to a process model to apply to new instances?","options":["Just save the model; new instances always use the latest saved version","Delete previous instances","Save and publish a new model version","Restart the server"],"explanation":"New instances use the published version; saving without publishing doesn't affect them."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Tras publicar una nueva versión de un process model, ¿qué ocurre con las instancias que ya estaban en curso?","options":["Siguen con la versión con la que empezaron","Se actualizan automáticamente a la nueva versión al publicar","Se reinician","Se cancelan"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las instancias en curso continúan con su versión; solo las nuevas usan la publicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After publishing a new process model version, what happens to instances already running?","options":["They continue on the version they started with","They update automatically to the new version on publish","They restart","They're cancelled"],"explanation":"Running instances continue on their version; only new ones use the published one."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar un process model paso a paso y ver los valores de las variables en cada nodo. ¿Qué herramienta usa?","options":["Publicar el modelo en producción y revisar las quejas de los usuarios","Leer el XML del modelo","Usar el AppMarket","Iniciar el proceso para depuración y supervisarlo en el monitor de procesos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El modo de depuración y el monitor muestran el recorrido, los nodos y los valores de las variables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to test a process model step by step and see variable values at each node. Which tool do they use?","options":["Publish the model to production and review user complaints","Read the model's XML","Use the AppMarket","Start the process for debugging and inspect it in the process monitor"],"explanation":"Debug mode and the monitor show the path, nodes and variable values."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso se ha detenido en un nodo con error. ¿Dónde lo identifica el desarrollador?","options":["En el AppMarket","En el monitor del proceso, que marca el nodo con error y su mensaje","En los grupos","En el sitio de usuarios, que muestra un aviso de error a todos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El monitor de procesos muestra los nodos con errores y sus detalles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process has stopped at a node with an error. Where does the developer identify it?","options":["In the AppMarket","In the process monitor, which flags the failing node and its message","In groups","On the users' site, which shows an error notice to everyone"],"explanation":"The process monitor shows failing nodes and their details."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo se usa para ejecutar lógica automática (p. ej. calcular un valor y guardarlo en una variable) sin interacción humana?","options":["User input task, que también puede ejecutarse sin usuario","Evento de fin","Gateway AND","Script task"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El script task evalúa expresiones y guarda resultados sin asignarse a nadie.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which node runs automatic logic (e.g. compute a value and store it in a variable) with no human interaction?","options":["User input task, which can also run without a user","End event","AND gateway","Script task"],"explanation":"A script task evaluates expressions and saves results without being assigned to anyone."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo se usa para asignar a un usuario un formulario que debe completar dentro del proceso?","options":["Script task con una interfaz asociada","Gateway","User input task","Start Process"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La User input task asigna una interfaz a un usuario o grupo y espera su respuesta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which node assigns a user a form they must complete within the process?","options":["Script task with an associated interface","Gateway","User input task","Start Process"],"explanation":"The User input task assigns an interface to a user or group and waits for their response."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe seguir un camino distinto según si el importe supera 1.000 €. ¿Qué nodo se usa?","options":["Un gateway XOR (exclusivo) con condiciones","Un gateway AND, que elige el camino según la condición","Un script task","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El XOR elige exactamente un camino según las condiciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must follow a different path depending on whether the amount exceeds €1,000. Which node is used?","options":["An XOR (exclusive) gateway with conditions","An AND gateway, which picks the path by condition","A script task","An end event"],"explanation":"The XOR picks exactly one path based on conditions."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Tras aprobar un pedido, el proceso debe notificar a almacén y a contabilidad en paralelo. ¿Qué nodo divide el flujo en ambos caminos a la vez?","options":["Un gateway AND (paralelo)","Un script task","Un gateway XOR, que sigue todos los caminos que cumplen la condición","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El gateway AND activa todos los caminos salientes en paralelo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After approving an order, the process must notify warehouse and accounting in parallel. Which node splits the flow into both paths at once?","options":["An AND (parallel) gateway","A script task","An XOR gateway, which follows every path meeting the condition","An end event"],"explanation":"The AND gateway activates all outgoing paths in parallel."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe seguir uno o varios caminos según qué condiciones se cumplan (p. ej. notificar a legal si hay riesgo legal y a finanzas si hay riesgo financiero). ¿Qué gateway encaja?","options":["Ninguno","AND","OR (inclusivo)","XOR, que permite seguir varios caminos si se cumplen varias condiciones"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El gateway OR sigue todos los caminos cuyas condiciones se cumplan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must follow one or more paths depending on which conditions hold (e.g. notify legal on legal risk and finance on financial risk). Which gateway fits?","options":["None","AND","OR (inclusive)","XOR, which allows several paths if several conditions hold"],"explanation":"The OR gateway follows every path whose condition holds."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si en un gateway XOR ninguna condición se cumple y no hay camino por defecto?","options":["Se elige un camino al azar","El proceso termina con éxito","El proceso se detiene con error en el gateway","El proceso continúa por el primer camino dibujado"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Conviene definir siempre un camino por defecto para evitar que el proceso se quede sin salida.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if no condition holds on an XOR gateway and there's no default path?","options":["A random path is chosen","The process ends successfully","The process stops with an error at the gateway","The process continues along the first drawn path"],"explanation":"Always define a default path so the process isn't left without an exit."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de variable almacena datos durante toda la vida de una instancia de proceso?","options":["Variable de proceso (pv!)","Constante (cons!)","Variable local de una interfaz (local!)","Rule input (ri!)"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las variables de proceso persisten durante la instancia y pasan datos entre nodos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which variable type holds data for the whole life of a process instance?","options":["Process variable (pv!)","Constant (cons!)","Interface local variable (local!)","Rule input (ri!)"],"explanation":"Process variables persist for the instance and pass data between nodes."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario de inicio de proceso debe recibir datos del usuario y guardarlos en variables de proceso. ¿Qué configuración es necesaria?","options":["Declarar las variables como constantes globales del proceso","Usar un temporizador","Crear un grupo","Marcar las variables como parámetro y mapearlas a los rule inputs del formulario"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los rule inputs del formulario de inicio se mapean a variables de proceso marcadas como parámetro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process start form must receive user data and store it in process variables. What configuration is needed?","options":["Declare the variables as global process constants","Use a timer","Create a group","Mark the variables as parameters and map them to the form's rule inputs"],"explanation":"Start form rule inputs map to process variables marked as parameters."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"En un nodo, ¿qué representan las entradas de nodo (ac!)?","options":["Variables locales del nodo que se rellenan desde el proceso y pueden guardar salidas","Grupos","Constantes","Variables globales visibles desde cualquier proceso del entorno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las entradas de nodo (activity class parameters) existen en el ámbito del nodo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In a node, what do node inputs (ac!) represent?","options":["Node-local variables populated from the process that can save outputs","Groups","Constants","Global variables visible from any process in the environment"],"explanation":"Node inputs (activity class parameters) exist in the node's scope."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un sub-proceso síncrono calcula un resultado que el proceso padre necesita. ¿Cómo lo recibe el padre?","options":["Con una constante","El padre lee automáticamente todas las variables del hijo sin configurar nada","Con un correo","Mapeando la variable de salida del sub-proceso a una variable del padre"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las entradas y salidas del sub-proceso se mapean explícitamente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A synchronous sub-process computes a result the parent needs. How does the parent receive it?","options":["With a constant","The parent automatically reads every child variable without configuration","By email","By mapping the sub-process's output variable to a parent variable"],"explanation":"Sub-process inputs and outputs are mapped explicitly."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario completa un formulario y la siguiente tarea es suya; quiere que aparezca de inmediato sin volver a la lista de tareas. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Un gateway AND","Un temporizador de un minuto entre las tareas","Activity chaining entre las tareas","Un sub-proceso asíncrono"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El encadenamiento de actividades lleva al usuario a la siguiente tarea directamente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user completes a form and the next task is theirs; they want it to appear immediately without returning to the task list. What's configured?","options":["An AND gateway","A one-minute timer between the tasks","Activity chaining between the tasks","An asynchronous sub-process"],"explanation":"Activity chaining takes the user straight to the next task."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene encadenar demasiados nodos automáticos con activity chaining?","options":["Que se duplican las tareas","El usuario espera más y se consumen recursos durante la cadena","Ninguno, porque la cadena acelera siempre todos los procesos","Que se pierden las variables"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El encadenamiento largo hace que el usuario espere y retiene recursos; debe usarse solo cuando aporta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of chaining too many automatic nodes with activity chaining?","options":["Tasks are duplicated","The user waits longer and resources are held during the chain","None, since chaining always speeds up every process","Variables are lost"],"explanation":"Long chains make users wait and hold resources; use chaining only where it helps."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una tarea asignada debe escalarse a un supervisor si no se completa en 48 horas. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Un script task que comprueba cada hora si la tarea sigue abierta","Una escalada o excepción con temporizador en la tarea","Un grupo","Un gateway OR"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las escaladas y temporizadores de nodo gestionan plazos en tareas humanas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An assigned task must escalate to a supervisor if not completed in 48 hours. What's configured?","options":["A script task checking every hour whether the task is still open","An escalation or timer exception on the task","A group","An OR gateway"],"explanation":"Node escalations and timers handle deadlines on human tasks."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe crear una tarea de revisión por cada documento de una lista de tamaño variable. ¿Qué configuración de nodo se usa?","options":["Un temporizador","Un gateway AND","Copiar el nodo de revisión tantas veces como documentos se esperan como máximo","Múltiples instancias de nodo (MNI) sobre la lista"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"MNI ejecuta el nodo una vez por elemento de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must create one review task per document in a variable-size list. Which node configuration is used?","options":["A timer","An AND gateway","Copy the review node as many times as the maximum expected documents","Multiple node instances (MNI) over the list"],"explanation":"MNI runs the node once per list item."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un evento de fin normal y uno de terminación (terminate)?","options":["El de terminación finaliza toda la instancia, incluidas otras ramas activas","El normal finaliza toda la instancia y el de terminación solo su rama","Ninguna","El de terminación reinicia el proceso"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Terminate detiene la instancia entera; un fin normal solo cierra su rama.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a normal end event and a terminate end event?","options":["Terminate ends the whole instance, including other active branches","Normal ends the whole instance and terminate only its branch","None","Terminate restarts the process"],"explanation":"Terminate stops the entire instance; a normal end only closes its branch."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos formas de iniciar un proceso no requieren que un usuario pulse un botón? (Elige 2)","options":["Una acción de sitio","Un formulario de inicio","Una llamada desde una Web API","Un evento de inicio programado","Una acción de registro"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Los inicios programados y por Web API no requieren interacción del usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two ways of starting a process don't require a user to click a button? (Choose 2)","options":["A site action","A start form","A call from a Web API","A scheduled start event","A record action"],"explanation":"Scheduled and Web API starts need no user interaction."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso necesita llamar a una API externa para validar un NIF. ¿Qué nodo es adecuado?","options":["Send E-Mail","Gateway XOR","User input task asignada al sistema externo","Call Integration con un integration object"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El nodo Call Integration ejecuta un objeto de integración dentro del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process needs to call an external API to validate a tax ID. Which node fits?","options":["Send E-Mail","XOR gateway","User input task assigned to the external system","Call Integration with an integration object"],"explanation":"The Call Integration node runs an integration object within the process."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una tarea asignada a un grupo la vea quien primero la acepte y desaparezca para los demás. ¿Qué comportamiento describe?","options":["Un temporizador","Asignación individual a cada miembro del grupo con una copia de la tarea","Asignación a grupo con aceptación de la tarea","Una escalada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Con asignación a grupo, la tarea queda en manos de quien la acepta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a group-assigned task seen by whoever accepts it first, disappearing for the others. Which behavior is this?","options":["A timer","Individual assignment to each group member with a copy of the task","Group assignment with task acceptance","An escalation"],"explanation":"With group assignment, the task goes to whoever accepts it."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario de tarea guarda la decisión del aprobador en una variable de proceso. ¿Cómo se configura el flujo de datos?","options":["Con un grupo","Con un correo","Escribiendo la decisión en una constante desde la interfaz","Mapeando el rule input de la interfaz a la variable de proceso en las entradas/salidas del nodo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los rule inputs de la interfaz se mapean a variables de proceso en la configuración del nodo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A task form saves the approver's decision into a process variable. How is the data flow configured?","options":["With a group","By email","Writing the decision to a constant from the interface","Mapping the interface rule input to the process variable in the node's inputs/outputs"],"explanation":"Interface rule inputs map to process variables in the node configuration."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos son smart services? (Elige 2)","options":["Gateway AND","Evento de inicio","Gateway XOR","Write Records","Send E-Mail"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Los smart services ejecutan acciones; los gateways y eventos controlan el flujo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two nodes are smart services? (Choose 2)","options":["AND gateway","Start event","XOR gateway","Write Records","Send E-Mail"],"explanation":"Smart services perform actions; gateways and events control flow."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador comprueba que un proceso falló porque una variable de proceso era nula al llegar a un nodo. ¿Dónde revisa el valor de las variables en esa instancia?","options":["En la consola de administración","En el diseño del process model guardado","En el monitor de la instancia, pestaña de variables","En el AppMarket"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El monitor de instancias muestra los valores de las variables durante y después de la ejecución.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer finds a process failed because a process variable was null at a node. Where do they check that instance's variable values?","options":["In the Admin Console","In the saved process model design","In the instance monitor, variables tab","In the AppMarket"],"explanation":"The instance monitor shows variable values during and after execution."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Tras corregir el error de un nodo en una instancia en curso, ¿qué puede hacer el desarrollador para que la instancia continúe?","options":["Reanudar o reintentar el nodo desde el monitor","Nada","Reiniciar el servidor","Borrar la instancia y esperar a que el usuario la inicie de nuevo sin avisar"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Desde el monitor se pueden reanudar nodos con error tras corregir la causa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After fixing a node's error in a running instance, what can the developer do so the instance continues?","options":["Resume or retry the node from the monitor","Nothing","Restart the server","Delete the instance and wait for the user to start it again without notice"],"explanation":"From the monitor, failed nodes can be resumed after fixing the cause."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una variable de proceso marcada como \"parámetro\"?","options":["Que se muestra a todos los usuarios","Que es una constante","Que su valor no puede cambiar durante el proceso","Que puede recibir un valor al iniciar el proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las variables parámetro reciben valores al inicio (formulario, a!startProcess o sub-proceso).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a process variable marked as \"parameter\" indicate?","options":["It's shown to every user","It's a constant","Its value can't change during the process","It can receive a value when the process starts"],"explanation":"Parameter variables receive values at start (form, a!startProcess or sub-process)."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso padre debe lanzar un sub-proceso por cada línea de pedido y esperar a que terminen todos. ¿Qué combinación es adecuada?","options":["Un sub-proceso asíncrono por línea, que espera automáticamente a todos","Un temporizador","Sub-proceso síncrono con MNI sobre las líneas","Un gateway XOR"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"MNI sobre un sub-proceso síncrono ejecuta uno por línea y espera a que terminen.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A parent process must launch a sub-process per order line and wait for all to finish. Which combination fits?","options":["One asynchronous sub-process per line, which waits for all automatically","A timer","Synchronous sub-process with MNI over the lines","An XOR gateway"],"explanation":"MNI over a synchronous sub-process runs one per line and waits for them to finish."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo detiene el flujo de un proceso hasta que se cumpla una fecha concreta (p. ej. el día de inicio del contrato)?","options":["Un evento de fin","Un evento intermedio de temporizador","Un gateway OR","Un script task con un bucle de espera"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los eventos de temporizador esperan hasta una fecha o durante un periodo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which node pauses a process flow until a specific date (e.g. the contract start date)?","options":["An end event","An intermediate timer event","An OR gateway","A script task with a wait loop"],"explanation":"Timer events wait until a date or for a period."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe esperar a recibir un mensaje de otro proceso antes de continuar. ¿Qué elemento se usa?","options":["Un gateway AND","Un evento de recepción de mensaje","Una constante","Un script task que consulta la base de datos cada minuto"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los eventos de mensaje permiten que un proceso espere señales de otros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must wait for a message from another process before continuing. Which element is used?","options":["An AND gateway","A receive message event","A constant","A script task polling the database every minute"],"explanation":"Message events let a process wait for signals from others."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas facilitan depurar un process model? (Elige 2)","options":["Probar con el modo de depuración y revisar el monitor","Nombrar los nodos y flujos de forma descriptiva","No definir caminos por defecto","Usar nombres genéricos como \"Nodo 1\"","Publicar sin probar"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Nombres descriptivos y la depuración en el monitor facilitan encontrar fallos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices make a process model easier to debug? (Choose 2)","options":["Test in debug mode and check the monitor","Name nodes and flows descriptively","Leave out default paths","Use generic names like \"Node 1\"","Publish without testing"],"explanation":"Descriptive names and debugging in the monitor make faults easier to find."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador usa una regla de expresión en un script task para calcular un descuento. ¿Dónde se guarda el resultado para usarlo en nodos posteriores?","options":["En una variable de proceso a través de las salidas del nodo","En la propia regla de expresión, que mantiene el último valor calculado","En una constante","En un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las salidas del script task se guardan en variables de proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer uses an expression rule in a script task to compute a discount. Where is the result saved for later nodes?","options":["In a process variable via the node outputs","In the expression rule itself, which keeps the last computed value","In a constant","In a group"],"explanation":"Script task outputs are saved into process variables."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso tiene un gateway AND que divide en dos ramas y más adelante deben juntarse antes de continuar. ¿Qué nodo se usa para unirlas?","options":["Un script task","Un evento de fin","Un gateway XOR, que espera a que lleguen todas las ramas","Otro gateway AND que espera a ambas ramas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Un AND de unión espera a que lleguen todas las ramas paralelas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process has an AND gateway splitting into two branches that must join before continuing. Which node joins them?","options":["A script task","An end event","An XOR gateway, which waits for all branches to arrive","Another AND gateway waiting for both branches"],"explanation":"A joining AND waits for every parallel branch to arrive."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dato necesita a!startProcess para iniciar un proceso?","options":["El process model (normalmente vía constante) y los parámetros","Un grupo","El nombre del usuario que aprobará la primera tarea","Una interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!startProcess recibe el process model y los valores de sus parámetros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!startProcess need to start a process?","options":["The process model (usually via a constant) and the parameters","A group","The name of the user who'll approve the first task","An interface"],"explanation":"a!startProcess takes the process model and its parameter values."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador referencia el process model en a!startProcess mediante una constante. ¿Por qué es buena práctica?","options":["Evita usar parámetros","Es obligatorio para publicar","Hace que el proceso se ejecute más rápido","Centraliza la referencia y facilita los despliegues"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las constantes centralizan referencias a objetos y se mantienen en los despliegues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer references the process model in a!startProcess via a constant. Why is this good practice?","options":["It avoids using parameters","It's mandatory for publishing","It makes the process run faster","It centralizes the reference and eases deployments"],"explanation":"Constants centralize object references and survive deployments."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una tarea de usuario no aparece a nadie tras iniciar el proceso. El monitor muestra que la asignación es un grupo vacío. ¿Qué corrección aplica?","options":["Reiniciar el servidor","Usar un script task","Asignar a un grupo con miembros (o revisar la expresión de asignación)","Publicar de nuevo el modelo sin cambios"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las tareas asignadas a grupos vacíos no llegan a nadie; hay que corregir la asignación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user task appears to no one after the process starts. The monitor shows assignment to an empty group. Which fix applies?","options":["Restart the server","Use a script task","Assign to a group with members (or fix the assignment expression)","Republish the model unchanged"],"explanation":"Tasks assigned to empty groups reach no one; fix the assignment."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro de Solicitud debe ofrecer una acción \"Cancelar solicitud\" que inicie un proceso sobre ese registro concreto. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Un grupo","Un temporizador","Una related action del record type que pasa el identificador al proceso","Una acción de sitio general que pide al usuario escribir el número de solicitud"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las related actions inician procesos en el contexto de un registro y reciben su identificador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Request record must offer a \"Cancel request\" action starting a process on that specific record. What's configured?","options":["A group","A timer","A record type related action passing the identifier to the process","A general site action asking the user to type the request number"],"explanation":"Related actions start processes in a record's context and receive its identifier."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre una record list action y una related action?","options":["La related crea registros nuevos desde la lista y la de lista modifica un registro","La de lista no inicia procesos","Ninguna","La de lista crea algo nuevo desde la lista; la related actúa sobre un registro concreto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las acciones de lista suelen crear registros; las related actions operan sobre un registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a record list action and a related action?","options":["The related one creates new records from the list and the list action modifies a record","The list action doesn't start processes","None","The list action creates something new from the list; the related one acts on a specific record"],"explanation":"List actions usually create records; related actions operate on one record."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso desatendido escribe en la base de datos con un nodo automático. ¿Qué configuración de asignación se suele usar para que tenga los permisos necesarios?","options":["Asignarlo a un grupo de usuarios finales para que lo aprueben","Sin asignación","Ejecutarlo como el diseñador del process model (o una cuenta de servicio)","Ejecutarlo como cualquier usuario al azar"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los nodos automáticos se ejecutan con una identidad definida, a menudo la del diseñador o una cuenta de servicio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An unattended process writes to the database with an automatic node. Which assignment setting is usually used so it has the needed permissions?","options":["Assign it to an end-user group for approval","No assignment","Run as the process model designer (or a service account)","Run as a random user"],"explanation":"Automatic nodes run with a defined identity, often the designer or a service account."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que el nombre de cada tarea en la lista del usuario muestre el número de solicitud (p. ej. \"Aprobar solicitud 1234\"). ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un nombre fijo y una descripción que el usuario debe abrir para ver el número","Un grupo","Una constante por solicitud","El nombre de la tarea con una expresión que use la variable del proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El nombre de las tareas admite expresiones con datos del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants each task's name in the user's list to show the request number (e.g. \"Approve request 1234\"). What do they configure?","options":["A fixed name and a description the user must open to see the number","A group","One constant per request","The task name with an expression using the process variable"],"explanation":"Task names support expressions with process data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso termina y sus datos se mantienen en memoria indefinidamente. ¿Qué configuración del process model ayuda a liberar recursos?","options":["Aumentar la memoria del servidor de forma periódica","Activity chaining","El archivado o borrado automático de procesos completados tras un periodo","Más variables de proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Configurar el archivado/borrado de procesos completados reduce el uso de memoria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process completes and its data stays in memory indefinitely. Which process model setting helps free resources?","options":["Periodically adding server memory","Activity chaining","Automatic archiving or deletion of completed processes after a period","More process variables"],"explanation":"Configuring archive/delete for completed processes reduces memory use."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Quién recibe por defecto las alertas de error de un process model si no se configura otra cosa?","options":["Los destinatarios de alertas configurados (p. ej. administradores del proceso)","Nadie nunca","Todos los usuarios que han iniciado alguna vez el proceso","El usuario final de la tarea"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las alertas de proceso se envían a los destinatarios configurados para que actúen ante errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Who receives a process model's error alerts by default if nothing else is configured?","options":["The configured alert recipients (e.g. process administrators)","Nobody ever","Every user who has ever started the process","The task's end user"],"explanation":"Process alerts go to the configured recipients so they can act on errors."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso tiene un bucle que vuelve a un nodo anterior para repetir una revisión hasta que se apruebe. ¿Qué riesgo debe controlarse?","options":["Que el bucle siempre termina en la primera vuelta","Que el bucle sea infinito; conviene limitar las iteraciones","Que no se puedan usar variables","Que no se pueda publicar"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los bucles en procesos deben tener una condición de salida y un límite para evitar instancias infinitas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process has a loop returning to an earlier node to repeat a review until approved. Which risk must be controlled?","options":["The loop always ends on the first pass","An infinite loop; limit the iterations","Variables can't be used","It can't be published"],"explanation":"Process loops need an exit condition and a limit to avoid infinite instances."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué smart service guarda en una variable el resultado de evaluar una decisión o regla sin intervención humana?","options":["Send E-Mail","User input task","Start Process","Script task"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El script task evalúa expresiones (incluidas reglas y decisiones) y guarda el resultado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which node saves the result of evaluating a decision or rule into a variable with no human involvement?","options":["Send E-Mail","User input task","Start Process","Script task"],"explanation":"The script task evaluates expressions (including rules and decisions) and saves the result."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere enviar un correo con datos de la solicitud a una lista de destinatarios. ¿Qué configura en el nodo Send E-Mail?","options":["Una constante por destinatario","Destinatarios, asunto y cuerpo con expresiones o plantilla","Un formulario que el usuario debe rellenar antes de enviar el correo","Un gateway"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Send E-Mail admite destinatarios, asunto y cuerpo dinámicos o desde plantilla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to email request data to a list of recipients. What do they configure in the Send E-Mail node?","options":["One constant per recipient","Recipients, subject and body with expressions or a template","A form the user must fill in before the email is sent","A gateway"],"explanation":"Send E-Mail supports dynamic recipients, subject and body, or a template."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Tras un formulario de inicio, el proceso guarda los datos y luego asigna una tarea a un aprobador. Los datos guardados no coinciden con los del formulario. ¿Qué revisa primero?","options":["El nombre del process model","El mapeo de los rule inputs del formulario a las variables de proceso","El AppMarket","La lista de grupos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los fallos de datos suelen deberse a mapeos incorrectos entre interfaz y variables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After a start form, the process saves the data and then assigns an approver task. The saved data doesn't match the form's. What's checked first?","options":["The process model's name","The mapping of the form's rule inputs to the process variables","The AppMarket","The group list"],"explanation":"Data faults usually come from wrong mappings between interface and variables."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos de un process model controlan el flujo (por dónde va el proceso) en lugar de ejecutar acciones? (Elige 2)","options":["Gateways","Eventos de temporizador y de mensaje","Call Integration","Write Records","Send E-Mail"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Gateways y eventos controlan el flujo; los smart services ejecutan acciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two process model elements control flow (where the process goes) rather than performing actions? (Choose 2)","options":["Gateways","Timer and message events","Call Integration","Write Records","Send E-Mail"],"explanation":"Gateways and events control flow; smart services perform actions."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe aprobarse por varios responsables en paralelo y continuar solo cuando todos hayan aprobado. ¿Qué diseño encaja?","options":["Tareas en paralelo (AND o MNI) y una unión que espere a todas","Un evento de fin","Una única tarea asignada a un grupo, que se completa cuando la aprueba el primero","Un gateway XOR"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Para requerir todas las aprobaciones, se crean tareas paralelas y se espera a que todas terminen.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must be approved by several managers in parallel and continue only when all have approved. Which design fits?","options":["Parallel tasks (AND or MNI) and a join waiting for all","An end event","A single group-assigned task, completed when the first approves","An XOR gateway"],"explanation":"To require every approval, create parallel tasks and wait for all to finish."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de variable usa una interfaz de tarea para recibir datos del proceso?","options":["Rule inputs (ri!) mapeados desde el nodo","Variables de proceso (pv!) accedidas directamente desde la interfaz","Grupos","Constantes"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las interfaces reciben datos por rule inputs, que el nodo mapea desde el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which variable type does a task interface use to receive process data?","options":["Rule inputs (ri!) mapped from the node","Process variables (pv!) accessed directly from the interface","Groups","Constants"],"explanation":"Interfaces receive data via rule inputs, which the node maps from the process."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador modifica un process model publicado y quiere comparar con la versión anterior. ¿Qué capacidad usa?","options":["Los grupos","El historial de versiones del process model","El AppMarket","Los logs del servidor de aplicaciones"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los process models mantienen versiones que pueden consultarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer modifies a published process model and wants to compare it with the previous version. Which capability do they use?","options":["Groups","The process model's version history","The AppMarket","Application server logs"],"explanation":"Process models keep versions that can be reviewed."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso usa a!startProcess desde una interfaz y debe mostrar un mensaje si el inicio falla. ¿Qué parámetro de a!startProcess se usa?","options":["onError","onSuccess","processModel","processParameters, que muestra el error en la interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"onError define qué hacer si el inicio falla; onSuccess, si va bien.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process uses a!startProcess from an interface and must show a message if the start fails. Which a!startProcess parameter is used?","options":["onError","onSuccess","processModel","processParameters, which displays the error in the interface"],"explanation":"onError defines what to do if the start fails; onSuccess, if it succeeds."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario de inicio de proceso no se muestra a los usuarios al pulsar la acción. El monitor no registra ninguna instancia. ¿Qué es lo más probable?","options":["Que el proceso es demasiado largo","Falta de permisos para iniciar el process model","Un error en el evento de fin del proceso","Que la base de datos está llena"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Si no se crea instancia, suele faltar permiso de inicio o la configuración de la acción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process start form doesn't show for users when they click the action. The monitor records no instance. What's most likely?","options":["The process is too long","Missing permission to start the process model","An error in the process end event","The database is full"],"explanation":"If no instance is created, start permission or the action configuration is usually missing."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso envía un recordatorio si una tarea lleva más de 3 días abierta, pero la tarea debe seguir asignada al mismo usuario. ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un grupo","Una escalada con temporizador que envíe el recordatorio sin reasignar","Un gateway XOR después de la tarea que compruebe la fecha","Cancelar la tarea a los 3 días"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las escaladas pueden notificar sin reasignar ni cancelar la tarea.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process sends a reminder if a task has been open over 3 days, but the task must stay assigned to the same user. What's configured?","options":["A group","A timer escalation sending the reminder without reassigning","An XOR gateway after the task checking the date","Cancel the task after 3 days"],"explanation":"Escalations can notify without reassigning or cancelling the task."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un nodo automático falla y no hay flujo de excepción configurado?","options":["Se borra la instancia","El proceso continúa como si el nodo hubiera funcionado","El proceso se reinicia desde el principio","El proceso se detiene en ese nodo con error y se generan alertas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los nodos con error detienen el flujo hasta que se resuelven; las alertas avisan a los administradores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if an automatic node fails and no exception flow is configured?","options":["The instance is deleted","The process continues as if the node had worked","The process restarts from the beginning","The process stops at that node with an error and alerts are generated"],"explanation":"Failing nodes halt the flow until resolved; alerts notify administrators."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos datos suelen mapearse como entradas al iniciar un sub-proceso? (Elige 2)","options":["La contraseña del usuario","Los datos de negocio que necesita (p. ej. la solicitud)","Todas las variables de todos los procesos del entorno","El diseño del process model padre","Identificadores para relacionarlo con el padre"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Se pasan los datos necesarios y las referencias al contexto del padre.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two pieces of data are usually mapped as inputs when starting a sub-process? (Choose 2)","options":["The user's password","The business data it needs (e.g. the request)","Every variable of every process in the environment","The parent process model's design","Identifiers to relate it to the parent"],"explanation":"Pass the needed data and references to the parent's context."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué conviene reutilizar sub-procesos para lógica común (p. ej. notificar y registrar un cambio de estado) en varios procesos?","options":["Porque no necesitan publicarse","Porque los sub-procesos se ejecutan siempre más rápido que los nodos individuales","Se mantiene en un solo lugar y se evita duplicar nodos","Porque no consumen memoria"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los sub-procesos reutilizables reducen duplicación y facilitan el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why reuse sub-processes for common logic (e.g. notify and log a status change) across several processes?","options":["Because they need no publishing","Because sub-processes always run faster than individual nodes","It's maintained in one place and avoids duplicated nodes","Because they use no memory"],"explanation":"Reusable sub-processes reduce duplication and ease maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso tiene 60 nodos y es difícil de entender y mantener. ¿Qué mejora de diseño recomienda Appian?","options":["Añadir más anotaciones de texto sin cambiar la estructura","Dividirlo en sub-procesos con responsabilidades claras","Eliminar los nombres de los nodos","Publicar más versiones"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Dividir procesos grandes en sub-procesos mejora la legibilidad, la reutilización y el rendimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process has 60 nodes and is hard to understand and maintain. Which design improvement does Appian recommend?","options":["Add more text annotations without changing structure","Split it into sub-processes with clear responsibilities","Remove node names","Publish more versions"],"explanation":"Splitting large processes into sub-processes improves readability, reuse and performance."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una tarea asignada debe mostrar al usuario los datos de la solicitud y permitirle aprobar o rechazar. ¿Qué objetos se combinan?","options":["Un evento de fin","Una constante","Un script task que muestra un mensaje en el sitio","Una User input task con una interfaz que recibe la solicitud por rule input"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La tarea de usuario presenta una interfaz que recibe los datos y devuelve la decisión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An assigned task must show the user the request data and let them approve or reject. Which objects combine?","options":["An end event","A constant","A script task showing a message on the site","A User input task with an interface receiving the request via rule input"],"explanation":"The user task presents an interface that receives the data and returns the decision."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de inicio de proceso usa un formulario que el usuario rellena antes de que exista la instancia?","options":["Formulario de inicio (start form) del process model","Un temporizador","Una user input task situada justo después del evento de inicio","Una Web API"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El formulario de inicio se muestra antes de crear la instancia y pasa los datos como parámetros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process start type uses a form the user fills in before the instance exists?","options":["The process model's start form","A timer","A user input task placed right after the start event","A Web API"],"explanation":"The start form is shown before the instance is created and passes data as parameters."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una tarea vaya al responsable del departamento del solicitante. ¿Cómo se define la asignación?","options":["Con un nombre fijo","Asignándola a todos los usuarios del entorno para que la acepte quien corresponda","Con una expresión que calcule el usuario o grupo responsable","Sin asignación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La asignación admite expresiones que determinan el destinatario según los datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a task to go to the requester's department manager. How is the assignment defined?","options":["With a fixed name","Assign it to every user in the environment so the right one accepts it","With an expression computing the responsible user or group","No assignment"],"explanation":"Assignment supports expressions that determine the recipient from data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe registrar en la base de datos cada vez que una solicitud cambia de estado. ¿Qué nodo añade tras cada cambio?","options":["Un gateway AND","Write Records (o Write to Data Store Entity)","Send E-Mail al administrador con el cambio","Un evento de fin"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los nodos de escritura persisten los cambios en la base de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must log to the database each time a request changes status. Which node is added after each change?","options":["An AND gateway","Write Records (or Write to Data Store Entity)","Send E-Mail to the administrator with the change","An end event"],"explanation":"Write nodes persist changes to the database."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a mantener bajo el consumo de memoria de los procesos? (Elige 2)","options":["Usar variables de proceso con listas enormes","Configurar el archivado de procesos completados","Guardar los datos de negocio en la base de datos, no en grandes variables de proceso","Mantener todas las instancias completadas indefinidamente","Encadenar todos los nodos"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Datos persistidos fuera del proceso y archivado reducen la memoria usada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices help keep process memory use low? (Choose 2)","options":["Use process variables with huge lists","Configure archiving of completed processes","Store business data in the database, not large process variables","Keep every completed instance indefinitely","Chain every node"],"explanation":"Data persisted outside the process and archiving reduce memory use."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso lanzado desde una related action necesita el registro completo, pero solo recibe el identificador. ¿Qué hace el proceso al empezar?","options":["Pedir al usuario que escriba todos los datos del registro en un formulario","Nada","Usar una constante","Consultar el registro por su identificador y guardarlo en una variable"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Lo habitual es pasar el identificador y consultar los datos actuales dentro del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process launched from a related action needs the full record, but only receives the identifier. What does the process do at the start?","options":["Ask the user to type all the record's data in a form","Nothing","Use a constant","Query the record by its identifier and store it in a variable"],"explanation":"It's typical to pass the identifier and query current data inside the process."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el icono de un nodo en rojo en el monitor de procesos?","options":["Que el nodo se completó con éxito antes de lo previsto","Que el nodo tiene un error que requiere atención","Que está esperando a un usuario","Que está desactivado"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El monitor marca los nodos con error para que el desarrollador los revise.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a red node icon in the process monitor indicate?","options":["The node completed successfully ahead of schedule","The node has an error needing attention","It's waiting for a user","It's disabled"],"explanation":"The monitor flags failing nodes for the developer to review."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe iniciarse cuando llega un correo a un buzón concreto. ¿Qué capacidad de Appian lo permite?","options":["Un inicio por recepción de correo (email start) configurado para el process model","Una user input task que espera correos","Un gateway OR","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Appian permite iniciar procesos a partir de correos entrantes con la configuración adecuada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must start when an email arrives at a specific mailbox. Which Appian capability allows this?","options":["An email start configured for the process model","A user input task waiting for emails","An OR gateway","A group"],"explanation":"Appian can start processes from incoming emails with the right configuration."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa pv!initiator en un process model?","options":["El primer nodo","El usuario que inició la instancia del proceso","El grupo de administradores del proceso","La fecha de inicio"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"pv!initiator contiene el usuario que inició la instancia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does pv!initiator represent in a process model?","options":["The first node","The user who started the process instance","The process administrators group","The start date"],"explanation":"pv!initiator holds the user who started the instance."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una tarea asignada al iniciador debe devolver la solicitud para correcciones. ¿Qué expresión de asignación es adecuada?","options":["Un usuario fijo","Una constante con el administrador","pv!initiator","El grupo de todos los usuarios de la aplicación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"pv!initiator asigna la tarea a quien inició el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A task assigned back to the initiator must return the request for corrections. Which assignment expression fits?","options":["A fixed user","A constant with the administrator","pv!initiator","The group of every application user"],"explanation":"pv!initiator assigns the task to whoever started the process."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere evitar que un proceso con MNI cree miles de tareas por error si la lista es enorme. ¿Qué medida aplica?","options":["Aumentar el número máximo de instancias permitidas en el entorno","Usar un grupo","Validar el tamaño de la lista antes del nodo","Publicar varias versiones"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Comprobar el tamaño de la lista antes de un MNI evita crear instancias masivas por error.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to prevent an MNI process from creating thousands of tasks by mistake if the list is huge. Which measure applies?","options":["Raise the environment's maximum allowed instances","Use a group","Validate the list size before the node","Publish several versions"],"explanation":"Checking list size before an MNI prevents mass instance creation by mistake."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe quedarse esperando hasta que un usuario actualice un registro desde otra parte de la aplicación. ¿Qué mecanismo es adecuado?","options":["Un temporizador de 1 año","Un script task en bucle que consulta el registro cada segundo","Una constante","Enviar un mensaje al proceso que lo espera con un evento de recepción"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los mensajes permiten despertar a un proceso en espera cuando ocurre un evento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must wait until a user updates a record elsewhere in the application. Which mechanism fits?","options":["A 1-year timer","A looping script task querying the record every second","A constant","Send a message to the waiting process with a receive event"],"explanation":"Messages let you wake a waiting process when an event happens."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a hacer el flujo de datos de un proceso claro y mantenible? (Elige 2)","options":["Variables con nombres genéricos (var1, var2)","Guardar todo en una sola variable de texto","Mapeos explícitos de entradas y salidas en cada nodo","Nombres descriptivos de variables de proceso","Sin documentación"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Nombres claros y mapeos explícitos facilitan seguir el flujo de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a process's data flow clear and maintainable? (Choose 2)","options":["Generic variable names (var1, var2)","Storing everything in one text variable","Explicit input and output mappings at each node","Descriptive process variable names","No documentation"],"explanation":"Clear names and explicit mappings make data flow easy to follow."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con una tarea de usuario si el proceso que la contiene termina por un evento de terminación en otra rama?","options":["Se reasigna al iniciador","La tarea sigue abierta para el usuario hasta que la complete","La tarea se cancela junto con la instancia","Se duplica"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un evento de terminación finaliza toda la instancia, incluidas sus tareas activas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to a user task if its process ends via a terminate event on another branch?","options":["It's reassigned to the initiator","The task stays open for the user until completed","The task is cancelled with the instance","It's duplicated"],"explanation":"A terminate event ends the whole instance, including its active tasks."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un process model debe iniciarse con unos datos mínimos validados. ¿Dónde se validan los datos de entrada del usuario antes de crear la instancia?","options":["En el evento de fin, comprobando que los datos eran correctos","En el AppMarket","En una constante","En el formulario de inicio con validaciones de interfaz"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las validaciones en el formulario de inicio evitan instancias con datos incorrectos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process model must start with minimal validated data. Where is user input validated before the instance is created?","options":["At the end event, checking the data was correct","In the AppMarket","In a constant","In the start form with interface validations"],"explanation":"Start form validations prevent instances with incorrect data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso debe enviar un correo al iniciador solo si la solicitud se rechaza. ¿Dónde se coloca el nodo Send E-Mail?","options":["En un sub-proceso asíncrono siempre","Antes del gateway, para que se envíe en todos los casos","En la rama de rechazo tras un gateway XOR","En paralelo con la aprobación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El nodo se sitúa en la rama correspondiente a la condición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process must email the initiator only if the request is rejected. Where's the Send E-Mail node placed?","options":["Always in an asynchronous sub-process","Before the gateway, so it's sent in every case","On the rejection branch after an XOR gateway","In parallel with approval"],"explanation":"The node sits on the branch matching the condition."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar el proceso completo con distintos datos antes de publicarlo para los usuarios. ¿Qué práctica es adecuada?","options":["Probar solo el formulario","No probarlo","Probarlo en desarrollo con casos representativos y revisar el monitor","Publicarlo en producción y pedir a los usuarios que informen de los fallos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las pruebas con casos representativos y la revisión del monitor detectan fallos antes del despliegue.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to test the full process with different data before publishing it for users. Which practice fits?","options":["Test only the form","Don't test it","Test it in development with representative cases and review the monitor","Publish to production and ask users to report bugs"],"explanation":"Testing with representative cases and reviewing the monitor catches faults before deployment."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos formas tiene un proceso de pasar datos a otro proceso que lanza? (Elige 2)","options":["Constantes modificadas en tiempo de ejecución","Leer las variables del padre desde el hijo sin mapear","Parámetros de un sub-proceso","Parámetros del smart service Start Process","Variables globales compartidas entre todos los procesos"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Los datos se pasan explícitamente mediante parámetros de sub-proceso o de Start Process.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two ways can a process pass data to another process it launches? (Choose 2)","options":["Constants modified at runtime","Reading the parent's variables from the child without mapping","Sub-process parameters","Start Process smart service parameters","Global variables shared by all processes"],"explanation":"Data is passed explicitly via sub-process or Start Process parameters."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una instancia de proceso lleva semanas esperando en una tarea de un empleado que ya no está en la empresa. ¿Qué acción toma un gestor del proceso?","options":["Borrar el grupo","Publicar de nuevo el modelo","Reasignar la tarea desde el monitor","Esperar a que el sistema la reasigne sola tras un mes"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los gestores pueden reasignar tareas de instancias en curso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process instance has waited weeks on a task for an employee who left the company. What does a process manager do?","options":["Delete the group","Republish the model","Reassign the task from the monitor","Wait for the system to reassign it after a month"],"explanation":"Managers can reassign tasks in running instances."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un process model tiene un formulario de inicio y un nodo que escribe en la base de datos justo después. Si la escritura falla, ¿qué ve el usuario?","options":["Un correo automático","Siempre un mensaje de error en el formulario antes de enviarlo","Nada nunca","Depende del diseño: si no hay encadenamiento, el usuario ya salió y el error queda en el monitor"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Sin encadenamiento, el usuario no espera a los nodos posteriores; los errores se gestionan en el monitor y con alertas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A process model has a start form and a database-writing node right after. If the write fails, what does the user see?","options":["An automatic email","Always an error message on the form before submitting","Nothing ever","It depends: without chaining, the user has already left and the error stays in the monitor"],"explanation":"Without chaining, the user doesn't wait for later nodes; errors are handled in the monitor and with alerts."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere conocer cuánto tardan de media las instancias de un proceso en completarse. ¿Qué recurso de Appian ofrece esa información sin construir nada?","options":["Los informes de proceso o las métricas del monitor","El AppMarket","El historial de versiones del process model","La lista de grupos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los informes y métricas de procesos muestran duraciones y estados de las instancias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to know how long a process's instances take on average. Which Appian resource offers this without building anything?","options":["Process reports or monitor metrics","The AppMarket","The process model's version history","The group list"],"explanation":"Process reports and metrics show instance durations and statuses."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos nodos pueden quedar esperando un tiempo indefinido en un proceso? (Elige 2)","options":["Gateway XOR","Script task","Evento de recepción de mensaje","User input task","Write Records"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Las tareas humanas y los eventos de mensaje esperan a algo externo; los nodos automáticos se ejecutan al llegar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two nodes can wait indefinitely in a process? (Choose 2)","options":["XOR gateway","Script task","Receive message event","User input task","Write Records"],"explanation":"Human tasks and message events wait for something external; automatic nodes run on arrival."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente de diseño envuelve un formulario con título, contenido y botones de envío?","options":["a!richTextDisplayField","a!gridField, que agrupa campos y botones en filas","a!cardLayout","a!formLayout"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!formLayout estructura formularios con título, contenidos y botones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which layout wraps a form with a title, contents and submit buttons?","options":["a!richTextDisplayField","a!gridField, which groups fields and buttons in rows","a!cardLayout","a!formLayout"],"explanation":"a!formLayout structures forms with title, contents and buttons."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar los campos en dos columnas en escritorio y apilados en móvil. ¿Qué layout se usa?","options":["Un sitio con dos páginas","Dos a!formLayout uno al lado del otro","a!columnsLayout con columnas","a!gridLayout"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!columnsLayout distribuye contenido en columnas que se adaptan a la pantalla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show fields in two columns on desktop and stacked on mobile. Which layout is used?","options":["A site with two pages","Two a!formLayout side by side","a!columnsLayout with columns","a!gridLayout"],"explanation":"a!columnsLayout spreads content into columns that adapt to the screen."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario largo debe agrupar campos por temas (Datos personales, Dirección) con encabezados. ¿Qué layout encaja?","options":["a!gridField","a!sectionLayout","a!localVariables","a!buttonArrayLayout, que agrupa campos bajo un encabezado"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!sectionLayout agrupa componentes bajo un título de sección.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A long form must group fields by topic (Personal data, Address) with headings. Which layout fits?","options":["a!gridField","a!sectionLayout","a!localVariables","a!buttonArrayLayout, which groups fields under a heading"],"explanation":"a!sectionLayout groups components under a section heading."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué se usa a!localVariables en una interfaz?","options":["Declarar las variables de proceso que se guardan en la base de datos","Definir rule inputs","Declarar variables locales que guardan estado en la interfaz","Iniciar procesos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!localVariables declara variables con ámbito de la interfaz o expresión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a!localVariables used for in an interface?","options":["Declaring process variables saved to the database","Defining rule inputs","Declaring local variables that hold state in the interface","Starting processes"],"explanation":"a!localVariables declares variables scoped to the interface or expression."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre un rule input y una variable local en una interfaz?","options":["El rule input recibe datos desde fuera; la local guarda estado interno","La variable local recibe datos del proceso y el rule input solo existe dentro de la interfaz","El rule input no se puede modificar","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los rule inputs son la interfaz de entrada/salida del objeto; las locales son estado interno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a rule input and a local variable in an interface?","options":["A rule input receives data from outside; a local holds internal state","A local variable receives process data and a rule input only exists inside the interface","A rule input can't be modified","None"],"explanation":"Rule inputs are the object's input/output interface; locals are internal state."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una variable local guarda el resultado de una consulta que depende de un filtro seleccionado por el usuario. ¿Cómo se consigue que la consulta se repita al cambiar el filtro?","options":["No es posible","Pidiendo al usuario que recargue la página tras cambiar el filtro","Usando una constante","Referenciando la variable del filtro en la definición (se refresca al cambiar)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Por defecto, una variable local se recalcula cuando cambian las variables que referencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A local variable holds a query result that depends on a user-selected filter. How do you make the query re-run when the filter changes?","options":["It's not possible","Ask the user to reload the page after changing the filter","Use a constant","Reference the filter variable in its definition (it refreshes on change)"],"explanation":"By default, a local variable recalculates when the variables it references change."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un cuadro de mando debe actualizar sus datos automáticamente cada 5 minutos. ¿Qué configuración de variable local se usa?","options":["Un temporizador de proceso","Una constante","a!refreshVariable con refreshInterval","refreshOnReferencedVarChange: false, que refresca periódicamente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!refreshVariable con refreshInterval recalcula la variable periódicamente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A dashboard must refresh its data automatically every 5 minutes. Which local variable configuration is used?","options":["A process timer","A constant","a!refreshVariable with refreshInterval","refreshOnReferencedVarChange: false, which refreshes periodically"],"explanation":"a!refreshVariable with refreshInterval recalculates the variable periodically."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Tras guardar datos con un botón, una cuadrícula debe mostrar la información actualizada. ¿Qué técnica de refresco encaja?","options":["Recargar la página","refreshOnVarChange en la consulta, ligado a un contador que se incrementa al guardar","refreshAlways: true en todas las variables de la interfaz","Usar una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Incrementar un contador en el saveInto y refrescar la consulta cuando cambia (refreshOnVarChange) actualiza los datos sin el coste de refreshAlways.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After saving data with a button, a grid must show updated information. Which refresh technique fits?","options":["Reload the page","refreshOnVarChange on the query, tied to a counter incremented on save","refreshAlways: true on every interface variable","Use a constant"],"explanation":"Incrementing a counter in the saveInto and refreshing the query when it changes (refreshOnVarChange) updates data without refreshAlways' cost."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene usar refreshAlways: true en una variable local que contiene una consulta?","options":["Que se borra la base de datos","Que la variable nunca se actualiza","Se ejecuta la consulta en cada interacción y degrada el rendimiento","Ninguno, porque es la configuración recomendada para cualquier consulta"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"refreshAlways recalcula en cada evaluación; con consultas, multiplica la carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of using refreshAlways: true on a local variable holding a query?","options":["The database is deleted","The variable never updates","The query runs on every interaction and degrades performance","None, since it's the recommended setting for any query"],"explanation":"refreshAlways recalculates on every evaluation; with queries, it multiplies load."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desplegable debe mostrar nombres de países pero guardar el código ISO. ¿Qué parámetros de a!dropdownField se usan?","options":["choiceValues para los nombres y label para los códigos","value y validations","choiceLabels para los nombres y choiceValues para los códigos","Solo label"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"choiceLabels son lo que ve el usuario; choiceValues, lo que se guarda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A dropdown must show country names but save the ISO code. Which a!dropdownField parameters are used?","options":["choiceValues for names and label for codes","value and validations","choiceLabels for names and choiceValues for codes","Only label"],"explanation":"choiceLabels are what users see; choiceValues are what's saved."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desplegable debe empezar sin selección y mostrar el texto \"Selecciona un país\". ¿Qué parámetro se usa?","options":["instructions","placeholder","helpTooltip","label, que también actúa como opción vacía seleccionable"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"placeholder muestra un texto cuando no hay selección; value debe ser nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A dropdown must start with no selection and show \"Select a country\". Which parameter is used?","options":["instructions","placeholder","helpTooltip","label, which also acts as a selectable empty option"],"explanation":"placeholder shows text when nothing is selected; value must be null."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para que un campo de texto guarde lo que escribe el usuario en una variable?","options":["Solo label","validations","value: la variable; saveInto: la misma variable","Solo value, porque guarda automáticamente lo que escribe el usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"value muestra el valor y saveInto define dónde guardar la entrada del usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern makes a text field save what the user types into a variable?","options":["Only label","validations","value: the variable; saveInto: the same variable","Only value, since it saves what the user types automatically"],"explanation":"value displays the value and saveInto defines where to save user input."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un campo debe aparecer solo si el usuario marca \"Tiene empresa\". ¿Qué parámetro se usa?","options":["showWhen con la condición","required","disabled: true, que oculta el campo cuando no se cumple la condición","readOnly"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"showWhen controla la visibilidad del componente según una condición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A field must appear only if the user ticks \"Has a company\". Which parameter is used?","options":["showWhen with the condition","required","disabled: true, which hides the field when the condition isn't met","readOnly"],"explanation":"showWhen controls component visibility based on a condition."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un botón debe guardar un valor y además ejecutar otra acción al pulsarlo. ¿Cómo se definen varias acciones en saveInto?","options":["Con dos botones idénticos que el usuario debe pulsar uno tras otro","Con una lista de acciones (p. ej. varios a!save) en saveInto","Con showWhen","No es posible"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"saveInto admite una lista de acciones que se ejecutan en orden.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A button must save a value and also perform another action when clicked. How are several actions defined in saveInto?","options":["With two identical buttons the user must click in turn","With a list of actions (e.g. several a!save) in saveInto","With showWhen","It's not possible"],"explanation":"saveInto accepts a list of actions executed in order."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace a!save(local!estado, \"Aprobado\") en el saveInto de un botón?","options":["Guarda el valor \"Aprobado\" en local!estado al pulsarlo","Muestra un mensaje","Inicia un proceso","Guarda \"Aprobado\" en la base de datos de forma permanente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!save asigna un valor a una variable como resultado de una interacción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!save(local!status, \"Approved\") do in a button's saveInto?","options":["Saves \"Approved\" into local!status when clicked","Shows a message","Starts a process","Permanently saves \"Approved\" to the database"],"explanation":"a!save assigns a value to a variable as the result of an interaction."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una cuadrícula debe mostrar una lista de solicitudes de solo lectura con paginación y ordenación. ¿Qué componente se usa?","options":["a!gridField","a!dropdownField","a!gridLayout, que es el componente para cuadrículas de solo lectura","a!sectionLayout"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!gridField es la cuadrícula de solo lectura con paginación y ordenación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A grid must show a read-only list of requests with paging and sorting. Which component is used?","options":["a!gridField","a!dropdownField","a!gridLayout, the component for read-only grids","a!sectionLayout"],"explanation":"a!gridField is the read-only grid with paging and sorting."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe permitir añadir, editar y eliminar líneas de detalle en una tabla. ¿Qué componente se usa?","options":["a!gridLayout (cuadrícula editable)","a!columnsLayout","a!cardLayout","a!gridField con la opción de edición activada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!gridLayout es la cuadrícula editable con filas de componentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must allow adding, editing and removing detail lines in a table. Which component is used?","options":["a!gridLayout (editable grid)","a!columnsLayout","a!cardLayout","a!gridField with editing turned on"],"explanation":"a!gridLayout is the editable grid with rows of components."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En una cuadrícula editable, ¿cómo se generan las filas a partir de una lista de elementos?","options":["Con un sitio","Con una consulta que devuelve las filas ya formateadas","Con a!forEach que devuelve un a!gridRowLayout por elemento","Con una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Se itera la lista con a!forEach y se construye una fila por elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In an editable grid, how are rows generated from a list of items?","options":["With a site","With a query returning already formatted rows","With a!forEach returning an a!gridRowLayout per item","With a constant"],"explanation":"Iterate the list with a!forEach and build a row per item."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un botón \"Añadir línea\" debe agregar un elemento vacío a la lista de una cuadrícula editable. ¿Qué saveInto es adecuado?","options":["a!startProcess","a!queryEntity","a!save(local!lineas, null), que añade una línea nueva","a!save(local!lineas, append(local!lineas, elemento vacío))"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se añade el nuevo elemento a la lista con append (u otra función de lista).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An \"Add line\" button must append an empty item to an editable grid's list. Which saveInto fits?","options":["a!startProcess","a!queryEntity","a!save(local!lines, null), which adds a new line","a!save(local!lines, append(local!lines, empty item))"],"explanation":"Append the new item to the list (with append or another list function)."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un campo de correo debe mostrar un error si el formato no es válido. ¿Qué parámetro del componente se usa?","options":["placeholder","validations con una expresión que devuelva el mensaje","showWhen","required: true, que comprueba el formato del correo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"validations muestra mensajes según una condición; required solo comprueba que no esté vacío.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An email field must show an error if the format is invalid. Which component parameter is used?","options":["placeholder","validations with an expression returning the message","showWhen","required: true, which checks the email format"],"explanation":"validations shows messages by condition; required only checks it's not empty."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario no debe enviarse si un campo obligatorio está vacío. ¿Qué configuración lo garantiza?","options":["Un mensaje en el label pidiendo al usuario que no lo deje vacío","showWhen","required: true en el campo y un botón de envío que valide","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los botones de envío validan los campos required y las validaciones antes de enviar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must not submit if a required field is empty. Which configuration guarantees this?","options":["A label message asking the user not to leave it empty","showWhen","required: true on the field and a validating submit button","A constant"],"explanation":"Submit buttons validate required fields and validations before submitting."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un botón \"Guardar borrador\" debe enviar el formulario sin exigir los campos obligatorios. ¿Qué configuración del botón lo permite?","options":["No es posible","Eliminar required de todos los campos del formulario","Usar showWhen en el botón","Un botón que no valide (p. ej. validate: false o un validationGroup distinto)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los botones pueden omitir la validación o usar grupos de validación específicos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A \"Save draft\" button must submit the form without requiring mandatory fields. Which button configuration allows this?","options":["It's not possible","Remove required from every field","Use showWhen on the button","A non-validating button (e.g. validate: false or a different validationGroup)"],"explanation":"Buttons can skip validation or use specific validation groups."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos validaciones se recomiendan en interfaces? (Elige 2)","options":["Validar formatos y rangos antes de enviar","No validar","Mostrar mensajes claros junto al campo afectado","Mostrar un único error genérico al final","Validar solo después de guardar en la base de datos"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Las validaciones inmediatas y claras junto al campo mejoran la experiencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two validation practices are recommended in interfaces? (Choose 2)","options":["Validate formats and ranges before submitting","Don't validate","Show clear messages next to the affected field","Show a single generic error at the end","Validate only after saving to the database"],"explanation":"Immediate, clear validations next to the field improve the experience."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar una interfaz con distintos valores de entrada sin ejecutar el proceso. ¿Qué usa en el diseñador de interfaces?","options":["Los valores de prueba de los rule inputs","El AppMarket","La consola de administración","Un proceso de prueba que se publica en producción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El diseñador permite definir valores de prueba para los rule inputs y ver el resultado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to test an interface with different input values without running the process. What do they use in the interface designer?","options":["Rule input test values","The AppMarket","The Admin Console","A test process published to production"],"explanation":"The designer lets you set rule input test values and see the result."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz tarda en cargar. ¿Qué herramienta del diseñador ayuda a identificar qué parte es lenta?","options":["El historial de versiones","La vista de rendimiento (performance) de la interfaz","Los grupos","El monitor de procesos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La vista de rendimiento muestra el tiempo de evaluación de cada parte de la interfaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface loads slowly. Which designer tool helps identify the slow part?","options":["Version history","The interface's performance view","Groups","The process monitor"],"explanation":"The performance view shows each part's evaluation time."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz muestra un error de expresión al cargarse. ¿Dónde lo revisa el desarrollador primero?","options":["En los grupos","En el AppMarket","En el mensaje de error del diseñador, que indica la línea y la causa","En la base de conocimiento, buscando el texto completo del formulario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El diseñador de interfaces muestra el error y su ubicación en la expresión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface shows an expression error on load. Where does the developer look first?","options":["Groups","The AppMarket","The designer's error message, showing the line and cause","The Knowledge Base, searching the whole form's text"],"explanation":"The interface designer shows the error and its location in the expression."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué práctica recomienda Appian para que las interfaces sean accesibles?","options":["Usar fuentes muy pequeñas","Ocultar las etiquetas","Usar solo colores para indicar los errores, sin texto","Etiquetas descriptivas en los campos y texto alternativo en imágenes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Etiquetas y textos alternativos ayudan a lectores de pantalla y a todos los usuarios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which practice does Appian recommend for accessible interfaces?","options":["Very small fonts","Hiding labels","Using only color to indicate errors, without text","Descriptive field labels and alt text on images"],"explanation":"Labels and alt text help screen readers and all users."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario largo con 60 campos abruma a los usuarios. ¿Qué patrón de diseño recomienda Appian?","options":["Eliminar las etiquetas","Reducir el tamaño de letra","Poner los 60 campos en una sola columna sin agrupación","Dividirlo en pasos (wizard) o secciones"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los asistentes por pasos y las secciones reducen la carga cognitiva.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A long 60-field form overwhelms users. Which design pattern does Appian recommend?","options":["Remove labels","Shrink the font","Put all 60 fields in one ungrouped column","Split it into steps (wizard) or sections"],"explanation":"Step-by-step wizards and sections reduce cognitive load."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente muestra texto con formato (negrita, enlaces, iconos) en una interfaz?","options":["a!dropdownField","a!gridLayout","a!richTextDisplayField","a!textField, que admite formato enriquecido para mostrar"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!richTextDisplayField muestra texto enriquecido con estilos e iconos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component displays formatted text (bold, links, icons) in an interface?","options":["a!dropdownField","a!gridLayout","a!richTextDisplayField","a!textField, which supports rich formatting for display"],"explanation":"a!richTextDisplayField displays rich text with styles and icons."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe permitir seleccionar varios valores de una lista corta de opciones. ¿Qué componente encaja?","options":["a!radioButtonField, que permite seleccionar varias opciones","a!checkboxField","a!dropdownField simple","a!dateField"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las casillas permiten selección múltiple; los botones de opción, una sola.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must allow selecting several values from a short option list. Which component fits?","options":["a!radioButtonField, which allows several selections","a!checkboxField","A simple a!dropdownField","a!dateField"],"explanation":"Checkboxes allow multiple selection; radio buttons, only one."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente es adecuado para elegir una sola opción entre tres visibles a la vez (p. ej. Prioridad: Alta, Media, Baja)?","options":["a!fileUploadField","a!radioButtonField","a!checkboxField, que obliga a elegir una sola opción","a!gridField"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Con pocas opciones excluyentes, los botones de opción las muestran todas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component fits choosing one option among three shown at once (e.g. Priority: High, Medium, Low)?","options":["a!fileUploadField","a!radioButtonField","a!checkboxField, which forces a single choice","a!gridField"],"explanation":"With few exclusive options, radio buttons show them all."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe permitir adjuntar documentos. ¿Qué componente se usa y qué configuración necesita?","options":["a!textField donde el usuario pega el contenido del documento","a!dropdownField","a!richTextDisplayField","a!fileUploadField con una carpeta de destino"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El campo de subida guarda documentos en la carpeta configurada al enviar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must allow attaching documents. Which component is used and what does it need?","options":["a!textField where users paste the document content","a!dropdownField","a!richTextDisplayField","a!fileUploadField with a target folder"],"explanation":"The upload field stores documents in the configured folder on submit."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador repite el mismo bloque de campos de dirección en cinco interfaces. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Crear una interfaz reutilizable para la dirección y llamarla desde las cinco","Copiar el bloque en las cinco interfaces y mantenerlas por separado","Crear un proceso","Usar una constante"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las interfaces reutilizables evitan duplicar componentes y facilitan el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer repeats the same address field block in five interfaces. Which best practice applies?","options":["Create a reusable address interface and call it from all five","Copy the block into all five interfaces and maintain them separately","Create a process","Use a constant"],"explanation":"Reusable interfaces avoid duplicated components and ease maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se pasan datos a una interfaz reutilizable llamada desde otra interfaz?","options":["Mediante sus rule inputs","Con variables de proceso","Con constantes","Leyendo las variables locales de la interfaz padre directamente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las interfaces hijas reciben datos y devuelven cambios a través de rule inputs.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is data passed to a reusable interface called from another interface?","options":["Through its rule inputs","With process variables","With constants","By reading the parent interface's local variables directly"],"explanation":"Child interfaces receive data and return changes via rule inputs."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos componentes son layouts (organizan otros componentes) y no campos? (Elige 2)","options":["a!dateField","a!columnsLayout","a!sectionLayout","a!dropdownField","a!textField"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Los layouts agrupan y distribuyen componentes; los campos recogen o muestran datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two components are layouts (organizing others) rather than fields? (Choose 2)","options":["a!dateField","a!columnsLayout","a!sectionLayout","a!dropdownField","a!textField"],"explanation":"Layouts group and arrange components; fields collect or display data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe mostrar tarjetas clicables con información resumida de cada cliente. ¿Qué componente se usa?","options":["a!buttonArrayLayout","a!dropdownField","a!cardLayout con un link","a!gridLayout con una fila por cliente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las tarjetas (cardLayout) agrupan contenido y admiten enlaces.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must show clickable cards summarizing each customer. Which component is used?","options":["a!buttonArrayLayout","a!dropdownField","a!cardLayout with a link","a!gridLayout with one row per customer"],"explanation":"Cards (cardLayout) group content and support links."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere mostrar un campo como solo lectura cuando la solicitud ya está aprobada. ¿Qué parámetro usa?","options":["placeholder","showWhen: false, que mantiene el campo visible pero no editable","required","readOnly (o disabled) con una condición"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"readOnly/disabled impiden editar manteniendo el valor visible; showWhen lo oculta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to show a field as read-only once the request is approved. Which parameter do they use?","options":["placeholder","showWhen: false, which keeps the field visible but not editable","required","readOnly (or disabled) with a condition"],"explanation":"readOnly/disabled prevent editing while keeping the value visible; showWhen hides it."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario muestra un desplegable de provincias que depende del país elegido. ¿Qué debe hacer el saveInto del desplegable de país?","options":["Iniciar un proceso","Guardar solo el país y mantener la provincia aunque ya no corresponda","Nada","Guardar el país y limpiar la provincia seleccionada"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Al cambiar un valor del que dependen otros, se reinician los valores dependientes para evitar incoherencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form shows a province dropdown depending on the chosen country. What should the country dropdown's saveInto do?","options":["Start a process","Save only the country and keep the province even if it no longer applies","Nothing","Save the country and clear the selected province"],"explanation":"When changing a value others depend on, reset dependent values to avoid inconsistencies."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desplegable muestra un error porque su value no está entre los choiceValues. ¿Qué causa es más probable?","options":["Que el label está vacío","Que el desplegable tiene demasiadas opciones para mostrarse","Que falta un placeholder","El valor guardado ya no existe en la lista de opciones"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El value de un desplegable debe ser nulo o uno de sus choiceValues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A dropdown shows an error because its value isn't among the choiceValues. What's the most likely cause?","options":["The label is empty","The dropdown has too many options to display","A placeholder is missing","The saved value no longer exists in the option list"],"explanation":"A dropdown's value must be null or one of its choiceValues."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos formas existen de controlar qué componentes ve cada usuario en una interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["No mostrar etiquetas","Interfaces distintas según el rol, elegidas por una regla","Cambiar el tamaño de letra","Ocultar con colores","showWhen con condiciones (p. ej. pertenencia a grupo)"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Las condiciones de visibilidad y las interfaces por rol adaptan la interfaz al usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two ways exist to control which components each user sees in an interface? (Choose 2)","options":["Not showing labels","Different role-based interfaces chosen by a rule","Changing font size","Hiding with colors","showWhen with conditions (e.g. group membership)"],"explanation":"Visibility conditions and role-based interfaces adapt the interface to the user."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz consulta la base de datos dentro de un a!forEach que recorre 100 elementos. ¿Qué mejora de buenas prácticas aplica?","options":["Añadir refreshAlways para que la consulta esté siempre actualizada","Nada","Usar más variables locales dentro del bucle","Consultar una sola vez fuera del bucle y cruzar los datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las consultas en bucle degradan el rendimiento; se agrupan en una sola consulta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface queries the database inside an a!forEach over 100 items. Which best practice improvement applies?","options":["Add refreshAlways so the query is always current","Nothing","Use more local variables inside the loop","Query once outside the loop and match the data"],"explanation":"Queries in loops hurt performance; group them into one query."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar el total de las líneas de una cuadrícula editable y actualizarlo al cambiar las cantidades. ¿Cómo se calcula?","options":["Con un proceso","Con una expresión sobre la lista de líneas mostrada en un campo de solo lectura","Con una constante","Guardando el total en la base de datos cada vez que el usuario cambia una cantidad"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los valores derivados se calculan en la interfaz a partir de las variables y se recalculan al cambiar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show the total of an editable grid's lines and update it when quantities change. How is it computed?","options":["With a process","With an expression over the line list shown in a read-only field","With a constant","Saving the total to the database every time a quantity changes"],"explanation":"Derived values are computed in the interface from variables and recalculated on change."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz de tarea debe guardar la decisión del usuario y cerrar la tarea al pulsar \"Aprobar\". ¿Qué configura el botón?","options":["submit: true y un saveInto que guarde la decisión en el rule input","showWhen","Un saveInto que inicia un nuevo proceso de aprobación","Un enlace a otra página"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un botón de envío guarda en el rule input y completa la tarea.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A task interface must save the user's decision and close the task on \"Approve\". What does the button configure?","options":["submit: true and a saveInto saving the decision into the rule input","showWhen","A saveInto starting a new approval process","A link to another page"],"explanation":"A submit button saves into the rule input and completes the task."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario usa un a!dateField para la fecha de inicio. Debe impedir fechas pasadas. ¿Cómo se implementa?","options":["Con una constante","Con showWhen","Con una validación que compare la fecha con today()","Con un placeholder que diga \"no uses fechas pasadas\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las validaciones comparan el valor con la fecha actual y muestran un mensaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form uses an a!dateField for the start date. It must prevent past dates. How is this implemented?","options":["With a constant","With showWhen","With a validation comparing the date to today()","With a placeholder saying \"don't use past dates\""],"explanation":"Validations compare the value with the current date and show a message."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda Appian para que los botones de acción de un formulario sean consistentes?","options":["Agruparlos con a!buttonArrayLayout, con la acción principal destacada","Repartir los botones por todo el formulario junto a cada campo","Usar enlaces de texto en lugar de botones","No usar botones"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Agrupar botones y destacar la acción principal mejora la usabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does Appian recommend for consistent form action buttons?","options":["Group them with a!buttonArrayLayout, highlighting the primary action","Spread buttons across the form next to each field","Use text links instead of buttons","Use no buttons"],"explanation":"Grouping buttons and highlighting the primary action improves usability."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe permitir elegir un usuario de Appian como responsable. ¿Qué componente se usa?","options":["a!gridLayout","Un picker de usuarios (a!pickerFieldUsers)","a!checkboxField con todos los usuarios","Un a!textField donde el usuario escribe el nombre de usuario completo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los pickers de usuarios buscan y validan usuarios existentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must allow choosing an Appian user as owner. Which component is used?","options":["a!gridLayout","A user picker (a!pickerFieldUsers)","a!checkboxField with every user","An a!textField where the user types the full username"],"explanation":"User pickers search and validate existing users."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe permitir seleccionar un cliente entre miles de registros buscando por nombre. ¿Qué componente encaja?","options":["Un a!dropdownField con los miles de clientes cargados","Un picker de registros (a!pickerFieldRecords)","a!radioButtonField","a!checkboxField"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los pickers buscan bajo demanda; un desplegable con miles de opciones es lento e incómodo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must allow selecting a customer among thousands of records by searching by name. Which component fits?","options":["An a!dropdownField with thousands of customers loaded","A record picker (a!pickerFieldRecords)","a!radioButtonField","a!checkboxField"],"explanation":"Pickers search on demand; a dropdown with thousands of options is slow and awkward."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente se usa para capturar un número entero (p. ej. cantidad)?","options":["a!textField, que convierte automáticamente el texto en número","a!dateField","a!paragraphField","a!integerField"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!integerField valida y guarda números enteros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component captures an integer (e.g. quantity)?","options":["a!textField, which converts text to a number automatically","a!dateField","a!paragraphField","a!integerField"],"explanation":"a!integerField validates and stores integers."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario necesita un campo para comentarios de varias líneas. ¿Qué componente encaja?","options":["a!paragraphField","a!textField, que admite varias líneas con su parámetro de altura","a!dateField","a!integerField"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!paragraphField captura texto de varias líneas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form needs a multi-line comments field. Which component fits?","options":["a!paragraphField","a!textField, which supports multiple lines via its height parameter","a!dateField","a!integerField"],"explanation":"a!paragraphField captures multi-line text."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una lista de registros debe tener un enlace que abra la vista del registro de cada cliente. ¿Qué tipo de enlace se usa?","options":["a!startProcess","a!dynamicLink, que navega a la vista de cualquier registro","a!recordLink","Un texto plano"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!recordLink abre la vista de un registro; a!dynamicLink ejecuta un saveInto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record list must link to each customer's record view. Which link type is used?","options":["a!startProcess","a!dynamicLink, which navigates to any record's view","a!recordLink","Plain text"],"explanation":"a!recordLink opens a record view; a!dynamicLink runs a saveInto."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un enlace en una interfaz debe cambiar el valor de una variable local (p. ej. seleccionar una pestaña) sin navegar a otra página. ¿Qué enlace se usa?","options":["a!dynamicLink con saveInto","a!documentDownloadLink","a!recordLink, que también actualiza variables","a!safeLink"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!dynamicLink ejecuta su saveInto al pulsarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A link in an interface must change a local variable (e.g. select a tab) without navigating. Which link is used?","options":["a!dynamicLink with saveInto","a!documentDownloadLink","a!recordLink, which also updates variables","a!safeLink"],"explanation":"a!dynamicLink runs its saveInto when clicked."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un asistente de alta tiene tres pasos. ¿Cómo se implementa habitualmente la navegación entre pasos en una interfaz?","options":["Una variable local con el paso actual y showWhen en cada sección","Tres sitios","Tres grupos","Tres process models, uno por paso, encadenados con temporizadores"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un patrón común usa una variable de paso, botones que la cambian y showWhen por sección.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An onboarding wizard has three steps. How is navigation between steps usually implemented in an interface?","options":["A local variable holding the current step and showWhen on each section","Three sites","Three groups","Three process models, one per step, chained with timers"],"explanation":"A common pattern uses a step variable, buttons changing it and showWhen per section."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Dentro de a!forEach, ¿qué representa fv!item?","options":["El elemento actual de la lista que se recorre","El índice del elemento actual en la lista","La lista completa","El primer elemento"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"fv!item es el elemento actual; fv!index, su posición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Inside a!forEach, what does fv!item represent?","options":["The current item of the list being iterated","The current item's index in the list","The whole list","The first item"],"explanation":"fv!item is the current item; fv!index is its position."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"En una cuadrícula editable, un botón de borrar fila debe eliminar el elemento correspondiente. ¿Qué dato de a!forEach se usa para saber cuál eliminar?","options":["fv!isFirst","fv!item, que indica la posición del elemento","fv!itemCount","fv!index"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"fv!index identifica la posición del elemento para eliminarlo de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In an editable grid, a delete-row button must remove the matching item. Which a!forEach value tells which one to remove?","options":["fv!isFirst","fv!item, which indicates the item's position","fv!itemCount","fv!index"],"explanation":"fv!index identifies the item's position to remove it from the list."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe mostrar \"Sin datos\" cuando la consulta no devuelve resultados. ¿Qué función ayuda a comprobarlo de forma segura?","options":["today","isnull, que también detecta listas vacías en todos los casos","a!isNullOrEmpty","len de un texto"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!isNullOrEmpty detecta valores nulos y listas vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must show \"No data\" when the query returns no results. Which function helps check this safely?","options":["today","isnull, which also detects empty lists in every case","a!isNullOrEmpty","len of a text"],"explanation":"a!isNullOrEmpty detects null values and empty lists."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un campo debe mostrar un valor por defecto si la variable es nula. ¿Qué función encaja?","options":["a!save, que asigna el valor por defecto al cargar","a!forEach","a!match","a!defaultValue"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!defaultValue devuelve el primer valor no nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A field must show a default value if the variable is null. Which function fits?","options":["a!save, which assigns the default on load","a!forEach","a!match","a!defaultValue"],"explanation":"a!defaultValue returns the first non-null value."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un cuadro de mando debe mostrar el número de solicitudes por estado de forma visual. ¿Qué componente encaja?","options":["Un picker","Un gráfico (p. ej. a!barChartField o a!pieChartField) con datos de un record type","Un a!paragraphField con los números escritos en texto","Una cuadrícula editable"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los componentes de gráfico muestran agregaciones, y pueden usar records como fuente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A dashboard must show request counts by status visually. Which component fits?","options":["A picker","A chart (e.g. a!barChartField or a!pieChartField) with record type data","An a!paragraphField with the numbers written as text","An editable grid"],"explanation":"Chart components show aggregations and can use records as a source."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente muestra el avance de un proceso en etapas (p. ej. Enviado → Revisado → Aprobado)?","options":["a!dropdownField con las etapas como opciones","a!fileUploadField","a!integerField","a!milestoneField"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!milestoneField muestra el paso actual en una secuencia de etapas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component shows a process's progress through stages (e.g. Submitted → Reviewed → Approved)?","options":["a!dropdownField with the stages as options","a!fileUploadField","a!integerField","a!milestoneField"],"explanation":"a!milestoneField shows the current step in a sequence of stages."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe mostrar un mensaje informativo destacado en la parte superior (p. ej. \"El plazo termina mañana\"). ¿Qué opción es adecuada?","options":["Un campo de texto editable con el mensaje como valor por defecto","Un a!messageBanner o un texto enriquecido con estilo destacado","Una cuadrícula","Un gráfico"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los banners o textos enriquecidos destacan mensajes sin confundirse con campos editables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must show a prominent informational message at the top (e.g. \"The deadline is tomorrow\"). Which option fits?","options":["An editable text field with the message as default value","An a!messageBanner or styled rich text","A grid","A chart"],"explanation":"Banners or rich text highlight messages without looking like editable fields."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función evalúa un valor contra varios casos y devuelve el resultado del que coincide (p. ej. color según estado)?","options":["a!localVariables","a!match","a!save","a!forEach, que recorre los casos posibles"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!match compara un valor con varios casos y devuelve el correspondiente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function evaluates a value against several cases and returns the matching result (e.g. color by status)?","options":["a!localVariables","a!match","a!save","a!forEach, which iterates the possible cases"],"explanation":"a!match compares a value with several cases and returns the matching one."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe ocultar un botón \"Eliminar\" a los usuarios que no pertenecen al grupo de administradores. ¿Qué expresión se usa en showWhen?","options":["No es posible","Una comparación del nombre del usuario con una lista escrita en la interfaz","Una comprobación de pertenencia del usuario actual al grupo (p. ej. a!isUserMemberOfGroup)","Una constante con valor true"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las funciones de pertenencia a grupo permiten condicionar componentes por rol.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must hide a \"Delete\" button from users not in the administrators group. Which expression goes in showWhen?","options":["It's not possible","Comparing the username with a list typed in the interface","A check of the current user's group membership (e.g. a!isUserMemberOfGroup)","A constant set to true"],"explanation":"Group membership functions condition components by role."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Ocultar un botón con showWhen según el rol, ¿es suficiente para proteger la acción que ejecuta?","options":["Solo en móvil","Sí, porque un usuario no puede ejecutar nada que no vea en la interfaz","Sí, siempre","No: la acción también debe protegerse con seguridad en el proceso o los datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La interfaz no es un control de seguridad suficiente; los permisos deben aplicarse en procesos y datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Is hiding a button with showWhen by role enough to protect the action it performs?","options":["Only on mobile","Yes, because users can't run anything they don't see in the interface","Yes, always","No: the action must also be secured in the process or data"],"explanation":"The interface isn't a sufficient security control; permissions must be enforced in processes and data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas mejoran el rendimiento de una interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["Guardar resultados de consultas en variables locales y reutilizarlos","Usar refreshAlways en todas las variables","Cargar todos los registros en desplegables","Paginar los datos en cuadrículas","Llamar a la misma consulta en varios componentes"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Reutilizar resultados y paginar reduce el trabajo de cada evaluación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices improve interface performance? (Choose 2)","options":["Store query results in local variables and reuse them","Use refreshAlways on every variable","Load every record into dropdowns","Page data in grids","Call the same query in several components"],"explanation":"Reusing results and paging reduce work on each evaluation."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz llama a la misma regla de consulta en tres componentes distintos. ¿Qué mejora aplica?","options":["Llamar a la regla con refreshAlways para que los resultados coincidan","Crear tres reglas distintas","Nada","Guardar el resultado en una variable local y usarla en los tres"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Evaluar la consulta una vez y reutilizar el resultado evita trabajo duplicado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface calls the same query rule in three different components. Which improvement applies?","options":["Call the rule with refreshAlways so results match","Create three different rules","Nothing","Store the result in a local variable and use it in all three"],"explanation":"Evaluating the query once and reusing the result avoids duplicated work."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz de solicitud usa un rule input de tipo registro. El desarrollador quiere probar el caso de una solicitud nueva (sin datos). ¿Cómo lo prueba en el diseñador?","options":["Creando una solicitud real en producción para usarla como prueba","Publicando la interfaz","No se puede","Dejando el rule input nulo en los valores de prueba"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los valores de prueba permiten simular casos como entrada nula (alta) o con datos (edición).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A request interface uses a record-type rule input. The developer wants to test the new-request case (no data). How do they test it in the designer?","options":["Create a real production request to use as a test","Publish the interface","It can't be done","Leave the rule input null in the test values"],"explanation":"Test values simulate cases such as null input (create) or with data (edit)."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz falla con un error al acceder a un campo de un rule input nulo. ¿Qué corrección es adecuada?","options":["Comprobar si es nulo antes de acceder o usar un valor por defecto","Eliminar el campo","Exigir a todos los usuarios que siempre rellenen el rule input","Usar refreshAlways"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las interfaces deben manejar entradas nulas para no fallar en casos como el alta de un registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface errors when accessing a field of a null rule input. Which fix fits?","options":["Check for null before accessing, or use a default value","Remove the field","Require every user to always fill in the rule input","Use refreshAlways"],"explanation":"Interfaces must handle null inputs so they don't fail in cases like record creation."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente muestra una imagen (p. ej. el logo de la empresa o una foto de un documento) en una interfaz?","options":["a!imageField","a!fileUploadField","a!gridLayout","a!richTextDisplayField, que es el único que muestra imágenes"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!imageField muestra imágenes de documentos o URLs.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component displays an image (e.g. company logo or a document photo) in an interface?","options":["a!imageField","a!fileUploadField","a!gridLayout","a!richTextDisplayField, the only one that shows images"],"explanation":"a!imageField displays images from documents or URLs."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe verse bien en móvil. ¿Qué práctica recomienda Appian?","options":["Crear una aplicación distinta para móvil","Fijar anchos en píxeles para todos los componentes","No usar columnas","Usar layouts adaptativos (columnas que se apilan) y probar en vista móvil"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los layouts de Appian se adaptan; conviene revisar la vista móvil durante el diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must look good on mobile. Which practice does Appian recommend?","options":["Build a separate mobile application","Set pixel widths on every component","Use no columns","Use adaptive layouts (columns that stack) and test the mobile preview"],"explanation":"Appian layouts adapt; review the mobile preview while designing."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una cuadrícula de solo lectura muestre los registros de un record type con filtros que el usuario pueda usar. ¿Qué opción ofrece más funcionalidad con menos código?","options":["Usar el record type como fuente de la cuadrícula con filtros de usuario","Usar una cuadrícula editable","Usar un desplegable","Consultar todos los registros y filtrar a mano en la interfaz con a!forEach"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las cuadrículas con records como fuente ofrecen paginación, ordenación y filtros de usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a read-only grid showing a record type's records with filters the user can apply. Which option offers most functionality with least code?","options":["Use the record type as the grid source with user filters","Use an editable grid","Use a dropdown","Query every record and filter manually in the interface with a!forEach"],"explanation":"Grids with records as source offer paging, sorting and user filters."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de validación muestra un mensaje que afecta a todo el formulario (p. ej. \"La suma de porcentajes debe ser 100\")?","options":["Validaciones del formulario o de la sección","showWhen","Un placeholder","Una validación en cada campo con el mismo mensaje repetido"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las validaciones a nivel de formulario o sección expresan reglas que implican varios campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which kind of validation shows a message affecting the whole form (e.g. \"Percentages must sum to 100\")?","options":["Form- or section-level validations","showWhen","A placeholder","A validation on every field repeating the same message"],"explanation":"Form- or section-level validations express rules spanning several fields."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario tiene dos botones: \"Enviar\" (exige todos los campos) y \"Consultar disponibilidad\" (solo exige la fecha). ¿Qué mecanismo permite validar distinto según el botón?","options":["showWhen","required en todos los campos y quitarlo al pulsar el botón","validationGroup","Dos formularios distintos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los grupos de validación asocian validaciones a botones concretos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form has two buttons: \"Submit\" (requires all fields) and \"Check availability\" (requires only the date). Which mechanism validates differently per button?","options":["showWhen","required on every field, removed when the button is clicked","validationGroup","Two separate forms"],"explanation":"Validation groups tie validations to specific buttons."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar un indicador de carga mientras se sube un archivo grande. ¿Qué componente del propio campo lo gestiona?","options":["a!fileUploadField muestra el progreso de subida","Un a!progressBarField que el desarrollador actualiza manualmente cada segundo","Una cuadrícula","Un gráfico"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El campo de subida gestiona el estado de carga de los archivos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show a loading indicator while a large file uploads. Which component handles this itself?","options":["a!fileUploadField shows upload progress","An a!progressBarField the developer updates manually every second","A grid","A chart"],"explanation":"The upload field manages files' upload status."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos componentes son de solo visualización y no capturan datos del usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["a!dropdownField","a!richTextDisplayField","a!textField","a!imageField","a!dateField"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Los campos de texto enriquecido e imagen muestran contenido; los demás capturan datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two components are display-only and don't capture user data? (Choose 2)","options":["a!dropdownField","a!richTextDisplayField","a!textField","a!imageField","a!dateField"],"explanation":"Rich text and image fields display content; the others capture data."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar el nombre completo del usuario conectado en la cabecera. ¿Qué función obtiene el usuario actual?","options":["pv!initiator, disponible en cualquier interfaz","today()","loggedInUser()","now()"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"loggedInUser() devuelve el usuario que está viendo la interfaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show the logged-in user's full name in the header. Which function gets the current user?","options":["pv!initiator, available in any interface","today()","loggedInUser()","now()"],"explanation":"loggedInUser() returns the user viewing the interface."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz de tarea muestra los datos que recibió el rule input al abrirse, aunque otro usuario los cambió después en la base de datos. ¿Por qué?","options":["Porque la caché del navegador está llena","Porque las interfaces siempre consultan la base de datos al abrirse","Por un error de Appian","El rule input contiene los datos que el proceso pasó al crear la tarea"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los rule inputs reflejan lo que mapeó el proceso; para datos actuales hay que consultarlos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A task interface shows the data its rule input received on open, though another user changed it later in the database. Why?","options":["Because the browser cache is full","Because interfaces always query the database on open","Due to an Appian bug","The rule input holds the data the process passed when creating the task"],"explanation":"Rule inputs reflect what the process mapped; for current data, query it."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda Appian para mostrar en una vista de registro la información más importante arriba y los detalles debajo?","options":["Un solo párrafo de texto","Un resumen destacado (p. ej. tarjetas o cabecera) seguido de secciones de detalle","Todos los campos en una sola lista alfabética","Una cuadrícula editable"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Priorizar la información clave mejora la usabilidad de las vistas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does Appian recommend for showing the most important information at the top of a record view and details below?","options":["A single text paragraph","A highlighted summary (e.g. cards or header) followed by detail sections","Every field in a single alphabetical list","An editable grid"],"explanation":"Prioritizing key information improves view usability."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador escribe toda la lógica de cálculo de una interfaz dentro de los componentes, repetida en varios sitios. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Extraer la lógica a reglas de expresión reutilizables","Mover la lógica a un grupo","Repetir la lógica en cada componente para que sea más fácil de leer","Usar constantes para todo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las reglas de expresión separan la lógica de la presentación y se reutilizan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer writes all of an interface's calculation logic inside components, repeated in several places. Which best practice applies?","options":["Extract the logic into reusable expression rules","Move logic into a group","Repeat the logic in each component to make it easier to read","Use constants for everything"],"explanation":"Expression rules separate logic from presentation and are reusable."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario usa un campo de fecha y hora para citas. ¿Qué componente se usa?","options":["a!dateTimeField","a!textField","a!integerField","a!dateField, que también recoge la hora"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!dateTimeField recoge fecha y hora; a!dateField solo fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form uses a date and time field for appointments. Which component is used?","options":["a!dateTimeField","a!textField","a!integerField","a!dateField, which also captures time"],"explanation":"a!dateTimeField captures date and time; a!dateField only the date."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar etiquetas de estado de colores (p. ej. \"Urgente\" en rojo) en una lista. ¿Qué componente encaja?","options":["a!checkboxField","a!fileUploadField","a!dropdownField con colores en las opciones","a!tagField"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!tagField muestra etiquetas con color de fondo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show colored status tags (e.g. \"Urgent\" in red) in a list. Which component fits?","options":["a!checkboxField","a!fileUploadField","a!dropdownField with colors in the options","a!tagField"],"explanation":"a!tagField displays tags with a background color."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con los valores de las variables locales de una interfaz cuando el usuario cierra la pantalla sin enviar?","options":["Se envían por correo","Se pierden, porque solo existen mientras la interfaz está abierta","Se convierten en variables de proceso","Se guardan automáticamente en la base de datos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las variables locales no persisten; para conservar datos hay que guardarlos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to an interface's local variable values when the user closes the screen without submitting?","options":["They're emailed","They're lost, since they only exist while the interface is open","They become process variables","They're automatically saved to the database"],"explanation":"Local variables don't persist; to keep data, save it."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario muestra campos en función de un tipo de solicitud elegido. Al cambiar de tipo, quedan valores de campos ocultos que se envían. ¿Qué buena práctica evita datos incoherentes?","options":["Limpiar los valores de los campos que se ocultan al cambiar el tipo","Eliminar showWhen","Usar refreshAlways","Enviar todos los valores y filtrarlos más tarde en el proceso con una regla"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Al ocultar campos por un cambio, conviene reiniciar sus valores para no enviar datos obsoletos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form shows fields based on a chosen request type. When the type changes, hidden fields keep values that get submitted. Which best practice avoids inconsistent data?","options":["Clear the values of fields hidden when the type changes","Remove showWhen","Use refreshAlways","Submit everything and filter later in the process with a rule"],"explanation":"When fields are hidden by a change, reset their values so stale data isn't submitted."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar las líneas de un pedido con un subtotal por línea calculado (cantidad × precio). ¿Cómo se construye la columna de subtotal en una cuadrícula editable?","options":["Un componente de solo lectura cuyo valor es la expresión sobre fv!item","Una constante","Una consulta a la base de datos por cada línea","Un campo editable donde el usuario escribe el subtotal"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El subtotal es un valor derivado que se calcula a partir de los campos de la fila.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show order lines with a per-line computed subtotal (quantity × price). How is the subtotal column built in an editable grid?","options":["A read-only component whose value is the expression over fv!item","A constant","A database query per line","An editable field where the user types the subtotal"],"explanation":"The subtotal is a derived value computed from the row's fields."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas del diseñador de interfaces ayudan a solucionar problemas? (Elige 2)","options":["El AppMarket","La vista de rendimiento","La lista de grupos del entorno","La consola de administración","Los valores de prueba de rule inputs"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Probar con distintos valores y medir el rendimiento ayuda a diagnosticar interfaces.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two interface designer tools help troubleshoot? (Choose 2)","options":["The AppMarket","The performance view","The environment's group list","The Admin Console","Rule input test values"],"explanation":"Testing with different values and measuring performance help diagnose interfaces."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz de registro de un cliente debe mostrar sus pedidos relacionados. ¿Qué enfoque aprovecha mejor los records?","options":["Una cuadrícula con el record type de pedidos filtrado por la relación con el cliente","Un desplegable con los pedidos","Un correo con los pedidos","Una consulta de todos los pedidos con a!queryEntity filtrada en la interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las relaciones de record type permiten mostrar datos relacionados de forma directa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A customer record interface must show their related orders. Which approach best leverages records?","options":["A grid with the orders record type filtered by the customer relationship","A dropdown of the orders","An email with the orders","A query of every order with a!queryEntity filtered in the interface"],"explanation":"Record type relationships allow showing related data directly."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe mostrar un aviso de confirmación antes de ejecutar una acción irreversible (p. ej. eliminar). ¿Qué configuración del botón es adecuada?","options":["Ocultar el botón","Un mensaje de confirmación en el botón","Usar un enlace de texto","Ejecutar la acción y mostrar después un mensaje para deshacerla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los botones admiten confirmaciones antes de ejecutar acciones críticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must show a confirmation prompt before an irreversible action (e.g. delete). Which button configuration fits?","options":["Hide the button","A confirmation message on the button","Use a text link","Run the action and show an undo message afterwards"],"explanation":"Buttons support confirmations before critical actions."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz muestra 2.000 filas en una cuadrícula sin paginar y el navegador se ralentiza. ¿Qué cambio es adecuado?","options":["Cambiar los colores","Usar una cuadrícula editable","Aumentar la memoria del navegador del usuario","Paginar la cuadrícula (p. ej. 25 filas por página)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La paginación limita las filas renderizadas y consultadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface shows 2,000 unpaged rows in a grid and the browser slows down. Which change fits?","options":["Change colors","Use an editable grid","Increase the user's browser memory","Page the grid (e.g. 25 rows per page)"],"explanation":"Paging limits rendered and queried rows."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe mostrar a cada usuario solo sus tareas pendientes. ¿Qué fuente de datos o componente encaja?","options":["Un desplegable con todos los procesos","Una constante","Un informe de tareas filtrado por el usuario actual","Una consulta de todas las tareas del entorno sin filtro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los informes de tareas pueden filtrarse por el usuario que los ve.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must show each user only their pending tasks. Which data source or component fits?","options":["A dropdown of every process","A constant","A task report filtered by the current user","A query of every task in the environment without a filter"],"explanation":"Task reports can be filtered by the viewing user."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas recomienda Appian sobre los textos de las interfaces? (Elige 2)","options":["Mensajes técnicos con códigos internos para el usuario final","Instrucciones o ayudas solo cuando aportan","Textos largos en cada campo","Etiquetas en mayúsculas en todos los campos","Etiquetas breves y claras"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Textos claros y ayudas oportunas mejoran la usabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices does Appian recommend for interface text? (Choose 2)","options":["Technical messages with internal codes for end users","Instructions or help only when useful","Long text on every field","All-caps labels on every field","Short, clear labels"],"explanation":"Clear text and timely help improve usability."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario debe impedir que el usuario envíe dos veces haciendo doble clic. ¿Qué comportamiento de Appian ayuda?","options":["Usar refreshAlways","Los botones de envío deshabilitan el formulario mientras se procesa","Ninguno: hay que pedir al usuario que haga un solo clic","Usar enlaces"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los botones de envío bloquean nuevas interacciones mientras se procesa el envío.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form must prevent double submission via double-click. Which Appian behavior helps?","options":["Use refreshAlways","Submit buttons disable the form while processing","None: users must be asked to click once","Use links"],"explanation":"Submit buttons block further interaction while the submission processes."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz debe mostrar distintos contenidos en pestañas. ¿Cómo se implementa habitualmente?","options":["Una variable local con la pestaña activa y enlaces o botones que la cambian","Varios process models","Un grupo por pestaña","Un sitio con una página por pestaña dentro del formulario"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un patrón común usa una variable de pestaña y showWhen o choose para mostrar el contenido.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An interface must show different content in tabs. How is this usually implemented?","options":["A local variable with the active tab and links or buttons changing it","Several process models","One group per tab","A site with one page per tab inside the form"],"explanation":"A common pattern uses a tab variable and showWhen or choose to show content."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Una interfaz de edición recibe un registro por rule input y el usuario modifica campos. Si pulsa \"Cancelar\", los cambios no deben guardarse. ¿Qué patrón ayuda?","options":["Usar una constante","Editar una copia en una variable local y guardar en el rule input solo al enviar","Editar directamente el rule input y revertir los cambios campo a campo al cancelar","Reiniciar el proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Trabajar sobre una copia local permite descartar cambios fácilmente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An edit interface receives a record via rule input and the user changes fields. If they click \"Cancel\", changes mustn't be saved. Which pattern helps?","options":["Use a constant","Edit a copy in a local variable and save to the rule input only on submit","Edit the rule input directly and revert field by field on cancel","Restart the process"],"explanation":"Working on a local copy makes discarding changes easy."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un icono de advertencia en el diseñador de interfaces junto a una expresión?","options":["Que la interfaz no se puede guardar hasta corregirlo","Un posible problema (p. ej. de rendimiento o buenas prácticas) que conviene revisar","Nada","Que la interfaz está publicada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las advertencias señalan posibles problemas sin impedir guardar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a warning icon in the interface designer next to an expression indicate?","options":["The interface can't be saved until it's fixed","A possible issue (e.g. performance or best practice) worth reviewing","Nothing","The interface is published"],"explanation":"Warnings flag possible issues without blocking save."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un componente debe deshabilitarse mientras no se haya seleccionado un cliente. ¿Qué parámetro y condición se usan?","options":["placeholder","required: a!isNullOrEmpty(local!cliente), que deshabilita el componente","showWhen: true","disabled: a!isNullOrEmpty(local!cliente)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"disabled con la condición adecuada impide la interacción mientras falta el dato.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A component must be disabled until a customer is selected. Which parameter and condition are used?","options":["placeholder","required: a!isNullOrEmpty(local!customer), which disables the component","showWhen: true","disabled: a!isNullOrEmpty(local!customer)"],"explanation":"disabled with the right condition prevents interaction while the data is missing."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un formulario muestra un mensaje de error genérico \"Error\" cuando falla la validación de un IBAN. ¿Qué mejora aplica?","options":["Mantener el mensaje genérico para no confundir al usuario con detalles","Ocultar el error","Mostrar el error solo en los logs","Un mensaje específico que explique qué está mal y cómo corregirlo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los mensajes de validación deben ser claros y accionables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A form shows a generic \"Error\" message when an IBAN validation fails. Which improvement applies?","options":["Keep the generic message so users aren't confused by details","Hide the error","Show the error only in logs","A specific message explaining what's wrong and how to fix it"],"explanation":"Validation messages should be clear and actionable."}}},{"domain":"D5","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere reutilizar en varias interfaces el mismo estilo de tarjeta de resumen con distintos datos. ¿Qué crea?","options":["Un grupo","Una constante con el código de la tarjeta","Una interfaz componente con rule inputs para los datos","Un proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las interfaces componente parametrizadas se reutilizan con distintos datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to reuse the same summary card style with different data across interfaces. What do they create?","options":["A group","A constant holding the card's code","A component interface with rule inputs for the data","A process"],"explanation":"Parameterized component interfaces are reused with different data."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo tiene una tabla de clientes existente en su base de datos y quiere crear un record type sobre ella. ¿Qué paso es el primero?","options":["Crear una tabla nueva con codeless data modeling y copiar los datos a mano","Configurar la fuente de datos del record type apuntando a esa tabla","Crear un proceso","Crear un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un record type puede usar una tabla existente como fuente de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team has an existing customers table in its database and wants a record type over it. What's the first step?","options":["Create a new table with codeless data modeling and copy the data by hand","Configure the record type's data source pointing to that table","Create a process","Create a group"],"explanation":"A record type can use an existing table as its data source."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué fuentes de datos puede usar un record type?","options":["Solo hojas de cálculo","Bases de datos, integraciones y fuentes como Salesforce","Solo procesos","Solo la base de datos interna de Appian creada con codeless data modeling"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los record types admiten diversas fuentes, incluidas bases de datos e integraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which data sources can a record type use?","options":["Only spreadsheets","Databases, integrations and sources like Salesforce","Only processes","Only Appian's internal database created with codeless data modeling"],"explanation":"Record types support various sources, including databases and integrations."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la vista de resumen (summary view) de un registro?","options":["La lista de todos los registros con columnas y filtros","Un informe de auditoría","La interfaz principal que se muestra al abrir un registro","Un proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La vista de resumen es la pantalla principal del registro individual.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a record's summary view?","options":["The list of all records with columns and filters","An audit report","The main interface shown when opening a record","A process"],"explanation":"The summary view is the main screen of an individual record."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro de Cliente necesita, además de la vista de resumen, una vista con sus pedidos y otra con sus documentos. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Vistas adicionales del record type","Tres record types distintos para el mismo cliente","Tres sitios","Tres grupos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un record type puede tener varias vistas que se muestran como pestañas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Customer record needs, besides the summary view, a view of their orders and one of their documents. What's configured?","options":["Additional record type views","Three separate record types for the same customer","Three sites","Three groups"],"explanation":"A record type can have several views shown as tabs."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se configura en la lista de registros (record list) de un record type?","options":["Los permisos de los process models","Columnas, filtros, búsqueda y acciones","La interfaz de cada registro individual","Los grupos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La lista define cómo se ven, buscan y filtran los registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's configured in a record type's record list?","options":["Process model permissions","Columns, filters, search and actions","Each individual record's interface","Groups"],"explanation":"The list defines how records are viewed, searched and filtered."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Los usuarios quieren filtrar la lista de solicitudes por estado con un desplegable. ¿Qué se configura en el record type?","options":["Una related action","Un filtro de usuario sobre el campo de estado","Un filtro por defecto que no puede cambiarse","Un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los filtros de usuario permiten a los usuarios filtrar la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Users want to filter the request list by status with a dropdown. What's configured in the record type?","options":["A related action","A user filter on the status field","A default filter that can't be changed","A group"],"explanation":"User filters let users filter the list."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"La lista de solicitudes debe mostrar por defecto solo las abiertas, sin que el usuario pueda quitar ese criterio. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Un filtro de usuario con el valor \"Abierta\" preseleccionado","Una related action","Una constante","Un filtro por defecto (default filter) en la lista"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los filtros por defecto restringen siempre la lista; los de usuario son opcionales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"The request list must show only open ones by default, without users being able to remove that criterion. What's configured?","options":["A user filter with \"Open\" preselected","A related action","A constant","A default filter on the list"],"explanation":"Default filters always restrict the list; user filters are optional."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de acción de registro se muestra en la lista para crear un nuevo registro?","options":["Un enlace dinámico","Related action, que aparece en la lista para crear registros","Record list action","Un filtro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las acciones de lista suelen usarse para crear registros nuevos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record action type shows on the list to create a new record?","options":["A dynamic link","Related action, which appears on the list to create records","Record list action","A filter"],"explanation":"List actions are typically used to create new records."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una acción \"Aprobar\" solo debe mostrarse en las solicitudes pendientes. ¿Qué se configura en la related action?","options":["Un mensaje en la interfaz que indique que no se puede aprobar si no está pendiente","Una condición de visibilidad según el estado del registro","Un filtro de usuario","Un grupo nuevo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las acciones de registro admiten condiciones de visibilidad basadas en datos y grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An \"Approve\" action must only show on pending requests. What's configured on the related action?","options":["A message in the interface saying it can't be approved unless pending","A visibility condition based on the record's status","A user filter","A new group"],"explanation":"Record actions support visibility conditions based on data and groups."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos definen una related action? (Elige 2)","options":["El color del sitio","El esquema de la base de datos","El process model que se inicia","El contexto del registro que se le pasa (p. ej. el identificador)","Una constante de entorno"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"La related action inicia un proceso pasando el contexto del registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements define a related action? (Choose 2)","options":["The site color","The database schema","The process model it starts","The record context passed to it (e.g. the identifier)","An environment constant"],"explanation":"A related action starts a process passing the record's context."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type Pedido debe relacionarse con Cliente para mostrar el nombre del cliente en la lista de pedidos. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Una related action","Un filtro de usuario","Una relación muchos a uno y una columna relacionada","Copiar el nombre del cliente en cada pedido con un proceso nocturno"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las relaciones permiten usar campos relacionados en listas, vistas y consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An Order record type must relate to Customer to show the customer's name in the order list. What's configured?","options":["A related action","A user filter","A many-to-one relationship and a related column","Copy the customer's name into each order with a nightly process"],"explanation":"Relationships allow using related fields in lists, views and queries."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un cliente tiene exactamente un perfil fiscal y cada perfil pertenece a un cliente. ¿Qué relación se configura?","options":["Uno a uno","Uno a muchos","Muchos a muchos","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Una correspondencia exacta entre dos entidades es una relación uno a uno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A customer has exactly one tax profile and each profile belongs to one customer. Which relationship is configured?","options":["One-to-one","One-to-many","Many-to-many","None"],"explanation":"An exact correspondence between two entities is one-to-one."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué campos se necesitan para definir una relación entre dos record types?","options":["Una constante","Los nombres de los dos record types únicamente","Los campos que enlazan ambos (claves)","Un grupo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La relación se define sobre los campos que unen ambos registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which fields are needed to define a relationship between two record types?","options":["A constant","Only the two record types' names","The fields linking both (keys)","A group"],"explanation":"The relationship is defined on the fields joining both records."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Con codeless data modeling, un desarrollador añade una relación uno a muchos de Cliente a Pedido. ¿Qué hace Appian?","options":["Borra los pedidos","Crea el campo de clave foránea en la tabla de pedidos","Nada","Crea una tabla intermedia nueva para la relación uno a muchos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El modelado sin código crea la estructura necesaria, como la clave foránea en el lado \"muchos\".","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"With codeless data modeling, a developer adds a one-to-many relationship from Customer to Order. What does Appian do?","options":["Deletes orders","Creates the foreign key field in the orders table","Nothing","Creates a new join table for the one-to-many relationship"],"explanation":"Codeless modeling creates the needed structure, such as the foreign key on the \"many\" side."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Los usuarios de ventas solo deben ver los clientes de su región en la lista de registros y en las consultas. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Un record type por región","Ocultar la columna región","Seguridad a nivel de registro con reglas por región","Un filtro de usuario de región que los usuarios deben aplicar"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La seguridad a nivel de registro se aplica en listas, vistas y consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Sales users should only see customers in their region in the record list and in queries. What's configured?","options":["One record type per region","Hide the region column","Record-level security with rules by region","A region user filter users must apply"],"explanation":"Record-level security applies to lists, views and queries."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Con qué frecuencia se mantienen actualizados los datos de un record type sincronizado cuando se modifican desde Appian (p. ej. con Write Records)?","options":["Se sincronizan al escribir mediante Appian","Nunca","Solo una vez al día en la sincronización programada","Solo al reiniciar"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las escrituras a través de Appian actualizan los datos sincronizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How quickly is a synced record type's data updated when modified from Appian (e.g. with Write Records)?","options":["It syncs when written through Appian","Never","Only once a day at the scheduled sync","Only on restart"],"explanation":"Writes through Appian update the synced data."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una tabla de origen recibe cambios de un sistema externo varias veces al día. ¿Qué configuración del record type sincronizado ayuda a reflejarlos?","options":["Desactivar la sincronización para leer siempre directamente","Una related action","Una sincronización programada (o disparada por un proceso)","Un filtro de usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cambios externos se recogen con sincronizaciones programadas o invocadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A source table gets changes from an external system several times a day. Which synced record type setting helps reflect them?","options":["Disable sync to always read directly","A related action","A scheduled sync (or one triggered by a process)","A user filter"],"explanation":"External changes are picked up by scheduled or triggered syncs."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos capacidades ofrecen los record types con sincronización frente a los no sincronizados? (Elige 2)","options":["Escribir directamente en el sistema de origen sin integraciones","Evitar cualquier configuración","Relaciones entre record types","Campos de registro personalizados","No necesitar fuente de datos"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"La sincronización habilita relaciones, campos personalizados y consultas rápidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two capabilities do synced record types offer over unsynced ones? (Choose 2)","options":["Writing directly to the source system without integrations","Avoiding any configuration","Relationships between record types","Custom record fields","Needing no data source"],"explanation":"Sync enables relationships, custom fields and fast queries."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro de solicitud debe mostrar en su cabecera el título \"Solicitud 1234 - Juan Pérez\". ¿Qué se configura?","options":["El nombre del record type con el número de solicitud","El título del registro con una expresión","Un grupo","Un filtro"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El título del registro admite expresiones con sus campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A request record must show \"Request 1234 - John Smith\" in its header. What's configured?","options":["The record type's name with the request number","The record title with an expression","A group","A filter"],"explanation":"The record title supports expressions with its fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué estilo de lista conviene para mostrar registros con muchas columnas comparables (p. ej. importes y fechas)?","options":["Un párrafo","Una cuadrícula (grid)","Un feed de tarjetas con texto libre","Un gráfico"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las cuadrículas facilitan comparar valores en columnas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which list style suits records with many comparable columns (e.g. amounts and dates)?","options":["A paragraph","A grid","A feed of cards with free text","A chart"],"explanation":"Grids make comparing column values easy."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que la lista de registros permita buscar por nombre de cliente. ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un filtro por defecto con el nombre de un cliente","Un grupo","La búsqueda de la lista sobre el campo de nombre","Una related action"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La lista de registros puede ofrecer un cuadro de búsqueda sobre campos configurados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants the record list to support searching by customer name. What do they configure?","options":["A default filter with one customer's name","A group","List search on the name field","A related action"],"explanation":"The record list can offer a search box over configured fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa el identificador de un registro?","options":["El usuario que lo creó","La fecha","El nombre visible del registro en la cabecera","El valor único de cada registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El identificador del registro es su clave única.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a record identifier represent?","options":["The user who created it","The date","The record's visible name in the header","Each record's unique value"],"explanation":"The record identifier is its unique key."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una related action inicia un proceso, pero el proceso no sabe sobre qué registro actuar. ¿Qué falta?","options":["Pasar el identificador del registro al parámetro del proceso","Que el proceso consulte el último registro modificado","Una constante","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las related actions deben pasar el contexto del registro a los parámetros del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A related action starts a process, but the process doesn't know which record to act on. What's missing?","options":["Passing the record identifier to the process parameter","Having the process query the most recently modified record","A constant","A group"],"explanation":"Related actions must pass the record context to the process parameters."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos se configuran en la vista de resumen de un registro? (Elige 2)","options":["La interfaz que muestra los datos del registro","La lista de todos los registros","El esquema de la base de datos","Los filtros de usuario de la lista","Las related actions destacadas"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"La vista de resumen combina la interfaz del registro y sus acciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements are configured in a record's summary view? (Choose 2)","options":["The interface showing the record's data","The list of all records","The database schema","The list's user filters","Featured related actions"],"explanation":"The summary view combines the record's interface and its actions."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type de Empleado debe mostrar un campo \"Antigüedad en años\" calculado a partir de la fecha de alta. ¿Qué capacidad encaja sin guardar el valor en la tabla?","options":["Una constante","Una columna nueva en la tabla actualizada cada día por un proceso","Un campo de registro personalizado calculado","Un filtro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los campos personalizados calculan valores a partir de otros campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An Employee record type must show a \"Years of service\" field computed from the hire date. Which capability fits without storing the value in the table?","options":["A constant","A new table column updated daily by a process","A calculated custom record field","A filter"],"explanation":"Custom fields compute values from other fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite la acción de registro configurada como \"related action\" frente a una acción de sitio?","options":["Actuar en el contexto de un registro concreto","Nada","Crear registros sin contexto desde cualquier página","Ejecutar sin process model"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las related actions se ejecutan sobre un registro y reciben su contexto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a record action configured as a \"related action\" allow compared to a site action?","options":["Acting in a specific record's context","Nothing","Creating records without context from any page","Running without a process model"],"explanation":"Related actions run on a record and receive its context."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type usa como fuente un servicio web externo sin sincronizar. ¿Qué limitación hay que tener en cuenta?","options":["Que no tiene lista de registros","Algunas capacidades requieren sincronización","Ninguna","Que no se pueden mostrar los datos en ninguna interfaz"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las capacidades avanzadas de records dependen de la sincronización de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type uses an unsynced external web service as its source. Which limitation must be considered?","options":["It has no record list","Some capabilities require sync","None","Data can't be shown in any interface"],"explanation":"Advanced record capabilities depend on data sync."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador debe decidir quién puede ver un record type en Appian (acceso al objeto). ¿Dónde lo configura?","options":["En un process model","En la seguridad del record type","En los filtros de usuario de la lista","En la vista de resumen"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad del objeto define qué grupos pueden acceder al record type.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer must decide who can see a record type in Appian (object access). Where do they configure it?","options":["In a process model","In the record type's security","In the list's user filters","In the summary view"],"explanation":"Object security defines which groups can access the record type."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una related action \"Editar\" debe mostrarse solo a los usuarios del grupo de gestores. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Una constante","Ocultar el botón en la interfaz del formulario de edición","Un filtro por defecto","La visibilidad de la acción para ese grupo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La visibilidad de las acciones puede condicionarse a grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An \"Edit\" related action must only show to users in the managers group. What's configured?","options":["A constant","Hide the button in the edit form's interface","A default filter","The action's visibility for that group"],"explanation":"Action visibility can be conditioned on groups."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una relación \"muchos a uno\" desde Pedido hacia Cliente?","options":["Cada cliente se relaciona con un solo pedido","Cada pedido tiene muchos clientes","Ninguna","Un cliente por pedido; varios pedidos por cliente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Muchos pedidos apuntan a un mismo cliente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"many-to-one\" relationship from Order to Customer mean?","options":["Each customer relates to one order only","Each order has many customers","None","One customer per order; many orders per customer"],"explanation":"Many orders point to the same customer."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro debe mostrar los eventos de su historial (creado, modificado, aprobado) sin construir una tabla de auditoría a mano. ¿Qué capacidad de records ayuda?","options":["Las vistas de lista","Una constante","Los filtros de usuario","Los eventos de registro (record events)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los record events registran acciones sobre los registros para mostrar su historial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record must show its history events (created, modified, approved) without building an audit table by hand. Which records capability helps?","options":["List views","A constant","User filters","Record events"],"explanation":"Record events log actions on records to show their history."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son necesarias para que los usuarios accedan a la lista de un record type desde un sitio? (Elige 2)","options":["Dar a sus grupos permiso de visualización sobre el record type","Crear un proceso","Hacerlos administradores del sistema","Darles acceso a Appian Designer","Añadir una página de record type al sitio"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Hace falta una página en el sitio y permisos de visualización del record type.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are needed for users to access a record type's list from a site? (Choose 2)","options":["Give their groups view permission on the record type","Create a process","Make them system administrators","Give them Appian Designer access","Add a record type page to the site"],"explanation":"A site page and view permissions on the record type are needed."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador cambia la interfaz de la vista de resumen. ¿Cuándo ven los usuarios el cambio en ese entorno?","options":["Solo tras publicar una nueva versión de un process model","Tras guardar los objetos modificados","Tras reiniciar el servidor","Nunca"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios en interfaces y record types se aplican al guardarlos en el entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer changes the summary view's interface. When do users in that environment see the change?","options":["Only after publishing a new process model version","After saving the modified objects","After restarting the server","Never"],"explanation":"Changes to interfaces and record types apply when saved in the environment."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene configurar una related action con un formulario de inicio en lugar de llevar al usuario a una tarea?","options":["Que no requiere permisos","Ninguna","Se completa desde el propio registro","Que el proceso no necesita publicarse"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El formulario de inicio permite completar la acción en el contexto del registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of configuring a related action with a start form rather than sending the user to a task?","options":["It requires no permissions","None","It's completed from the record itself","The process needn't be published"],"explanation":"The start form lets the action be completed in the record's context."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una lista de registros muestra muchas columnas y es difícil de leer. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Mostrar solo las columnas clave y dejar el detalle en la vista","Usar texto en mayúsculas","Añadir todavía más columnas para que el usuario tenga toda la información","Quitar los filtros"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las listas deben mostrar la información clave; el detalle va en las vistas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record list shows many columns and is hard to read. Which best practice applies?","options":["Show only key columns and leave detail to the view","Use all-caps text","Add even more columns so users have all the information","Remove filters"],"explanation":"Lists should show key information; detail goes in views."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type de Proyecto necesita mostrar en su vista una cuadrícula con las tareas relacionadas. ¿Cómo se filtran?","options":["Con una constante","Con la relación Proyecto-Tarea o un filtro por ID","Con un filtro por defecto del record type de tareas","Mostrando todas las tareas del sistema y pidiendo al usuario que busque"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las relaciones o filtros por identificador limitan la cuadrícula a las tareas del proyecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Project record type must show a grid of related tasks in its view. How are they filtered?","options":["With a constant","With the Project-Task relationship or an ID filter","With a default filter on the task record type","Showing every task in the system and asking the user to search"],"explanation":"Relationships or ID filters limit the grid to the project's tasks."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador elimina un campo de la tabla de origen, pero el record type aún lo tiene configurado. ¿Qué ocurrirá?","options":["Nada, Appian elimina el campo del record type automáticamente sin avisar","Se borra la tabla","Errores al sincronizar o consultar hasta actualizar el record type","Se crea el campo de nuevo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cambios de esquema deben reflejarse en el record type para evitar errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer removes a field from the source table, but the record type still has it configured. What will happen?","options":["Nothing; Appian silently removes the field from the record type","The table is deleted","Errors when syncing or querying until the record type is updated","The field is recreated"],"explanation":"Schema changes must be reflected in the record type to avoid errors."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos tipos de acciones de registro existen en Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Constant actions","Related actions","Folder actions","Record list actions","Gateway actions"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Las acciones de registro son de lista o relacionadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two record action types exist in Appian? (Choose 2)","options":["Constant actions","Related actions","Folder actions","Record list actions","Gateway actions"],"explanation":"Record actions are list actions or related actions."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una vista de registro debe mostrar datos de un sistema externo que no se pueden sincronizar. ¿Qué opción es adecuada?","options":["Copiar los datos a mano en la base de datos de Appian cada semana","Usar un filtro","Llamar a una integración desde la interfaz de la vista","Crear un grupo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las interfaces pueden mostrar datos externos mediante integraciones de consulta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record view must show data from an external system that can't be synced. Which option fits?","options":["Manually copy the data into Appian's database weekly","Use a filter","Call an integration from the view's interface","Create a group"],"explanation":"Interfaces can show external data via query integrations."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre cuando un usuario sin permiso de visualización sobre un record type intenta abrir un enlace a uno de sus registros?","options":["Se le añade al grupo","Ve una copia sin datos","No puede ver el registro","Ve el registro en modo de solo lectura"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Sin permiso sobre el record type, el registro no es accesible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens when a user without view permission on a record type opens a link to one of its records?","options":["They're added to the group","They see a copy with no data","They can't see the record","They see the record in read-only mode"],"explanation":"Without permission on the record type, the record isn't accessible."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda Appian para que las listas de registros carguen rápido con muchos datos?","options":["Usar consultas en bucle","Paginar, usar sincronización y mostrar solo columnas necesarias","Desactivar la paginación para mostrar todo de una vez","Añadir todas las columnas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Paginación, sincronización y columnas mínimas mejoran el rendimiento de las listas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does Appian recommend so record lists load fast with lots of data?","options":["Using queries in loops","Paging, using sync and showing only needed columns","Disabling paging to show everything at once","Adding every column"],"explanation":"Paging, sync and minimal columns improve list performance."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un proceso de \"Nuevo cliente\" se inicia desde la lista de clientes. Tras completarlo, el usuario debería ver el nuevo cliente en la lista. ¿Qué garantiza que aparezca?","options":["Que el proceso envíe un correo al usuario con los datos del cliente","Que se escriba con Write Records en la fuente","Un filtro de usuario","Una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Escribir en la fuente a través de Appian hace que el registro aparezca en la lista sincronizada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A \"New customer\" process starts from the customer list. After completing it, the user should see the new customer in the list. What ensures it appears?","options":["The process emailing the user the customer data","Writing it with Write Records to the source","A user filter","A constant"],"explanation":"Writing to the source via Appian makes the record appear in the synced list."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una related action debe abrir un formulario prellenado con los datos actuales del registro. ¿Cómo recibe el formulario esos datos?","options":["El formulario lee los datos de la vista de resumen abierta en el navegador","No es posible","El proceso recibe el identificador, consulta el registro y lo pasa al formulario","Con una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El proceso usa el identificador para obtener los datos y los mapea al formulario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A related action must open a form prefilled with the record's current data. How does the form receive the data?","options":["The form reads data from the summary view open in the browser","It's not possible","The process receives the identifier, queries the record and passes it to the form","With a constant"],"explanation":"The process uses the identifier to fetch the data and maps it to the form."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas facilitan el mantenimiento de un record type? (Elige 2)","options":["No documentar las relaciones","Copiar el mismo record type para cada departamento","Relaciones definidas en lugar de duplicar datos","Guardar todos los datos en un campo de texto","Nombres de campo claros y descripciones"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Claridad y relaciones bien definidas evitan duplicación y confusión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices ease record type maintenance? (Choose 2)","options":["Not documenting relationships","Copying the same record type for each department","Defined relationships instead of duplicating data","Storing all data in a text field","Clear field names and descriptions"],"explanation":"Clarity and well-defined relationships avoid duplication and confusion."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la opción de sincronización de un record type?","options":["Que se sincroniza el diseño de las interfaces","Que los datos se envían a otro entorno de Appian automáticamente","Que se sincronizan los grupos","Que Appian guarda una copia de los datos de la fuente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La sincronización almacena en Appian los datos de la fuente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a record type's sync option indicate?","options":["Interface design is synced","Data is automatically sent to another Appian environment","Groups are synced","That Appian stores a copy of the source data"],"explanation":"Sync stores source data in Appian."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type necesita mostrar en su lista el número de pedidos de cada cliente. ¿Cómo se consigue con records?","options":["Con un grupo","Con una columna que ejecuta una consulta por cada fila de la lista","Con un filtro","Con un campo personalizado de agregación sobre la relación con pedidos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las agregaciones como campos personalizados evitan consultas por fila.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type must show each customer's order count in its list. How is this done with records?","options":["With a group","With a column running one query per list row","With a filter","With an aggregation custom field over the orders relationship"],"explanation":"Aggregations as custom fields avoid per-row queries."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de relación necesita una tabla intermedia?","options":["Uno a uno","Muchos a muchos","Muchos a uno","Uno a muchos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las relaciones muchos a muchos se resuelven mediante una entidad intermedia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which relationship type needs a join table?","options":["One-to-one","Many-to-many","Many-to-one","One-to-many"],"explanation":"Many-to-many relationships are resolved via an intermediate entity."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que los usuarios de soporte vean todos los campos de un cliente salvo los datos bancarios. ¿Qué enfoque encaja?","options":["Mostrarlos solo a grupos autorizados y limitar su consulta","No mostrar nada","Crear un segundo record type con los mismos datos sin los campos bancarios","Ocultar el campo con un color blanco"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La visibilidad por grupo y el control de acceso a los datos protegen campos sensibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants support users to see all customer fields except banking details. Which approach fits?","options":["Show them only to authorized groups and restrict querying","Show nothing","Create a second record type with the same data minus banking fields","Hide the field with white text"],"explanation":"Group-based visibility and data access control protect sensitive fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type se usa en una página de sitio. Los usuarios piden ver primero las solicitudes más recientes. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Una related action","El orden por defecto de la lista por fecha descendente","Un filtro por defecto por fecha de hoy","Un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La lista admite un orden por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record type is used on a site page. Users want to see the most recent requests first. What's configured?","options":["A related action","The list's default sort by date descending","A default filter on today's date","A group"],"explanation":"The list supports a default sort."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos aporta un record type a una aplicación frente a una simple consulta en una interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["Que sustituye a los procesos","Relaciones y seguridad a nivel de registro","Que no necesita datos","Que elimina la necesidad de interfaces","Una lista, vistas y acciones reutilizables para la entidad"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Los records ofrecen una experiencia completa y reutilizable de la entidad, con relaciones y seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things does a record type bring to an application compared to a plain query in an interface? (Choose 2)","options":["It replaces processes","Relationships and record-level security","It needs no data","It removes the need for interfaces","A reusable list, views and actions for the entity"],"explanation":"Records provide a complete, reusable entity experience with relationships and security."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un nuevo campo \"Prioridad\" se añade con codeless data modeling a un record type existente. ¿Qué ocurre con la tabla?","options":["Appian añade la columna a la tabla que gestiona","Nada","Se crea una tabla nueva","Hay que crear la columna a mano en la base de datos externa"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Con el modelado sin código, Appian gestiona la estructura de las tablas que crea.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A new \"Priority\" field is added via codeless data modeling to an existing record type. What happens to the table?","options":["Appian adds the column to the table it manages","Nothing","A new table is created","The column must be created by hand in the external database"],"explanation":"With codeless modeling, Appian manages the structure of tables it creates."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un usuario abre un registro y la vista de resumen tarda mucho en cargar porque consulta 10 fuentes distintas. ¿Qué mejora es adecuada?","options":["Añadir más consultas para mostrar información adicional","Usar refreshAlways","Quitar la paginación","Lo esencial en la vista principal; el resto en otras vistas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Repartir el contenido en varias vistas reduce la carga de la vista principal.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A user opens a record and the summary view is slow because it queries 10 different sources. Which improvement fits?","options":["Add more queries to show extra information","Use refreshAlways","Remove paging","Essentials in the main view; the rest in other views"],"explanation":"Spreading content across views reduces the main view's load."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos configuraciones de un record type afectan a qué datos ve un usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["El título del registro","Seguridad a nivel de registro","El icono","Filtros por defecto de la lista","El color de la cabecera"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"La seguridad de registros y los filtros por defecto limitan los datos visibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two record type settings affect what data a user sees? (Choose 2)","options":["Record title","Record-level security","Icon","The list's default filters","Header color"],"explanation":"Record security and default filters limit visible data."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere probar las reglas de seguridad a nivel de registro antes de desplegar. ¿Qué prueba es adecuada?","options":["Probar solo con un administrador del sistema","Probar en producción","No probar","Entrar con usuarios de cada grupo y revisar lo que ven"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas de seguridad se verifican con usuarios que representen cada perfil.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to test record-level security rules before deploying. Which test fits?","options":["Test only with a system administrator","Test in production","Don't test","Log in as users from each group and check what they see"],"explanation":"Security rules are verified with users representing each profile."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Una relación entre record types está configurada con campos de distinto tipo (texto e entero). ¿Qué problema puede aparecer?","options":["Se duplican los datos","La relación no se puede crear o no devuelve resultados correctos","Ninguno, Appian convierte los tipos automáticamente en todos los casos","Se borran los registros"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los campos de una relación deben tener tipos compatibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A relationship between record types is configured with fields of different types (text and integer). What problem can arise?","options":["Data is duplicated","The relationship can't be created or doesn't return correct results","None; Appian converts types automatically in every case","Records are deleted"],"explanation":"Relationship fields must have compatible types."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas aporta usar records como fuente de datos en cuadrículas y gráficos? (Elige 2)","options":["Eliminar la base de datos","Uso de campos relacionados y agregaciones","Paginación y ordenación integradas","No necesitar seguridad","No necesitar interfaces"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Los records integran paginación, ordenación, campos relacionados y agregaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages come from using records as the data source in grids and charts? (Choose 2)","options":["Removing the database","Use of related fields and aggregations","Built-in paging and sorting","No need for security","No need for interfaces"],"explanation":"Records integrate paging, sorting, related fields and aggregations."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo crea un record type nuevo sin base de datos existente y no quiere escribir SQL. ¿Qué opción usa?","options":["Codeless data modeling para crear las tablas desde el record type","Crear las tablas a mano en una base de datos externa con un cliente SQL","Usar un CDT sin data store","No usar records"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El modelado sin código crea las tablas desde Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team creates a new record type with no existing database and doesn't want to write SQL. Which option does it use?","options":["Codeless data modeling to create tables from the record type","Create tables by hand in an external database with a SQL client","Use a CDT without a data store","Don't use records"],"explanation":"Codeless modeling creates tables from Appian."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro debe ofrecer una acción \"Descargar contrato\" que genera un PDF con sus datos. ¿Qué combinación es adecuada?","options":["Una related action con un proceso que genera el documento","Una columna de la lista","Un filtro de usuario que genera el PDF al aplicarse","Una constante"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las related actions inician procesos que pueden generar documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record must offer a \"Download contract\" action that generates a PDF with its data. Which combination fits?","options":["A related action with a process generating the document","A list column","A user filter that generates the PDF when applied","A constant"],"explanation":"Related actions start processes that can generate documents."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere mostrar en la lista de pedidos solo los del año actual de forma permanente para todos los usuarios. ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un grupo","Un filtro por defecto con la condición del año actual","Una related action","Un filtro de usuario sobre el año"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un filtro por defecto restringe siempre la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants the orders list to permanently show only current-year orders for every user. What do they configure?","options":["A group","A default filter with the current-year condition","A related action","A user filter on year"],"explanation":"A default filter always restricts the list."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos son necesarios para que una related action funcione para un usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["Que tenga acceso a Appian Designer","Que conozca el SQL","Que sea administrador del sistema","Que tenga permiso para iniciar el process model","Que vea la acción (visibilidad)"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"El usuario debe ver la acción y poder iniciar el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things are needed for a related action to work for a user? (Choose 2)","options":["That they have Appian Designer access","That they know SQL","That they're a system administrator","That they have permission to start the process model","That they can see the action (visibility)"],"explanation":"The user must see the action and be able to start the process."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type de Cliente tiene una relación con Pedido. Una consulta debe devolver los clientes con al menos un pedido este mes. ¿Qué capacidad de records ayuda?","options":["Filtrar por campos del registro relacionado en la consulta","Un grupo","Una constante","Consultar todos los clientes y luego todos los pedidos por separado y cruzarlos en la interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las relaciones permiten filtrar por campos de registros relacionados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Customer record type is related to Order. A query must return customers with at least one order this month. Which records capability helps?","options":["Filtering on related record fields in the query","A group","A constant","Querying all customers and all orders separately and matching in the interface"],"explanation":"Relationships allow filtering on related record fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un record type de Contrato debe mostrar en la lista un indicador \"Vence pronto\" para los contratos que caducan en menos de 30 días. ¿Qué capacidad encaja sin cambiar la tabla?","options":["Un filtro de usuario","Un campo personalizado calculado con la condición de fecha","Una columna nueva en la tabla actualizada cada noche por un proceso","Un grupo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los campos personalizados calculados derivan valores de otros campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Contract record type must show a \"Expiring soon\" indicator in the list for contracts expiring within 30 days. Which capability fits without changing the table?","options":["A user filter","A calculated custom field with the date condition","A new table column updated nightly by a process","A group"],"explanation":"Calculated custom fields derive values from other fields."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene definir al configurar las columnas de la lista de un record type? (Elige 2)","options":["Si las columnas permiten ordenar","Las contraseñas de los usuarios","Qué campos se muestran","El esquema de la base de datos","Los permisos de los process models"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Las columnas definen qué se muestra y cómo se ordena.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should be defined when configuring a record type's list columns? (Choose 2)","options":["Whether columns are sortable","User passwords","Which fields are shown","The database schema","Process model permissions"],"explanation":"Columns define what's shown and how it's sorted."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere que una vista de registro solo la vean los gestores. ¿Qué configura?","options":["Un proceso","Un filtro por defecto","La visibilidad de esa vista para el grupo de gestores","Una validación en la interfaz de la vista que muestre un error a los demás"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las vistas de registro admiten condiciones de visibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants a record view visible only to managers. What do they configure?","options":["A process","A default filter","That view's visibility for the managers group","A validation in the view's interface showing an error to others"],"explanation":"Record views support visibility conditions."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro se abre desde la lista y el usuario quiere volver a la lista con los mismos filtros. ¿Qué ventaja ofrece usar la lista de registros estándar?","options":["Navegación integrada entre lista y registro","Ninguna","Que no necesita permisos","Que los filtros se guardan en la base de datos de la aplicación"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La experiencia de records integra la navegación entre lista y vistas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record is opened from the list and the user wants to return to the list with the same filters. What advantage does the standard record list offer?","options":["Built-in navigation between list and record","None","No permissions needed","Filters being saved to the application's database"],"explanation":"The records experience integrates navigation between list and views."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve la expresión sum({4, 6, 10})?","options":["{4, 6, 10}","3","20","10"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"sum suma los elementos de la lista: 4 + 6 + 10 = 20.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the expression sum({4, 6, 10}) return?","options":["{4, 6, 10}","3","20","10"],"explanation":"sum adds the list items: 4 + 6 + 10 = 20."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve if(ri!importe > 1000, \"Alta\", \"Normal\") cuando ri!importe es 500?","options":["Un error","null","\"Normal\"","\"Alta\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La condición es falsa, así que devuelve el tercer argumento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does if(ri!amount > 1000, \"High\", \"Normal\") return when ri!amount is 500?","options":["An error","null","\"Normal\"","\"High\""],"explanation":"The condition is false, so it returns the third argument."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({\"rojo\", \"verde\", \"azul\"}, 2, null)?","options":["\"azul\"","2","\"rojo\"","\"verde\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"En Appian los índices empiezan en 1: el segundo elemento es \"verde\".","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\"}, 2, null) return?","options":["\"blue\"","2","\"red\"","\"green\""],"explanation":"Appian indexes start at 1: the second item is \"green\"."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * 10)?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","10","60","{10, 20, 30}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!forEach aplica la expresión a cada elemento y devuelve una lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * 10) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","10","60","{10, 20, 30}"],"explanation":"a!forEach applies the expression to each item and returns a list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve length({\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"})?","options":["1","\"abcd\"","4","3"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"length devuelve el número de elementos de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does length({\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}) return?","options":["1","\"abcd\"","4","3"],"explanation":"length returns the number of list items."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve wherecontains(\"b\", {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"b\"})?","options":["{2, 4}","{\"b\", \"b\"}","2","true"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"wherecontains devuelve los índices donde aparece el valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does wherecontains(\"b\", {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"b\"}) return?","options":["{2, 4}","{\"b\", \"b\"}","2","true"],"explanation":"wherecontains returns the indexes where the value appears."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve joinarray({\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}, \", \")?","options":["\"Ana, Luis, Eva\"","\"AnaLuisEva\"","{\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}","3"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"joinarray une los elementos con el separador indicado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does joinarray({\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}, \", \") return?","options":["\"Ana, Luis, Eva\"","\"AnaLuisEva\"","{\"Ana\", \"Luis\", \"Eva\"}","3"],"explanation":"joinarray joins items with the given separator."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve append({1, 2}, 3)?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{3, 1, 2}","6","{1, 2}"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"append añade el valor al final de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does append({1, 2}, 3) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{3, 1, 2}","6","{1, 2}"],"explanation":"append adds the value at the end of the list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve \"Hola \" & \"mundo\" en una expresión de Appian?","options":["{\"Hola \", \"mundo\"}","\"Hola mundo\"","true","Un error, porque & solo sirve para valores booleanos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El operador & concatena textos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does \"Hello \" & \"world\" return in an Appian expression?","options":["{\"Hello \", \"world\"}","\"Hello world\"","true","An error, because & only works with booleans"],"explanation":"The & operator concatenates text."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve and(true, false)?","options":["null","Un error","false","true"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"and devuelve true solo si todos los argumentos son verdaderos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does and(true, false) return?","options":["null","An error","false","true"],"explanation":"and returns true only if every argument is true."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve or(false, true, false)?","options":["{false, true, false}","true","null","false"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"or devuelve true si al menos un argumento es verdadero.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does or(false, true, false) return?","options":["{false, true, false}","true","null","false"],"explanation":"or returns true if at least one argument is true."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve max({7, 3, 12, 5})?","options":["27","3","4","12"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"max devuelve el valor más alto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does max({7, 3, 12, 5}) return?","options":["27","3","4","12"],"explanation":"max returns the highest value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve contains({10, 20, 30}, 20)?","options":["false","true","2","20"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"contains indica si el valor está en la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does contains({10, 20, 30}, 20) return?","options":["false","true","2","20"],"explanation":"contains indicates whether the value is in the list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!match(value: \"B\", equals: \"A\", then: 1, equals: \"B\", then: 2, default: 0)?","options":["1","0","2","\"B\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!match devuelve el then del primer caso que coincide.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!match(value: \"B\", equals: \"A\", then: 1, equals: \"B\", then: 2, default: 0) return?","options":["1","0","2","\"B\""],"explanation":"a!match returns the then of the first matching case."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!isNullOrEmpty({})?","options":["null","0","true","false"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Una lista vacía se considera vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!isNullOrEmpty({}) return?","options":["null","0","true","false"],"explanation":"An empty list counts as empty."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!defaultValue(null, \"Sin asignar\")?","options":["\"Sin asignar\"","true","Un error","null"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!defaultValue devuelve el primer valor no nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!defaultValue(null, \"Unassigned\") return?","options":["\"Unassigned\"","true","An error","null"],"explanation":"a!defaultValue returns the first non-null value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve left(\"Appian\", 3)?","options":["3","\"Appian\"","\"ian\"","\"App\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"left devuelve los primeros caracteres indicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does left(\"Appian\", 3) return?","options":["3","\"Appian\"","\"ian\"","\"App\""],"explanation":"left returns the first given characters."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve round(3.456, 2)?","options":["3","3.46","3.45","3.5"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"round redondea al número de decimales indicado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does round(3.456, 2) return?","options":["3","3.46","3.45","3.5"],"explanation":"round rounds to the given number of decimals."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve mod(10, 3)?","options":["1","0","3.33","3"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"mod devuelve el resto de la división.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does mod(10, 3) return?","options":["1","0","3.33","3"],"explanation":"mod returns the division remainder."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve upper(\"appian\")?","options":["\"Appian\"","6","\"APPIAN\"","\"appian\""],"correct":[2],"explanation":"upper convierte el texto a mayúsculas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does upper(\"appian\") return?","options":["\"Appian\"","6","\"APPIAN\"","\"appian\""],"explanation":"upper converts text to uppercase."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve difference({1, 2, 3, 4}, {2, 4})?","options":["2","{2, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"difference devuelve los elementos de la primera lista que no están en la segunda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does difference({1, 2, 3, 4}, {2, 4}) return?","options":["2","{2, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}"],"explanation":"difference returns items of the first list not in the second."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve union({1, 2}, {2, 3})?","options":["{1, 2, 2, 3}","{2}","5","{1, 2, 3}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"union combina las listas sin duplicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does union({1, 2}, {2, 3}) return?","options":["{1, 2, 2, 3}","{2}","5","{1, 2, 3}"],"explanation":"union combines lists without duplicates."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla recibe ri!lista = {5, 8, 2} y devuelve a!forEach(items: ri!lista, expression: fv!index). ¿Qué devuelve?","options":["{5, 8, 2}","{1, 2, 3}","15","3"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"fv!index es la posición de cada elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule receives ri!list = {5, 8, 2} and returns a!forEach(items: ri!list, expression: fv!index). What does it return?","options":["{5, 8, 2}","{1, 2, 3}","15","3"],"explanation":"fv!index is each item's position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\"}, expression: upper(fv!item) & fv!index)?","options":["{\"a1\", \"b2\"}","{\"A1\", \"B2\"}","{\"A\", \"B\"}","\"AB12\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Para cada elemento, concatena su mayúscula con su posición.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\"}, expression: upper(fv!item) & fv!index) return?","options":["{\"a1\", \"b2\"}","{\"A1\", \"B2\"}","{\"A\", \"B\"}","\"AB12\""],"explanation":"For each item, it concatenates its uppercase with its position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla devuelve if(a!isNullOrEmpty(ri!nombre), \"Anónimo\", ri!nombre). ¿Cuál es su propósito?","options":["Devolver el nombre o \"Anónimo\" si está vacío","Validar que el nombre tiene un formato correcto","Guardar el nombre en la base de datos","Convertir el nombre a mayúsculas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Proporciona un valor por defecto cuando la entrada está vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule returns if(a!isNullOrEmpty(ri!name), \"Anonymous\", ri!name). What's its purpose?","options":["Return the name, or \"Anonymous\" if empty","Validate the name's format","Save the name to the database","Convert the name to uppercase"],"explanation":"It provides a default when the input is empty."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!localVariables(local!a: 2, local!b: 3, local!a * local!b)?","options":["23","6","{2, 3}","5"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Declara dos variables locales y devuelve su producto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!localVariables(local!a: 2, local!b: 3, local!a * local!b) return?","options":["23","6","{2, 3}","5"],"explanation":"It declares two local variables and returns their product."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve {1, 2, 3} + 1 en Appian?","options":["7","Un error","{2, 3, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 1}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las operaciones aritméticas con listas se aplican elemento a elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does {1, 2, 3} + 1 return in Appian?","options":["7","An error","{2, 3, 4}","{1, 2, 3, 1}"],"explanation":"Arithmetic with lists applies element by element."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe devolver el nombre completo a partir de nombre y apellidos. ¿Qué implementación es adecuada?","options":["Una constante con el nombre completo de cada usuario","Rule inputs nombre y apellidos y la expresión ri!nombre & \" \" & ri!apellidos","Una consulta a la base de datos por cada llamada","Un process model"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Una regla sencilla con rule inputs concatena los valores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must return a full name from first name and last name. Which implementation fits?","options":["A constant with each user's full name","Rule inputs firstName and lastName with ri!firstName & \" \" & ri!lastName","A database query on every call","A process model"],"explanation":"A simple rule with rule inputs concatenates the values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve isnull(null)?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"isnull indica si el valor es nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does isnull(null) return?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"explanation":"isnull indicates whether the value is null."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve text(7, \"00\")?","options":["\"7.00\"","\"07\"","7","\"00\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"text aplica el formato indicado; \"00\" rellena con ceros a dos dígitos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does text(7, \"00\") return?","options":["\"7.00\"","\"07\"","7","\"00\""],"explanation":"text applies the given format; \"00\" zero-pads to two digits."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve len(\"Appian\")?","options":["1","6","5","\"Appian\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"len devuelve la longitud de un texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does len(\"Appian\") return?","options":["1","6","5","\"Appian\""],"explanation":"len returns a text's length."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve reverse({1, 2, 3})?","options":["{3, 2, 1}","{1, 2, 3}","3","6"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"reverse invierte el orden de la lista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does reverse({1, 2, 3}) return?","options":["{3, 2, 1}","{1, 2, 3}","3","6"],"explanation":"reverse inverts the list's order."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión usa ri!fecha y devuelve ri!fecha + 30. ¿Qué devuelve si ri!fecha es 1 de enero de 2026?","options":["Un error, porque no se pueden sumar números a fechas","1 de febrero de 2026","31 de enero de 2026","30"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Sumar un entero a una fecha añade días.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule uses ri!date and returns ri!date + 30. What does it return if ri!date is January 1, 2026?","options":["An error, because numbers can't be added to dates","February 1, 2026","January 31, 2026","30"],"explanation":"Adding an integer to a date adds days."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {}, expression: fv!item + 1)?","options":["Una lista vacía","{1}","1","null con un error de ejecución"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Con una lista vacía, a!forEach no evalúa la expresión y devuelve una lista vacía.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {}, expression: fv!item + 1) return?","options":["An empty list","{1}","1","null with a runtime error"],"explanation":"With an empty list, a!forEach doesn't evaluate the expression and returns an empty list."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve where({true, false, true})?","options":["{2}","{1, 3}","2","{true, true}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"where devuelve los índices de los valores verdaderos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does where({true, false, true}) return?","options":["{2}","{1, 3}","2","{true, true}"],"explanation":"where returns the indexes of true values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({10, 20, 30}, {1, 3}, null)?","options":["{10, 30}","10","{1, 3}","40"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"index admite varios índices y devuelve los elementos correspondientes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({10, 20, 30}, {1, 3}, null) return?","options":["{10, 30}","10","{1, 3}","40"],"explanation":"index accepts several indexes and returns the matching items."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve index({\"a\", \"b\"}, 5, \"ninguno\")?","options":["\"ninguno\"","\"b\"","null","Un error"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Si el índice no existe, index devuelve el valor por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index({\"a\", \"b\"}, 5, \"none\") return?","options":["\"none\"","\"b\"","null","An error"],"explanation":"If the index doesn't exist, index returns the default."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve not(true)?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"not invierte un valor booleano.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does not(true) return?","options":["false","0","true","null"],"explanation":"not inverts a boolean."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador ve en una regla el valor 0.21 escrito directamente en cinco cálculos de IVA. ¿Qué mejora recomienda Appian?","options":["Pedir el valor al usuario cada vez","Escribirlo como texto","Definir el tipo de IVA en una constante y referenciarla","Mantener el número en cada cálculo para que sea más legible"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Evitar valores codificados: las constantes centralizan los valores reutilizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer sees the value 0.21 hard-coded in five VAT calculations in a rule. Which improvement does Appian recommend?","options":["Ask the user for the value every time","Write it as text","Define the VAT rate in a constant and reference it","Keep the number in each calculation so it's more readable"],"explanation":"Avoid hard-coded values: constants centralize reused values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirven los casos de prueba (test cases) de una regla de expresión?","options":["Documentar quién creó la regla","Ejecutar la regla en producción con datos reales cada noche","Mejorar su rendimiento","Guardar entradas y salidas esperadas para comprobar la regla tras cambios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los test cases verifican que la regla devuelve lo esperado y detectan regresiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are an expression rule's test cases for?","options":["Documenting who created the rule","Running the rule in production with real data every night","Improving its performance","Storing inputs and expected outputs to check the rule after changes"],"explanation":"Test cases verify the rule returns what's expected and catch regressions."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador cambia una regla usada en 20 objetos. ¿Qué práctica reduce el riesgo de romper algo?","options":["Ejecutar sus casos de prueba y revisar los objetos dependientes","Copiar la regla con otro nombre para cada objeto","No cambiarla nunca","Desplegarla directamente y revisar los errores de los usuarios después"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los test cases y el análisis de dependencias detectan impactos antes de desplegar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer changes a rule used by 20 objects. Which practice reduces the risk of breaking something?","options":["Run its test cases and review dependent objects","Copy the rule under a new name for each object","Never change it","Deploy it directly and review user errors afterwards"],"explanation":"Test cases and dependency analysis catch impact before deployment."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un caso de prueba de una regla tiene entradas definidas, pero no se ha indicado qué debe devolver. ¿Qué se recomienda añadir?","options":["Más rule inputs","Un comentario con el nombre del autor","Una aserción o resultado esperado","Una constante"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las aserciones permiten que el caso de prueba indique si pasa o falla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule's test case has defined inputs but no expected result. What's recommended to add?","options":["More rule inputs","A comment with the author's name","An assertion or expected result","A constant"],"explanation":"Assertions let the test case show whether it passes or fails."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos casos conviene cubrir con test cases en una regla que calcula descuentos? (Elige 2)","options":["Casos límite y entradas nulas","Ningún caso","Solo valores inventados al azar sin resultado esperado","Valores típicos","Solo el caso más frecuente"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Los test cases deben cubrir lo habitual, los límites y las entradas vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two kinds of cases should test cases cover for a discount rule? (Choose 2)","options":["Edge cases and null inputs","No cases","Only random values without expected results","Typical values","Only the most frequent case"],"explanation":"Test cases should cover the typical, the edges and empty inputs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de dato conviene asignar a los rule inputs de una regla?","options":["El tipo concreto esperado (p. ej. Integer, Date, un record type)","Any Type siempre, para que la regla acepte cualquier valor","No asignar tipo","Text siempre"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los tipos concretos evitan errores y documentan la regla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What data type should a rule's rule inputs have?","options":["The specific expected type (e.g. Integer, Date, a record type)","Always Any Type, so the rule accepts any value","No type","Always Text"],"explanation":"Specific types prevent errors and document the rule."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión tiene 300 líneas que mezclan consultas, cálculos y formato de texto. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Copiarla a cada interfaz","Convertirla en un process model","Añadir comentarios y dejar toda la lógica en la misma regla","Dividirla en reglas más pequeñas con una responsabilidad cada una"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Reglas pequeñas y enfocadas son más fáciles de probar, reutilizar y mantener.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule has 300 lines mixing queries, calculations and text formatting. Which best practice applies?","options":["Copy it into each interface","Turn it into a process model","Add comments and keep all the logic in one rule","Split it into smaller rules with one responsibility each"],"explanation":"Small, focused rules are easier to test, reuse and maintain."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar a!localVariables dentro de una regla que calcula el mismo valor intermedio varias veces?","options":["Ninguna","Exponer el valor a todas las interfaces","Guardar el valor en la base de datos para otras reglas","Calcularlo una vez y reutilizarlo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las variables locales evitan recalcular expresiones y mejoran la legibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of using a!localVariables in a rule that computes the same intermediate value several times?","options":["None","Exposing the value to every interface","Saving the value to the database for other rules","Computing it once and reusing it"],"explanation":"Local variables avoid recomputation and improve readability."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {3, 4}, expression: if(fv!item > 3, \"alto\", \"bajo\"))?","options":["\"alto\"","{3, 4}","{\"bajo\", \"alto\"}","{\"alto\", \"bajo\"}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"3 no es mayor que 3 (\"bajo\"); 4 sí (\"alto\").","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {3, 4}, expression: if(fv!item > 3, \"high\", \"low\")) return?","options":["\"high\"","{3, 4}","{\"low\", \"high\"}","{\"high\", \"low\"}"],"explanation":"3 isn't greater than 3 (\"low\"); 4 is (\"high\")."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve sum(a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * fv!item))?","options":["36","{1, 4, 9}","14","6"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cuadrados son 1, 4 y 9; su suma es 14.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does sum(a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item * fv!item)) return?","options":["36","{1, 4, 9}","14","6"],"explanation":"The squares are 1, 4 and 9; their sum is 14."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla recibe una lista de pedidos (record type) y debe devolver solo los importes. ¿Qué expresión es adecuada?","options":["Acceder al campo importe de la lista (p. ej. ri!pedidos[recordType!Pedido.fields.importe])","Una consulta a la base de datos por cada pedido","Una constante","joinarray de los pedidos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Acceder a un campo de una lista devuelve la lista de valores de ese campo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule receives a list of orders (record type) and must return just the amounts. Which expression fits?","options":["Access the amount field of the list (e.g. ri!orders[recordType!Order.fields.amount])","A database query per order","A constant","joinarray of the orders"],"explanation":"Accessing a field of a list returns the list of that field's values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve month(date(2026, 3, 15))?","options":["15","3","2026","\"marzo\""],"correct":[1],"explanation":"month devuelve el número de mes de la fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does month(date(2026, 3, 15)) return?","options":["15","3","2026","\"March\""],"explanation":"month returns the date's month number."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve now() frente a today()?","options":["Ninguna devuelve fecha","now() devuelve fecha y hora; today() solo la fecha","today() devuelve fecha y hora; now() solo la hora","Son idénticas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"now() es un Date and Time; today() es un Date.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does now() return compared to today()?","options":["Neither returns a date","now() returns date and time; today() only the date","today() returns date and time; now() only the time","They're identical"],"explanation":"now() is a Date and Time; today() is a Date."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe indicar si un usuario pertenece a un grupo para usarla en showWhen de varias interfaces. ¿Qué buena práctica aplica?","options":["Encapsular la comprobación en una regla reutilizable con el grupo como constante","Crear un proceso","No reutilizar","Escribir el ID del grupo en cada interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Reglas reutilizables y constantes evitan duplicar lógica y valores codificados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must indicate whether a user belongs to a group, for use in showWhen across several interfaces. Which best practice applies?","options":["Encapsulate the check in a reusable rule with the group as a constant","Create a process","Don't reuse","Write the group ID in each interface"],"explanation":"Reusable rules and constants avoid duplicate logic and hard-coded values."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla devuelve un error cuando ri!lista es nula y se intenta acceder a su primer elemento. ¿Qué corrección es adecuada?","options":["Exigir que ri!lista nunca sea nula en ningún objeto que la llame","Eliminar el rule input","Usar refreshAlways","Usar index con valor por defecto o comprobar si es nula antes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas robustas gestionan entradas nulas o vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule errors when ri!list is null and it tries to access the first item. Which fix fits?","options":["Require ri!list never to be null in any calling object","Remove the rule input","Use refreshAlways","Use index with a default or check for null first"],"explanation":"Robust rules handle null or empty inputs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3, 4}, expression: if(mod(fv!item, 2) = 0, fv!item, {}))?","options":["6","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}","{2, 4}"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Devolver una lista vacía para un elemento lo omite; quedan los pares.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3, 4}, expression: if(mod(fv!item, 2) = 0, fv!item, {})) return?","options":["6","{1, 2, 3, 4}","{1, 3}","{2, 4}"],"explanation":"Returning an empty list for an item drops it; the even ones remain."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"}, expression: fv!isLast)?","options":["{true, false, false}","{false, false, true}","3","true"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"fv!isLast es verdadero solo en el último elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"}, expression: fv!isLast) return?","options":["{true, false, false}","{false, false, true}","3","true"],"explanation":"fv!isLast is true only on the last item."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve concat(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\")?","options":["\"A B C\"","{\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"}","3","\"ABC\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"concat une los textos sin separador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does concat(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\") return?","options":["\"A B C\"","{\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"}","3","\"ABC\""],"explanation":"concat joins texts without a separator."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve sum({1, 2}, {3})?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{4, 2}","6","3"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"sum suma todos los valores de sus argumentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does sum({1, 2}, {3}) return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","{4, 2}","6","3"],"explanation":"sum adds all values of its arguments."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla calcula una fecha de vencimiento sumando días laborables. ¿Qué función de Appian es útil?","options":["workday","now","today, que también salta fines de semana","len"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"workday suma días laborables a una fecha según el calendario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule computes a due date by adding business days. Which Appian function helps?","options":["workday","now","today, which also skips weekends","len"],"explanation":"workday adds business days to a date per the calendar."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos buenas prácticas recomienda Appian para las reglas de expresión? (Elige 2)","options":["Gestionar entradas nulas","Descripción clara y rule inputs con nombres significativos","Reglas enormes con todo dentro","Valores codificados repetidos","Nombres genéricos como \"regla1\""],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Documentar, nombrar bien y gestionar nulos hacen las reglas robustas y mantenibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two best practices does Appian recommend for expression rules? (Choose 2)","options":["Handling null inputs","Clear description and meaningful rule input names","Huge rules containing everything","Repeated hard-coded values","Generic names like \"rule1\""],"explanation":"Documenting, naming well and handling nulls make rules robust and maintainable."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve if(isnull(ri!x), 0, ri!x * 2) cuando ri!x es 4?","options":["4","8","null","0"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"ri!x no es nulo, así que devuelve 4 × 2.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does if(isnull(ri!x), 0, ri!x * 2) return when ri!x is 4?","options":["4","8","null","0"],"explanation":"ri!x isn't null, so it returns 4 × 2."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve insert({\"a\", \"c\"}, \"b\", 2)?","options":["{\"a\", \"c\", \"b\"}","\"abc\"","{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}","{\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"}"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"insert coloca el valor en la posición indicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does insert({\"a\", \"c\"}, \"b\", 2) return?","options":["{\"a\", \"c\", \"b\"}","\"abc\"","{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}","{\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"}"],"explanation":"insert places the value at the given position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve remove({10, 20, 30}, 2)?","options":["{30}","{10, 30}","{20}","{10, 20}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"remove elimina el elemento en la posición indicada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does remove({10, 20, 30}, 2) return?","options":["{30}","{10, 30}","{20}","{10, 20}"],"explanation":"remove deletes the item at the given position."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla de expresión consulta datos con a!queryRecordType y se llama desde una interfaz en cada fila de una cuadrícula. ¿Qué riesgo tiene?","options":["Que se borra la cuadrícula","Una consulta por fila, con impacto en rendimiento","Ninguno, porque las reglas se ejecutan en paralelo sin coste","Que no devuelve datos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Llamar a reglas con consultas en cada fila multiplica las consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An expression rule queries data with a!queryRecordType and is called from an interface on every grid row. What's the risk?","options":["The grid is deleted","One query per row, hurting performance","None, since rules run in parallel at no cost","It returns no data"],"explanation":"Calling query rules on every row multiplies queries."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve displayvalue(2, {1, 2, 3}, {\"Bajo\", \"Medio\", \"Alto\"}, \"N/A\")?","options":["2","\"N/A\"","\"Bajo\"","\"Medio\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"displayvalue busca el valor en la primera lista y devuelve el correspondiente de la segunda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does displayvalue(2, {1, 2, 3}, {\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\"}, \"N/A\") return?","options":["2","\"N/A\"","\"Low\"","\"Medium\""],"explanation":"displayvalue finds the value in the first list and returns the matching one from the second."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {2, 3}, expression: a!localVariables(local!doble: fv!item * 2, local!doble + 1))?","options":["{3, 4}","{5, 7}","12","{4, 6}"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Para 2: 4 + 1 = 5; para 3: 6 + 1 = 7.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {2, 3}, expression: a!localVariables(local!double: fv!item * 2, local!double + 1)) return?","options":["{3, 4}","{5, 7}","12","{4, 6}"],"explanation":"For 2: 4 + 1 = 5; for 3: 6 + 1 = 7."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere interpretar qué hace una regla heredada sin documentación. ¿Qué es lo más útil?","options":["Desplegarla en producción para ver cómo se comporta con usuarios","Probarla con distintas entradas en el editor y revisar sus casos de prueba","Preguntar en el AppMarket","Borrarla y reescribirla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Probar entradas y revisar test cases ayuda a entender el comportamiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants to understand what an undocumented legacy rule does. What's most useful?","options":["Deploy it to production to see how it behaves with users","Test it with various inputs in the editor and review its test cases","Ask in the AppMarket","Delete and rewrite it"],"explanation":"Testing inputs and reviewing test cases help understand behavior."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve tointeger(\"42\") + 1?","options":["\"421\"","Un error","42","43"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"tointeger convierte el texto a entero; luego se suma 1.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does tointeger(\"42\") + 1 return?","options":["\"421\"","An error","42","43"],"explanation":"tointeger converts text to an integer; then 1 is added."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item)[2]?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","2","3","1"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El resultado es la lista {1, 2, 3}; el índice 2 devuelve 2.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {1, 2, 3}, expression: fv!item)[2] return?","options":["{1, 2, 3}","2","3","1"],"explanation":"The result is the list {1, 2, 3}; index 2 returns 2."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla que devuelve el estado traducido de una solicitud usa una cadena de 8 if anidados. ¿Qué alternativa es más legible?","options":["a!match o una decisión","Un process model","Añadir más if anidados con comentarios","Una consulta por cada estado"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!match o un decision object simplifican múltiples casos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule returning a request's translated status uses a chain of 8 nested ifs. Which alternative is more readable?","options":["a!match or a decision","A process model","More nested ifs with comments","A query per status"],"explanation":"a!match or a decision object simplifies multiple cases."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos funciones devuelven valores de fecha? (Elige 2)","options":["len(\"texto\")","upper(\"a\")","sum({1})","date(2026, 1, 15)","today()"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"today y date devuelven fechas; las demás, números o texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two functions return date values? (Choose 2)","options":["len(\"text\")","upper(\"a\")","sum({1})","date(2026, 1, 15)","today()"],"explanation":"today and date return dates; the others return numbers or text."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}, expression: fv!isFirst)?","options":["true","{false, false, true}","{true, false, false}","1"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"fv!isFirst es verdadero solo en el primer elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!forEach(items: {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"}, expression: fv!isFirst) return?","options":["true","{false, false, true}","{true, false, false}","1"],"explanation":"fv!isFirst is true only on the first item."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve min({8, 3, 5})?","options":["8","5","16","3"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"min devuelve el valor más bajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does min({8, 3, 5}) return?","options":["8","5","16","3"],"explanation":"min returns the lowest value."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Una regla debe devolver true si una solicitud tiene importe mayor que 0 y un responsable asignado. ¿Qué expresión es correcta?","options":["isnull(ri!responsable)","ri!importe > 0","or(ri!importe > 0, isnull(ri!responsable))","and(ri!importe > 0, not(isnull(ri!responsable)))"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"and exige ambas condiciones; el responsable no debe ser nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A rule must return true if a request has an amount over 0 and an assigned owner. Which expression is correct?","options":["isnull(ri!owner)","ri!amount > 0","or(ri!amount > 0, isnull(ri!owner))","and(ri!amount > 0, not(isnull(ri!owner)))"],"explanation":"and requires both conditions; the owner must not be null."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador quiere usar la misma lógica de cálculo en una interfaz, en un process model y en una Web API. ¿Dónde la coloca?","options":["En la interfaz, y la copia en el proceso y en la Web API","En una constante","En un grupo","En una regla de expresión que llaman los tres"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas de expresión son reutilizables desde interfaces, procesos y Web APIs.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer wants the same calculation logic in an interface, a process model and a Web API. Where do they put it?","options":["In the interface, copied into the process and the Web API","In a constant","In a group","In an expression rule all three call"],"explanation":"Expression rules are reusable from interfaces, processes and Web APIs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve right(\"2026-ABC\", 3)?","options":["\"ABC\"","3","\"202\"","\"6-A\""],"correct":[0],"explanation":"right devuelve los últimos caracteres indicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does right(\"2026-ABC\", 3) return?","options":["\"ABC\"","3","\"202\"","\"6-A\""],"explanation":"right returns the last given characters."}}}]}$exam$::jsonb);

-- appian-lead-developer.json: 500 preguntas
select public.import_exam_unchecked($exam${"slug":"appian-lead-developer","name":"Appian Certified Lead Developer","vendor":"Appian","code":"ACD301","language":"es","description":"Preguntas de práctica escritas a partir de los objetivos oficiales publicados por Appian (actualización de febrero de 2025). Appian no publica pesos por dominio; los usados aquí son estimados. No son preguntas del examen real.","exam":{"questions":45,"minutes":90,"passing":"54%","mini":{"questions":20,"minutes":40}},"domains":[{"code":"D1","name":"Platform Management","weight":15,"docs":[{"title":"Deploy to target environments","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Deploy_to_Target_Environments.html"},{"title":"Managing import customization files","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Managing_Import_Customization_Files.html"},{"title":"Enterprise architecture overview","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Enterprise_Architecture_Overview.html"}]},{"code":"D2","name":"Application Design and Development","weight":20,"docs":[{"title":"Appian design guidance","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/appian-recommendations.html"},{"title":"Sub-process activity","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Sub-Process_Activity.html"},{"title":"Sites","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Sites.html"}]},{"code":"D3","name":"Data Management","weight":20,"docs":[{"title":"What is Data Fabric?","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/data-fabric.html"},{"title":"Record-level security","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/record-level-security.html"},{"title":"Data sync for record types","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/about-data-sync.html"}]},{"code":"D4","name":"Proactively Design for Scalability and Performance","weight":20,"docs":[{"title":"Scaling Appian","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Scaling_Appian.html"},{"title":"Performance view","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Performance_View.html"},{"title":"Performance and load testing","url":"https://community.appian.com/w/article/3216/performance-and-load-testing"}]},{"code":"D5","name":"Extending Appian","weight":15,"docs":[{"title":"Connected systems","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Connected_System.html"},{"title":"Web API authentication","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Web_API_Authentication.html"},{"title":"Plug-ins","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Appian_Plug-ins.html"}]},{"code":"D6","name":"Project and Resource Management","weight":10,"docs":[{"title":"The Appian Delivery Methodology","url":"https://community.appian.com/success/w/guide/2973/the-appian-delivery-methodology"},{"title":"Recommended delivery methodology","url":"https://community.appian.com/w/article/3303/recommended-delivery-methodology"},{"title":"Health Check","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/health-check.html"}]}],"questions":[{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un despliegue a producción falla a mitad por un script de base de datos con error. ¿Qué debe prever el plan de despliegue del lead?","options":["Desactivar los scripts para siempre","Un procedimiento de vuelta atrás probado para BD y objetos","Nada","Reintentar el despliegue hasta que funcione sin investigar la causa"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un rollback probado limita el impacto de fallos parciales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A production deployment fails midway on a DB script error. What should the lead's deployment plan include?","options":["Disabling scripts forever","A tested rollback procedure for DB and objects","Nothing","Retrying until it works without finding the cause"],"explanation":"A tested rollback limits partial-failure impact."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué estrategia de ramas/entornos recomienda un lead para varios equipos trabajando en la misma aplicación?","options":["Que cada equipo despliegue la aplicación completa a producción cuando quiera","Coordinar cambios con paquetes por funcionalidad y un calendario de despliegues","Ninguna","Un entorno para todos sin coordinación"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La coordinación evita sobrescribir cambios ajenos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which branching/environment strategy does a lead recommend for several teams on one app?","options":["Each team deploys the whole app to production whenever","Coordinate with feature packages and a deployment calendar","None","One shared environment without coordination"],"explanation":"Coordination avoids overwriting others' changes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Dos equipos modifican la misma interfaz en desarrollo para releases distintas. ¿Qué riesgo identifica el lead?","options":["Desplegar cambios no terminados del otro equipo","Ninguno","Que Appian bloquee la interfaz para siempre","Que se duplique la interfaz automáticamente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un objeto solo tiene una versión actual en el entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Two teams change the same interface in dev for different releases. What risk does the lead see?","options":["Deploying the other team's unfinished changes","None","Appian locking the interface forever","The interface auto-duplicating"],"explanation":"An object has only one current version in the environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas mitigan conflictos cuando varios equipos comparten objetos? (Elige 2)","options":["Editar objetos compartidos sin avisar a los demás equipos","Desplegar todo siempre","Feature toggles o versiones paralelas de objetos","Prohibir la reutilización","Componentes compartidos con un responsable claro"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Gobierno de lo compartido y técnicas de aislamiento ayudan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices reduce conflicts when teams share objects? (Choose 2)","options":["Editing shared objects without telling other teams","Always deploying everything","Feature toggles or parallel object versions","Banning reuse","Shared components with a clear owner"],"explanation":"Governing shared items and isolation techniques help."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta de DevOps de Appian permite automatizar despliegues desde un pipeline CI/CD?","options":["El AppMarket","El log de expresiones, que lanza despliegues","Las APIs de despliegue de Appian","Ninguna"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las APIs de despliegue permiten exportar, inspeccionar e importar desde herramientas externas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian DevOps tool lets a CI/CD pipeline automate deployments?","options":["The AppMarket","The expression log, which triggers deployments","Appian's deployment APIs","None"],"explanation":"Deployment APIs allow exporting, inspecting and importing from external tools."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene versionar los paquetes exportados en un repositorio externo (p. ej. Git)?","options":["Ninguna","Trazabilidad y posibilidad de recuperar versiones","Que los objetos se editan en Git y se reflejan en Appian en tiempo real","Más espacio"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un repositorio aporta historial y auditoría de releases.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of versioning exported packages in an external repo (e.g. Git)?","options":["None","Traceability and recoverable versions","Objects edited in Git reflect in Appian in real time","More space"],"explanation":"A repository gives release history and auditability."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Tras un despliegue, una integración funciona en test pero falla en producción. ¿Qué revisa primero el lead?","options":["Nada","Valores por entorno del connected system y la red","El código de la interfaz que llama a la integración","Los grupos de diseño"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"URL, credenciales y conectividad suelen diferir por entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"After deployment, an integration works in test but fails in prod. What does the lead check first?","options":["Nothing","The connected system's per-environment values and network","The calling interface's code","Design groups"],"explanation":"URL, credentials and connectivity often differ per environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos fuentes usa un lead para diagnosticar un problema de entorno? (Elige 2)","options":["Logs del sistema","Reinicios aleatorios","Opiniones sin datos","Health Check y monitorización","Borrar caché del navegador de todos"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Datos objetivos guían el diagnóstico.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two sources does a lead use to diagnose an environment issue? (Choose 2)","options":["System logs","Random restarts","Opinions without data","Health Check and monitoring","Clearing everyone's browser cache"],"explanation":"Objective data guides diagnosis."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Usuarios reportan lentitud general en producción a una hora concreta. ¿Qué hipótesis investiga el lead?","options":["Nada","Un fallo del logo","Procesos programados o sincronizaciones coincidentes","Que los usuarios usan un navegador incorrecto"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las cargas programadas pueden saturar el entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Users report general production slowness at a specific time. Which hypothesis does the lead investigate?","options":["Nothing","A logo failure","Coinciding scheduled processes or syncs","Users using the wrong browser"],"explanation":"Scheduled loads can saturate the environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una arquitectura empresarial en el contexto de un lead Appian?","options":["Cómo encaja Appian con los demás sistemas de la organización","Un plug-in","El diseño de las interfaces de una aplicación concreta","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El lead considera integraciones, datos e identidad a nivel empresa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is enterprise architecture in an Appian lead's context?","options":["How Appian fits with the organization's other systems","A plug-in","The interface design of one specific app","A group"],"explanation":"The lead considers integrations, data and identity enterprise-wide."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe definir un lead en la arquitectura de una solución Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Nada","Modelo de identidad y seguridad","El color de cada botón de todas las interfaces de la aplicación","El nombre de cada variable","Sistemas de origen de datos y cómo se integran"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Datos, integración e identidad son pilares de arquitectura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements must a lead define in an Appian solution's architecture? (Choose 2)","options":["Nothing","Identity and security model","The color of every button in every app interface","Each variable's name","Data source systems and how they integrate"],"explanation":"Data, integration and identity are architecture pillars."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ajuste de la consola de administración afecta a qué tipos de archivos pueden subir los usuarios?","options":["Extensiones de documentos permitidas/bloqueadas","Los grupos de diseño","Nada","La configuración de branding de la página de inicio"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Restringir extensiones reduce riesgos de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Admin Console setting affects which file types users can upload?","options":["Allowed/blocked document extensions","Design groups","Nothing","Home page branding settings"],"explanation":"Restricting extensions reduces security risk."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración tiene un lead antes de cambiar la configuración de autenticación en producción?","options":["Ninguna","Probar en un entorno previo y tener acceso de emergencia","Desactivar todos los usuarios","Aplicarlo directamente porque solo afecta a usuarios nuevos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un error de autenticación puede bloquear a todos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead consider before changing authentication settings in production?","options":["None","Testing in a prior environment and having emergency access","Deactivating all users","Applying directly since it only affects new users"],"explanation":"An auth error can lock everyone out."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el aumento sostenido del uso de memoria en los motores tras varias releases?","options":["Un comportamiento normal que no requiere acción","Acumulación de procesos o datos; revisar archivado","Nada","Más usuarios contentos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El crecimiento sostenido suele indicar acumulación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does sustained engine memory growth over several releases indicate?","options":["Normal behavior needing no action","Accumulating processes or data; review archiving","Nothing","Happier users"],"explanation":"Sustained growth usually means accumulation."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una ventana de mantenimiento y por qué la planifica el lead?","options":["Nada","El horario en el que los desarrolladores pueden editar en producción","Un log","Un periodo acordado para despliegues con impacto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Minimiza el impacto a usuarios en cambios mayores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a maintenance window and why does the lead plan it?","options":["Nothing","Hours when developers may edit in production","A log","An agreed period for impactful deployments"],"explanation":"It minimizes user impact for major changes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe contener un runbook de despliegue? (Elige 2)","options":["Pasos ordenados y responsables","Opiniones","Las contraseñas de producción escritas en claro para agilizar","Verificaciones post-despliegue y rollback","Nada"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Un runbook hace el despliegue repetible y seguro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements belong in a deployment runbook? (Choose 2)","options":["Ordered steps and owners","Opinions","Production passwords in plain text to speed things up","Post-deploy checks and rollback","Nothing"],"explanation":"A runbook makes deployment repeatable and safe."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un paquete contiene un cambio en un tipo de registro sincronizado. ¿Qué paso posterior considera el lead?","options":["Borrar la tabla","Nada, los registros nunca requieren acción tras desplegar","Reiniciar Appian","Verificar o lanzar la resincronización en destino"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Algunos cambios de registro requieren resincronizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A package changes a synced record type. Which follow-up step does the lead consider?","options":["Drop the table","Nothing, records never need post-deploy action","Restart Appian","Verify or trigger resync in the target"],"explanation":"Some record changes require resyncing."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con plug-ins al desplegar a un nuevo entorno?","options":["Que no se pueden usar","Deben estar instalados en destino en la versión correcta","Ninguna","Que se copian solos desde el entorno de origen sin incluirlos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Sin el plug-in, los objetos que lo usan fallan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration for plug-ins when deploying to a new environment?","options":["They can't be used","They must be installed in the target at the right version","None","They copy themselves from source without inclusion"],"explanation":"Without the plug-in, objects using it fail."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tienen las aprobaciones en despliegues directos entre entornos?","options":["Que eliminan la necesidad de probar en test","Más velocidad sin control","Ninguna","Control y revisión antes de aplicar cambios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las aprobaciones añaden gobierno al proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of approvals in direct deployments between e