esactivar todos los procesos activos de producción","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Probar en un entorno inferior detecta incompatibilidades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before a scheduled Appian Cloud upgrade?","options":["Delete logs","Test apps in an already-upgraded environment","Disable every active production process","Nothing"],"explanation":"Testing in a lower environment catches incompatibilities."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos responsabilidades tiene un lead sobre la consola de administración? (Elige 2)","options":["No documentar cambios","Dar permisos de administrador a todos los desarrolladores del equipo","Definir qué ajustes pueden cambiarse y quién","Documentar la configuración de cada entorno","Cambiar ajustes sin probar"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Gobierno y documentación de la configuración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two responsibilities does a lead have over the Admin Console? (Choose 2)","options":["Not documenting changes","Giving admin rights to every developer on the team","Defining which settings can change and by whom","Documenting each environment's configuration","Changing settings untested"],"explanation":"Configuration governance and documentation."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué principio aplica un lead a la cantidad de administradores del sistema?","options":["El mínimo necesario","Ninguno","Todos los desarrolladores","Cuantos más mejor, para que siempre haya alguien disponible"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Pocos administradores reducen riesgos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which principle does a lead apply to the number of system administrators?","options":["The minimum needed","None","Every developer","The more the better so someone is always available"],"explanation":"Few admins reduce risk."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene revisar periódicamente en la seguridad de un entorno?","options":["Usuarios con permisos elevados y cuentas inactivas","El número de interfaces creadas cada mes","El color del tema","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las revisiones de acceso reducen riesgos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be periodically reviewed in an environment's security?","options":["Users with elevated rights and inactive accounts","Interfaces created each month","Theme color","Nothing"],"explanation":"Access reviews reduce risk."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para gestionar valores de configuración distintos por entorno?","options":["Constantes/connected systems con archivo de personalización","Valores fijos en el código","Ninguno","Editar los valores a mano tras cada despliegue en cada entorno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las personalizaciones de importación son repetibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for per-environment config values?","options":["Constants/connected systems with a customization file","Hardcoded values","None","Hand-edit values after each deployment per environment"],"explanation":"Import customizations are repeatable."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos indicadores sugieren que la arquitectura de una aplicación debe revisarse? (Elige 2)","options":["Incidencias de rendimiento recurrentes","Despliegues sencillos","Cambios pequeños requieren tocar muchos objetos","Usuarios satisfechos","Pocos defectos reportados por los usuarios en las últimas releases"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Acoplamiento y problemas recurrentes indican deuda arquitectónica.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two indicators suggest an app's architecture needs review? (Choose 2)","options":["Recurring performance incidents","Simple deployments","Small changes touch many objects","Satisfied users","Few user-reported defects in recent releases"],"explanation":"Coupling and recurring issues signal architectural debt."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el acoplamiento entre aplicaciones Appian y por qué preocupa al lead?","