 residen los datos"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Registrar decisiones clave (ADR) da contexto futuro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two architecture decisions should be formally recorded? (Choose 2)","options":["The button colors of each interface","Choice of integration patterns","Lunch schedule","Local variable names","Decisions on where data lives"],"explanation":"Recording key decisions (ADRs) gives future context."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el lead si Health Check muestra un riesgo alto que requiere cambios en muchas aplicaciones?","options":["Ignorarlo porque requiere demasiado esfuerzo","Priorizarlo con el negocio y planificarlo por fases","Desactivar Health Check","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los riesgos importantes deben planificarse aunque sean costosos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the lead do if Health Check shows a high risk requiring changes across many apps?","options":["Ignore it since it's too much effort","Prioritize it with the business and plan in phases","Disable Health Check","Nothing"],"explanation":"Important risks must be planned even if costly."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que los despliegues fallen a menudo por objetos que faltan?","options":["Falta de disciplina al construir paquetes","Nada","Muchos usuarios","Un fallo de la plataforma que debe reportarse siempre a Appian"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Revisar precedentes y procesos de empaquetado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does frequent deployment failure from missing objects indicate?","options":["Lack of discipline building packages","Nothing","Many users","A platform bug to always report to Appian"],"explanation":"Review precedents and packaging processes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene revisar si un proceso de producción queda en error tras un despliegue?","options":["El color de los carriles y la disposición visual del diagrama del modelo","Nada","Si el despliegue cambió nodos o variables usados por instancias activas","El nombre del modelo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cambios en modelos pueden afectar a instancias en curso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be checked if a production process errors after a deployment?","options":["The model diagram's lane colors and visual layout","Nothing","Whether the deploy changed nodes/variables used by active instances","The model name"],"explanation":"Model changes can affect running instances."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con las instancias activas de un proceso cuando se despliega una nueva versión del modelo?","options":["Se actualizan automáticamente a la nueva versión al instante","Se borran","Se cancelan","Siguen con la versión con la que se iniciaron"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las instancias usan la versión de inicio salvo que se migren.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to active instances when a new process model version is deployed?","options":["They auto-update to the new version instantly","They're deleted","They're cancelled","They continue on the version they started with"],"explanation":"Instances use their start version unless migrated."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos considera el lead cuando cambia un subproceso usado por instancias de larga duración? (Elige 2)","options":["Menos memoria","Incompatibilidad de parámetros con instancias existentes","Ninguno","Mayor velocidad de ejecución de todas las instancias existentes","Comportamientos mixtos entre versiones"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Los cambios deben ser compatibles con instancias en curso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks does the lead consider when changing a subprocess used by long-running instances? (Choose 2)","options":["Less memory","Parameter incompatibility with existing instances","None","Faster execution of every existing instance","Mixed behavior across versions"],"explanation":"Changes must be compatible with in-flight instances."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene antes de cambiar un modelo de proceso con muchas instancias activas?","options":["Nada","Evaluar el impacto en instancias en curso","Renombrar el modelo","Cancelar todas las instancias activas para evitar problemas de versiones"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios pueden requerir compatibilidad o migración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable before changing a process model with many active instances?","options":["Nothing","Assess impact on in-flight instances","Rename the model","Cancel every active instance to avoid version issues"],"explanation":"Changes may need compatibility or migration."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas de Appian ayudan a comparar objetos entre entornos? (Elige 2)","options":["Compare and Deploy","El log de inicios de sesión de usuarios","La configuración de branding del sitio","Historial de versiones del objeto","El AppMarket con plug-ins de terceros"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Permiten ver diferencias antes de desplegar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian tools help compare objects across environments? (Choose 2)","options":["Compare and Deploy","The users' login log","Site branding settings","Object version history","The AppMarket with third-party plug-ins"],"explanation":"They show differences before deploying."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para activar una funcionalidad solo cuando el negocio esté listo?","options":["Un feature toggle configurable","Mantener el código en desarrollo sin desplegar durante meses","Nada","Desplegar y ocultarlo con CSS"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los toggles desacoplan despliegue de activación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend to enable a feature only when the business is ready?","options":["A configurable feature toggle","Keep the code undeployed in dev for months","Nothing","Deploy and hide it with CSS"],"explanation":"Toggles decouple deployment from activation."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tienen los feature toggles si no se gestionan?","options":["Más seguridad","Que la aplicación se vuelve más rápida y simple","Ninguno","Acumulación de código muerto y complejidad"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los toggles obsoletos deben retirarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of unmanaged feature toggles?","options":["More security","The app becomes faster and simpler","None","Accumulating dead code and complexity"],"explanation":"Stale toggles must be removed."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda un lead sobre la frecuencia de despliegues a producción?","options":["Desplegar a diario sin pruebas","Nunca desplegar","Despliegues pequeños y frecuentes con buena automatización","Un único gran despliegue anual con todos los cambios"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Cambios pequeños reducen riesgo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead recommend about production deployment frequency?","options":["Deploy daily without tests","Never deploy","Small, frequent deployments with good automation","One big yearly deployment with all changes"],"explanation":"Small changes reduce risk."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos verificaciones automáticas puede incluir un pipeline de despliegue de Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Ejecución de pruebas automatizadas","Borrado de usuarios inactivos","Reinicio del servidor de producción","Cambio aleatorio de constantes","Inspección del paquete"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Inspección y pruebas son puertas de calidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two automated checks can an Appian deployment pipeline include? (Choose 2)","options":["Running automated tests","Deleting inactive users","Restarting the production server","Random constant changes","Package inspection"],"explanation":"Inspection and tests are quality gates."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un entorno efímero o de feature en la estrategia DevOps?","options":["El entorno de producción durante las horas de mantenimiento","Un log","Nada","Un entorno temporal para probar una funcionalidad aislada"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Permite aislar pruebas, aunque tiene coste de gestión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's an ephemeral or feature environment in DevOps strategy?","options":["Production during maintenance hours","A log","Nothing","A temporary environment to test an isolated feature"],"explanation":"It isolates tests, at a management cost."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene configurar para recibir avisos de errores de procesos en producción?","options":["Desactivar alertas","Alertas de procesos a un grupo de soporte","Que los usuarios finales reporten cada error por correo","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las alertas llegan al equipo que puede actuar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be set up to get process error notices in production?","options":["Disable alerts","Process alerts to a support group","End users emailing each error","Nothing"],"explanation":"Alerts reach the team that can act."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración tiene un lead sobre la zona horaria y locales del entorno?","options":["Usar la zona horaria del desarrollador que configuró el entorno","Ninguna","Cambiarla cada mes","Configurarlos coherentemente para usuarios y procesos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Afectan a fechas, calendarios y escalados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead consider about environment time zone and locales?","options":["Using the time zone of the developer who set it up","None","Changing it monthly","Setting them consistently for users and processes"],"explanation":"They affect dates, calendars and escalations."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el calendario de trabajo de procesos y qué afecta?","options":["Un plug-in","El calendario de vacaciones del equipo de desarrollo","Días y horas laborables; afecta a plazos y temporizadores","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cálculos de días laborables usan el calendario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the process work calendar and what does it affect?","options":["A plug-in","The dev team's vacation calendar","Working days and hours; affects deadlines and timers","Nothing"],"explanation":"Business-day calculations use the calendar."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene conceder acceso de diseñador en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Mejor trazabilidad","Despliegues más seguros","Menos incidencias","Exposición de datos y configuraciones","Cambios no controlados"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Producción debe tener acceso de diseño mínimo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from granting designer access in production? (Choose 2)","options":["Better traceability","Safer deployments","Fewer incidents","Exposure of data and configuration","Uncontrolled changes"],"explanation":"Production should have minimal design access."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay al importar un paquete que incluye grupos de seguridad?","options":["Que se borran los grupos destino","Ninguna","Que los usuarios del grupo se copian también desde el origen","La pertenencia de usuarios no viaja; hay que gestionarla en destino"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los objetos grupo se despliegan, pero los miembros se gestionan por entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration when importing a package with security groups?","options":["Target groups get deleted","None","Group users are also copied from the source","User membership doesn't travel; manage it in the target"],"explanation":"Group objects deploy, but members are managed per environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón facilita gestionar la pertenencia a grupos en producción sin desarrolladores?","options":["Una interfaz de administración para responsables de negocio","Grupos públicos","Pedir a los desarrolladores que editen grupos en cada solicitud","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Delegar la gestión reduce dependencia del equipo técnico.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern eases managing group membership in production without developers?","options":["An admin interface for business owners","Public groups","Asking developers to edit groups on each request","Nothing"],"explanation":"Delegating management reduces dependence on the technical team."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda un lead respecto al uso del rol de administrador del sistema para tareas diarias?","options":["Que todo el equipo trabaje siempre con cuentas de administrador","Usar cuentas con privilegios mínimos para el día a día","Nada","Compartir la cuenta"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Reducir el uso de privilegios elevados limita riesgos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead recommend about using the system admin role for daily tasks?","options":["The whole team always works as admin","Use least-privilege accounts day to day","Nothing","Share the account"],"explanation":"Limiting elevated privileges reduces risk."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una cola creciente de procesos pendientes de ejecutar?","options":["Más usuarios contentos","Que los procesos se están ejecutando más rápido de lo normal","Saturación de motores o procesos costosos","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Hay que identificar qué procesos generan la carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a growing queue of pending processes indicate?","options":["Happier users","Processes running faster than usual","Engine saturation or costly processes","Nothing"],"explanation":"Identify which processes create the load."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son adecuadas tras detectar un proceso que genera miles de errores? (Elige 2)","options":["Borrar los logs","Ignorarlo","Contener el problema (pausar origen o corregir)","Analizar la causa raíz","Reiniciar sin investigar"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Contener primero, después corregir la causa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions fit after finding a process generating thousands of errors? (Choose 2)","options":["Delete logs","Ignore it","Contain the issue (pause source or fix)","Analyze the root cause","Restart without investigating"],"explanation":"Contain first, then fix the cause."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda un lead sobre la documentación de la configuración de cada entorno?","options":["Confiar en que los administradores lo recuerden","Publicarla en internet","Nada","Mantenerla actualizada y versionada"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La documentación facilita recuperar y replicar entornos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead recommend about documenting each environment's configuration?","options":["Trust admins to remember","Publish it online","Nothing","Keep it current and versioned"],"explanation":"Documentation eases recovering and replicating environments."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con integraciones que dependen de listas de IPs permitidas?","options":["Las IPs de cada entorno deben estar autorizadas","Que no funcionan","Que Appian usa siempre la misma IP en todos los entornos","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Cada entorno puede salir por IPs distintas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration with integrations relying on IP allowlists?","options":["Each environment's IPs must be authorized","They don't work","Appian always uses the same IP everywhere","None"],"explanation":"Each environment may egress from different IPs."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué enfoque usa un lead para traducir requisitos complejos en un diseño Appian?","options":["Nada","Descomponer en registros, procesos, interfaces e integraciones","Copiar otra aplicación","Empezar construyendo interfaces y decidir el modelo de datos al final"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un diseño por capas aclara responsabilidades.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which approach does a lead use to turn complex requirements into an Appian design?","options":["Nothing","Break into records, processes, interfaces and integrations","Copy another app","Build interfaces first and decide the data model last"],"explanation":"A layered design clarifies responsibilities."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos criterios guían la decisión de crear un componente reutilizable? (Elige 2)","options":["Se usa o usará en varios lugares","Tiene una responsabilidad clara","Depende de datos de una sola pantalla","Es único y nunca se repetirá","Tiene cientos de parámetros"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"La reutilización tiene sentido con uso múltiple y foco claro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two criteria guide creating a reusable component? (Choose 2)","options":["It is or will be used in several places","It has a clear responsibility","It depends on one screen's data","It's unique and never repeats","It has hundreds of parameters"],"explanation":"Reuse makes sense with multiple uses and clear focus."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene sobregeneralizar un componente para cubrir todos los casos posibles?","options":["Más rendimiento","Complejidad excesiva y difícil mantenimiento","Que el componente se vuelve más sencillo y fácil de usar","Ninguno"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El exceso de parámetros complica la reutilización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of over-generalizing a component to cover every case?","options":["More performance","Excess complexity and hard maintenance","The component becomes simpler and easier","None"],"explanation":"Too many parameters hinder reuse."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para gestionar varias aplicaciones relacionadas?","options":["Duplicar objetos en cada app","Nada","Una aplicación común para objetos compartidos y apps de negocio separadas","Una única aplicación gigante con todos los objetos de todas las áreas"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Separar lo común facilita despliegues independientes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for several related apps?","options":["Duplicate objects per app","Nothing","A common app for shared objects plus separate business apps","One giant app with every area's objects"],"explanation":"Separating the common core eases independent deploys."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que un objeto esté en varias aplicaciones a la vez en Appian Designer?","options":["Que existen varias copias independientes del objeto","Se comparte; cambiarlo afecta a todas","Un error","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Un objeto puede pertenecer a varias aplicaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an object belonging to several apps in Appian Designer indicate?","options":["Several independent copies of the object exist","It's shared; changing it affects all","An error","Nothing"],"explanation":"An object can belong to multiple apps."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos decisiones toma un lead al diseñar la seguridad de una nueva aplicación? (Elige 2)","options":["Grupos y roles de negocio","Seguridad de registros y objetos","El orden alfabético de las carpetas","El color de cada grupo de usuarios","El nombre de las variables locales"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Roles y seguridad de datos/objetos son la base.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two decisions does a lead make designing a new app's security? (Choose 2)","options":["Business groups and roles","Record and object security","Folders' alphabetical order","Each user group's color","Local variable names"],"explanation":"Roles and data/object security are the foundation."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene cuando varias aplicaciones necesitan la misma lógica de aprobación?","options":["Nada","Copiar el flujo de aprobación en cada aplicación","Un subproceso común parametrizable","Un correo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un subproceso reutilizable centraliza la lógica.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits several apps needing the same approval logic?","options":["Nothing","Copy the approval flow into each app","A shared parameterized subprocess","An email"],"explanation":"A reusable subprocess centralizes logic."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué considera un lead al decidir entre un proceso o una escritura directa desde la interfaz?","options":["Necesidad de tareas, auditoría, asincronía y errores","Nada","El color","Solo la preferencia personal del desarrollador asignado"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los procesos aportan orquestación; las escrituras directas, simplicidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead weigh choosing a process vs a direct interface write?","options":["Need for tasks, audit, async and error handling","Nothing","Color","Only the assigned developer's preference"],"explanation":"Processes add orchestration; direct writes add simplicity."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos estándares de desarrollo suele definir un lead para el equipo? (Elige 2)","options":["Que cada desarrollador use su propio estilo","Checklist de revisión de código","Prohibir los comentarios en el código","Convenciones de nombres y estructura","Libertad total sin normas comunes"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Los estándares mantienen la calidad homogénea.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two dev standards does a lead usually define for the team? (Choose 2)","options":["Each developer using their own style","A code review checklist","Banning code comments","Naming and structure conventions","Total freedom without shared rules"],"explanation":"Standards keep quality consistent."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para manejar errores en interfaces de forma consistente?","options":["Componentes comunes de mensajes y validaciones","Nada","Que cada desarrollador muestre los errores a su manera","Mostrar errores técnicos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La consistencia mejora la experiencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for consistent error handling in interfaces?","options":["Shared message and validation components","Nothing","Each developer shows errors their own way","Show technical errors"],"explanation":"Consistency improves the experience."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un requisito pide que un caso pase por estados con reglas de transición complejas. ¿Qué diseño propone el lead?","options":["Un único estado","Nada","Modelar estados y transiciones como datos y reglas centralizadas","Codificar las transiciones dentro de cada interfaz por separado"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Centralizar transiciones evita inconsistencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A requirement has cases moving through states with complex transition rules. What design does the lead propose?","options":["A single state","Nothing","Model states and transitions as data and central rules","Hardcode transitions in each interface separately"],"explanation":"Centralizing transitions avoids inconsistency."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene un modelo de casos (case management) con registros y acciones?","options":["Flexibilidad para que el usuario elija la siguiente acción","Ninguna","Que obliga a seguir un único flujo lineal sin excepciones","Más código"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El case management soporta trabajo no estructurado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a case management model with records and actions?","options":["Flexibility for users to choose the next action","None","It forces one linear flow without exceptions","More code"],"explanation":"Case management supports unstructured work."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos factores llevan a un lead a preferir un flujo de proceso estructurado frente a acciones libres? (Elige 2)","options":["Secuencia de pasos fija y auditable","Usuarios expertos que deciden siempre","Trabajo muy variable caso a caso","Ninguna regla de negocio","Cumplimiento normativo estricto"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Los procesos estructurados aseguran secuencias controladas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two factors make a lead prefer a structured process flow over free actions? (Choose 2)","options":["Fixed, auditable step sequence","Experts always deciding","Highly variable case-by-case work","No business rules","Strict regulatory compliance"],"explanation":"Structured processes ensure controlled sequences."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón aplica un lead para que una aplicación soporte varios países con reglas distintas?","options":["Un if gigante en cada interfaz","Reglas parametrizadas por configuración de país","Nada","Una copia completa de la aplicación por cada país"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Parametrizar evita duplicar aplicaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead apply so an app supports several countries with different rules?","options":["A giant if in each interface","Rules parameterized by country configuration","Nothing","A full app copy per country"],"explanation":"Parameterizing avoids duplicating apps."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene duplicar aplicaciones por región?","options":["Ninguno","Mantener y corregir varias copias divergentes","Más seguridad","Que cada región tenga un rendimiento mejor que con una sola"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las copias divergen y multiplican el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of duplicating apps per region?","options":["None","Maintaining and fixing several diverging copies","More security","Each region performing better than with one app"],"explanation":"Copies diverge and multiply maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a que una aplicación sea mantenible a largo plazo? (Elige 2)","options":["Separar lógica de negocio de la presentación","Lógica duplicada en interfaces","Pruebas automatizadas de reglas clave","Objetos sin descripción ni prefijo","Valores codificados en cada regla"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Separación de responsabilidades y pruebas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices keep an app maintainable long term? (Choose 2)","options":["Separating business logic from presentation","Duplicated logic in interfaces","Automated tests for key rules","Objects without description or prefix","Hardcoded values in each rule"],"explanation":"Separation of concerns and tests."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que muchas interfaces llamen directamente a a!queryRecordType con los mismos filtros?","options":["Nada","Más seguridad","Oportunidad de centralizar la consulta en una regla","Una buena práctica para que cada interfaz sea independiente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Centralizar evita duplicación y facilita optimizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does many interfaces calling a!queryRecordType with the same filters indicate?","options":["Nothing","More security","A chance to centralize the query in a rule","Good practice so each interface is independent"],"explanation":"Centralizing avoids duplication and eases optimization."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la deuda técnica y cómo la gestiona un lead?","options":["Atajos que encarecen cambios futuros; se registra y prioriza","Nada","Un plug-in","Un coste de licencias que debe pagarse cada año a Appian"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La deuda debe hacerse visible y amortizarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's technical debt and how does a lead manage it?","options":["Shortcuts that make future changes costlier; logged and prioritized","Nothing","A plug-in","A yearly license cost paid to Appian"],"explanation":"Debt must be made visible and paid down."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones ayudan a reducir deuda técnica de forma sostenida? (Elige 2)","options":["No registrarla en el backlog","Reservar capacidad en cada sprint para mejoras","Posponerla indefinidamente hasta el final","Incluir refactorizaciones en historias relacionadas","Añadir más atajos para ir rápido"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"La amortización continua evita acumulación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions reduce technical debt sustainably? (Choose 2)","options":["Not log it in the backlog","Reserve capacity each sprint for improvements","Postpone it indefinitely until the end","Include refactors in related stories","Add more shortcuts to go fast"],"explanation":"Continuous paydown avoids accumulation."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para pantallas con lógica muy compleja?","options":["Una única interfaz con toda la lógica para verla junta","Dividir en componentes con responsabilidades claras","Nada","Usar plug-ins siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La modularidad facilita pruebas y cambios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for screens with very complex logic?","options":["One interface with all logic to see it together","Split into components with clear responsibilities","Nothing","Always use plug-ins"],"explanation":"Modularity eases testing and change."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un lead cuando un requisito no puede cumplirse con funcionalidades nativas?","options":["Nada","Rechazarlo sin explicación","Prometer que se hará igual sin analizar su viabilidad técnica","Evaluar alternativas y explicar el coste de cada una"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El lead orienta al negocio con opciones y trade-offs.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead do when a requirement can't be met natively?","options":["Nothing","Reject it without explanation","Promise it anyway without assessing feasibility","Evaluate alternatives and explain each one's cost"],"explanation":"The lead guides the business with options and trade-offs."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos componen una buena revisión de diseño antes de construir? (Elige 2)","options":["El nombre de los desarrolladores asignados","Flujos principales y de excepción","El color de los iconos de las pantallas","Modelo de datos y relaciones","La fecha de la próxima retrospectiva"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Datos y flujos son la base del diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a good design review before building? (Choose 2)","options":["Assigned developers' names","Main and exception flows","Screen icon colors","Data model and relationships","Next retrospective date"],"explanation":"Data and flows are the design foundation."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene construir primero una rebanada vertical completa (datos, proceso, interfaz) de una funcionalidad?","options":["Validar la arquitectura de extremo a extremo pronto","Ninguna","Que se evita tener que probar las capas por separado nunca","Más tiempo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Una rebanada temprana revela problemas de integración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of first building a full vertical slice (data, process, UI) of a feature?","options":["Validating the architecture end to end early","None","Never needing to test layers separately","More time"],"explanation":"An early slice reveals integration problems."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para interfaces usadas tanto en tareas como en acciones de registro?","options":["Nada","Dos interfaces diferentes que se mantienen sincronizadas a mano","Una interfaz base con entradas que reciben el contexto","Una por usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reutilizar la interfaz evita divergencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits interfaces used both in tasks and record actions?","options":["Nothing","Two different interfaces kept in sync by hand","A base interface with inputs receiving context","One per user"],"explanation":"Reusing the interface avoids divergence."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un lead si el diseño de un desarrollador no sigue los estándares?","options":["Rehacer el trabajo él mismo sin comentar nada al desarrollador","Aprobarlo igualmente","Explicar el estándar y acordar los cambios en la revisión","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La revisión es una oportunidad de aprendizaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead do if a developer's design doesn't follow standards?","options":["Redo the work silently without telling the developer","Approve it anyway","Explain the standard and agree changes in review","Nothing"],"explanation":"Review is a learning opportunity."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos de UX revisa un lead en una aplicación compleja? (Elige 2)","options":["Claridad de acciones y mensajes","Que los errores muestren trazas técnicas","Coherencia de navegación y patrones","Que cada pantalla tenga un estilo diferente","Que haya el máximo de campos posible"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Coherencia y claridad mejoran la adopción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two UX aspects does a lead review in a complex app? (Choose 2)","options":["Clarity of actions and messages","Errors showing technical traces","Navigation and pattern consistency","Each screen having a different style","Having as many fields as possible"],"explanation":"Consistency and clarity improve adoption."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón facilita probar la lógica de negocio independientemente de las interfaces?","options":["Probar la lógica únicamente a través de UAT manual","Reglas de expresión con casos de prueba","Lógica dentro de las interfaces","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las reglas aisladas son fáciles de probar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern eases testing business logic independently of interfaces?","options":["Testing logic only through manual UAT","Expression rules with test cases","Logic inside interfaces","Nothing"],"explanation":"Isolated rules are easy to test."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué considera un lead al elegir entre un sitio y la navegación estándar de Tempo?","options":["Que los sitios no admiten seguridad por grupos","Nada","Experiencia enfocada por rol frente a acceso general","El color"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los sitios ofrecen experiencias a medida por rol.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead weigh choosing a site vs standard Tempo navigation?","options":["Sites don't support group security","Nothing","Role-focused experience vs general access","Color"],"explanation":"Sites offer tailored role experiences."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos requisitos llevan a diseñar un portal en vez de un sitio interno? (Elige 2)","options":["Acceso público o de clientes","Usuarios externos sin cuenta Appian","Solo empleados internos","Administración del sistema","Tareas de procesos internos"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Los portales sirven a usuarios externos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two requirements lead to a portal instead of an internal site? (Choose 2)","options":["Public or customer access","External users without Appian accounts","Internal employees only","System administration","Internal process tasks"],"explanation":"Portals serve external users."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración de seguridad aplica a los portales?","options":["Que no necesitan revisión","Ninguna","Que heredan la sesión del usuario interno que los publica","Exponen solo lo necesario y se protegen frente a abusos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los portales son públicos y requieren diseño defensivo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which security consideration applies to portals?","options":["They need no review","None","They inherit the publishing internal user's session","Expose only what's needed and guard against abuse"],"explanation":"Portals are public and need defensive design."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para textos de la interfaz que pueden cambiar a menudo?","options":["En constantes por pantalla","Escribirlos directamente en cada componente","Centralizarlos en translation sets o configuración","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Centralizar textos facilita cambios y traducciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for UI texts that change often?","options":["Per-screen constants","Write them directly in each component","Centralize them in translation sets or config","Nothing"],"explanation":"Centralizing texts eases changes and translation."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un equipo propone guardar lógica de negocio en procedimientos almacenados para \"ganar rendimiento\". ¿Qué evalúa el lead?","options":["El color","Beneficio real frente a visibilidad y mantenibilidad","Que siempre es mejor mover toda la lógica a la base de datos","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La lógica fuera de Appian es menos visible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A team proposes stored procedures for business logic to \"gain performance\". What does the lead evaluate?","options":["Color","Real benefit vs visibility and maintainability","That moving all logic to the DB is always better","Nothing"],"explanation":"Logic outside Appian is less visible."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características tiene un buen diseño de modelo de proceso a nivel lead? (Elige 2)","options":["Subprocesos para separar responsabilidades","Lógica duplicada en nodos script","Un único nivel con cientos de nodos","Gestión explícita de excepciones","Variables con nombres genéricos"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Modularidad y robustez.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two traits mark a good lead-level process design? (Choose 2)","options":["Subprocesses separating responsibilities","Duplicated logic in script nodes","One level with hundreds of nodes","Explicit exception handling","Generic variable names"],"explanation":"Modularity and robustness."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una funcionalidad crítica depende de un único desarrollador que la conoce?","options":["Prohibir cambios","Asignarle siempre esas historias para ir más rápido","Documentar y compartir conocimiento en el equipo","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reducir el \"bus factor\" protege al proyecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a critical feature relies on one developer who knows it?","options":["Ban changes","Always assign them those stories to go faster","Document and share knowledge across the team","Nothing"],"explanation":"Lowering the bus factor protects the project."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón de diseño reduce el impacto de cambios en un sistema externo?","options":["Encapsular la integración tras reglas propias","Llamar al sistema externo desde cada interfaz directamente","Copiar sus datos a mano","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Una capa de abstracción aísla los cambios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which design pattern reduces the impact of changes in an external system?","options":["Wrap the integration behind your own rules","Call the external system directly from each interface","Copy its data by hand","Nothing"],"explanation":"An abstraction layer isolates changes."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene no definir criterios de aceptación técnicos (rendimiento, seguridad)? (Elige 2)","options":["Mejor calidad automáticamente","Lanzamientos más seguros","Discusiones sobre si algo está terminado","Menos defectos","Problemas descubiertos tarde"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Los criterios técnicos evitan ambigüedad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from not defining technical acceptance criteria (performance, security)? (Choose 2)","options":["Automatically better quality","Safer releases","Debates over whether it's done","Fewer defects","Problems found late"],"explanation":"Technical criteria avoid ambiguity."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda un lead para nombrar reglas que consultan datos?","options":["Nada","Números","Un patrón consistente (p. ej. PREFIJO_get...)","Nombres libres para que cada desarrollador elija"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Patrones de nombre facilitan encontrar y entender objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead recommend for naming data-query rules?","options":["Nothing","Numbers","A consistent pattern (e.g. PREFIX_get...)","Free names chosen by each developer"],"explanation":"Naming patterns ease finding and understanding objects."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón facilita la incorporación de nuevos desarrolladores a una aplicación grande?","options":["Nada","Darles acceso a producción","Que aprendan revisando objetos al azar en el diseñador","Guía de arquitectura y estándares del proyecto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La documentación acelera el onboarding.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern eases onboarding new developers to a large app?","options":["Nothing","Giving them production access","Learning by reviewing random objects in the designer","An architecture and standards guide for the project"],"explanation":"Documentation speeds onboarding."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe evaluar un lead al revisar una nueva interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["Rendimiento de sus consultas","Que muestre todos los datos sin filtro","Que cada campo use una fuente distinta","Que tenga el máximo de colores","Uso de componentes reutilizables"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Rendimiento y reutilización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements must a lead assess reviewing a new interface? (Choose 2)","options":["Query performance","Showing all data unfiltered","Each field using a different font","Having as many colors as possible","Use of reusable components"],"explanation":"Performance and reuse."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer cuando un requisito cambia el modelo de datos de forma importante en mitad del proyecto?","options":["Ignorarlo","Evaluar impacto, planificar migración y comunicar","Nada","Aplicar el cambio sin evaluar porque es solo un requisito"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios estructurales requieren plan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done when a requirement significantly changes the data model mid-project?","options":["Ignore it","Assess impact, plan migration and communicate","Nothing","Apply it without assessment since it's just a requirement"],"explanation":"Structural changes need a plan."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para mostrar el historial de un caso a distintos roles con distinto detalle?","options":["Un componente común con visibilidad por rol","Una interfaz copiada para cada rol con su detalle","Nada","Mostrar todo a todos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Un componente con lógica de rol evita duplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern shows a case's history to different roles with different detail?","options":["A shared component with role-based visibility","A copied interface per role with its detail","Nothing","Show everything to everyone"],"explanation":"A role-aware component avoids duplication."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas de revisión de código aplica un lead? (Elige 2)","options":["Revisar solo después de producción","Revisiones antes de desplegar a test","Aprobar sin leer para no retrasar","Revisar únicamente el nombre de los objetos","Checklist con seguridad, rendimiento y estándares"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Revisiones tempranas y sistemáticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two code review practices does a lead apply? (Choose 2)","options":["Reviewing only after production","Reviews before deploying to test","Approving unread to avoid delays","Reviewing only object names","A checklist covering security, performance and standards"],"explanation":"Early, systematic reviews."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando el negocio pide una funcionalidad que contradice buenas prácticas de seguridad?","options":["Implementarla sin comentar porque lo pide el cliente","Rechazarla sin explicar","Nada","Explicar riesgos y proponer una alternativa segura"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El lead protege al cliente aportando criterio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when the business requests a feature contradicting security best practice?","options":["Build it silently since the customer asked","Reject it without explanation","Nothing","Explain risks and propose a secure alternative"],"explanation":"The lead protects the customer with judgment."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a cumplir requisitos de auditoría en acciones críticas?","options":["Logs del navegador","Nada","Registrar evento con usuario, fecha y detalle","Confiar en que los usuarios anoten lo que hacen"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El registro de eventos da trazabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps meet audit requirements on critical actions?","options":["Browser logs","Nothing","Log an event with user, date and detail","Trust users to note what they do"],"explanation":"Event logging gives traceability."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos criterios usa un lead para decidir si algo va en una constante o en una tabla de configuración? (Elige 2)","options":["El color del valor","La longitud del nombre","El autor del objeto","Quién debe poder cambiarlo","Frecuencia de cambio"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Valores cambiantes y gestionados por negocio van en tablas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two criteria does a lead use to choose a constant vs a config table? (Choose 2)","options":["The value's color","Name length","Object author","Who must be able to change it","Change frequency"],"explanation":"Changing, business-managed values go in tables."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para gestionar estados de UI complejos (pasos, modos, selecciones) en una interfaz?","options":["Variables de proceso","Muchas variables sueltas sin relación entre sí","Nada","Variables locales bien estructuradas y nombradas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Un estado claro reduce errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for complex UI state (steps, modes, selections) in an interface?","options":["Process variables","Many loose unrelated variables","Nothing","Well-structured, well-named local variables"],"explanation":"Clear state reduces errors."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que una aplicación tenga muchas reglas casi idénticas con pequeñas diferencias?","options":["Más rendimiento","Una buena práctica para que cada caso sea independiente","Oportunidad de parametrizar y consolidar","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Consolidar reduce mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What do many near-identical rules with small differences indicate?","options":["More performance","Good practice so each case is independent","A chance to parameterize and consolidate","Nothing"],"explanation":"Consolidating cuts maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos considera un lead para que una aplicación sea accesible? (Elige 2)","options":["Solo colores para transmitir información","Iconos sin texto","Textos muy pequeños","Etiquetas y textos alternativos","Contraste y navegación por teclado"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Accesibilidad requiere etiquetas, contraste y teclado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two aspects does a lead consider for app accessibility? (Choose 2)","options":["Only colors to convey information","Icons without text","Very small text","Labels and alt text","Contrast and keyboard navigation"],"explanation":"Accessibility needs labels, contrast and keyboard support."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene si dos historias del sprint requieren cambiar el mismo componente compartido?","options":["Coordinar el cambio para hacerlo una vez y bien","Que cada desarrollador lo cambie por su cuenta sin avisar","Duplicar el componente","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Coordinar evita conflictos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable if two sprint stories need the same shared component changed?","options":["Coordinate to change it once, properly","Each developer changes it independently without notice","Duplicate the component","Nothing"],"explanation":"Coordination avoids conflicts."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de pruebas automatizadas tienen más retorno en Appian según un lead?","options":["Pruebas de cada etiqueta de todas las interfaces","Ninguna","Solo manuales","Pruebas de reglas clave y flujos críticos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Priorizar lo crítico maximiza el valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which automated tests give the most return in Appian per a lead?","options":["Tests of every label in every interface","None","Manual only","Tests of key rules and critical flows"],"explanation":"Prioritizing critical areas maximizes value."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene un componente compartido sin responsable claro? (Elige 2)","options":["Cambios descoordinados","Menos errores","Más coherencia","Nadie lo mantiene ni prueba","Mejor calidad"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Lo compartido necesita gobierno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from a shared component with no clear owner? (Choose 2)","options":["Uncoordinated changes","Fewer errors","More consistency","Nobody maintains or tests it","Better quality"],"explanation":"Shared items need governance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para diálogos de confirmación reutilizables?","options":["Nada","Escribir la confirmación cada vez en cada interfaz","No confirmar","Un componente de confirmación parametrizable"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Reutilizar unifica la experiencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for reusable confirmation dialogs?","options":["Nothing","Writing the confirmation in each interface","No confirmation","A parameterizable confirmation component"],"explanation":"Reuse unifies the experience."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una regla compartida devuelve estructuras distintas según parámetros?","options":["Mantener un contrato de salida claro y estable","Duplicar la regla","Cambiar la estructura libremente en cada versión","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Contratos estables evitan errores en consumidores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a shared rule returns different structures by parameter?","options":["Keep a clear, stable output contract","Duplicate the rule","Change the structure freely each version","Nothing"],"explanation":"Stable contracts avoid consumer errors."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a que la lista de registros sea útil para el usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["Datos sin formato","Sin búsqueda","Columnas relevantes y ordenables","Todas las columnas de la tabla","Filtros de usuario adecuados"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Columnas y filtros enfocados mejoran la usabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a record list useful to users? (Choose 2)","options":["Unformatted data","No search","Relevant, sortable columns","Every table column","Suitable user filters"],"explanation":"Focused columns and filters improve usability."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para notificaciones que el negocio quiere personalizar sin desarrollo?","options":["Correos manuales","Plantillas de texto almacenadas como configuración","Textos escritos en el modelo de proceso que solo cambian con despliegue","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La configuración permite autonomía al negocio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits notifications the business wants to customize without development?","options":["Manual emails","Text templates stored as configuration","Texts in the process model changed only by deployment","Nothing"],"explanation":"Configuration gives the business autonomy."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evalúa un lead antes de aprobar el uso de un componente de interfaz personalizado (plug-in)?","options":["Nada","Solo que se vea más moderno que los componentes nativos","Necesidad real, seguridad, accesibilidad y mantenimiento","El color"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los componentes personalizados añaden riesgo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead evaluate before approving a custom UI component (plug-in)?","options":["Nothing","Only that it looks more modern than native ones","Real need, security, accessibility and maintenance","Color"],"explanation":"Custom components add risk."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones ayudan a alinear el diseño técnico con el negocio? (Elige 2)","options":["Demos frecuentes de funcionalidades","Cambiar requisitos sin avisar","Esperar a UAT para enseñar algo","Revisar prototipos con usuarios clave","Diseñar sin consultar al negocio"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"El feedback temprano evita desvíos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions align technical design with the business? (Choose 2)","options":["Frequent feature demos","Changing requirements without notice","Waiting until UAT to show anything","Reviewing prototypes with key users","Designing without consulting the business"],"explanation":"Early feedback avoids drift."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para lógica que decide a quién asignar una tarea?","options":["Lógica de asignación escrita en cada nodo de tarea","Nada","Una regla de asignación centralizada y probada","Asignar siempre al administrador"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Centralizar facilita cambios en reglas de asignación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for logic deciding task assignment?","options":["Assignment logic written in each task node","Nothing","A centralized, tested assignment rule","Always assign to the admin"],"explanation":"Centralizing eases changes to assignment rules."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando el negocio quiere ver todos los datos en una sola pantalla?","options":["Proponer una vista resumen con navegación al detalle","Negarse","Nada","Mostrar todas las tablas completas en una sola interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Resumir y permitir profundizar equilibra UX y rendimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when the business wants all data on one screen?","options":["Propose a summary view with drill-down","Refuse","Nothing","Show every full table in one interface"],"explanation":"Summarize and allow drill-down to balance UX and performance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos son clave en el diseño de un flujo de aprobación multinivel? (Elige 2)","options":["Sin registro de decisiones","Un único aprobador fijo para todo","Reglas de quién aprueba en cada nivel","Aprobaciones sin plazos","Gestión de rechazos y devoluciones"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Reglas de aprobación y caminos alternativos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements are key in a multi-level approval flow design? (Choose 2)","options":["No decision log","One fixed approver for everything","Rules for who approves at each level","Approvals with no deadlines","Handling rejections and returns"],"explanation":"Approval rules and alternate paths."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda un lead para aplicaciones que deben funcionar en móvil y escritorio?","options":["Nada","Dos aplicaciones separadas, una para cada dispositivo","Solo escritorio","Diseño adaptable probado en ambos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Appian adapta interfaces; hay que probar ambos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead recommend for apps that must work on mobile and desktop?","options":["Nothing","Two separate apps, one per device","Desktop only","Responsive design tested on both"],"explanation":"Appian adapts interfaces; test both."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para datos que el usuario introduce y que deben validarse contra un sistema externo?","options":["Validar al enviar con la integración y mostrar errores claros","No validar","Validar en cada pulsación de tecla llamando al sistema externo","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Validar en momentos adecuados equilibra UX y carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits user-entered data that must be validated against an external system?","options":["Validate on submit via the integration with clear errors","Don't validate","Validate on every keystroke calling the external system","Nothing"],"explanation":"Validating at the right moments balances UX and load."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una interfaz requiere datos de un proceso en curso (p. ej. tareas abiertas del caso)?","options":["Mostrar todas las tareas del sistema","Guardar copias de las tareas en la base de datos a mano en cada nodo","Nada","Consultar los datos de procesos/tareas de forma filtrada"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los datos de procesos se consultan filtrados por caso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when an interface needs in-flight process data (e.g. the case's open tasks)?","options":["Show every task in the system","Hand-copy tasks to the DB at each node","Nothing","Query process/task data with filters"],"explanation":"Process data is queried filtered by case."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos mecanismos permiten a un usuario retomar trabajo pendiente en un caso? (Elige 2)","options":["Hojas de cálculo compartidas","Correos sin enlace","Acciones relacionadas en el registro del caso","Tareas asignadas en su lista","Recordarlo de memoria"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Tareas y acciones de registro guían el trabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two mechanisms let a user resume pending work on a case? (Choose 