ra","Menos defectos","Problemas de escalabilidad"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Ahorrar diseño suele costar más después.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from skipping technical design to deliver faster? (Choose 2)","options":["Later rework","Lower total cost","Better architecture","Fewer defects","Scalability problems"],"explanation":"Saving on design usually costs more later."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para formularios con secciones que dependen de respuestas previas complejas?","options":["Nada","Condiciones distintas escritas en cada componente","Mostrar todo","Reglas de visibilidad centralizadas y probadas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Centralizar reglas de visibilidad evita incoherencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits forms with sections depending on complex prior answers?","options":["Nothing","Different conditions in each component","Show everything","Centralized, tested visibility rules"],"explanation":"Centralizing visibility rules avoids inconsistency."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene comprobar antes de aprobar una nueva acción de registro?","options":["El nombre del desarrollador","Solo que el icono de la acción sea el adecuado","Nada","Seguridad de la acción y del proceso subyacente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Ambas capas deben estar alineadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be checked before approving a new record action?","options":["Developer name","Only that the action icon is right","Nothing","Security of the action and underlying process"],"explanation":"Both layers must align."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas aseguran la calidad cuando hay desarrolladores junior en el equipo? (Elige 2)","options":["No dar feedback","Asignarles solo lo más crítico sin apoyo","Revisiones de código por seniors","Despliegues sin revisión","Pair programming o mentoría"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Mentoría y revisión elevan la calidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices ensure quality with junior developers on the team? (Choose 2)","options":["No feedback","Giving them the most critical work unsupported","Code reviews by seniors","Unreviewed deployments","Pairing or mentoring"],"explanation":"Mentoring and review raise quality."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para guardar preferencias de usuario (p. ej. filtros favoritos)?","options":["Variables de proceso permanentes","Una constante por usuario modificada en ejecución","Nada","Una tabla de preferencias por usuario"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los datos de usuario van en tablas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for user preferences (e.g. favorite filters)?","options":["Permanent process variables","A per-user constant modified at runtime","Nothing","A per-user preferences table"],"explanation":"User data goes in tables."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando un requisito exige mostrar información en tiempo real de un sistema externo lento?","options":["Rechazarlo","Prometer tiempo real sin considerar el rendimiento del sistema","Nada","Acordar con negocio un compromiso (caché, refresco, carga diferida)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El lead explica trade-offs y propone opciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a requirement demands real-time info from a slow external system?","options":["Reject it","Promise real time ignoring the system's performance","Nothing","Agree a compromise with the business (cache, refresh, lazy load)"],"explanation":"The lead explains trade-offs and proposes options."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a garantizar que una aplicación cumple los requisitos? (Elige 2)","options":["Demos y aceptación del PO","Suposiciones no validadas","Ignorar criterios","Trazabilidad requisito–historia–prueba","Pruebas solo del desarrollador"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Trazabilidad y aceptación 