rmite sincronizar registros concretos tras cambios externos?","options":["Start Process","Write Records, que escribe y además lee cambios externos","Send E-Mail","Sync Records"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Sync Records actualiza filas específicas en la caché.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which smart service syncs specific records after external changes?","options":["Start Process","Write Records, which writes and reads external changes","Send E-Mail","Sync Records"],"explanation":"Sync Records refreshes specific rows in the cache."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas garantizan integridad referencial en el modelo de datos? (Elige 2)","options":["Duplicar datos en varias tablas sin relación","Guardar IDs relacionados como texto libre","Borrar padres sin revisar hijos","Claves foráneas en la base de datos","Escrituras de padre e hijos en una operación"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"FK y escrituras conjuntas protegen la integridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices ensure referential integrity in the data model? (Choose 2)","options":["Duplicating data across unrelated tables","Storing related IDs as free text","Deleting parents without checking children","Foreign keys in the database","Writing parent and children in one operation"],"explanation":"FKs and joint writes protect integrity."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para datos que deben conservarse por cumplimiento pero no consultarse a diario?","options":["Archivarlos aparte con acceso controlado","Nada","Mantenerlos en las tablas activas sincronizadas junto a los datos del día","Borrarlos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Separar históricos mantiene rendimiento y cumplimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for data kept for compliance but not queried daily?","options":["Archive them separately with controlled access","Nothing","Keep them in active synced tables alongside daily data","Delete it"],"explanation":"Separating history keeps performance and compliance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay al diseñar claves primarias para datos que se migrarán desde otro sistema?","options":["Nada","Mapear claves antiguas y evitar colisiones","No usar claves","Reutilizar siempre las claves antiguas aunque se repitan"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Guardar la clave de origen facilita trazabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration designing primary keys for data migrated from another system?","options":["Nothing","Map old keys and avoid collisions","No keys","Always reuse old keys even if duplicated"],"explanation":"Keeping the source key aids traceability."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos componen un plan de migración sólido? (Elige 2)","options":["No hacer copia de seguridad previa","Validar solo con una muestra de una fila","Ejecutarla directamente en producción sin ensayo","Plan de vuelta atrás","Ensayos en entornos previos"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Ensayos y rollback reducen riesgo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a solid migration plan? (Choose 2)","options":["No prior backup","Validating with a one-row sample only","Running it straight in production unrehearsed","Rollback plan","Rehearsals in prior environments"],"explanation":"Rehearsals and rollback reduce risk."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a mantener el rendimiento de un registro sincronizado con muchas relaciones?","options":["Relacionar solo lo necesario y limitar campos personalizados","Relacionar todos los registros entre sí por si acaso","Nada","Desactivar índices"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La complejidad excesiva afecta al sync y consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps keep a synced record with many relationships performant?","options":["Relate only what's needed and limit custom fields","Relate every record to every other just in case","Nothing","Disable indexes"],"explanation":"Excess complexity hurts sync and querie