iene cuando varias aplicaciones escriben en la misma tabla?","options":["Centralizar la escritura en reglas o servicios comunes","Que cada app escriba directamente con su propia lógica","Duplicar la tabla","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Centralizar asegura reglas coherentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits several apps writing to the same table?","options":["Centralize writes in shared rules or services","Each app writes directly with its own logic","Duplicate the table","Nothing"],"explanation":"Centralizing ensures consistent rules."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué considera un lead al diseñar el borrado de datos en un modelo con muchas relaciones?","options":["Que el borrado físico inmediato es siempre la mejor opción en cualquier caso","Nada","El color","Borrado lógico, cascadas y efecto en relacionados"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El borrado afecta a relaciones e historial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead consider designing deletion in a heavily related model?","options":["Immediate physical deletion is always best in any case","Nothing","Color","Soft delete, cascades and effect on related records"],"explanation":"Deletion affects relationships and history."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a probar el modelo de datos antes de producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Probar casos límite de relaciones","Saltarse las pruebas de migración","Usar datos reales sin anonimizar","Probar solo con datos vacíos","Cargar volúmenes realistas en test"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Volumen y casos límite revelan problemas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices help test the data model before production? (Choose 2)","options":["Test relationship edge cases","Skip migration tests","Use real unanonymized data","Test only with empty data","Load realistic volumes in test"],"explanation":"Volume and edge cases reveal issues."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para datos con alta concurrencia de escritura (p. ej. contadores)?","options":["Constantes","Nada","Leer, sumar en Appian y escribir el valor completo","Operaciones atómicas en base de datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las operaciones atómicas evitan pérdidas de actualización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits high write-concurrency data (e.g. counters)?","options":["Constants","Nothing","Read, add in Appian and write the full value","Atomic database operations"],"explanation":"Atomic operations prevent lost updates."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe documentar un lead sobre el modelo de datos? (Elige 2)","options":["Los colores preferidos de cada usuario","Diagrama entidad-relación","Las contraseñas de la base de datos","Fuentes, propietarios y reglas de cada entidad","El historial de reuniones del equipo"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"La documentación facilita mantenimiento y gobierno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things should a lead document about the data model? (Choose 2)","options":["Each user's favorite colors","Entity-relationship diagram","Database passwords","Each entity's sources, owners and rules","The team's meeting history"],"explanation":"Documentation eases maintenance and governance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un crecimiento inesperado de una tabla de log de la aplicación?","options":["Más usuarios","Revisar qué se registra y definir retención","Nada","Que la aplicación funciona mejor que nunca"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los logs sin retención crecen sin control.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does unexpected growth of an app log table indicate?","options":["More users","Review what's logged and define retention","Nothing","The app works better than ever"],"explanation":"Logs without retention grow unchecked."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro sincronizado con 3 millones de filas tarda en sincronizar. ¿Qué evalúa primero el lead?","options":["Nada","Quitar la seguridad del registro","Si hacen falta todas las filas","Aumentar la frecuencia de sincronización para que vaya más rápido"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reducir alcance suele ser la mejora más eficaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A synced record with 3 million rows is slow to sync. What does the lead assess first?","options":["Nothing","Removing record security","Whether all rows are needed","Raising sync frequency so it goes faster"],"explanation":"Reducing scope is usually the most effective fix."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón protege el acceso a documentos ligados a registros?","options":["Una carpeta pública con enlaces difíciles de adivinar para cada documento","Nada","Adjuntar a correos","Carpetas seguras y acceso vía registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los documentos deben heredar controles coherentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern protects access to record-linked documents?","options":["A public folder with hard-to-guess links per document","Nothing","Email attachments","Secured folders and access via the record"],"explanation":"Documents need consistent controls."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones minimizan el riesgo en un cambio de esquema en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Omitir la validación posterior","Aplicarlo en horario punta sin aviso","Ensayo en preproducción","Cambiarlo a mano sin script versionado","Copia de seguridad previa"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Backup y ensayo reducen el riesgo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions minimize risk in a production schema change? (Choose 2)","options":["Skip post-validation","Apply at peak time without notice","Rehearsal in pre-prod","Change by hand without a versioned script","Prior backup"],"explanation":"Backup and rehearsal reduce risk."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que los scripts de base de datos sean repetibles entre entornos?","options":["Copiar la base de datos completa","Ejecutar comandos a mano en cada en