ing con mucho volumen","Nunca"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Desnormalizar puede acelerar lecturas analíticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When can denormalizing be justified in Appian?","options":["To write faster","Always, normalization never adds value in Appian","For high-volume reporting reads","Never"],"explanation":"Denormalizing can speed analytical reads."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evalúa un lead antes de aprobar una relación muchos a muchos en registros?","options":["Nada","Una tabla intermedia con claves e índices adecuados","El color","Que se guarden los IDs relacionados en una lista separada por comas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La tabla de unión es la forma correcta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead check before approving a many-to-many between records?","options":["Nothing","A join table with proper keys and indexes","Color","That related IDs are stored as a comma-separated list"],"explanation":"The join table is the right approach."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para identificar de forma única datos que llegan de varios sistemas?","options":["No usar claves","Clave interna más clave del sistema de origen","Nada","Usar el nombre del cliente como clave primaria"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Mantener ambas claves facilita la conciliación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern uniquely identifies data arriving from several systems?","options":["No keys","An internal key plus the source system key","Nothing","Using the customer name as primary key"],"explanation":"Keeping both keys eases reconciliation."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a la calidad de datos de entrada? (Elige 2)","options":["Campos de texto libre para todo","Eliminar campos obligatorios","Aceptar cualquier valor y corregir después a mano","Restricciones en la base de datos","Validaciones en interfaces y en servidor"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Validar en varias capas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"