o","Que los usuarios lo hagan a mano caso a caso","Editar en la base sin registro","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los cambios masivos deben ser controlados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for bulk data changes the business requests (e.g. reassign 10,000 cases)?","options":["A tested, audited batch script or process","Users doing it by hand case by case","Editing the DB unlogged","Nothing"],"explanation":"Bulk changes must be controlled."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a gestionar datos con distintos niveles de confidencialidad?","options":["Tratar todos los datos igual sin clasificación","Nada","Clasificar datos y aplicar seguridad por nivel","Ocultarlos en interfaces"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La clasificación guía los controles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern manages data with different confidentiality levels?","options":["Treat all data the same unclassified","Nothing","Classify data and apply security per level","Hide it in interfaces"],"explanation":"Classification guides controls."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas de Appian aplican seguridad a nivel de datos? (Elige 2)","options":["Colores de la interfaz","Seguridad de campos de registros","Ocultar componentes con showWhen","Nombres de las carpetas","Seguridad de registros (filas)"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Filas y campos son seguridad de datos real.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian tools apply data-level security? (Choose 2)","options":["Interface colors","Record field security","Hiding components with showWhen","Folder names","Record row security"],"explanation":"Rows and fields are real data security."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando un campo calculado se usa como filtro frecuente en grids grandes?","options":["Nada","Calcularlo en tiempo real en cada consulta de la grid","Quitar el filtro","Precalcularlo en sincronización o persistirlo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los valores precalculados permiten filtrar eficientemente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a computed field is a frequent filter on large grids?","options":["Nothing","Compute it live on every grid query","Remove the filter","Precompute it at sync or persist it"],"explanation":"Precomputed values filter efficiently."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para integrar datos de un ERP que cambia poco y se consulta mucho?","options":["Sincronizar periódicamente en registros","Consultar el ERP en tiempo real en cada pantalla","Copiar a mano","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Datos estables y muy consultados se benefician del sync.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits ERP data that rarely changes and is heavily read?","options":["Sync it periodically into records","Query the ERP live on every screen","Copy by hand","Nothing"],"explanation":"Stable, heavily-read data benefits from sync."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene consultar un ERP en tiempo real desde muchas interfaces? (Elige 2)","options":["Menos llamadas","Mayor resiliencia","Dependencia de su disponibilidad","Sobrecarga del ERP","Mejor rendimiento del ERP"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Las consultas en tiempo real acoplan Appian al ERP.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from querying an ERP live from many interfaces? (Choose 2)","options":["Fewer calls","Greater resilience","Dependence on its availability","Overloading the ERP","Better ERP performance"],"explanation":"Live queries couple Appian to the ERP."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evalúa un lead sobre el tamaño de los tipos de registro (número de campos)?","options":["Incluir solo campos necesarios","El color","Nada","Incluir todas las columnas por si se necesitan algún día"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Menos campos = sync y consultas más ligeras.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead assess about record type size (field count)?","options":["Including only needed fields","Color","Nothing","Including every column in case needed someday"],"explanation":"Fewer fields = lighter sync and queries."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para versiones de un documento que cambia (p. ej. contratos)?","options":["Versionado con historial consultable","Correos","Sobrescribir el documento anterior en cada cambio","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las versiones permiten auditoría.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits versions of a changing document (e.g. contracts)?","options":["Versioning with queryable history","Emails","Overwriting the previous document on each change","Nothing"],"explanation":"Versions enable auditing."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos considera un lead para el backup y recuperación de datos de negocio? (Elige 2)","options":["No documentar el procedimiento","Confiar en que nunca fallará","Guardar copias en el mismo servidor","Pruebas de restauración","Frecuencia de copias"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Las copias deben probarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two aspects does a lead consider for business data backup/recovery? (Choose 2)","options":["Not documenting the procedure","Trusting it'll never fail","Keeping backups on the same server","Restore testing","Backup frequency"],"explanation":"Backups must be tested."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para datos que diferentes regiones no deben ver entre sí?","options":["Nada","Seguridad de registros por región","Interfaces distintas por región sin seguridad de datos","Constantes"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad de datos garantiza la separación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for data regions mustn't see from each other?","options":["Nothing","Record security by region","Separate interfaces per region without data security","Constants"],"explanation":"Data security guarantees separation."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón facilita informes sobre datos de varias aplicaciones?","options":["Nada","Registros relacionados o vistas de reporting comunes","Una interfaz por app","Copiar datos de cada aplicación a mano en una hoja"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Una capa común de reporting unifica datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern eases reporting across several apps' data?","options":["Nothing","Related records or shared reporting views","One interface per app","Hand-copying each app's data into a sheet"],"explanation":"A common reporting layer unifies data."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene guardar listas de valores en campos de texto delimitados? (Elige 2)","options":["Imposible filtrar o relacionar bien","Errores de formato","Más simplicidad a largo plazo","Mejor integridad","Consultas más rápidas"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Las listas deben ir en tablas hijas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from storing value lists in delimited text fields? (Choose 2)","options":["Can't filter or relate properly","Format errors","More long-term simplicity","Better integrity","Faster queries"],"explanation":"Lists belong in child tables."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una entidad crece con columnas para cada nuevo atributo opcional?","options":["Borrar columnas","Evaluar un modelo de atributos o tablas relacionadas","Seguir añadiendo columnas indefinidamente sin revisar","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El diseño debe evolucionar con los datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when an entity keeps growing a column per optional attribute?","options":["Drop columns","Evaluate an attribute model or related tables","Keep adding columns indefinitely without review","Nothing"],"explanation":"Design must evolve with the data."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evalúa un lead sobre el uso de procedimientos almacenados en la arquitectura?","options":["Beneficio frente a lógica oculta y portabilidad","Que deben usarse para toda la lógica de negocio","El color","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Equilibrio entre rendimiento y mantenibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead weigh on using stored procedures in the architecture?","options":["Benefit vs hidden logic and portability","They should hold all business logic","Color","Nothing"],"explanation":"Balance performance and maintainability."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas facilitan que otros equipos consuman datos de Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["APIs documentadas","Cambiar formatos sin aviso","Datos sin descripción","Acceso directo a tablas internas","Contratos de datos estables"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"APIs y contratos estables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices help other teams consume Appian data? (Choose 2)","options":["Documented APIs","Changing formats without notice","Undescribed data","Direct access to internal tables","Stable data contracts"],"explanation":"APIs and stable contracts."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando el negocio pide borrar datos personales de un cliente?","options":["Proceso controlado que localiza y elimina o anonimiza","Ignorarlo","Nada","Borrar a mano algunas filas sin registrar la acción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los derechos de supresión requieren un proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when the business asks to erase a customer's personal data?","options":["A controlled process that finds and deletes or anonymizes","Ignoring it","Nothing","Deleting some rows by hand without logging"],"explanation":"Erasure rights need a process."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para gestionar estados de un caso en el modelo de datos?","options":["Constantes","Nada","Texto libre del estado escrito por el usuario","Tabla de estados de referencia y campo de estado"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La referencia garantiza valores válidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern manages case statuses in the data model?","options":["Constants","Nothing","Free-text status typed by users","A status reference table and status field"],"explanation":"A reference guarantees valid values."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos debe tener un plan de archivado de datos? (Elige 2)","options":["Sin documentación","Borrar sin criterio","Archivar datos activos","Criterio de qué archivar y cuándo","Cómo consultar lo archivado si se necesita"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Criterio y acceso posterior.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should a data archiving plan have? (Choose 2)","options":["No documentation","Deleting without criteria","Archiving active data","Criteria for what to archive and when","How to query archived data if needed"],"explanation":"Criteria and later access."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando dos sistemas son fuente de verdad del mismo dato?","options":["Duplicar en Appian","Nada","Definir uno como maestro y sincronizar","Permitir que ambos lo modifiquen sin reglas de conciliación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un solo maestro evita conflictos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when two systems are the source of truth for the same data?","options":["Duplicate in Appian","Nothing","Define one as master and sync","Let both modify it without reconciliation rules"],"explanation":"One master avoids conflicts."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a conciliar datos entre Appian y un sistema externo?","options":["Procesos de conciliación con informes de diferencias","Borrar diferencias","Asumir que siempre coinciden sin verificarlo","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La conciliación detecta divergencias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps reconcile data between Appian and an external system?","options":["Reconciliation processes with difference reports","Delete differences","Assume they always match without checking","Nothing"],"explanation":"Reconciliation detects divergence."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones reducen el impacto de cargas masivas de datos en usuarios? (Elige 2)","options":["Procesar por lotes","Sin control de errores","Una única transacción gigante","Ejecutarlas en horario punta","Programarlas fuera de horas punta"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Horario y lotes reducen impacto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions reduce bulk-load impact on users? (Choose 2)","options":["Batch processing","No error control","One giant transaction","Running at peak time","Scheduling off-peak"],"explanation":"Timing and batching reduce impact."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué evalúa un lead sobre los límites de la plataforma al diseñar registros?","options":["El color","Que la plataforma no tiene ningún límite que considerar","Nada","Límites de filas, campos y relaciones sincronizables"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Conocer límites evita rediseños.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead assess about platform limits when designing records?","options":["Color","The platform has no limits to consider","Nothing","Syncable row, field and relationship limits"],"explanation":"Knowing limits avoids redesigns."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para datos de configuración por entorno almacenados en BD?","options":["Nada","Copiarlos de producción a desarrollo","Scripts de carga por entorno versionados","Introducirlos a mano en cada entorno sin registro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los scripts hacen la configuración reproducible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits per-environment config data stored in the DB?","options":["Nothing","Copying from prod to dev","Versioned per-environment load scripts","Entering them by hand per environment unlogged"],"explanation":"Scripts make config reproducible."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones ayudan a detectar problemas de calidad de datos pronto? (Elige 2)","options":["Validaciones automáticas en cargas","Aceptar duplicados","Informes de excepciones de datos","Ignorar datos nulos","No revisar cargas"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Detección temprana reduce el coste de corrección.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions help detect data quality issues early? (Choose 2)","options":["Automated validations on loads","Accepting duplicates","Data exception reports","Ignoring nulls","Not reviewing loads"],"explanation":"Early detection lowers fix cost."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una consulta necesita unir muchas tablas para un informe complejo?","options":["Una vista optimizada o tabla de reporting","Encadenar decenas de consultas en la interfaz y unirlas en memoria","Nada","Copiar datos a mano"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La BD es mejor uniendo datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a query must join many tables for a complex report?","options":["An optimized view or reporting table","Chain dozens of interface queries joined in memory","Nothing","Hand-copy data"],"explanation":"The DB is better at joining."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos criterios guían qué datos guardar en Appian y cuáles dejar en origen? (Elige 2)","options":["La fecha de creación de la app","El color de la pantalla","Necesidades de rendimiento y disponibilidad","Quién es el propietario del dato","El nombre del desarrollador"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Propiedad y requisitos técnicos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two criteria guide what data to store in Appian vs leave at source? (Choose 2)","options":["App creation date","Screen color","Performance and availability needs","Who owns the data","Developer name"],"explanation":"Ownership and technical requirements."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando se detecta que una relación de registro produce resultados duplicados?","options":["Nada","Revisar la cardinalidad y las claves de la relación","Eliminar duplicados en cada interfaz con lógica adicional","Quitar la relación"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La causa suele estar en la definición de la relación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a record relationship yields duplicate results?","options":["Nothing","Review the relationship's cardinality and keys","Remove duplicates in each interface with extra logic","Remove the relationship"],"explanation":"The cause is usually in the relationship definition."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene revisar antes de añadir una relación nueva a un registro muy consultado?","options":["Solo que la relación tenga un nombre descriptivo en inglés","Su impacto en consultas y sincronización","El color","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Cada relación añade coste potencial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be reviewed before adding a relationship to a heavily queried record?","options":["Only that it has a descriptive English name","Its impact on queries and sync","Color","Nothing"],"explanation":"Each relationship adds potential cost."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características debe tener un buen identificador para integraciones entre sistemas? (Elige 2)","options":["Que cambie con cada actualización","Estable en el tiempo","Reutilizado entre entidades","Único","Basado en nombres editables"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Identificadores únicos y estables evitan errores de enlace.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two traits should a good identifier for cross-system integrations have? (Choose 2)","options":["Changing with each update","Stable over time","Reused across entities","Unique","Based on editable names"],"explanation":"Unique, stable IDs avoid linking errors."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué significa diseñar proactivamente para la escalabilidad?","options":["Nada","Añadir más servidores siempre","Esperar a que los usuarios se quejen para optimizar","Considerar crecimiento de datos y usuarios desde el diseño"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Anticiparse es más barato que corregir.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does proactively designing for scalability mean?","options":["Nothing","Always adding servers","Waiting for user complaints to optimize","Considering data and user growth from design"],"explanation":"Anticipating is cheaper than fixing."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos datos necesita un lead para estimar la carga futura de una aplicación? (Elige 2)","options":["La versión del navegador del lead","El número de desarrolladores del equipo","El color corporativo de la empresa cliente","Usuarios concurrentes en horas punta","Volumen de casos esperado y crecimiento"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Volumen y concurrencia definen la carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two data points does a lead need to estimate an app's future load? (Choose 2)","options":["The lead's browser version","Team developer count","The customer's brand color","Peak concurrent users","Expected case volume and growth"],"explanation":"Volume and concurrency define load."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón de proceso escala mejor con alto volumen de casos?","options":["Nada","Procesos cortos y orientados a eventos","Un proceso por caso abierto durante toda la vida del caso","Procesos con bucles de espera"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Menos instancias activas = menos memoria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process pattern scales best with high case volume?","options":["Nothing","Short, event-driven processes","One process per case open for its whole life","Processes with wait loops"],"explanation":"Fewer active instances = less memory."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene un proceso con un temporizador que espera meses?","options":["Ninguno","Mantiene instancias activas consumiendo memoria","Que el temporizador deja de funcionar al cabo de una semana","Más rendimiento"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Mejor programar un proceso nuevo cuando llegue la fecha.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of a process with a timer waiting months?","options":["None","It keeps instances active consuming memory","The timer stops working after a week","More performance"],"explanation":"Better to schedule a new process when the date arrives."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué alternativa escala mejor que esperar meses en un temporizador de proceso?","options":["Nada","Una tarea manual","Guardar la fecha y lanzar un proceso programado que la revise","Añadir más temporizadores en paralelo en el mismo proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un proceso batch periódico evita instancias dormidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What scales better than waiting months on a process timer?","options":["Nothing","A manual task","Store the date and run a scheduled process that checks it","Add more parallel timers in the same process"],"explanation":"A periodic batch process avoids dormant instances."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos técnicas evitan que un proceso por lotes sature el sistema? (Elige 2)","options":["Desactivar el control de errores","Ejecución fuera de horas punta","Iniciar miles de procesos en el mismo segundo","Procesar todo en una sola transacción","Tamaños de lote controlados"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Lotes y horarios reducen el impacto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two techniques keep a batch process from saturating the system? (Choose 2)","options":["Disabling error control","Off-peak execution","Starting thousands of processes at once","Processing everything in one transaction","Controlled batch sizes"],"explanation":"Batches and timing reduce impact."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué valida una prueba de carga diseñada por un lead?","options":["La seguridad de las contraseñas","Que la app cumple objetivos de rendimiento con la carga prevista","Que la interfaz se ve bien en todos los navegadores posibles","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Compara resultados con objetivos acordados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead-designed load test validate?","options":["Password security","The app meets performance targets under expected load","The interface looks right in every browser","Nothing"],"explanation":"It compares results to agreed targets."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos definen un buen escenario de prueba de carga? (Elige 2)","options":["Volumen de datos representativo","Base de datos vacía","Tiempo de prueba de un segundo","Mezcla realista de acciones de usuario","Un único usuario haciendo una sola acción repetida durante la prueba"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Realismo en acciones y datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements define a good load test scenario? (Choose 2)","options":["Representative data volume","Empty database","One-second test duration","Realistic mix of user actions","A single user repeating one action during the test"],"explanation":"Realism in actions and data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el lead si la prueba de carga muestra que una interfaz concreta degrada el sistema?","options":["Nada","Analizar su rendimiento y optimizarla antes del lanzamiento","Quitar la prueba","Lanzar igualmente y revisar si hay quejas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Corregir antes de producción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the lead do if a load test shows a specific interface degrading the system?","options":["Nothing","Analyze and optimize it before launch","Drop the test","Launch anyway and see if complaints arrive"],"explanation":"Fix before production."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué métrica describe el número de operaciones que el sistema completa por unidad de tiempo?","options":["Disponibilidad","Latencia, que mide el número de usuarios conectados","Throughput (rendimiento)","Ninguna"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El throughput mide capacidad de trabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which metric describes operations completed per unit of time?","options":["Availability","Latency, which measures connected users","Throughput","None"],"explanation":"Throughput measures work capacity."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué métrica describe el tiempo que tarda una operación individual?","options":["Disponibilidad","Ninguna","Throughput, que mide el tiempo de cada operación","Latencia / tiempo de respuesta"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La latencia es el tiempo por operación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which metric describes how long a single operation takes?","options":["Availability","None","Throughput, which times each operation","Latency / response time"],"explanation":"Latency is time per operation."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué un lead analiza percentiles (p. ej. p95) y no solo la media de tiempos?","options":["No importa","Porque los percentiles siempre dan valores más bajos","Por estética","La media oculta casos lentos que afectan a usuarios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los percentiles revelan la cola lenta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why does a lead look at percentiles (e.g. p95), not just average times?","options":["It doesn't matter","Percentiles always give lower values","Aesthetics","Averages hide slow cases affecting users"],"explanation":"Percentiles reveal the slow tail."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos patrones de interfaz escalan con volúmenes grandes? (Elige 2)","options":["Calcular totales en el navegador","Grids paginadas en servidor","Búsqueda con filtros obligatorios u opcionales","Consultas por fila","Cargar todos los registros al abrir la interfaz para filtrarlos luego"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Paginación y filtros acotan datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two interface patterns scale with large volumes? (Choose 2)","options":["Compute totals in the browser","Server-paged grids","Search with required or optional filters","Per-row queries","Loading every record on open to filter later"],"explanation":"Paging and filters bound data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo de escalabilidad tienen los grupos con decenas de miles de miembros asignados a tareas?","options":["Más rendimiento","Evaluación costosa y listas de tareas enormes","Que los miembros no reciben nunca las tareas","Ninguno"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Asignaciones masivas afectan a rendimiento y usabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What scalability risk do groups with tens of thousands of members assigned to tasks pose?","options":["More performance","Costly evaluation and huge task lists","Members never receive the tasks","None"],"explanation":"Mass assignments hurt performance and usability."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para distribuir trabajo entre muchos agentes de forma escalable?","options":["Colas de trabajo con asignación por reglas","Nada","Asignar cada tarea a todos los agentes a la vez","Asignación manual por correo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las colas con reglas reparten carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern distributes work across many agents scalably?","options":["Work queues with rule-based assignment","Nothing","Assign every task to all agents at once","Manual assignment by email"],"explanation":"Rule-based queues spread load."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones reducen el uso de memoria en procesos con mucho volumen? (Elige 2)","options":["Evitar variables de proceso grandes","Guardar documentos en pv","Borrar procesos completados pronto","Duplicar subprocesos","No archivar nunca los procesos para conservar todo el historial"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Limpieza y variables pequeñas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions reduce memory in high-volume processes? (Choose 2)","options":["Avoid large process variables","Store documents in pvs","Delete completed processes early","Duplicate subprocesses","Never archiving processes to keep all history"],"explanation":"Cleanup and small variables."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración de escalabilidad hay con MNI sobre listas variables?","options":["Que el MNI escala sin límite con cualquier tamaño de lista","Que es más rápido siempre","Ninguna","Acotar el tamaño o procesar por lotes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las listas grandes deben dividirse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a scalability consideration with MNI over variable lists?","options":["MNI scales without limit for any list size","It's always faster","None","Bound the size or batch"],"explanation":"Large lists must be split."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a que una integración de alto volumen no bloquee procesos?","options":["Integración en interfaz","Llamadas síncronas encadenadas sin timeout","Nada","Llamadas asíncronas con reintentos controlados"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La asincronía aísla latencias externas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern keeps a high-volume integration from blocking processes?","options":["Integration in the interface","Chained synchronous calls with no timeout","Nothing","Async calls with controlled retries"],"explanation":"Async isolates external latency."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos técnicas mejoran el rendimiento de consultas a registros? (Elige 2)","options":["Seleccionar solo campos necesarios","Pedir siempre todos los campos del registro por si hacen falta","Filtrar por campos indexados","Usar batchSize -1","Filtrar en memoria tras traer todo"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Menos datos y filtros eficientes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two techniques improve record query performance? (Choose 2)","options":["Selecting only needed fields","Always requesting every record field in case needed","Filtering on indexed fields","Using batchSize -1","Filtering in memory after fetching all"],"explanation":"Less data and efficient filters."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que el tiempo de una interfaz crezca linealmente con los datos del usuario?","options":["Error de seguridad","Consultas o bucles sin acotar","Un comportamiento esperado y deseable","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El coste debe ser acotado por paginación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an interface's time growing linearly with user data indicate?","options":["Security error","Unbounded queries or loops","Expected, desirable behavior","Nothing"],"explanation":"Cost should be bounded by paging."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un lead para que el rendimiento sea parte del proceso de desarrollo?","options":["Incluir revisiones de rendimiento en la DoD","Delegarlo al negocio","Nada","Revisar el rendimiento solo cuando el cliente se queje"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Sistematizar evita sorpresas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead do to make performance part of the dev process?","options":["Include performance reviews in the DoD","Delegate it to the business","Nothing","Review performance only when the customer complains"],"explanation":"Systematizing avoids surprises."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas usa un lead para identificar cuellos de botella en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Cambios aleatorios","Logs de rendimiento","Reinicios periódicos","Opiniones de usuarios sin datos","Health Check"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Datos objetivos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two tools does a lead use to find production bottlenecks? (Choose 2)","options":["Random changes","Performance logs","Periodic restarts","User opinions without data","Health Check"],"explanation":"Objective data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón escala mejor para notificar eventos a muchos usuarios?","options":["Notificaciones agrupadas o asíncronas","Tareas a cada usuario","Nada","Un proceso síncrono por usuario lanzado desde la interfaz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Agrupar reduce sobrecarga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern scales better to notify many users of events?","options":["Grouped or async notifications","Tasks to each user","Nothing","One synchronous process per user from the interface"],"explanation":"Grouping reduces overhead."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando una funcionalidad necesita recalcular datos de todos los casos cada noche?","options":["Procesamiento por lotes en BD o procesos optimizados","Nada","Un proceso por caso iniciado a la vez cada noche","Hacerlo manualmente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El trabajo masivo se hace mejor en lotes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a feature must recompute all cases nightly?","options":["Batch processing in the DB or optimized processes","Nothing","One process per case started simultaneously nightly","Doing it manually"],"explanation":"Bulk work is best batched."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos de rendimiento tiene la seguridad de registros muy compleja? (Elige 2)","options":["Ninguno","Menor uso de memoria en los motores de procesos de Appian","Más velocidad","Consultas más lentas","Sincronizaciones más costosas"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"La seguridad compleja se evalúa en cada acceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two performance risks come from very complex record security? (Choose 2)","options":["None","Lower memory use in Appian's process engines","More speed","Slower queries","Costlier syncs"],"explanation":"Complex security is evaluated on each access."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón simplifica la seguridad de registros para mejorar rendimiento?","options":["Calcular la seguridad con consultas anidadas en cada acceso","Nada","Quitar la seguridad","Precalcular atributos de seguridad (p. ej. región) en el registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Atributos directos simplifican filtros de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern simplifies record security to improve performance?","options":["Compute security with nested queries on every access","Nothing","Remove security","Precompute security attributes (e.g. region) on the record"],"explanation":"Direct attributes simplify security filters."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué considera un lead sobre la escalabilidad de Web APIs expuestas a socios?","options":["Límites de uso, paginación y respuestas ligeras","Que los socios nunca harán muchas llamadas","Nada","El color"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las APIs externas deben protegerse de picos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead consider about scalability of partner-facing Web APIs?","options":["Usage limits, paging and light responses","Partners will never make many calls","Nothing","Color"],"explanation":"External APIs must withstand spikes."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones forman parte de un plan de capacidad? (Elige 2)","options":["Ignorar el crecimiento de datos","Asumir que la carga de la aplicación nunca cambiará con el tiempo","Revisar periódicamente métricas reales","Proyectar crecimiento","No medir"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Proyectar y verificar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are part of a capacity plan? (Choose 2)","options":["Ignoring data growth","Assuming the app's load will never change over time","Regularly reviewing real metrics","Projecting growth","Not measuring"],"explanation":"Project and verify."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un pico de memoria de motores coincidiendo con un proceso programado?","options":["El proceso programado es costoso y debe optimizarse","Que los motores están infrautilizados el resto del día","Nada","Error de red"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Correlacionar picos con procesos identifica la causa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an engine memory spike coinciding with a scheduled process indicate?","options":["The scheduled process is costly and needs optimizing","Engines are underused the rest of the day","Nothing","Network error"],"explanation":"Correlating spikes with processes finds the cause."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué