],"explanation":"Repartir y optimizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions help if the process queue slows at peak hours? (Choose 2)","options":["Optimize the most frequent processes","Adding more audit nodes to each running process","Disable archiving","Move non-urgent work off-peak","Start more processes"],"explanation":"Redistribute and optimize."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para medir el impacto real de una optimización?","options":["Medir solo una vez","Nada","Confiar en la impresión del desarrollador","Comparar métricas antes y después"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La comparación objetiva confirma la mejora.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable to measure an optimization's real impact?","options":["Measure only once","Nothing","Trust the developer's impression","Compare metrics before and after"],"explanation":"Objective comparison confirms improvement."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a escalar la generación de informes pesados?","options":["Precalcular datos y generar en segundo plano","Nada","Generar en la interfaz con todas las filas en memoria","Hacerlo a mano"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El trabajo pesado fuera de la interacción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps scale heavy report generation?","options":["Precompute data and generate in the background","Nothing","Generate in the interface with all rows in memory","Do it by hand"],"explanation":"Heavy work outside the interaction."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos considera un lead al diseñar una aplicación para miles de usuarios externos? (Elige 2)","options":["Que los externos usen la misma cuenta","Rendimiento del portal bajo carga","Exponer todos los datos","Sin límites de uso","Protección frente a abusos"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Carga y seguridad públicas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two aspects does a lead consider designing for thousands of external users? (Choose 2)","options":["Externals sharing one account","Portal performance under load","Exposing all data","No usage limits","Abuse protection"],"explanation":"Public load and security."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que los tiempos de respuesta empeoren a fin de mes?","options":["Error del navegador","Picos de negocio previsibles; planificar capacidad","Que la aplicación tiene un fallo aleatorio sin patrón","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los patrones estacionales se planifican.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does response time worsening at month-end indicate?","options":["Browser error","Predictable business peaks; plan capacity","A random bug with no pattern","Nothing"],"explanation":"Seasonal patterns are planned for."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón recomienda un lead para datos consultados con mucha frecuencia y que cambian poco?","options":["Consultarlos en origen en cada evaluación","Nada","Sincronizarlos o cachearlos","Constantes"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reducir accesos repetidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does a lead recommend for frequently read, rarely changed data?","options":["Query the source on every evaluation","Nothing","Sync or cache it","Constants"],"explanation":"Reduce repeated access."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para que una interfaz no consulte la base de datos en cada interacción del usuario?","options":["Nada","Variables locales con refresco controlado","refreshAlways en todas las variables para tener siempre datos frescos","Consultas dentro de cada componente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Controlar el refresco reduce consultas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern keeps an interface from querying the DB on every interaction?","options":["Nothing","Locals with controlled refresh","refreshAlways on every variable for fresh data","Queries inside each component"],"explanation":"Controlling refresh cuts queries."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos efectos tiene guardar grandes estructuras en variables de proceso en procesos frecuentes? (Elige 2)","options":["Mejor escalabilidad de la plataforma en horas punta","Más memoria en motores","Consultas a base de datos más rápidas","Peor rendimiento general","Menos instancias activas en los motores de procesos"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Las pv grandes penalizan a escala.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two effects come from storing large structures in pvs in frequent processes? (Choose 2)","options":["Better platform scalability at peak","More engine memory","Faster DB queries","Worse overall performance","Fewer active instances in engines"],"explanation":"Large pvs penalize at scale."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando un subproceso se llama miles de veces al día?","options":["Nada","Añadirle auditoría detallada en cada nodo para depurar mejor","Hacerlo síncrono siempre","Mantenerlo mínimo y sin datos innecesarios"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El coste se multiplica por el número de llamadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when a subprocess is called thousands of times a day?","options":["Nothing","Add detailed per-node auditing for debugging","Always make it synchronous","Keep it minimal without unneeded data"],"explanation":"Cost multiplies by call count."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una regla que hace una consulta y se llama dentro de a!forEach en una grid de 500 filas?","options":["Una única consulta optimizada automáticamente por Appian","Más seguridad","Nada","500 consultas por carga"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Hay que consultar una vez para todas las filas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a rule doing a query, called inside a!forEach over a 500-row grid, imply?","options":["One query auto-optimized by Appian","More security","Nothing","500 queries per load"],"explanation":"Query once for all rows."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos técnicas sustituyen consultas por fila en una grid? 