bajo"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"El criterio técnico es clave al estimar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from not involving the lead in a project's commercial estimate? (Choose 2)","options":["Unbudgeted technical risks","More accurate estimates","Technically unfeasible commitments","Better quality","Less rework"],"explanation":"Technical judgment is key when estimating."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que las decisiones técnicas importantes sean comprensibles meses después?","options":["Confiar en la memoria del equipo","Comentarlas solo en reuniones","Nada","Registrarlas con contexto y alternativas consideradas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los registros de decisiones dan contexto futuro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable so major technical decisions are understandable months later?","options":["Rely on team memory","Only discuss them in meetings","Nothing","Record them with context and alternatives considered"],"explanation":"Decision records give future context."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a un lead a mantener alineados a varios equipos Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Despliegues sin coordinación","Sincronizaciones técnicas periódicas entre equipos","Que cada equipo trabaje aislado sin comunicar","Duplicar componentes en cada equipo","Estándares y componentes comunes"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Comunicación y base común.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices help a lead keep several Appian teams aligned? (Choose 2)","options":["Uncoordinated deployments","Regular cross-team technical syncs","Each team working in isolation","Duplicating components per team","Shared standards and components"],"explanation":"Communication and a common base."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un lead para que la calidad no dependa solo de las pruebas finales?","options":["Integrar calidad en cada paso: diseño, revisión y pruebas automatizadas","Nada","Confiar en el negocio","Concentrar todo el esfuerzo de calidad en la UAT final"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La calidad se construye durante el desarrollo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead do so quality doesn't rely only on final testing?","options":["Build quality into each step: design, review and automated tests","Nothing","Rely on the business","Concentrate all quality effort in final UAT"],"explanation":"Quality is built during development."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones debe tomar un lead tras una incidencia grave causada por un despliegue? (Elige 2)","options":["Dejar de desplegar indefinidamente","Mejorar el proceso de despliegue","Buscar al responsable para sancionarlo","Ocultar la incidencia al negocio","Post-mortem sin culpables"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Aprender y mejorar el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions should a lead take after a serious deployment-caused incident? (Choose 2)","options":["Stopping deployments indefinitely","Improving the deployment process","Finding someone to punish","Hiding the incident from the business","A blameless post-mortem"],"explanation":"Learn and improve the process."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene cuando el negocio pide fechas de entrega cerradas para todo el backlog?","options":["Negarse a planificar","Dar previsiones basadas en velocidad, con márgenes y revisión","Prometer fechas exactas para cada historia sin datos","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las previsiones con datos son más fiables.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable when the business wants fixed dates for the whole backlog?","options":["Refuse to plan","Velocity-based forecasts with ranges and review","Promise exact dates per story without data","Nothing"],"explanation":"Data-based forecasts are more reliable."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones ayudan a un lead a asegurar que los requisitos de seguridad se cumplen? (Elige 2)","options":["Delegarla por completo en el negocio","Revisar la seguridad solo si hay un incidente","Revisiones de seguridad antes de producción","Asumir que Appian lo cubre todo","Incluirlos en la DoD y en las revisiones"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Seguridad sistemática.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions help a lead ensure security requirements are met? (Choose 2)","options":["Delegating it entirely to the business","Reviewing security only after an incident","Security reviews before production","Assuming Appian covers everything","Including them in the DoD and reviews"],"explanation":"Systematic security."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un lead si un recurso clave se asigna a otro proyecto en mitad de una release?","options":["Mantener el plan intacto y esperar que el resto compense","Nada","Evaluar el impacto y replanificar con el negocio","Cancelar la release"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los cambios de capacidad exigen replanificar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a lead do if a key resource is moved to another project mid-release?","options":["Keep the plan and hope others compensate","Nothing","Assess impact and replan with the business","Cancel the release"],"explanation":"Capacity changes require replanning."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos características tiene un buen estándar de gobernanza? (Elige 2)","options":["Revisado y actualizado periódicamente","Desconocido por los equipos","Claro y documentado","Distinto para cada desarrollador","Imposible de cumplir en la práctica"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Claridad y vigencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two traits does a good governance standard have? (Choose 2)","options":["Periodically reviewed and updated","Unknown to teams","Clear and documented","Different per developer","Impossible to follow in practice"],"explanation":"Clarity and currency."}}}]}$exam$::jsonb);

-- appian-senior-developer.json: 500 preguntas
select public.import_exam_unchecked($exam${"slug":"appian-senior-developer","name":"Appian Certified Senior Developer","vendor":"Appian","code":"ACD201","language":"es","description":"Preguntas de práctica escritas a partir de los objetivos oficiales publicados por Appian (blueprint de diciembre de 2023). No son preguntas del examen real.","exam":{"questions":50,"minutes":60,"passing":"60%","mini":{"questions":20,"minutes":25}},"domains":[{"code":"D1","name":"Platform and Application Management","weight":12,"docs":[{"title":"Health Check","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/health-check.html"},{"title":"Deploy to target environments","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Deploy_to_Target_Environments.html"},{"title":"Managing log files","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/managing-log-files.html"}]},{"code":"D2","name":"Data Management","weight":20,"docs":[{"title":"Record type relationships","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/record-type-relationships.html"},{"title":"Data sync for record types","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/about-data-sync.html"},{"title":"Custom record fields","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/custom-record-fields.html"}]},{"code":"D3","name":"Application Design and Development","weight":28,"docs":[{"title":"Object security","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/object-security.html"},{"title":"Record-level security","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/record-level-security.html"},{"title":"Appian design guidance","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/appian-recommendations.html"}]},{"code":"D4","name":"Advanced Appian Concepts","weight":18,"docs":[{"title":"Connected system authentication","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/connected_system_authentication.html"},{"title":"Integration object","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Integration_Object.html"},{"title":"Web API authentication","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Web_API_Authentication.html"}]},{"code":"D5","name":"Performance & Scalability","weight":22,"docs":[{"title":"Performance view","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Performance_View.html"},{"title":"Process node properties (multiple instances)","url":"https://docs.appian.com/suite/help/latest/Process_Node_and_Smart_Service_Properties.html"},{"title":"Performance and load testing","url":"https://community.appian.com/w/article/3216/performance-and-load-testing"}]}],"questions":[{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve Appian Health Check?","options":["Crear usuarios","Analizar diseño y ejecución para detectar riesgos","Reiniciar automáticamente los motores de procesos cuando hay errores","Desplegar paquetes entre entornos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Health Check genera un informe de riesgos de diseño, configuración y rendimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Appian Health Check for?","options":["Creating users","Analyzing design and runtime to detect risks","Automatically restarting process engines on errors","Deploying packages between environments"],"explanation":"Health Check produces a report of design, configuration and performance risks."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿En qué entorno aporta Health Check información más útil sobre rendimiento real?","options":["Desarrollo, porque contiene los objetos más recientes","Un entorno vacío","Producción","Un portátil local"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los datos de ejecución reales están en producción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In which environment does Health Check give the most useful information about real performance?","options":["Development, because it holds the newest objects","An empty environment","Production","A local laptop"],"explanation":"Real runtime data lives in production."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con los hallazgos de riesgo alto de un informe de Health Check?","options":["Ignorarlos hasta que provoquen una caída en producción","Desactivar Health Check","Priorizarlos y planificar su corrección","Borrar el informe"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los riesgos altos deben corregirse con prioridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with high-risk findings in a Health Check report?","options":["Ignore them until they cause a production outage","Disable Health Check","Prioritize and plan their fix","Delete the report"],"explanation":"High risks should be fixed with priority."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas son recomendables al usar Health Check? (Elige 2)","options":["No compartir los resultados","Ejecutarlo únicamente en desarrollo","Ejecutarlo solo una vez en la vida del proyecto","Programarlo de forma periódica","Revisar las tendencias entre informes"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Ejecutarlo regularmente permite ver la evolución de los riesgos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices are recommended when using Health Check? (Choose 2)","options":["Not sharing the results","Running it only in development","Running it only once in the project's life","Scheduling it regularly","Reviewing trends across reports"],"explanation":"Running it regularly shows how risks evolve."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde configura un administrador la autenticación SAML de Appian?","options":["En la consola de administración","En una constante","En cada interfaz de la aplicación mediante una regla","En el modelo de proceso"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La autenticación (SAML, LDAP, etc.) se configura en la Admin Console.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where does an administrator configure Appian SAML authentication?","options":["In the Admin Console","In a constant","In each app interface via a rule","In the process model"],"explanation":"Authentication (SAML, LDAP, etc.) is configured in the Admin Console."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de ajustes se gestionan en la consola de administración de Appian?","options":["Ajustes del sistema como autenticación, correo y plug-ins","El diseño de las interfaces","Las historias de usuario","La lógica de las reglas de expresión de cada aplicación"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La Admin Console agrupa la configuración a nivel de entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which kind of settings are managed in the Appian Admin Console?","options":["System settings such as authentication, email and plug-ins","Interface design","User stories","The logic of each app's expression rules"],"explanation":"The Admin Console groups environment-level configuration."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se instalan plug-ins del AppMarket en Appian Cloud?","options":["Desde una interfaz","Desde la consola de administración","No se pueden instalar","Copiando los JAR en el servidor por FTP"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"En Cloud, los plug-ins aprobados se instalan desde la Admin Console.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where are AppMarket plug-ins installed on Appian Cloud?","options":["From an interface","From the Admin Console","They can't be installed","By copying JARs to the server via FTP"],"explanation":"On Cloud, approved plug-ins are installed from the Admin Console."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se guardan credenciales que usan algunos plug-ins para conectarse a terceros?","options":["En un documento compartido","En el nombre de una interfaz","Third-Party Credentials (consola de administración)","En constantes de texto dentro de la aplicación que usa el plug-in"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Third-Party Credentials almacena credenciales de forma segura para plug-ins.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where are credentials used by some plug-ins to connect to third parties stored?","options":["In a shared document","In an interface's name","Third-Party Credentials in the Admin Console","In text constants inside the app that uses the plug-in"],"explanation":"Third-Party Credentials stores credentials securely for plug-ins."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué log revisar primero para investigar errores generales del servidor de aplicaciones?","options":["application_server.log","Un CSV de diseño","Ninguno","login-audit.csv, que registra solo los inicios de sesión"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"application_server.log recoge errores y avisos del servidor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which log should be checked first to investigate general application server errors?","options":["application_server.log","A design CSV","None","login-audit.csv, which only records logins"],"explanation":"application_server.log captures server errors and warnings."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué log permite ver los intentos de inicio de sesión de los usuarios?","options":["application_server.log, que solo contiene errores de procesos","expressions_details.csv","Ninguno","login-audit.csv"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"login-audit.csv registra los intentos de autenticación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which log shows users' login attempts?","options":["application_server.log, which only contains process errors","expressions_details.csv","None","login-audit.csv"],"explanation":"login-audit.csv records authentication attempts."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de log ayuda a identificar expresiones lentas?","options":["El log de auditoría de inicios de sesión de los usuarios","Los logs de rendimiento de expresiones","Los logs de correo","Ninguno"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los logs de rendimiento muestran tiempos de evaluación de expresiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which kind of log helps identify slow expressions?","options":["The user login audit log","Expression performance logs","Email logs","None"],"explanation":"Performance logs show expression evaluation times."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se consultan habitualmente los logs en Appian Cloud?","options":["Pidiéndolos a los usuarios","Con el plug-in Log Reader o descargándolos","No se pueden consultar","Accediendo por SSH directamente al servidor que aloja Appian Cloud"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"En Cloud no hay acceso al servidor; se usan herramientas de Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How are logs usually read on Appian Cloud?","options":["By asking users","With the Log Reader plug-in or by downloading them","They can't be read","By SSH directly into the server hosting Appian Cloud"],"explanation":"Cloud gives no server access; Appian tools are used."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son posibles sobre un proceso detenido por un error en un nodo? (Elige 2)","options":["Revisar los detalles del error en la monitorización del proceso","Corregir el problema y reanudar el nodo","Nada","Editar el historial de los nodos que ya se completaron","Cambiar la fecha de inicio"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Los procesos con error pueden diagnosticarse y reanudarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are possible on a process stopped by a node error? (Choose 2)","options":["Review error details in process monitoring","Fix the issue and resume the node","Nothing","Edit the history of already completed nodes","Change the start date"],"explanation":"Errored processes can be diagnosed and resumed."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde puede un desarrollador ver los procesos con errores de su aplicación?","options":["En el log de inicios de sesión","En la configuración de branding","En la monitorización de Appian Designer","En el AppMarket, en la sección de aplicaciones instaladas"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La monitorización de procesos muestra errores y actividad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where can a developer see their application's errored processes?","options":["In the login log","In branding settings","In Appian Designer's monitoring view","In the AppMarket, under installed applications"],"explanation":"Process monitoring shows errors and activity."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un archivo de personalización de importación (.properties) en un despliegue?","options":["Un log","Una copia de seguridad completa de la base de datos del entorno","Un plug-in","Valores propios del entorno destino para el paquete"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Permite ajustar constantes o connected systems por entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an import customization file (.properties) in a deployment?","options":["A log","A full backup of the environment's database","A plug-in","Target-environment values for objects in the package"],"explanation":"It adjusts constants or connected systems per environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Una constante con la URL de un servicio debe tener un valor distinto en test y en producción. ¿Qué se usa?","options":["Editar la constante a mano en producción tras cada despliegue","Nada","Una versión distinta de la aplicación para cada entorno","Un archivo de personalización de importación"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El archivo de personalización asigna valores por entorno en la importación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A constant with a service URL must differ in test and production. What's used?","options":["Hand-edit the constant in production after each deployment","Nothing","A separate app version per environment","An import customization file"],"explanation":"The customization file sets per-environment values on import."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos se pueden incluir en un paquete de despliegue de Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Datos de las instancias de proceso activas","Usuarios con sus contraseñas","Logs del servidor","Scripts de base de datos","Plug-ins"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Los paquetes pueden incluir objetos, scripts de BD y plug-ins.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two items can be included in an Appian deployment package? (Choose 2)","options":["Active process instance data","Users with their passwords","Server logs","Database scripts","Plug-ins"],"explanation":"Packages can include objects, DB scripts and plug-ins."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer antes de importar un paquete en un entorno superior?","options":["Borrar la aplicación destino","Inspeccionarlo para detectar errores y precedentes que faltan","Importarlo directamente y revisar los errores después en producción","Desactivar la seguridad"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La inspección detecta problemas antes de importar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before importing a package into a higher environment?","options":["Delete the target app","Inspect it for errors and missing precedents","Import it directly and review errors later in production","Disable security"],"explanation":"Inspection catches problems before import."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un aviso de \"precedente que falta\" al inspeccionar un paquete?","options":["Nada","Un objeto referencia otro que no está en el paquete ni en el destino","Que falta un usuario","Que el paquete contiene demasiados objetos y debe dividirse"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Hay que añadir el objeto dependiente o asegurarse de que existe en destino.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"missing precedent\" warning mean when inspecting a package?","options":["Nothing","An object references one not in the package or target","A user is missing","The package has too many objects and must be split"],"explanation":"Add the dependent object or ensure it exists in the target."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué funcionalidad de Appian permite desplegar directamente entre entornos conectados con aprobaciones?","options":["Despliegues directos (Compare and Deploy) entre entornos","Ninguna","Copiar la base de datos de un entorno a otro","Exportar a Excel"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Appian permite desplegar entre entornos conectados con flujo de revisión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian feature deploys directly between connected environments with approvals?","options":["Direct deployments (Compare and Deploy) between environments","None","Copying the database from one environment to another","Excel export"],"explanation":"Appian supports deploying across connected environments with review."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar el historial de despliegues de Appian?","options":["Saber qué se desplegó, cuándo y por quién","Revertir automáticamente cualquier despliegue sin probar","Crear usuarios","Borrar logs"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El historial da trazabilidad de los cambios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of Appian's deployment history?","options":["Knowing what was deployed, when and by whom","Automatically reverting any deployment untested","Creating users","Deleting logs"],"explanation":"History gives change traceability."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué rol de seguridad de objeto permite modificar un objeto de diseño pero no su seguridad?","options":["Denegar","Visor","Administrador, que solo puede ver el objeto","Editor"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El Editor modifica; el Administrador además gestiona la seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object security role allows modifying a design object but not its security?","options":["Deny","Viewer","Administrator, which can only view the object","Editor"],"explanation":"Editor modifies; Administrator also manages security."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el rol \"Deny\" en la seguridad de un objeto de Appian?","options":["Da permisos de solo lectura a todos los usuarios","Bloquea el acceso aunque otro grupo lo conceda","Elimina el objeto","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Deny prevalece sobre otros permisos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the \"Deny\" role do in Appian object security?","options":["Gives read-only rights to every user","Blocks access even if another group grants it","Deletes the object","Nothing"],"explanation":"Deny overrides other permissions."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta muestra un resumen de la seguridad de todos los objetos de una aplicación?","options":["El resumen de seguridad de la aplicación","El AppMarket, con la lista de plug-ins de seguridad instalados","La consola de procesos","El log de inicios de sesión"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El security summary ayuda a revisar y corregir permisos de objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which tool shows a security summary of all objects in an application?","options":["The application security summary","The AppMarket, with the list of installed security plug-ins","The process console","The login log"],"explanation":"The security summary helps review and fix object permissions."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué práctica de seguridad de objetos es recomendable?","options":["Dar Administrador a todos","Asignar permisos a grupos, no a usuarios individuales","No configurar seguridad","Asignar permisos directamente a cada usuario para más control"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad basada en grupos es más mantenible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object security practice is recommended?","options":["Give Administrator to everyone","Grant permissions to groups, not individual users","Configure no security","Grant permissions to each user directly for more control"],"explanation":"Group-based security is more maintainable."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos grupos se suelen crear para una aplicación Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Un grupo de administradores de la aplicación","Un grupo individual para cada usuario de la aplicación","Grupos de usuarios por rol de negocio","Ningún grupo","Un grupo por cada interfaz"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Se crean grupos de administración y de roles de negocio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two groups are typically created for an Appian application? (Choose 2)","options":["An application administrators group","A separate group for each app user","User groups by business role","No groups","One group per interface"],"explanation":"Admin and business-role groups are created."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con los objetos de diseño en un entorno de producción bien gestionado?","options":["Nada","Se borran tras cada release","Solo se modifican mediante despliegues","Los desarrolladores los editan directamente cuando hay urgencias"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Producción recibe cambios únicamente por despliegue controlado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to design objects in a well-managed production environment?","options":["Nothing","They're deleted after each release","They change only through deployments","Developers edit them directly in emergencies"],"explanation":"Production receives changes only via controlled deployment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ajuste de un modelo de proceso controla cuánto tiempo se conservan los procesos completados?","options":["El color de los carriles","El número máximo de nodos que puede tener el modelo","Archivar o borrar tras completarse","La seguridad"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Archivar o borrar procesos completados libera memoria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process model setting controls how long completed processes are kept?","options":["Lane colors","The maximum number of nodes the model may have","Archive or delete after completion","Security"],"explanation":"Archiving or deleting completed processes frees memory."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué impacto tiene conservar procesos completados mucho tiempo sin archivar?","options":["Ninguno","Reducen el tamaño de la base de datos","Mejoran el rendimiento de los informes de procesos","Consumen memoria de los motores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los procesos en memoria aumentan el uso de los motores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the impact of keeping completed processes long without archiving?","options":["None","They shrink the database","They improve process report performance","They consume engine memory"],"explanation":"In-memory processes increase engine usage."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un data source en la consola de administración?","options":["Un tipo de registro que lee datos de un CSV","Un grupo","Un plug-in","Una conexión configurada a una base de datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los data sources permiten a Appian conectarse a bases de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a data source in the Admin Console?","options":["A record type reading data from a CSV","A group","A plug-in","A configured database connection"],"explanation":"Data sources let Appian connect to databases."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ajustes se configuran normalmente en la consola de administración? (Elige 2)","options":["Configuración de correo saliente","Extensiones de documentos permitidas","Lógica de reglas de expresión","Nodos de un proceso","Campos de un tipo de registro"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Correo y extensiones permitidas son ajustes de sistema.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two settings are normally configured in the Admin Console? (Choose 2)","options":["Outbound email configuration","Allowed document extensions","Expression rule logic","Process nodes","Record type fields"],"explanation":"Email and allowed extensions are system settings."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer antes de un despliegue que cambia la estructura de tablas?","options":["Modificar la tabla en producción a mano después del despliegue","Borrar la tabla","Nada","Incluir y probar los scripts de BD en entornos previos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los scripts deben probarse y desplegarse con el paquete.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before a deployment that changes table structure?","options":["Hand-modify the production table after deployment","Drop the table","Nothing","Include and test the DB scripts in earlier environments"],"explanation":"Scripts must be tested and deployed with the package."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es Appian Designer?","options":["Un plug-in","El entorno donde se construyen las aplicaciones","La aplicación móvil que usan los usuarios finales para hacer tareas","La consola de logs"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Designer es el entorno de desarrollo de Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Appian Designer?","options":["A plug-in","The environment to build and manage apps and objects","The mobile app end users use to do tasks","The log console"],"explanation":"Designer is Appian's development environment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas facilitan la gestión de aplicaciones grandes? (Elige 2)","options":["Nombres aleatorios","Prefijo de aplicación en los nombres de objetos","Sin descripciones","Guardar todos los objetos en la carpeta raíz de la aplicación","Carpetas organizadas por tipo de objeto"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Nombres con prefijo y carpetas ordenadas facilitan la gestión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices ease managing large applications? (Choose 2)","options":["Random names","App prefix on object names","No descriptions","Keeping every object in the app's root folder","Folders organized by object type"],"explanation":"Prefixed names and tidy folders ease management."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la función \"Find in this application\" / dependencias de un objeto?","options":["Nada","El número de veces que se ha desplegado","Su autor","Qué objetos lo usan y cuáles usa él"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Ver dependencias ayuda a evaluar el impacto de un cambio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an object's dependents/precedents view show?","options":["Nothing","How many times it was deployed","Its author","Which objects use it and which it uses"],"explanation":"Viewing dependencies helps assess change impact."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador va a cambiar una regla de expresión usada en muchas interfaces. ¿Qué revisa primero?","options":["El número de líneas de la regla para que no supere un límite","Sus objetos dependientes","El historial de inicios de sesión","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los dependientes muestran el alcance del impacto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer will change an expression rule used in many interfaces. What do they check first?","options":["The rule's line count so it doesn't exceed a limit","Its dependents","Login history","Nothing"],"explanation":"Dependents show the scope of impact."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el historial de versiones de un objeto de diseño?","options":["Desplegar automáticamente la versión más antigua a producción","Borrar el objeto","Cambiar el autor","Ver y restaurar versiones anteriores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las versiones permiten comparar y revertir cambios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a design object's version history allow?","options":["Automatically deploying the oldest version to production","Deleting the object","Changing the author","Viewing and restoring earlier versions"],"explanation":"Versions allow comparing and reverting changes."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer antes de borrar un objeto de diseño?","options":["Comprobar que no tiene dependientes","Nada","Borrarlo directamente en todos los entornos a la vez","Cambiarle el nombre a \"borrar\""],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Borrar objetos usados rompe otros objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before deleting a design object?","options":["Check it has no dependents","Nothing","Delete it directly in every environment at once","Rename it to \"delete\""],"explanation":"Deleting used objects breaks others."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas ayudan a probar reglas de expresión? (Elige 2)","options":["Casos de prueba de la regla","El log de inicios de sesión de los usuarios del entorno","El AppMarket","Ejecución de pruebas en lote de la aplicación","La consola de branding"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Las reglas tienen casos de prueba que pueden ejecutarse en lote.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two tools help test expression rules? (Choose 2)","options":["Rule test cases","The environment's user login log","The AppMarket","Batch test runs for the application","The branding console"],"explanation":"Rules have test cases that can run in batch."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tienen los casos de prueba de reglas de expresión?","options":["Detectar regresiones al cambiar una regla","Mejorar el rendimiento de la regla en producción automáticamente","Sustituir las pruebas de UAT","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las pruebas guardadas verifican que el comportamiento no cambia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of expression rule test cases?","options":["Catching regressions when a rule changes","Automatically improving the rule's production performance","Replacing UAT","None"],"explanation":"Saved tests verify behavior doesn't change."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta se usa para pruebas automatizadas de interfaces de usuario de Appian?","options":["Automatización de navegador (p. ej. Selenium)","El log de expresiones","Nada","Los casos de prueba de reglas de expresión, que ejecutan las interfaces"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Appian ofrece bibliotecas para automatizar pruebas de UI.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which tool is used for automated UI tests of Appian interfaces?","options":["Browser automation (e.g. Selenium)","The expression log","Nothing","Expression rule test cases, which run the interfaces end to end"],"explanation":"Appian offers libraries to automate UI tests."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un error de diseño registrado en los logs de errores de diseño?","options":["Un objeto con una expresión o referencia inválida","Un despliegue correcto","Un usuario que ha olvidado su contraseña y no puede iniciar sesión","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los errores de diseño ayudan a detectar fallos en objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a design error recorded in the design error logs indicate?","options":["An object with an invalid expression or reference at runtime","A successful deployment","A user who forgot their password and can't log in","Nothing"],"explanation":"Design errors help detect faulty objects."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomendación aplica a las cuentas de servicio para APIs?","options":["No usarlas","Usar la cuenta de un administrador para evitar problemas de permisos","Permisos mínimos necesarios","Compartir la contraseña con todo el equipo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El principio de mínimo privilegio aplica a las cuentas de servicio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which recommendation applies to service accounts for APIs?","options":["Don't use them","Use an admin's account to avoid permission issues","Least necessary permissions","Share the password with the whole team"],"explanation":"Least privilege applies to service accounts."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se generan las claves de API para cuentas de servicio que llaman a Web APIs?","options":["En la definición de la Web API, como parámetro de texto","En la consola de administración (autenticación de Web API)","En el modelo de proceso","En una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las API keys se gestionan desde la Admin Console.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where are API keys for service accounts calling Web APIs generated?","options":["In the Web API definition, as a text parameter","In the Admin Console (Web API authentication)","In the process model","In a constant"],"explanation":"API keys are managed from the Admin Console."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene modificar objetos directamente en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Mejor control de versiones","Cambios sin probar ni trazar","Menos errores","Despliegues más seguros","Diferencias entre entornos"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Los cambios directos rompen la coherencia y la trazabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from modifying objects directly in production? (Choose 2)","options":["Better version control","Untested, untracked changes","Fewer errors","Safer deployments","Drift between environments"],"explanation":"Direct changes break consistency and traceability."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué representa una aplicación en Appian Designer?","options":["Una agrupación lógica de objetos de diseño","Un usuario","Un servidor","Un único modelo de proceso con sus interfaces"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La aplicación agrupa objetos para gestionarlos y desplegarlos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an application represent in Appian Designer?","options":["A logical grouping of design objects","A user","A server","A single process model with its interfaces"],"explanation":"The application groups objects for management and deployment."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el aviso de \"objetos que faltan\" en una aplicación (missing precedents)?","options":["Objetos usados por la aplicación que no están en ella","Objetos que han sido borrados de la base de datos","Nada","Usuarios inactivos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Añadirlos evita que falten en los paquetes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"missing precedents\" warning on an application indicate?","options":["Objects used by the app but not in it","Objects deleted from the database","Nothing","Inactive users"],"explanation":"Adding them prevents gaps in packages."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un administrador para investigar por qué un usuario no ve un registro?","options":["Revisar grupos del usuario y la seguridad del registro","Borrar el registro","Reiniciar el servidor","Dar permisos de administrador al usuario temporalmente en producción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La pertenencia a grupos y la seguridad determinan la visibilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an admin do to investigate why a user can't see a record?","options":["Review the user's groups and record security","Delete the record","Restart the server","Temporarily give the user admin rights in production"],"explanation":"Group membership and security determine visibility."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son buenas prácticas tras un despliegue a producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Modificar objetos a mano","Desactivar la monitorización","Borrar el paquete y su historial","Pruebas de humo de las funciones clave","Revisar logs y errores de procesos"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Verificar y vigilar después del despliegue detecta problemas pronto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are good practice after a production deployment? (Choose 2)","options":["Hand-editing objects","Disabling monitoring","Deleting the package and history","Smoke-testing key features","Reviewing logs and process errors"],"explanation":"Verifying and monitoring after deployment catches problems early."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un entorno de Appian en el ciclo de vida de una aplicación?","options":["Una carpeta dentro de la aplicación que contiene objetos de prueba","Un grupo","Un usuario","Una instancia independiente (dev, test, prod) con su propia configuración"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Cada entorno es una instancia separada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an Appian environment in an app's lifecycle?","options":["A folder inside the app holding test objects","A group","A user","A separate instance (dev, test, prod) with its own config"],"explanation":"Each environment is a separate instance."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué no deben incluirse credenciales reales en constantes de la aplicación?","options":["Quedan visibles y viajan en los paquetes","Porque ocupan mucho espacio","No hay problema","Porque las constantes no admiten texto con caracteres especiales"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las credenciales deben ir en connected systems o almacenes seguros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why shouldn't real credentials go in application constants?","options":["They're visible and travel in packages","Because they take up space","There's no problem","Because constants don't accept special characters"],"explanation":"Credentials belong in connected systems or secure stores."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ofrece la consola de administración respecto a la gestión de usuarios?","options":["Escribir reglas","Crear, desactivar y gestionar cuentas de usuario","Diseñar las interfaces que verán los usuarios","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los administradores gestionan cuentas desde la consola.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Admin Console offer for user management?","options":["Writing rules","Creating, deactivating and managing user accounts","Designing the interfaces users see","Nothing"],"explanation":"Admins manage accounts from the console."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con un usuario que deja la organización?","options":["Desactivarlo y reasignar su trabajo pendiente","Borrar todas sus tareas y documentos inmediatamente","Cambiarle el nombre","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Desactivar preserva el historial; el trabajo pendiente debe reasignarse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with a user leaving the organization?","options":["Deactivate them and reassign pending work","Delete all their tasks and documents immediately","Rename them","Nothing"],"explanation":"Deactivating keeps history; pending work must be reassigned."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos datos muestra la monitorización de un proceso en curso? (Elige 2)","options":["Logs de navegador","Nodos activos y completados","Valores de las variables del proceso","Las contraseñas de los usuarios asignados a las tareas","Código Java"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"La monitorización muestra el estado y los datos del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two pieces of data does monitoring a running process show? (Choose 2)","options":["Browser logs","Active and completed nodes","Process variable values","Passwords of users assigned to the tasks","Java code"],"explanation":"Monitoring shows process status and data."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite la opción \"Compare and Deploy\" frente a exportar manualmente?","options":["Nada","Borrar el destino","Desplegar sin revisión ni inspección de ningún tipo","Ver diferencias con el entorno destino antes de desplegar"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Comparar muestra qué cambia en el destino.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does \"Compare and Deploy\" offer over manual export?","options":["Nothing","Wiping the target","Deploying with no review or inspection at all","Seeing differences with the target before deploying"],"explanation":"Comparing shows what changes in the target."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomendación aplica a los paquetes de despliegue?","options":["Paquetes pequeños y frecuentes agrupados por funcionalidad","Un único paquete gigante con toda la aplicación en cada despliegue","Paquetes sin descripción","No usar paquetes"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Paquetes pequeños son más fáciles de revisar y revertir.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which recommendation applies to deployment packages?","options":["Small, frequent packages grouped by feature","One huge package with the whole app every deployment","Packages without descriptions","Not using packages"],"explanation":"Small packages are easier to review and roll back."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una caída del rendimiento general tras un despliegue?","options":["Revisar logs de rendimiento y los cambios desplegados","Borrar usuarios","Nada","Reiniciar todos los procesos activos sin investigar"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Correlacionar el cambio con los logs identifica la causa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a general performance drop after a deployment call for?","options":["Reviewing performance logs and the deployed changes","Deleting users","Nothing","Restarting every active process without investigating"],"explanation":"Correlating the change with logs finds the cause."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene programar Health Check fuera del horario laboral?","options":["Menor impacto en los usuarios","Ninguna","Que el informe se genera con datos falsos de prueba en lugar de reales","Que no hace falta revisarlo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La recopilación de datos consume recursos; mejor en horas valle.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of scheduling Health Check outside business hours?","options":["Less impact on users","None","The report uses fake test data instead of real data","No need to review it"],"explanation":"Data collection consumes resources; off-peak is better."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene documentar en cada despliegue? (Elige 2)","options":["Nada","Pasos manuales previos o posteriores","El color de la aplicación","Objetos y scripts incluidos","La contraseña del administrador del entorno"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Documentar contenido y pasos manuales hace los despliegues repetibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things should be documented for each deployment? (Choose 2)","options":["Nothing","Manual pre or post steps","App color","Included objects and scripts","The environment admin's password"],"explanation":"Documenting contents and manual steps makes deployments repeatable."}}},{"domain":"D1","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un proceso con estado \"Paused by exception\"?","options":["Que ha terminado","Que el usuario ha pausado voluntariamente la tarea para terminarla más tarde","Un nodo falló y el proceso espera intervención","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un error detiene el proceso hasta que se corrija y reanude.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a process with status \"Paused by exception\" indicate?","options":["It finished","The user voluntarily paused the task to finish it later","A node failed and the process awaits intervention","Nothing"],"explanation":"An error halts the process until fixed and resumed."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un tipo de registro (record type) en Appian?","options":["Un objeto que representa una entidad de negocio y sus datos","Un grupo","Un plug-in","Una tabla temporal que Appian crea para cada usuario al iniciar sesión"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El record type modela datos, relaciones, vistas y acciones de una entidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a record type in Appian?","options":["An object representing a business entity and its data","A group","A plug-in","A temporary table Appian creates per user at login"],"explanation":"The record type models an entity's data, relationships, views and actions."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene activar la sincronización de datos en un tipo de registro?","options":["Consultas más rápidas y funciones como relaciones y campos personalizados","Que los datos de la fuente se borran tras copiarlos a Appian","Que no hace falta base de datos","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los datos sincronizados habilitan funciones avanzadas y mejor rendimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of enabling data sync on a record type?","options":["Faster queries plus features like relationships and custom fields","Source data is deleted after copying into Appian","No database needed","None"],"explanation":"Synced data enables advanced features and better performance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Unos datos se modifican directamente en la base de datos sin pasar por Appian. ¿Qué ocurre con un registro sincronizado?","options":["Se borra","Hay que sincronizarlo para reflejar los cambios","Appian detecta el cambio al instante y lo refleja sin ninguna acción","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los cambios externos requieren sincronización programada o manual.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Data is changed directly in the database, bypassing Appian. What happens with a synced record?","options":["It's deleted","It must be synced to reflect the changes","Appian detects the change instantly with no action","Nothing"],"explanation":"External changes require scheduled or manual sync."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué forma de escribir datos mantiene actualizada automáticamente la caché de un registro sincronizado?","options":["Write Records / a!writeRecords","Un informe","Una sentencia UPDATE ejecutada directamente en la base de datos","Un correo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Escribir mediante registros actualiza la fuente y los datos sincronizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which way of writing data automatically keeps a synced record's cache updated?","options":["Write Records / a!writeRecords","A report","An UPDATE statement run directly on the database","An email"],"explanation":"Writing via records updates both source and synced data."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos se definen en las relaciones de un tipo de registro? (Elige 2)","options":["Los campos comunes que los unen","El tipo de registro relacionado","El nombre del desarrollador","El servidor","El color de la vista"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Las relaciones se definen por registro destino y campos clave.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things are defined in a record type relationship? (Choose 2)","options":["The common fields joining them","The related record type","Developer name","The server","The view's color"],"explanation":"Relationships are defined by target record and key fields."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipos de relación admite un tipo de registro?","options":["Solo jerárquicas","Ninguno","Solo muchos a muchos directos sin tabla intermedia","Uno a uno, uno a muchos y muchos a uno"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Muchos a muchos se modela con un registro intermedio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which relationship types does a record type support?","options":["Only hierarchical","None","Only direct many-to-many without a join table","One-to-one, one-to-many and many-to-one"],"explanation":"Many-to-many is modeled via an intermediate record."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se modela una relación muchos a muchos entre Proyectos y Empleados?","options":["No se puede","Con un campo de texto en Proyecto que liste los nombres separados por comas","Con un registro intermedio de asignaciones","Con dos grupos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Una tabla/registro de unión resuelve el muchos a muchos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is a many-to-many between Projects and Employees modeled?","options":["It can't be","With a text field on Project listing comma-separated names","With an intermediate assignment record","With two groups"],"explanation":"A join table/record resolves many-to-many."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un campo de registro personalizado (custom record field)?","options":["Una columna de otra base de datos","Un campo calculado a partir de otros datos del registro","Un grupo","Un campo que el usuario añade libremente en la interfaz en tiempo de ejecución"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los custom record fields calculan valores (concatenaciones, condiciones, agregados).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a custom record field?","options":["A column from another database","A field computed from other record data","A group","A field users freely add in the interface at runtime"],"explanation":"Custom record fields compute values (concatenations, conditions, aggregates)."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene un campo personalizado calculado en la sincronización frente a calcularlo en cada interfaz?","options":["Que ocupa menos espacio en la interfaz","Ninguna","Se calcula una vez y se puede filtrar y ordenar","Que se recalcula en cada clic del usuario con datos en tiempo real"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Calcular en sincronización mejora el rendimiento y permite filtrar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a sync-time custom field over computing it in each interface?","options":["It uses less interface space","None","It's computed once and can be filtered and sorted","It recalculates on each user click with real-time data"],"explanation":"Sync-time computation improves performance and enables filtering."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función se usa para consultar datos de un tipo de registro?","options":["a!save","a!queryRecordType","a!queryProcessAnalytics, que lee las tablas de registros","a!startProcess"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!queryRecordType consulta registros con filtros, campos y paginación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function queries a record type's data?","options":["a!save","a!queryRecordType","a!queryProcessAnalytics, which reads record tables","a!startProcess"],"explanation":"a!queryRecordType queries records with filters, fields and paging."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué conviene indicar solo los campos necesarios en a!queryRecordType?","options":["Porque si no se indican campos la consulta devuelve un error siempre","Reduce los datos devueltos y mejora el rendimiento","Para ocultar campos a los administradores","No importa"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Seleccionar campos limita la carga de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why specify only the needed fields in a!queryRecordType?","options":["Because without fields the query always errors","It reduces returned data and improves performance","To hide fields from administrators","It doesn't matter"],"explanation":"Selecting fields limits the data load."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué parámetro controla cuántas filas devuelve una consulta paginada?","options":["El nombre de la regla","Ninguno","El batchSize de pagingInfo","El número de campos incluidos en la consulta"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"pagingInfo define startIndex y batchSize.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which parameter controls how many rows a paged query returns?","options":["The rule's name","None","pagingInfo's batchSize","The number of fields included in the query"],"explanation":"pagingInfo defines startIndex and batchSize."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene usar registros sincronizados en grids frente a consultar entidades en cada carga? (Elige 2)","options":["Sin seguridad","Datos siempre desactualizados","Mejor rendimiento","Más código manual","Filtros y búsqueda integrados"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Los records ofrecen rendimiento y funcionalidades de grid listas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages do synced records in grids have over querying entities on each load? (Choose 2)","options":["No security","Always stale data","Better performance","More manual code","Built-in filters and search"],"explanation":"Records offer performance and ready grid features."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un CDT (Custom Data Type)?","options":["Un tipo de base de datos que Appian instala junto a la plataforma","Un grupo","Una estructura de datos definida en Appian","Un plug-in de datos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los CDT definen estructuras de datos, a menudo mapeadas a tablas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a CDT (Custom Data Type)?","options":["A database type Appian installs alongside the platform","A group","A data structure defined in Appian","A data plug-in"],"explanation":"CDTs define data structures, often mapped to tables."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un Data Store en Appian?","options":["Un grupo","Un objeto que conecta CDT con tablas de una fuente de datos","Una caché del navegador","Un almacén de documentos para guardar archivos subidos por usuarios"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El Data Store mapea entidades (CDT) a tablas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Data Store in Appian?","options":["A group","An object connecting CDTs to data source tables","A browser cache","A document store for user-uploaded files"],"explanation":"The Data Store maps entities (CDTs) to tables."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una vista de base de datos y cuándo conviene en Appian?","options":["Una consulta guardada; útil para lecturas complejas o agregadas","Una tabla que almacena físicamente copias de los datos para escribir en ella","Un tipo de interfaz","Nunca conviene"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las vistas simplifican lecturas complejas y reporting.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a database view and when is it useful in Appian?","options":["A saved query; useful for complex or aggregated reads","A table that physically stores data copies for writing","An interface type","Never useful"],"explanation":"Views simplify complex reads and reporting."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué limitación tiene normalmente una vista de base de datos usada como fuente de un registro?","options":["No puede tener más de diez columnas definidas","Suele ser de solo lectura","No puede filtrarse","No existe"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las vistas suelen usarse para lectura; escribir requiere la tabla base.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What limitation does a database view used as a record source usually have?","options":["It can't have more than ten columns","It's usually read-only","It can't be filtered","None"],"explanation":"Views are usually read; writing requires the base table."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tienen los triggers de base de datos en aplicaciones Appian?","options":["Que ralentizan el navegador","Que hacen que Appian ignore la seguridad de los registros sincronizados","Lógica oculta difícil de mantener y depurar","Ninguno"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los triggers ejecutan lógica fuera de Appian, poco visible para el equipo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of database triggers in Appian applications?","options":["They slow the browser","They make Appian ignore synced record security","Hidden logic that's hard to maintain and debug","None"],"explanation":"Triggers run logic outside Appian, invisible to the team."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuándo puede estar justificado un procedimiento almacenado en una aplicación Appian?","options":["Para mostrar una interfaz","Nunca","Operaciones masivas o complejas sobre muchas filas","Para cada lectura simple de un registro por su identificador"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los procedimientos son útiles para procesar grandes volúmenes en la BD.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When might a stored procedure be justified in an Appian application?","options":["To display an interface","Never","Bulk or complex operations over many rows","For every simple read of a record by its ID"],"explanation":"Procedures are useful for processing large volumes in the DB."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se ejecuta habitualmente un procedimiento almacenado desde Appian?","options":["Con un correo","Con a!queryRecordType indicando el nombre del procedimiento","Con el plug-in Execute Stored Procedure","No se puede"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El plug-in del AppMarket ofrece smart service y función para ello.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is a stored procedure usually executed from Appian?","options":["With an email","With a!queryRecordType passing the procedure name","With the Execute Stored Procedure plug-in","It can't be"],"explanation":"The AppMarket plug-in provides a smart service and function."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas de modelado de datos son recomendables? (Elige 2)","options":["Guardar listas en un campo de texto","Clave primaria en cada tabla","Nombres de columnas aleatorios","Normalizar para evitar duplicidades","Sin claves foráneas nunca"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Claves primarias y normalización mantienen datos consistentes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two data modeling practices are recommended? (Choose 2)","options":["Storing lists in a text field","A primary key on each table","Random column names","Normalizing to avoid duplication","Never using foreign keys"],"explanation":"Primary keys and normalization keep data consistent."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué conviene crear índices en columnas usadas a menudo en filtros?","options":["No conviene","Para ahorrar espacio","Aceleran las búsquedas en la base de datos","Porque Appian no permite filtrar columnas sin índice en ningún caso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los índices mejoran el rendimiento de consultas filtradas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why create indexes on columns often used in filters?","options":["You shouldn't","To save space","They speed up database searches","Because Appian forbids filtering unindexed columns"],"explanation":"Indexes improve filtered query performance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué contrapartida tiene crear demasiados índices?","options":["Que se borran datos","Escrituras más lentas y más almacenamiento","Que las lecturas dejan de funcionar en las tablas indexadas","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Cada índice debe mantenerse en cada escritura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the trade-off of creating too many indexes?","options":["Data gets deleted","Slower writes and more storage","Reads stop working on indexed tables","None"],"explanation":"Each index must be maintained on every write."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Una aplicación guarda el historial de cambios de estado de cada caso. ¿Cómo se modela mejor?","options":["Un grupo por estado","Una tabla de historial relacionada uno a muchos con el caso","Un campo de texto en el caso donde se concatenan todos los estados","Una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Una tabla hija permite consultar y analizar el historial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An app keeps a history of each case's status changes. How is it best modeled?","options":["A group per status","A history table related one-to-many to the case","A text field on the case concatenating every status","A constant"],"explanation":"A child table allows querying and analyzing history."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una tabla de referencia (lookup) y para qué sirve?","options":["Valores válidos (p. ej. estados) gestionables sin desplegar código","Una tabla donde se guardan los logs de errores de la aplicación","Un plug-in","Un tipo de usuario"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las tablas de referencia centralizan listas de valores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a reference (lookup) table and what is it for?","options":["Valid values (e.g. statuses) manageable without code deploys","A table storing the app's error logs","A plug-in","A user type"],"explanation":"Reference tables centralize value lists."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene guardar códigos de estado como texto libre sin tabla de referencia? (Elige 2)","options":["Menos duplicados","Consultas más fiables","Mejor integridad","Valores inconsistentes por errores de escritura","Cambios de etiqueta difíciles de aplicar"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Sin referencia, los valores se desordenan y son difíciles de mantener.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from storing status codes as free text without a lookup table? (Choose 2)","options":["Fewer duplicates","More reliable queries","Better integrity","Inconsistent values from typos","Label changes hard to apply"],"explanation":"Without a reference, values drift and are hard to maintain."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el término \"datos desnormalizados\" y cuándo puede aceptarse?","options":["Datos duplicados; aceptable en reporting para rendimiento","Datos borrados","Datos cifrados que solo puede leer el administrador del sistema","Nunca existe"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Desnormalizar puede mejorar lecturas a costa de duplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does \"denormalized data\" mean and when is it acceptable?","options":["Duplicated data; acceptable in reporting for performance","Deleted data","Encrypted data only the system admin can read","It never exists"],"explanation":"Denormalizing can speed reads at the cost of duplication."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de fuente de datos puede usar un tipo de registro en Appian?","options":["Solo hojas de cálculo subidas por los usuarios a una carpeta","Base de datos, proceso o servicio web (integración)","Solo constantes","Solo grupos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los registros pueden basarse en tablas, procesos o integraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which data source types can an Appian record type use?","options":["Only spreadsheets users upload to a folder","Database, process or web service (integration)","Only constants","Only groups"],"explanation":"Records can be based on tables, processes or integrations."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con registros cuya fuente es una integración (servicio web)?","options":["Ninguna","Depende de la disponibilidad y velocidad del servicio","Que siempre se sincronizan automáticamente cada segundo sin coste","Que no admiten seguridad"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las fuentes externas en tiempo real dependen del servicio remoto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration for records whose source is an integration (web service)?","options":["None","It depends on the service's availability and speed","They always sync automatically every second at no cost","They support no security"],"explanation":"Real-time external sources depend on the remote service."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la seguridad a nivel de registro (record-level security)?","options":["Un plug-in","Permisos que controlan quién puede editar el objeto de diseño del registro","Un tipo de log","Reglas que filtran qué filas ve cada usuario o grupo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Filtra filas según atributos del usuario o grupo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is record-level security?","options":["A plug-in","Permissions controlling who can edit the record's design object","A log type","Rules filtering which rows each user or group sees"],"explanation":"It filters rows based on user or group attributes."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene la seguridad de registros frente a filtrar en cada interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["Depende del navegador","Hay que repetirla en cada grid","Solo aplica a administradores","Se define en un solo lugar","Se aplica en cualquier consulta del registro"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"La seguridad centralizada evita fugas por olvidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages does record security have over filtering in each interface? (Choose 2)","options":["It depends on the browser","It must be repeated in every grid","It applies only to admins","It's defined in one place","It applies to any query on the record"],"explanation":"Centralized security prevents leaks from oversight."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de seguridad controla quién ve un campo concreto de un registro (p. ej. salario)?","options":["Ninguna","Seguridad a nivel de campo","Seguridad del objeto de diseño del tipo de registro","Seguridad de la carpeta"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad de campo restringe campos sensibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which security type controls who sees a specific record field (e.g. salary)?","options":["None","Field-level security","Design object security of the record type","Folder security"],"explanation":"Field-level security restricts sensitive fields."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre al consultar un registro sincronizado con seguridad de filas desde una regla ejecutada por un usuario?","options":["Nada","Solo devuelve las filas que el usuario puede ver","Devuelve todas las filas porque las reglas ignoran la seguridad","Da error siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad de registros se aplica en el contexto del usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens querying a synced record with row security from a rule run by a user?","options":["Nothing","It returns only rows the user may see","It returns every row since rules ignore security","It always errors"],"explanation":"Record security applies in the user's context."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la sincronización programada de un tipo de registro?","options":["Un proceso de usuario","Un plug-in","Una sincronización completa periódica configurada en el registro","Una copia diaria de la aplicación a otro entorno"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Mantiene los datos sincronizados alineados con la fuente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a record type's scheduled sync?","options":["A user process","A plug-in","A periodic full sync configured on the record","A daily copy of the app to another environment"],"explanation":"It keeps synced data aligned with the source."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si la tabla fuente de un registro sincronizado supera el límite de filas soportado?","options":["La sincronización falla o requiere filtros de sincronización","Se borran filas antiguas","Appian divide la tabla automáticamente en varias bases de datos","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los filtros de sincronización limitan las filas sincronizadas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if a synced record's source table exceeds the supported row limit?","options":["Sync fails or needs sync filters","Old rows are deleted","Appian automatically splits the table across databases","Nothing"],"explanation":"Sync filters limit the synced rows."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirven los filtros de sincronización (source filters) de un registro?","options":["Sincronizar solo un subconjunto de filas","Ordenar la grid","Ocultar filas a determinados usuarios en tiempo de ejecución","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Reducen el volumen sincronizado (p. ej. solo casos de los últimos años).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are a record's sync (source) filters for?","options":["Syncing only a subset of rows","Sorting the grid","Hiding rows from certain users at runtime","Nothing"],"explanation":"They cut the synced volume (e.g. only recent years' cases)."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos smart services/funciones escriben datos mediante registros? (Elige 2)","options":["Delete Records","Send E-Mail","Script task","a!queryRecordType","Write Records"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Write y Delete Records modifican datos y actualizan la sincronización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two smart services/functions write data via records? (Choose 2)","options":["Delete Records","Send E-Mail","Script task","a!queryRecordType","Write Records"],"explanation":"Write and Delete Records change data and update sync."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dato devuelve Write Records tras insertar un registro nuevo?","options":["El registro guardado, incluida su clave generada","Solo un valor booleano que indica si la escritura tuvo éxito","Nada","El número de usuarios"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El valor devuelto incluye la clave primaria generada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does Write Records return after inserting a new record?","options":["The saved record, including its generated key","Only a boolean saying whether the write succeeded","Nothing","User count"],"explanation":"The return value includes the generated primary key."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene escribir datos relacionados (padre e hijos) en una sola llamada de Write Records?","options":["Que se omiten los hijos","Ninguna","Se guardan juntos de forma consistente","Que cada hijo se guarda en una transacción separada sin relación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Escribir registros relacionados juntos simplifica y da coherencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of writing related data (parent and children) in one Write Records call?","options":["Children are skipped","None","They're saved together consistently","Each child saves in a separate unrelated transaction"],"explanation":"Writing related records together simplifies and ensures coherence."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una regla de datos de referencia en una constante y cuándo es mala idea?","options":["Siempre es buena idea","Una consulta a base de datos que se ejecuta cada vez que se usa la constante","Nunca existe","Valores fijos en una constante; malo si cambian a menudo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los valores cambiantes deben ir en tablas, no en constantes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's reference data in a constant and when is it a bad idea?","options":["Always a good idea","A DB query run every time the constant is used","It never exists","Fixed values in a constant; bad if they change often"],"explanation":"Changing values belong in tables, not constants."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de datos conviene usar para importes monetarios en la base de datos?","options":["Booleano","Fecha","Texto, para conservar el símbolo de la moneda junto al importe","Decimal con precisión fija"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los decimales evitan errores de redondeo y permiten calcular.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which data type suits monetary amounts in the database?","options":["Boolean","Date","Text, to keep the currency symbol with the amount","Fixed-precision decimal"],"explanation":"Decimals avoid rounding errors and allow calculation."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos campos de auditoría suelen añadirse a las tablas de negocio? (Elige 2)","options":["Dirección IP del servidor","Modificado por / fecha de modificación","Creado por / fecha de creación","Color favorito","Contraseña del usuario"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Los campos de auditoría registran quién y cuándo cambió los datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two audit fields are usually added to business tables? (Choose 2)","options":["Server IP address","Modified by / modified on","Created by / created on","Favorite color","User's password"],"explanation":"Audit fields record who changed data and when."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el historial de eventos de registros (record events) en Appian?","options":["Un plug-in","Registro de acciones sobre un registro para auditoría","Una interfaz","Un log del servidor con errores de sincronización exclusivamente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los record events almacenan qué pasó, quién y cuándo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Appian's record event history?","options":["A plug-in","A log of actions on a record for auditing","An interface","A server log of sync errors only"],"explanation":"Record events store what happened, by whom and when."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración tienen los documentos subidos a Appian respecto a la base de datos de negocio?","options":["Se guardan en Appian; la tabla guarda su identificador","Se almacenan en binario dentro de la tabla de negocio automáticamente","Se guardan en constantes","No se pueden subir"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Lo habitual es referenciar el documento por su ID.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How do documents uploaded to Appian relate to the business database?","options":["They're stored in Appian; the table holds their ID","They're stored as binary in the business table automatically","They're stored in constants","They can't be uploaded"],"explanation":"The usual approach is referencing the document by its ID."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene cambiar el tipo de una columna en producción sin plan de migración?","options":["Ninguno","Que la aplicación se actualiza más rápido","Más rendimiento","Pérdida o corrupción de datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los cambios de esquema necesitan scripts de migración probados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of changing a column type in production without a migration plan?","options":["None","The app updates faster","More performance","Data loss or corruption"],"explanation":"Schema changes need tested migration scripts."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta de Appian puede generar tablas a partir del diseño de un tipo de registro?","options":["Un plug-in de terceros obligatorio para cualquier tabla","La creación de tablas desde el diseñador de registros","El AppMarket","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Appian puede crear la tabla al diseñar un registro con datos gestionados por Appian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Appian tool can generate tables from a record type's design?","options":["A mandatory third-party plug-in for any table","Table creation from the record designer","The AppMarket","None"],"explanation":"Appian can create the table when designing a record with Appian-managed data."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un registro con \"sync status\" en error?","options":["Nada","Que no hay usuarios","La última sincronización falló y los datos pueden estar desactualizados","Que la sincronización ha terminado correctamente con todos los datos"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Hay que revisar la causa y volver a sincronizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a record with an error \"sync status\" indicate?","options":["Nothing","No users","The last sync failed and data may be stale","Sync finished successfully with all data"],"explanation":"Investigate the cause and resync."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos causas típicas provocan fallos de sincronización de registros? (Elige 2)","options":["Cambiar el logo","Superar los límites de filas o campos","Añadir un usuario","Cambiar el color de la vista","Cambios de esquema en la tabla fuente"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Esquema incompatible y límites superados son causas comunes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two typical causes make record sync fail? (Choose 2)","options":["Changing the logo","Exceeding row or field limits","Adding a user","Changing the view's color","Schema changes on the source table"],"explanation":"Incompatible schema and exceeded limits are common causes."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomendación aplica a la clave primaria de las tablas usadas por registros?","options":["Una clave única y estable (p. ej. entero autoincremental)","No usar clave","Usar la fecha","Usar un campo de texto descriptivo que el usuario pueda cambiar"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Claves estables y únicas evitan problemas de relaciones y sincronización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which recommendation applies to primary keys of tables used by records?","options":["A unique, stable key (e.g. auto-increment integer)","No key","The date","A descriptive text field users can change"],"explanation":"Stable, unique keys avoid relationship and sync issues."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un borrado lógico (soft delete) y por qué se usa?","options":["Un tipo de índice","Borrar la fila y todas sus filas relacionadas de forma definitiva","Nada","Marcar la fila como inactiva en vez de borrarla, para conservar historial"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El soft delete preserva datos para auditoría y relaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a soft delete and why use it?","options":["An index type","Permanently deleting the row and every related row","Nothing","Marking the row inactive instead of deleting, to keep history"],"explanation":"Soft delete preserves data for audit and relationships."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función devuelve datos de una entidad de Data Store (sin usar registros)?","options":["a!queryRecordType, indicando el nombre del Data Store como texto","a!save","a!writeToDataStoreEntity","a!queryEntity"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!queryEntity consulta entidades de Data Store.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function returns data from a Data Store entity (without records)?","options":["a!queryRecordType, passing the Data Store name as text","a!save","a!writeToDataStoreEntity","a!queryEntity"],"explanation":"a!queryEntity queries Data Store entities."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué smart service escribe un CDT en una entidad de Data Store?","options":["Send E-Mail","Write to Data Store Entity","Query Database, que también permite insertar filas","Start Process"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Write to Data Store Entity inserta o actualiza filas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which smart service writes a CDT to a Data Store entity?","options":["Send E-Mail","Write to Data Store Entity","Query Database, which also inserts rows","Start Process"],"explanation":"Write to Data Store Entity inserts or updates rows."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo decide Write to Data Store Entity si inserta o actualiza?","options":["Según el nombre del nodo del proceso que hace la escritura","Según si el valor de la clave primaria viene vacío o informado","Siempre inserta","Siempre actualiza"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Con clave vacía inserta; con clave existente actualiza.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How does Write to Data Store Entity decide whether to insert or update?","options":["By the name of the process node doing the write","By whether the primary key value is empty or set","Always inserts","Always updates"],"explanation":"An empty key inserts; an existing key updates."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos agregaciones puede calcular una consulta a registros? (Elige 2)","options":["Recuento (count)","Enviar correo","Suma (sum)","Concatenar documentos","Ordenar grupos de usuarios"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"a!aggregationFields admite count, sum, avg, min, max.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two aggregations can a record query compute? (Choose 2)","options":["Count","Send email","Sum","Concatenate documents","Sort user groups"],"explanation":"a!aggregationFields supports count, sum, avg, min, max."}}},{"