 en su zona y Appian no convierte nunca","Solo hay una zona","Appian guarda en UTC y muestra según la zona del usuario"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las fechas-hora se convierten a la zona horaria del usuario al mostrarlas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration with time zones in date-times?","options":["None","Each user stores local time and Appian never converts","There's only one zone","Appian stores UTC and displays in the user's zone"],"explanation":"Date-times are converted to the user's time zone on display."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos tipos de objetos de Appian pueden servir de fuente para una grid de solo lectura? (Elige 2)","options":["Una constante de tipo grupo","Una consulta que devuelve un DataSubset","Un modelo de proceso sin datos","Un tipo de registro","Una carpeta"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Las grids aceptan registros o conjuntos de datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian sources can feed a read-only grid? (Choose 2)","options":["A group constant","A query returning a DataSubset","A process model with no data","A record type","A folder"],"explanation":"Grids accept records or datasets."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un DataSubset?","options":["Un resultado paginado con datos, total y info de paginación","Un plug-in","Un subconjunto de usuarios de un grupo","Un log"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"DataSubset incluye data, totalCount, startIndex, batchSize.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a DataSubset?","options":["A paged result with data, total and paging info","A plug-in","A subset of a group's users","A log"],"explanation":"DataSubset includes data, totalCount, startIndex, batchSize."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Una consulta devuelve totalCount = 5000 y batchSize = 50. ¿Qué significa?","options":["Error","Hay 5000 filas en total y se han devuelto hasta 50","Que la consulta solo encontró 50 filas en total","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"totalCount es el total; batchSize limita la página.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A query returns totalCount = 5000 and batchSize = 50. What does it mean?","options":["Error","5000 rows total, up to 50 returned","The query only found 50 rows in total","Nothing"],"explanation":"totalCount is the total; batchSize limits the page."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace batchSize = -1 en pagingInfo?","options":["Error","Devuelve cero filas y solo el recuento total","Devuelve todas las filas","Una fila"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"-1 devuelve todos los resultados; usar con cuidado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does batchSize = -1 in pagingInfo do?","options":["Error","Returns zero rows and only the total count","Returns every row","One row"],"explanation":"-1 returns all results; use with care."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué riesgo tiene usar batchSize = -1 en tablas grandes?","options":["Ninguno","Que la consulta ignora los filtros indicados","Consumo de memoria y lentitud","Que se borran filas"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Traer todas las filas puede ser muy costoso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the risk of batchSize = -1 on large tables?","options":["None","The query ignores the given filters","Memory use and slowness","Rows get deleted"],"explanation":"Fetching every row can be very costly."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos operadores de filtro admite a!queryFilter? (Elige 2)","options":["\"in\"","\"send\"","\"deploy\"","\"delete\"","\"=\""],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Admite =, <>, >, <, in, not in, between, is null, etc.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two filter operators does a!queryFilter support? (Choose 2)","options":["\"in\"","\"send\"","\"deploy\"","\"delete\"","\"=\""],"explanation":"It supports =, <>, >, <, in, not in, between, is null, etc."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve el parámetro ignoreFiltersWithEmptyValues en filtros de consulta?","options":["Nada","Borrar filtros","Omitir filtros cuyo valor está vacío","Devolver error si algún filtro está vacío"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Útil para filtros opcionales de búsqueda.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does ignoreFiltersWithEmptyValues do on query filters?","options":["Nothing","Deletes filters","Skips filters whose value is empty","Returns an error if any filter is empty"],"explanation":"Useful for optional search filters."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es a!queryLogicalExpression?","options":["Combinar varios filtros con AND u OR","Un tipo de registro","Un plug-in","Una función que ordena los resultados de forma ascendente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Agrupa filtros con operadores lógicos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a!queryLogicalExpression?","options":["Combining filters with AND or OR","A record type","A plug-in","A function sorting results ascending"],"explanation":"It groups filters with logical operators."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tabla de procesos permite informar sobre tareas e instancias en curso?","options":["Ninguna","a!queryRecordType sobre una tabla de tareas que Appian crea automáticamente","Una constante","Informes de procesos (process reports) / a!queryProcessAnalytics"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los process reports consultan datos de procesos y tareas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What lets you report on in-flight tasks and process instances?","options":["None","a!queryRecordType over a task table Appian auto-creates","A constant","Process reports / a!queryProcessAnalytics"],"explanation":"Process reports query process and task data."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomendación aplica a los datos de negocio frente a variables de proceso para reporting?","options":["Reportar siempre desde las variables de proceso de las instancias","Guardarlos en documentos","Ninguna","Guardarlos en base de datos y reportar desde allí"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los datos de negocio persistidos son la fuente fiable de reporting.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which recommendation applies to business data versus process variables for reporting?","options":["Always report from process instance variables","Store it in documents","None","Store it in the database and report from there"],"explanation":"Persisted business data is the reliable reporting source."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene persistir datos en base de datos pronto en el proceso? (Elige 2)","options":["Se pueden consultar y reportar","Los datos sobreviven al archivado del proceso","Se pierden al terminar","Ocupan más memoria del motor","No se pueden filtrar"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Persistir reduce dependencia de la memoria del proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages come from persisting data to the database early in the process? (Choose 2)","options":["It can be queried and reported","Data survives process archiving","It's lost when done","It uses more engine memory","It can't be filtered"],"explanation":"Persisting reduces dependence on process memory."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay al relacionar un registro con datos de un sistema externo?","options":["Que se ignora la seguridad","Latencia y disponibilidad del sistema externo","Que Appian copia automáticamente todo el sistema externo a su base de datos","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los datos remotos dependen del rendimiento externo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration when relating a record to external system data?","options":["Security is ignored","External system latency and availability","Appian auto-copies the whole external system into its DB","None"],"explanation":"Remote data depends on external performance."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para guardar listas de valores asociados a un caso (p. ej. etiquetas)?","options":["Un único campo de texto separado por comas","Una constante","Un grupo","Una tabla hija con una fila por valor"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Una fila por valor permite filtrar y mantener integridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern stores lists of values tied to a case (e.g. tags)?","options":["A single comma-separated text field","A constant","A group","A child table with one row per value"],"explanation":"One row per value allows filtering and integrity."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de campo de registro personalizado concatena varios campos (p. ej. nombre completo)?","options":["Un plug-in","Ninguno","Una plantilla de concatenación (a!customFieldConcat)","Un campo de agregación que suma valores"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!customFieldConcat une valores de texto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which custom record field type concatenates fields (e.g. full name)?","options":["A plug-in","None","A concatenation template (a!customFieldConcat)","An aggregation field that sums values"],"explanation":"a!customFieldConcat joins text values."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de campo personalizado asigna un valor según condiciones (p. ej. prioridad Alta/Baja)?","options":["Un campo de concatenación con los valores posibles","Una constante","Un grupo","Un campo condicional (a!customFieldCondition)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!customFieldCondition evalúa condiciones para dar un valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which custom field type assigns a value by conditions (e.g. High/Low priority)?","options":["A concatenation field with the possible values","A constant","A group","A conditional field (a!customFieldCondition)"],"explanation":"a!customFieldCondition evaluates conditions to yield a value."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene definir métricas como campos personalizados del registro? (Elige 2)","options":["Se recalculan en cada clic","Reutilizables en varias interfaces","Disponibles para filtrar y ordenar","Solo para administradores","Más lentas"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Los campos personalizados centralizan la lógica.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages come from defining metrics as record custom fields? (Choose 2)","options":["Recompute on every click","Reusable across interfaces","Available for filtering and sorting","Admins only","Slower"],"explanation":"Custom fields centralize logic."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un desarrollador cambia la lógica de un campo personalizado calculado en la sincronización. ¿Qué hace falta?","options":["Reiniciar Appian","Borrar la tabla","Nada, porque se recalcula automáticamente en cada consulta","Volver a sincronizar el registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los valores calculados en sync se actualizan al resincronizar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A developer changes a sync-time custom field's logic. What's needed?","options":["Restart Appian","Drop the table","Nothing, since it recalculates on every query","Resync the record"],"explanation":"Sync-time values update on resync."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay al borrar filas de un registro con hijos relacionados?","options":["Que se duplica","Decidir qué ocurre con los hijos (borrar, conservar o impedir)","Que Appian borra siempre toda la base de datos relacionada","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Hay que definir el comportamiento en cascada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration when deleting rows of a record with related children?","options":["It duplicates","Deciding what happens to children (delete, keep or prevent)","Appian always wipes the whole related database","None"],"explanation":"Cascade behavior must be defined."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un rendimiento lento en una grid de registros con muchos campos personalizados en tiempo real?","options":["Que esos cálculos se hacen en cada consulta","Exceso de usuarios","Que la sincronización está desactivada por completo y no hay datos","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los cálculos en tiempo real tienen coste en cada carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does slowness in a record grid with many real-time custom fields indicate?","options":["Those computations run on every query","Too many users","Sync is entirely disabled and there's no data","Nothing"],"explanation":"Real-time computations cost on every load."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de registro conviene para mostrar instancias de proceso como registros?","options":["Ninguno","Un registro con fuente de base de datos que lee tablas internas de Appian","Un grupo","Un registro con fuente de proceso (process-backed)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los registros pueden basarse en procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record type suits showing process instances as records?","options":["None","A DB-backed record reading Appian's internal tables","A group","A process-backed record"],"explanation":"Records can be process-backed."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos datos conviene incluir en una tabla de auditoría de cambios? (Elige 2)","options":["El color de la interfaz","Contraseña del usuario","El tamaño de pantalla","Usuario y fecha del cambio","Valor anterior y nuevo"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"La auditoría necesita qué cambió, quién y cuándo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two pieces of data belong in a change audit table? (Choose 2)","options":["Interface color","User's password","Screen size","User and change date","Old and new value"],"explanation":"Auditing needs what changed, who and when."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para cargar un fichero CSV grande de datos en Appian?","options":["Procesarlo por lotes y validar antes de escribir","Leer todo el fichero en una variable de proceso y escribir fila a fila en un bucle de nodos","No se puede","Copiarlo a una constante"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El procesamiento por lotes limita memoria y errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for loading a large CSV data file into Appian?","options":["Process it in batches and validate before writing","Read it all into a process variable and write row by row in a node loop","It can't be done","Copy it into a constant"],"explanation":"Batch processing limits memory and errors."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error de clave duplicada al escribir en la base de datos?","options":["Que la base de datos no tiene espacio para más filas en esa tabla","Nada","Un problema de red","Se intenta insertar una clave que ya existe"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las claves únicas impiden duplicados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a duplicate key error on writing to the database indicate?","options":["The database has no room for more rows in that table","Nothing","A network problem","Inserting a key that already exists"],"explanation":"Unique keys prevent duplicates."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a separar datos de configuración de la aplicación de los datos de negocio?","options":["Tablas de configuración propias","Constantes para todo","Mezclarlos en la misma tabla con un campo tipo genérico","Ninguno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Separar configuración facilita su gestión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps separate app configuration data from business data?","options":["Dedicated configuration tables","Constants for everything","Mixing them in one table with a generic type field","None"],"explanation":"Separating configuration eases its management."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué limitación hay que tener en cuenta con relaciones entre registros sincronizados y no sincronizados?","options":["Algunas funcionalidades solo funcionan entre registros sincronizados","Ninguna","Que se duplican los datos","Que no existe ninguna diferencia funcional entre ambos tipos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Relaciones y campos personalizados requieren sincronización.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What limitation applies to relationships between synced and unsynced records?","options":["Some features only work between synced records","None","Data duplicates","There's no functional difference between the two types"],"explanation":"Relationships and custom fields require sync."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas ayudan a revisar el rendimiento de consultas a registros? (Elige 2)","options":["Los logs de rendimiento de consultas","El log de inicios de sesión","La configuración de branding","El AppMarket","La vista de rendimiento del diseñador de interfaces"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Muestran el coste de cada consulta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two tools help review record query performance? (Choose 2)","options":["Query performance logs","The login log","Branding settings","The AppMarket","The interface designer's performance view"],"explanation":"They show each query's cost."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"Un registro necesita mostrar el último comentario de cada caso. ¿Qué enfoque es eficiente?","options":["Un correo","Relación uno a muchos con orden y límite, o campo calculado","Consultar todos los comentarios de todos los casos y filtrar en la interfaz","Una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Evita traer todos los comentarios innecesariamente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A record must show each case's latest comment. Which approach is efficient?","options":["An email","A one-to-many with sort and limit, or a computed field","Query every comment of every case and filter in the interface","A constant"],"explanation":"It avoids fetching every comment needlessly."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene revisar si una escritura en base de datos falla en producción pero no en test?","options":["Diferencias de esquema o datos entre entornos","El color del tema de la aplicación en producción","El navegador del usuario","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los esquemas desalineados causan errores solo en algunos entornos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be checked if a DB write fails in production but not in test?","options":["Schema or data differences between environments","The app theme color in production","The user's browser","Nothing"],"explanation":"Misaligned schemas cause environment-specific errors."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un registro con datos gestionados por Appian (Appian-managed)?","options":["Un registro que no tiene datos y solo muestra procesos","Un plug-in","Un grupo","Appian crea y gestiona la tabla desde el diseñador del registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El diseñador de registros puede crear la tabla y su estructura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a record with Appian-managed data?","options":["A record with no data that only shows processes","A plug-in","A group","Appian creates and manages the table from the record designer"],"explanation":"The record designer can create the table and its structure."}}},{"domain":"D2","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar a!queryRecordByIdentifier para obtener un único registro?","options":["Devuelve todos los registros relacionados de la base de datos sin filtros","Ninguna","Obtiene un registro por su clave de forma directa","Escribe el registro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Es la forma directa de recuperar un registro por su identificador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a!queryRecordByIdentifier to get a single record?","options":["It returns every related record in the DB unfiltered","None","It fetches one record by key directly","It writes the record"],"explanation":"It's the direct way to fetch a record by identifier."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve a!localVariables en una interfaz?","options":["Declarar variables globales compartidas por todos los usuarios","Definir variables locales que guardan estado","Escribir en base de datos","Iniciar procesos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las variables locales mantienen estado en la interfaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a!localVariables for in an interface?","options":["Declaring global variables shared by all users","Defining local variables that hold state","Writing to the database","Starting processes"],"explanation":"Local variables hold interface state."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia hay entre una entrada de regla (rule input) y una variable local?","options":["Las locales no admiten listas","Ninguna","La variable local se pasa desde el proceso y la entrada se calcula dentro","La entrada se recibe de fuera; la local se define dentro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los rule inputs son parámetros; las locales son internas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the difference between a rule input and a local variable?","options":["Locals don't support lists","None","A local is passed from the process and an input is computed inside","An input comes from outside; a local is defined inside"],"explanation":"Rule inputs are parameters; locals are internal."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace a!save en un componente de interfaz?","options":["Despliega la interfaz","Guarda un valor en una variable al interactuar","Guarda los datos en la base de datos automáticamente","Envía un correo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!save actualiza variables en saveInto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!save do in an interface component?","options":["Deploys the interface","Saves a value to a variable on interaction","Saves data to the database automatically","Sends an email"],"explanation":"a!save updates variables in saveInto."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace a!refreshVariable con refreshOnVarChange?","options":["Nada","Recalcula la variable cada segundo aunque no cambie nada","Borra la variable","Recalcula la variable cuando cambian otras variables indicadas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"refreshOnVarChange controla cuándo se recalcula una local.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!refreshVariable with refreshOnVarChange do?","options":["Nothing","Recomputes the variable every second even if nothing changes","Deletes the variable","Recomputes the variable when listed variables change"],"explanation":"refreshOnVarChange controls when a local recomputes."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones puede realizar el parámetro saveInto de un botón? (Elige 2)","options":["Crear usuarios en la consola","Instalar plug-ins","Ejecutar escrituras con a!writeRecords","Cambiar el código de la interfaz","Guardar valores en variables locales"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"saveInto puede actualizar variables y ejecutar smart services permitidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things can a button's saveInto do? (Choose 2)","options":["Create users in the console","Install plug-ins","Run writes with a!writeRecords","Change the interface's code","Save values to local variables"],"explanation":"saveInto can update variables and run allowed smart services."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué no se deben ejecutar consultas costosas directamente dentro de a!forEach en una interfaz?","options":["No hay problema","Se ejecuta una consulta por elemento","Porque bloquea el navegador permanentemente","Porque a!forEach no admite llamadas a reglas dentro del bucle"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Consultas en bucle multiplican el coste; mejor una consulta conjunta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why shouldn't costly queries run directly inside a!forEach in an interface?","options":["No problem","One query runs per item","Because it permanently locks the browser","Because a!forEach doesn't allow rule calls inside the loop"],"explanation":"Queries in loops multiply cost; use one combined query."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se recomienda para interfaces reutilizables?","options":["Ninguno","Copiar y pegar el mismo código en cada interfaz que lo necesite","Usar solo interfaces enormes","Componentes en reglas de interfaz con entradas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los componentes reutilizables reducen duplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern is recommended for reusable interfaces?","options":["None","Copy-paste the same code into each interface needing it","Only huge interfaces","Components as interface rules with inputs"],"explanation":"Reusable components reduce duplication."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué parámetro de un campo muestra un error de validación al usuario?","options":["validations","instructions","required, que muestra el mensaje personalizado del error","label"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"validations devuelve mensajes de error del campo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which field parameter shows a validation error to the user?","options":["validations","instructions","required, which shows the custom error message","label"],"explanation":"validations returns the field's error messages."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve el parámetro validationGroup en botones y campos?","options":["Nada","Agrupar campos visualmente en secciones","Validar solo ciertos campos según el botón pulsado","Definir seguridad"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Permite que distintos botones validen distintos campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is the validationGroup parameter on buttons and fields for?","options":["Nothing","Grouping fields visually into sections","Validating only some fields depending on the button","Defining security"],"explanation":"It lets different buttons validate different fields."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas de UX son recomendables en formularios Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Errores sin mensaje","Mostrar solo los campos relevantes con showWhen","Etiquetas técnicas","Agrupar campos relacionados en secciones","Mostrar todos los campos siempre"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Organización y visibilidad condicional mejoran la experiencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two UX practices are recommended in Appian forms? (Choose 2)","options":["Errors with no message","Show only relevant fields with showWhen","Technical labels","Group related fields into sections","Always show every field"],"explanation":"Organization and conditional visibility improve the experience."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene el diseño de interfaces con Appian Design System / patrones?","options":["Que las interfaces se generan sin necesidad de ninguna regla ni dato","Más lentitud","Coherencia visual y buenas prácticas listas","Ninguna"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los patrones aceleran y homogeneizan el diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of designing interfaces with the Appian design system/patterns?","options":["Interfaces generate with no rules or data at all","More slowness","Visual consistency and ready best practices","None"],"explanation":"Patterns speed up and standardize design."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de acción de registro abre un formulario para crear un nuevo registro?","options":["Un grupo","Acción relacionada, que solo actúa sobre un registro existente","Acción de lista de registros (record list action)","Un informe"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las acciones de lista crean registros nuevos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record action type opens a form to create a new record?","options":["A group","Related action, which only acts on an existing record","Record list action","A report"],"explanation":"List actions create new records."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de acción de registro actúa sobre un registro concreto (p. ej. \"Aprobar\")?","options":["Un temporizador","Un plug-in","Acción de lista de registros, visible sobre la grid completa","Acción relacionada (related action)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las related actions operan en el contexto de un registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record action type acts on a specific record (e.g. \"Approve\")?","options":["A timer","A plug-in","Record list action, shown above the whole grid","Related action"],"explanation":"Related actions operate in a record's context."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué controla la visibilidad de una acción de registro para ciertos usuarios o estados?","options":["Nada","El nombre del proceso","La configuración de seguridad/visibilidad de la acción","El color del botón de la acción en la vista de resumen"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las acciones tienen condiciones de visibilidad y seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What controls a record action's visibility for certain users or statuses?","options":["Nothing","The process name","The action's security/visibility settings","The action button's color in the summary view"],"explanation":"Actions have visibility and security conditions."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué convención de nombres se recomienda para objetos de Appian?","options":["Prefijo de aplicación y nombre descriptivo","Nombres cortos y genéricos como \"regla1\" para escribir menos","Solo números","Nombres aleatorios"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Ejemplo: ABC_getCaseById.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which naming convention is recommended for Appian objects?","options":["App prefix and a descriptive name","Short generic names like \"rule1\" to type less","Numbers only","Random names"],"explanation":"Example: ABC_getCaseById."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto se usa para valores fijos reutilizados (p. ej. un grupo o un estado)?","options":["Variable local, definida en cada interfaz que la necesite","Proceso","Constante","Carpeta"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las constantes evitan valores codificados repetidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object type is used for reused fixed values (e.g. a group or status)?","options":["A local variable defined in each interface needing it","Process","Constant","Folder"],"explanation":"Constants avoid repeated hardcoded values."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué problema tiene codificar un ID de grupo directamente en varias reglas?","options":["Que el grupo deja de existir cuando se despliega la regla","Mejora el rendimiento","Ninguno","Cambia entre entornos y obliga a editar muchos objetos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Usar una constante centraliza el valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's wrong with hardcoding a group ID in several rules?","options":["The group stops existing when the rule is deployed","It improves performance","Nothing","It differs across environments and forces many edits"],"explanation":"Using a constant centralizes the value."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos objetos deben tener seguridad configurada explícitamente? (Elige 2)","options":["Parámetros de funciones","Modelos de proceso","Variables locales","Comentarios de código","Tipos de registro"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Los objetos de diseño requieren roles de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two objects must have security explicitly configured? (Choose 2)","options":["Function parameters","Process models","Local variables","Code comments","Record types"],"explanation":"Design objects require security roles."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué rol de un modelo de proceso permite iniciar procesos pero no editarlo?","options":["Initiator","Viewer","Administrador","Editor, que permite iniciar pero no modificar el modelo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Initiator puede iniciar instancias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process model role allows starting processes but not editing it?","options":["Initiator","Viewer","Administrator","Editor, which allows starting but not modifying the model"],"explanation":"Initiator can start instances."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el rol Manager en un modelo de proceso?","options":["Nada","Editar el diseño del modelo pero no ver las instancias","Gestionar instancias (p. ej. reasignar o cancelar) sin editar el diseño","Borrar el modelo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Manager administra instancias en curso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Manager role allow on a process model?","options":["Nothing","Editing the model's design but not seeing instances","Managing instances (e.g. reassign or cancel) without editing design","Deleting the model"],"explanation":"Manager administers running instances."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el encadenamiento de actividades (activity chaining)?","options":["Un plug-in","Ejecutar varios procesos en paralelo para mejorar el rendimiento","Pasar al usuario de una tarea a la siguiente sin volver a la lista","Un tipo de log"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Mejora la experiencia cuando un usuario completa pasos seguidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is activity chaining?","options":["A plug-in","Running several processes in parallel for performance","Taking the user from one task to the next without returning to the list","A log type"],"explanation":"It improves UX when a user completes consecutive steps."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuándo NO conviene usar activity chaining?","options":["Siempre conviene","Entre pasos largos o de distintos usuarios","Entre un formulario y su confirmación inmediata para el mismo usuario","Nunca existe"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Encadenar en exceso afecta al rendimiento y no aplica entre usuarios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When should activity chaining NOT be used?","options":["It's always fine","Across long steps or different users","Between a form and its immediate confirmation for the same user","It doesn't exist"],"explanation":"Excessive chaining hurts performance and doesn't apply across users."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene incluir en un modelo de proceso robusto? (Elige 2)","options":["Flujos de excepción","Nodos sin conexión","Variables sin uso","Bucles infinitos","Gestión de errores en integraciones"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Excepciones y errores deben estar previstos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements belong in a robust process model? (Choose 2)","options":["Exception flows","Disconnected nodes","Unused variables","Infinite loops","Error handling on integrations"],"explanation":"Exceptions and errors must be planned for."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se recomienda para modelos de proceso con mucha lógica repetida?","options":["Copiar los nodos en cada modelo que la necesite","Hacer un único proceso gigante","Ninguno","Extraerla a subprocesos reutilizables"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los subprocesos reutilizan lógica y simplifican modelos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's recommended for process models with much repeated logic?","options":["Copy the nodes into each model needing them","One giant process","None","Extract it into reusable subprocesses"],"explanation":"Subprocesses reuse logic and simplify models."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace a!startProcess desde una interfaz?","options":["Nada","Borra un proceso","Inicia un proceso desde un saveInto","Muestra el diagrama del proceso en la interfaz"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!startProcess lanza un proceso desde una interacción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!startProcess do from an interface?","options":["Nothing","Deletes a process","Starts a process from a saveInto","Shows the process diagram in the interface"],"explanation":"a!startProcess launches a process from an interaction."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene escribir datos con a!writeRecords desde la interfaz frente a iniciar un proceso?","options":["Que permite tareas humanas y aprobaciones posteriores","Ninguna","Que ignora la seguridad","Más ligero para escrituras simples"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Para operaciones simples evita la sobrecarga de un proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of writing with a!writeRecords from the interface over starting a process?","options":["It enables later human tasks and approvals","None","It ignores security","Lighter for simple writes"],"explanation":"For simple operations it avoids process overhead."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuándo conviene usar un proceso en lugar de escribir directamente desde la interfaz?","options":["Cuando hay tareas, aprobaciones o pasos asíncronos","Para cualquier cambio, incluso actualizar un único campo sin reglas","Nunca","Solo para lecturas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los procesos orquestan flujos con personas y sistemas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"When should a process be used instead of writing directly from the interface?","options":["When there are tasks, approvals or async steps","For any change, even a single field update with no rules","Never","Only for reads"],"explanation":"Processes orchestrate flows with people and systems."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un sitio (site) en Appian?","options":["Un grupo","Un servidor de Appian dedicado a un departamento","Un log","Una interfaz de navegación con páginas para un rol"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los sitios ofrecen experiencias enfocadas por rol.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a site in Appian?","options":["A group","An Appian server dedicated to a department","A log","A navigation interface with pages for a role"],"explanation":"Sites offer role-focused experiences."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos tipos de contenido puede tener una página de un sitio? (Elige 2)","options":["Una lista de registros","Un data store","Una constante","Una interfaz o informe","Un modelo de proceso editable"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Las páginas muestran registros, interfaces, informes o acciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two content types can a site page have? (Choose 2)","options":["A record list","A data store","A constant","An interface or report","An editable process model"],"explanation":"Pages show records, interfaces, reports or actions."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer para que una interfaz muestre opciones distintas según el grupo del usuario?","options":["Usar a!isUserMemberOfGroup con showWhen","Nada","Crear una interfaz completamente distinta por cada usuario","Usar colores"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La visibilidad condicional por grupo personaliza la interfaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How can an interface show different options depending on the user's group?","options":["Use a!isUserMemberOfGroup with showWhen","Nothing","Create an entirely different interface per user","Use colors"],"explanation":"Group-based conditional visibility personalizes the interface."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué ocultar un botón en la interfaz no basta como medida de seguridad?","options":["Porque el navegador muestra siempre los botones ocultos al usuario","Porque los botones no se pueden ocultar","Los datos y acciones deben protegerse en el servidor también","Sí basta"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La seguridad real se aplica en registros, procesos y objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why isn't hiding a button in the interface enough as security?","options":["Because browsers always show hidden buttons","Because buttons can't be hidden","Data and actions must also be protected server-side","It is enough"],"explanation":"Real security is enforced on records, processes and objects."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón ayuda a cumplir una historia que requiere confirmación antes de una acción destructiva?","options":["Ejecutar la acción y permitir deshacerla enviando un correo a soporte","Ocultar la acción","Nada","Un diálogo de confirmación en la acción"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las confirmaciones evitan errores irreversibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern helps satisfy a story needing confirmation before a destructive action?","options":["Run it and allow undo by emailing support","Hiding the action","Nothing","A confirmation dialog on the action"],"explanation":"Confirmations prevent irreversible mistakes."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente se usa para dividir un formulario en columnas?","options":["a!columnsLayout","a!gridField","a!buttonLayout","a!sectionLayout, que crea columnas automáticamente"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"columnsLayout organiza contenido en columnas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component splits a form into columns?","options":["a!columnsLayout","a!gridField","a!buttonLayout","a!sectionLayout, which auto-creates columns"],"explanation":"columnsLayout arranges content in columns."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente muestra un conjunto de tarjetas con contenido destacado?","options":["a!cardLayout","a!paragraphField con estilo de tarjeta","a!dateField","a!dropdownField"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"cardLayout agrupa contenido en tarjetas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component shows a set of cards with highlighted content?","options":["a!cardLayout","a!paragraphField with card styling","a!dateField","a!dropdownField"],"explanation":"cardLayout groups content into cards."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos parámetros ayudan a la accesibilidad de un campo? (Elige 2)","options":["label","showWhen = false siempre","style con colores aleatorios","ninguno","accessibilityText"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Etiquetas y textos de accesibilidad ayudan a lectores de pantalla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two parameters help a field's accessibility? (Choose 2)","options":["label","Always showWhen = false","Random-color style","none","accessibilityText"],"explanation":"Labels and accessibility text help screen readers."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con el texto visible de la interfaz en aplicaciones multilingües?","options":["Usar paquetes de traducción (translation sets) o constantes de texto","Escribir el texto en cada idioma dentro de cada componente con if","Nada","Solo un idioma"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los translation sets centralizan textos traducibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How should visible interface text be handled in multilingual apps?","options":["Use translation sets or text constants","Write each language inside each component with if","Nothing","One language only"],"explanation":"Translation sets centralize translatable text."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una regla de expresión (expression rule)?","options":["Lógica reutilizable que devuelve un valor","Un documento","Una interfaz que el usuario rellena para iniciar un proceso","Un grupo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las reglas encapsulan lógica reutilizable.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an expression rule?","options":["Reusable logic that returns a value","A document","An interface users fill in to start a process","A group"],"explanation":"Rules encapsulate reusable logic."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene que una regla de expresión haga una sola cosa?","options":["Que se ejecuta en paralelo automáticamente","Más fácil de probar y reutilizar","Ninguna","Que no necesita entradas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Reglas pequeñas y enfocadas son más mantenibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of an expression rule doing one thing?","options":["It runs in parallel automatically","Easier to test and reuse","None","It needs no inputs"],"explanation":"Small, focused rules are more maintainable."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas mejoran la legibilidad de expresiones complejas? (Elige 2)","options":["Variables locales con nombres claros","Nombres de una letra","Anidar diez if","Todo en una línea","Comentarios en el código"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Nombres claros y comentarios facilitan la lectura.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices improve complex expression readability? (Choose 2)","options":["Clearly named local variables","One-letter names","Nesting ten ifs","Everything on one line","Code comments"],"explanation":"Clear names and comments ease reading."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función evalúa varias condiciones y devuelve el valor de la primera verdadera?","options":["a!match o if anidados (choose/match)","a!save","a!localVariables","a!forEach, que recorre condiciones y devuelve la última"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"a!match simplifica múltiples condiciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function evaluates several conditions and returns the first true one's value?","options":["a!match or nested if","a!save","a!localVariables","a!forEach, which loops conditions and returns the last"],"explanation":"a!match simplifies multiple conditions."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función se usa para comprobar si un valor es nulo o vacío?","options":["len","a!isNullOrEmpty","a!save","len, que devuelve verdadero cuando el valor no tiene caracteres"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!isNullOrEmpty cubre nulos, cadenas y listas vacías.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function checks if a value is null or empty?","options":["len","a!isNullOrEmpty","a!save","len, which returns true when the value has no characters"],"explanation":"a!isNullOrEmpty covers nulls, empty strings and lists."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función devuelve un valor por defecto cuando otro es nulo?","options":["a!isNullOrEmpty, que devuelve el segundo argumento","a!defaultValue","index","a!save"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!defaultValue devuelve el primer valor no nulo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function returns a default when another value is null?","options":["a!isNullOrEmpty, which returns the second argument","a!defaultValue","index","a!save"],"explanation":"a!defaultValue returns the first non-null value."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace la función index(lista, 3, null)?","options":["Devuelve los tres primeros elementos de la lista","Devuelve el tercer elemento o null si no existe","Borra el elemento","Error"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"index accede de forma segura con valor por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does index(list, 3, null) do?","options":["Returns the first three items of the list","Returns the third item or null if absent","Deletes the item","Error"],"explanation":"index accesses safely with a default."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función recorre una lista aplicando una expresión a cada elemento?","options":["a!save","a!forEach","a!match","a!localVariables, que itera sobre sus variables"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!forEach usa fv!item y fv!index.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function loops a list applying an expression to each item?","options":["a!save","a!forEach","a!match","a!localVariables, which iterates its variables"],"explanation":"a!forEach uses fv!item and fv!index."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos variables de función están disponibles dentro de a!forEach? (Elige 2)","options":["fv!item","fv!user","ri!index","fv!index","pv!item"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"a!forEach expone fv!item, fv!index, fv!isFirst, fv!isLast, etc.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two function variables are available inside a!forEach? (Choose 2)","options":["fv!item","fv!user","ri!index","fv!index","pv!item"],"explanation":"a!forEach exposes fv!item, fv!index, fv!isFirst, fv!isLast, etc."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un objeto de tipo Decision en Appian?","options":["Un grupo","Una carpeta","Una tabla de reglas que devuelve resultados según entradas","Un nodo XOR dentro de un modelo de proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las decisiones modelan reglas tabulares.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Decision object in Appian?","options":["A group","A folder","A rule table returning outputs from inputs","An XOR node inside a process model"],"explanation":"Decisions model tabular rules."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene una Decision frente a un if anidado largo? (Elige 2)","options":["Reglas visibles en formato tabla","Solo admite una regla","Sin pruebas","Más fácil de mantener por cambios de negocio","Más difícil de leer"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Las tablas de decisión son claras y mantenibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages does a Decision have over a long nested if? (Choose 2)","options":["Rules visible as a table","Supports only one rule","No testing","Easier to maintain for business changes","Harder to read"],"explanation":"Decision tables are clear and maintainable."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto almacena un documento de plantilla para generar PDFs?","options":["Una constante de texto con el contenido completo del PDF","Un documento en una carpeta de la aplicación","Un grupo","Un proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las plantillas se guardan como documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object stores a template document for generating PDFs?","options":["A text constant with the full PDF content","A document in an app folder","A group","A process"],"explanation":"Templates are stored as documents."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomendación aplica a la estructura de carpetas de documentos?","options":["Sin carpetas","Carpetas con seguridad por grupo según el tipo de documento","Una sola carpeta con acceso público para todos los documentos","Una carpeta por usuario siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La seguridad de carpetas controla el acceso a documentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which recommendation applies to document folder structure?","options":["No folders","Folders with group security by document type","One folder with public access for all documents","Always one folder per user"],"explanation":"Folder security controls document access."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"Una historia pide que el solicitante vea el estado de su solicitud. ¿Qué diseño es adecuado?","options":["Un plug-in","Nada","Un correo diario con el estado de todas las solicitudes de la empresa","Una vista de registro con estado y seguridad por solicitante"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El registro con seguridad muestra solo sus solicitudes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A story asks that requesters see their request's status. What design fits?","options":["A plug-in","Nothing","A daily email with every company request's status","A record view with status and per-requester security"],"explanation":"A secured record shows only their requests."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos revisa un desarrollador senior en una revisión de código Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Rendimiento de consultas","Seguridad de objetos y datos","Nada","La fecha de nacimiento del autor","El color favorito del autor"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Rendimiento y seguridad son claves en revisiones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two aspects does a senior developer check in an Appian code review? (Choose 2)","options":["Query performance","Object and data security","Nothing","The author's birthdate","The author's favorite color"],"explanation":"Performance and security are key in reviews."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tienen los casos de prueba guardados en reglas antes de refactorizar?","options":["Que la refactorización se aplica automáticamente","Verificar que el comportamiento no cambia","Que eliminan la necesidad de revisión","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las pruebas son la red de seguridad del refactor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of saved rule test cases before refactoring?","options":["The refactor is applied automatically","Verifying behavior doesn't change","They remove the need for review","None"],"explanation":"Tests are the refactor's safety net."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente de grid permite seleccionar filas para una acción en lote?","options":["Una grid con selección habilitada (selectable)","Un gráfico","Un a!paragraphField con los identificadores separados por comas","Ninguno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las grids de solo lectura admiten selección.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which grid feature allows selecting rows for a bulk action?","options":["A grid with selection enabled (selectable)","A chart","An a!paragraphField with comma-separated IDs","None"],"explanation":"Read-only grids support selection."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se recomienda para mostrar datos de solo lectura de un registro relacionado dentro de un formulario?","options":["Un correo","Copiar sus datos en variables de proceso al iniciar el proceso y no actualizarlos","Ninguno","Consultarlo con su relación y mostrarlo sin edición"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Consultar en tiempo real evita datos obsoletos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern is recommended to show read-only related record data within a form?","options":["An email","Copy its data into process variables at start and never refresh","None","Query it via its relationship and show it read-only"],"explanation":"Querying live avoids stale data."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un portal de Appian y qué consideración de diseño tiene?","options":["Un plug-in","Un log","Un sitio interno que comparte la sesión de los usuarios de Appian","Una interfaz pública para externos; usa cuenta de servicio"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los portales se ejecutan con una cuenta de servicio y requieren diseño cuidadoso de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an Appian portal and what design consideration does it have?","options":["A plug-in","A log","An internal site sharing Appian users' sessions","A public interface for externals; runs as a service account"],"explanation":"Portals run as a service account and need careful security design."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una regla de interfaz (interface) con entradas de regla en Appian?","options":["Un grupo","Una constante","Una interfaz reutilizable que recibe datos por parámetros","Una interfaz que solo puede usarse dentro de un único modelo de proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las entradas permiten reutilizar la interfaz en contextos distintos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's an interface with rule inputs in Appian?","options":["A group","A constant","A reusable interface receiving data via parameters","An interface usable only within one process model"],"explanation":"Inputs allow reusing the interface in different contexts."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo pasa datos una tarea de usuario a su interfaz?","options":["Por correo","Mapeando variables de proceso a entradas de regla","No se puede","Mediante constantes globales que la interfaz lee al cargarse"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las entradas de la interfaz se mapean a pv o ac.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How does a user task pass data to its interface?","options":["By email","Mapping process variables to rule inputs","It can't","Via global constants the interface reads on load"],"explanation":"Interface inputs are mapped to pvs or acps."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con un valor guardado en una entrada de regla desde una tarea al enviar el formulario?","options":["Se guarda en la base de datos automáticamente","Se pierde, porque las entradas de regla son siempre de solo lectura","Nada","Se devuelve al proceso a través de la variable mapeada"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las entradas mapeadas devuelven valores al proceso al enviar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to a value saved into a rule input from a task on submit?","options":["It's saved to the DB automatically","It's lost, since rule inputs are always read-only","Nothing","It returns to the process via the mapped variable"],"explanation":"Mapped inputs return values to the process on submit."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de botón envía el formulario de una tarea?","options":["Un icono","Un botón con submit = true","Un enlace","Un botón con validate = false y sin saveInto"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"submit = true completa la tarea.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which kind of button submits a task form?","options":["An icon","A button with submit = true","A link","A button with validate = false and no saveInto"],"explanation":"submit = true completes the task."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el parámetro skipValidation de un botón?","options":["Nada","Enviar sin ejecutar validaciones (p. ej. Cancelar)","Borrar el formulario","Validar dos veces los campos obligatorios antes de enviar"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Útil para cancelar sin exigir campos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a button's skipValidation allow?","options":["Nothing","Submitting without validations (e.g. Cancel)","Clearing the form","Validating required fields twice before submit"],"explanation":"Useful for cancel without requiring fields."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas mejoran el diseño de un modelo de proceso? (Elige 2)","options":["Nombres descriptivos de nodos","Variables con nombres x1, x2","Un solo nodo gigante","Carriles por rol","Nodos sin conectar"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Claridad en nombres y carriles facilita el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices improve a process model's design? (Choose 2)","options":["Descriptive node names","Variables named x1, x2","One giant node","Lanes by role","Disconnected nodes"],"explanation":"Clear names and lanes ease maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que una variable de proceso está marcada como parámetro?","options":["Nada","Que se muestra a todos los usuarios en la lista de tareas","Que es una constante","Puede recibir un valor al iniciar el proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los parámetros se rellenan al iniciar el proceso o subproceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does marking a process variable as a parameter mean?","options":["Nothing","It's shown to every user in the task list","It's a constant","It can receive a value when the process starts"],"explanation":"Parameters are filled on process or subprocess start."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una variable de actividad (ac!) en un nodo?","options":["Un grupo","Una variable local del nodo para entradas y salidas","Una variable global compartida por todos los procesos del sistema","Un log"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las ac! existen en el contexto del nodo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an activity class variable (ac!) on a node?","options":["A group","A node-local variable for inputs and outputs","A global variable shared by every process in the system","A log"],"explanation":"ac! variables live in the node's context."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con los datos de salida de un nodo de integración?","options":["Nada","Ignorar el resultado porque Appian reintenta siempre automáticamente","Borrarlos","Guardar el resultado y comprobar si hubo error"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Hay que manejar resultado y errores de la integración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with an integration node's outputs?","options":["Nothing","Ignore them since Appian always retries automatically","Delete them","Save the result and check for errors"],"explanation":"Integration results and errors must be handled."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para que un proceso espere a que otro sistema confirme una operación?","options":["Nada","Un bucle de nodos script que comprueba el estado cada segundo","Un correo","Un evento de recepción de mensaje o una tarea que espera señal"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los eventos evitan bucles costosos de sondeo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern makes a process wait for another system to confirm an operation?","options":["Nothing","A loop of script nodes polling status every second","An email","A receive message event or a task awaiting a signal"],"explanation":"Events avoid costly polling loops."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos tipos de asignación admite una tarea de usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["A una constante de texto libre","A un grupo","A un usuario","A una carpeta","A un documento"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Las tareas se asignan a usuarios o grupos (directos o por expresión).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two assignment types does a user task support? (Choose 2)","options":["To a free text constant","To a group","To a user","To a folder","To a document"],"explanation":"Tasks go to users or groups (directly or by expression)."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre cuando una tarea se asigna a un grupo?","options":["Cualquier miembro puede aceptarla y completarla","Todos los miembros deben completarla para que avance el proceso","Se asigna al primer usuario alfabéticamente","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los miembros del grupo pueden aceptarla; uno la completa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens when a task is assigned to a group?","options":["Any member can accept and complete it","Every member must complete it for the process to continue","It goes to the alphabetically first user","Nothing"],"explanation":"Group members can accept it; one completes it."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué funcionalidad permite que una tarea se reasigne automáticamente si no se completa en un plazo?","options":["Activity chaining entre la tarea y la siguiente","Una constante","Escalados de la tarea","Un informe"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los escalados pueden reasignar, notificar o ejecutar acciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which feature automatically reassigns a task not completed by a deadline?","options":["Activity chaining between the task and the next","A constant","Task escalations","A report"],"explanation":"Escalations can reassign, notify or act."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de nodo permite ejecutar la misma tarea para cada elemento de una lista?","options":["Nada","Un subproceso único","Multiple Node Instances (MNI)","Un nodo AND con tantas ramas como elementos haya en la lista"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"MNI crea una instancia del nodo por elemento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which node feature runs the same task for each list item?","options":["Nothing","A single subprocess","Multiple Node Instances (MNI)","An AND node with as many branches as list items"],"explanation":"MNI creates one node instance per item."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con MNI sobre listas muy grandes?","options":["Que se ejecutan siempre en un solo hilo sin límite de tamaño","Que no funciona con grupos","Ninguna","Existe un límite de instancias y consume memoria"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Para volúmenes grandes conviene procesar por lotes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration with MNI over very large lists?","options":["They always run single-threaded with no size limit","It doesn't work with groups","None","There's an instance limit and it uses memory"],"explanation":"For large volumes, batch processing is advisable."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para procesar 50.000 registros desde un proceso?","options":["Un MNI con 50.000 instancias del mismo nodo","Procesarlos por lotes o con operaciones en base de datos","Un bucle de nodos fila a fila","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Lotes o procesamiento en BD evitan sobrecargar el motor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits processing 50,000 records from a process?","options":["An MNI with 50,000 instances of the node","Batch them or use database operations","A row-by-row node loop","Nothing"],"explanation":"Batches or DB processing avoid overloading the engine."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos objetos componen típicamente una acción de registro? (Elige 2)","options":["Un modelo de proceso","Un log","Una interfaz de inicio (start form)","Un grupo vacío","Una carpeta"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"La acción inicia un proceso con su formulario de inicio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two objects typically make up a record action? (Choose 2)","options":["A process model","A log","A start form interface","An empty group","A folder"],"explanation":"The action starts a process with its start form."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de vista de registro muestra la información principal de un registro?","options":["Un grupo","Un log","Vista de lista de registros, que muestra todos los registros","Vista de resumen (summary view)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La vista de resumen es la página principal del registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which record view shows a record's main information?","options":["A group","A log","The record list view, which shows every record","Summary view"],"explanation":"The summary view is the record's main page."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve el encabezado (header) de un registro?","options":["Nada","Definir relaciones","Mostrar título, datos clave y acciones de forma consistente","Configurar la seguridad de filas del registro"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El header da contexto en todas las vistas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a record header for?","options":["Nothing","Defining relationships","Showing title, key data and actions consistently","Configuring the record's row security"],"explanation":"The header gives context across views."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de filtro permite a los usuarios filtrar una lista de registros?","options":["Filtros de sincronización del origen de datos","Constantes","Nada","Filtros de usuario del tipo de registro"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los user filters aparecen en la lista de registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which filter type lets users filter a record list?","options":["Data source sync filters","Constants","Nothing","Record type user filters"],"explanation":"User filters appear on the record list."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos formas tiene un usuario de llegar a un registro concreto? (Elige 2)","options":["Desde la consola de administración","Desde los logs","Desde la lista de registros","Desde el AppMarket","Desde un enlace a registro en otra interfaz"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Listas y enlaces (a!recordLink) llevan a registros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two ways can a user reach a specific record? (Choose 2)","options":["From the Admin Console","From logs","From the record list","From the AppMarket","From a record link in another interface"],"explanation":"Lists and links (a!recordLink) lead to records."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente crea un enlace a la vista de un registro?","options":["a!startProcess","a!recordLink","a!save","a!dynamicLink, que solo abre registros en otra pestaña"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"a!recordLink navega a un registro y vista.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component creates a link to a record's view?","options":["a!startProcess","a!recordLink","a!save","a!dynamicLink, which only opens records in a new tab"],"explanation":"a!recordLink navigates to a record and view."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace a!dynamicLink?","options":["Nada","Borra datos","Ejecuta saveInto al hacer clic, sin navegar","Abre siempre una URL externa en una ventana nueva"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los dynamic links actualizan variables en la interfaz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!dynamicLink do?","options":["Nothing","Deletes data","Runs saveInto on click, without navigating","Always opens an external URL in a new window"],"explanation":"Dynamic links update variables in the interface."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar a!recordActionField para mostrar acciones en una interfaz?","options":["Que es más rápido que un botón","Que permite ejecutar cualquier acción sin comprobar permisos","Ninguna","Respeta la seguridad y visibilidad de la acción"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las acciones de registro mantienen su configuración de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a!recordActionField to show actions in an interface?","options":["It's faster than a button","It runs any action without checking permissions","None","It honors the action's security and visibility"],"explanation":"Record actions keep their security configuration."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se recomienda para formularios de creación y edición del mismo registro?","options":["Ninguno","Dos interfaces copiadas idénticas que se mantienen por separado","Una interfaz reutilizable con un indicador de modo","Una interfaz por usuario"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reutilizar reduce duplicación y errores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern is recommended for create and edit forms of the same record?","options":["None","Two identical copied interfaces maintained separately","One reusable interface with a mode flag","One interface per user"],"explanation":"Reuse cuts duplication and errors."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos componen una buena historia técnica para un desarrollador Appian? (Elige 2)","options":["Nada","El horario del PO","Criterios de aceptación claros","Contraseñas de producción","Objetos afectados y dependencias"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Criterios y contexto técnico permiten construir y probar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a good technical story for an Appian developer? (Choose 2)","options":["Nothing","The PO's schedule","Clear acceptance criteria","Production passwords","Affected objects and dependencies"],"explanation":"Criteria and technical context enable building and testing."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto conviene para cálculos de fechas laborables en Appian?","options":["Funciones de calendario de proceso (p. ej. workday)","Una constante con la lista de festivos de los próximos 100 años","Un grupo","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Appian tiene funciones de calendario laboral.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object suits business-day date calculations in Appian?","options":["Process calendar functions (e.g. workday)","A constant listing holidays for the next 100 years","A group","Nothing"],"explanation":"Appian has business calendar functions."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer para que una interfaz de búsqueda no consulte en cada pulsación de tecla?","options":["Usar un botón de búsqueda o refresco controlado","Usar a!forEach","Nada","Consultar en cada cambio de texto sin ninguna limitación"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Controlar cuándo se consulta reduce carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How can a search interface avoid querying on every keystroke?","options":["Use a search button or controlled refresh","Use a!forEach","Nothing","Query on every text change without limits"],"explanation":"Controlling when to query reduces load."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene el componente a!gridField con datos de registros frente a una grid con datos en memoria?","options":["Más código","Paginación y ordenación en servidor","Ninguna","Que carga todas las filas en el navegador de una vez"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La grid de registros pagina en el servidor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of a!gridField with record data over an in-memory grid?","options":["More code","Server-side paging and sorting","None","It loads every row into the browser at once"],"explanation":"Record grids page on the server."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con interfaces que muestran grandes cantidades de datos editables?","options":["Usar colores","Paginar o limitar filas para mantener el rendimiento","Nada","Mostrar todas las filas editables a la vez para comodidad"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Grids editables enormes son lentas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration for interfaces showing large amounts of editable data?","options":["Using colors","Paging or limiting rows to keep performance","Nothing","Showing every editable row at once for convenience"],"explanation":"Huge editable grids are slow."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos herramientas de Appian ayudan a diseñar una interfaz rápidamente? (Elige 2)","options":["La consola de branding","La configuración LDAP","Plantillas de interfaz","Modo de diseño visual del diseñador","El log de servidor"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Plantillas y editor visual aceleran el diseño.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two Appian tools help design an interface quickly? (Choose 2)","options":["Branding console","LDAP settings","Interface templates","The designer's visual design mode","The server log"],"explanation":"Templates and the visual editor speed up design."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es la vista previa de la interfaz con datos de prueba?","options":["Valores de prueba en las entradas para probar la interfaz","Una copia de la interfaz que se despliega automáticamente a test","Un plug-in","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los valores de prueba permiten probar sin ejecutar procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is the interface preview with test values?","options":["Test values on inputs to try the interface","A copy of the interface auto-deployed to test","A plug-in","Nothing"],"explanation":"Test values allow trying without running processes."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para notificaciones por correo con contenido formateado?","options":["Plantillas de correo con datos del proceso","Nada","Una constante por destinatario","Escribir el HTML completo del correo en cada nodo de envío"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Plantillas reutilizables simplifican el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits formatted email notifications?","options":["Email templates with process data","Nothing","One constant per recipient","Writing the email's full HTML in each send node"],"explanation":"Reusable templates simplify maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene usar para enviar notificaciones a un grupo de usuarios?","options":["Una lista de direcciones de correo escrita a mano en la constante","El grupo como destinatario","Nada","Un documento"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Usar grupos mantiene destinatarios actualizados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be used to notify a group of users?","options":["A hand-written email address list in a constant","The group as recipient","Nothing","A document"],"explanation":"Using groups keeps recipients current."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos de seguridad debe revisar el desarrollador en una acción de registro? (Elige 2)","options":["El tamaño de fuente","Quién puede ver la acción","El orden alfabético","Quién puede iniciar el proceso subyacente","El color del icono"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Visibilidad de la acción y seguridad del proceso deben alinearse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two security aspects should a developer check on a record action? (Choose 2)","options":["Font size","Who can see the action","Alphabetical order","Who can start the underlying process","Icon color"],"explanation":"Action visibility and process security must align."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error de que un usuario no puede iniciar un proceso desde una acción visible?","options":["Que el usuario debe reiniciar su navegador para ver el proceso","Que el proceso no existe","Nada","Le falta permiso Initiator en el modelo de proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La seguridad del modelo debe permitir iniciarlo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a user being unable to start a process from a visible action indicate?","options":["The user must restart the browser to see the process","The process doesn't exist","Nothing","They lack Initiator on the process model"],"explanation":"The model's security must allow starting it."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para que una interfaz muestre información de solo lectura cuando el caso está cerrado?","options":["Borrar el caso","Crear una copia de la interfaz sin campos para casos cerrados","Nada","Condicionar readOnly/disabled según el estado"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La lógica condicional simplifica el mantenimiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern makes an interface read-only when the case is closed?","options":["Delete the case","Create a fieldless copy of the interface for closed cases","Nothing","Set readOnly/disabled based on status"],"explanation":"Conditional logic simplifies maintenance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con objetos de diseño obsoletos de una aplicación?","options":["Retirarlos tras comprobar que no tienen dependientes","Mantenerlos para siempre por si acaso se necesitan algún día","Nada","Renombrarlos a \"zzz\""],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Eliminar lo obsoleto reduce complejidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with obsolete design objects in an app?","options":["Retire them after checking they have no dependents","Keep them forever in case they're needed someday","Nothing","Rename them \"zzz\""],"explanation":"Removing obsolete objects reduces complexity."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos prácticas ayudan a trabajar en equipo sobre la misma aplicación? (Elige 2)","options":["No documentar","Acordar convenciones y estándares","Editar el mismo objeto a la vez sin avisar","Revisiones de código entre pares","Trabajar en producción"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Estándares y revisiones mantienen la calidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two practices help teams work on the same app? (Choose 2)","options":["Not documenting","Agree on conventions and standards","Editing the same object at once without warning","Peer code reviews","Working in production"],"explanation":"Standards and reviews keep quality."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si dos desarrolladores editan el mismo objeto a la vez en Appian?","options":["Nada","Se borra el objeto","Appian avisa del conflicto al guardar","Appian fusiona automáticamente los cambios de ambos sin perder nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Appian detecta cambios concurrentes y avisa.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if two developers edit the same object at once in Appian?","options":["Nothing","The object is deleted","Appian warns of the conflict on save","Appian auto-merges both changes losing nothing"],"explanation":"Appian detects concurrent changes and warns."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de objeto conviene para agrupar objetos de una funcionalidad dentro de la aplicación?","options":["Un único grupo de seguridad para todos los objetos","Nada","Constantes","Carpetas de reglas y documentos organizadas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las carpetas organizan los objetos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which object suits grouping a feature's objects within the app?","options":["A single security group for every object","Nothing","Constants","Organized rule and document folders"],"explanation":"Folders organize objects."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el término \"experiencia de usuario consistente\" en una aplicación Appian?","options":["Un solo color","Nada","Que cada pantalla tiene un diseño distinto para que no aburra","Mismos patrones, nombres y comportamientos en toda la app"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"La consistencia reduce la curva de aprendizaje.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a \"consistent user experience\" in an Appian app mean?","options":["One color","Nothing","Each screen has a different design so it's not boring","Same patterns, names and behaviors throughout"],"explanation":"Consistency reduces the learning curve."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene mostrar al usuario tras enviar un formulario con éxito?","options":["Nada, para no interrumpir al usuario con mensajes","El log del servidor","Una confirmación clara del resultado","Un error"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El feedback confirma que la acción se completó.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should users see after successfully submitting a form?","options":["Nothing, so as not to interrupt the user with messages","The server log","Clear confirmation of the outcome","An error"],"explanation":"Feedback confirms the action completed."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos mensajes de error son adecuados para el usuario final? (Elige 2)","options":["\"Error 500\"","\"NullPointerException en línea 42\"","\"La fecha de fin debe ser posterior a la de inicio\"","\"El importe máximo es 10.000 €\"","\"Algo falló\""],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Los mensajes deben explicar qué corregir.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two error messages suit end users? (Choose 2)","options":["\"Error 500\"","\"NullPointerException at line 42\"","\"End date must be after start date\"","\"Maximum amount is €10,000\"","\"Something failed\""],"explanation":"Messages should explain what to fix."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para guardar un borrador de formulario largo antes de enviarlo?","options":["Nada","Mantenerlo solo en el navegador y confiar en que no se cierre","Guardar el estado en base de datos con un estado \"borrador\"","Un correo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Persistir borradores evita pérdida de trabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern saves a long form's draft before submitting?","options":["Nothing","Keep it only in the browser and hope it isn't closed","Save state to the database with a \"draft\" status","An email"],"explanation":"Persisting drafts avoids lost work."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con validaciones de negocio que dependen de datos del servidor?","options":["Validar también en el proceso o al guardar","Confiar únicamente en las validaciones visibles de la interfaz","Nada","Omitirlas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"La validación del lado servidor asegura integridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with business validations depending on server data?","options":["Also validate in the process or on save","Rely solely on visible interface validations","Nothing","Skip them"],"explanation":"Server-side validation ensures integrity."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente permite al usuario subir varios archivos a la vez?","options":["a!dropdownField","a!textField con las rutas separadas por punto y coma","a!fileUploadField con maxSelections mayor que 1","Ninguno"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El file upload admite múltiples archivos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component lets users upload several files at once?","options":["a!dropdownField","a!textField with semicolon-separated paths","a!fileUploadField with maxSelections above 1","None"],"explanation":"File upload supports multiple files."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos validaciones son recomendables en la subida de documentos? (Elige 2)","options":["Color del archivo","Tamaño máximo","Ninguna","Nombre del autor del PC","Extensiones permitidas"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Limitar tipo y tamaño protege la aplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two validations are recommended for document uploads? (Choose 2)","options":["File color","Maximum size","None","PC author name","Allowed extensions"],"explanation":"Limiting type and size protects the app."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica un diseño de proceso con un nodo script que hace diez consultas a base de datos?","options":["Nada","Un diseño óptimo que aprovecha la potencia del motor","Que faltan nodos","Posible ineficiencia; conviene consolidar consultas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Consolidar consultas reduce carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a process design with a script node doing ten DB queries indicate?","options":["Nothing","An optimal design exploiting the engine's power","Missing nodes","Possible inefficiency; consolidate queries"],"explanation":"Consolidating queries reduces load."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene revisar si una historia requiere un nuevo grupo de seguridad?","options":["Nada","Que tenga un nombre corto aunque no sea descriptivo","Su color","Dónde se usa y quién lo administra"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los grupos requieren gobierno claro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be reviewed if a story needs a new security group?","options":["Nothing","That it has a short name even if not descriptive","Its color","Where it's used and who administers it"],"explanation":"Groups need clear governance."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de grupo conviene para usuarios que se incorporan automáticamente según una regla?","options":["Un grupo con reglas de pertenencia","Un grupo personal creado a mano por cada administrador","Una constante","Ninguno"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las reglas de pertenencia automatizan la gestión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which group type suits users joining automatically by a rule?","options":["A group with membership rules","A personal group hand-made by each admin","A constant","None"],"explanation":"Membership rules automate management."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un tipo de grupo (group type) en Appian?","options":["Un log","Una categoría que define atributos comunes a varios grupos","Un plug-in","Un tipo de usuario con permisos de administrador"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los group types añaden atributos a grupos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a group type in Appian?","options":["A log","A category defining attributes shared by groups","A plug-in","A user type with admin permissions"],"explanation":"Group types add attributes to groups."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ventajas tiene definir componentes de interfaz reutilizables? (Elige 2)","options":["Más lentitud","Más errores","Consistencia visual","Más duplicación","Cambios en un solo sitio"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"La reutilización centraliza cambios y mantiene coherencia.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two advantages come from reusable interface components? (Choose 2)","options":["More slowness","More errors","Visual consistency","More duplication","Changes in one place"],"explanation":"Reuse centralizes changes and keeps coherence."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer antes de empezar a construir una historia compleja?","options":["Pedir que la divida el patrocinador","Empezar a construir de inmediato y ajustar el diseño en producción","Revisar requisitos y diseñar el enfoque técnico","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un diseño previo reduce retrabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before building a complex story?","options":["Ask the sponsor to split it","Start building immediately and adjust the design in production","Review requirements and design the technical approach","Nothing"],"explanation":"Upfront design reduces rework."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se recomienda para lógica de negocio compartida entre interfaces y procesos?","options":["Duplicarla en cada interfaz y en cada nodo de script","Una constante","Nada","Ponerla en reglas de expresión llamadas desde ambos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las reglas centralizan la lógica compartida.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern is recommended for business logic shared by interfaces and processes?","options":["Duplicate it in each interface and script node","A constant","Nothing","Put it in expression rules called from both"],"explanation":"Rules centralize shared logic."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos técnicas ayudan a depurar una interfaz con comportamiento inesperado? (Elige 2)","options":["Reiniciar el servidor de producción","Borrar la interfaz","Revisar el valor de las variables locales","Cambiar el tema","Probar con valores de prueba en el diseñador"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Los valores de prueba y el estado de variables ayudan a depurar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two techniques help debug an interface behaving unexpectedly? (Choose 2)","options":["Restarting the production server","Deleting the interface","Inspecting local variable values","Changing the theme","Testing with test values in the designer"],"explanation":"Test values and variable state help debugging."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer cuando una regla devuelve un tipo de dato distinto al esperado por la interfaz?","options":["Nada","Convertir o tipar correctamente el resultado","Ignorarlo porque Appian convierte siempre cualquier tipo sin errores","Borrar la regla"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los tipos incorrectos causan errores o comportamientos raros.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done when a rule returns a different type than the interface expects?","options":["Nothing","Cast or type the result correctly","Ignore it since Appian always converts any type without errors","Delete the rule"],"explanation":"Wrong types cause errors or odd behavior."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón facilita que una aplicación sea configurable por negocio sin despliegues?","options":["Constantes que solo pueden cambiarse mediante paquetes de despliegue","Logs","Tablas de configuración con una interfaz de administración","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La configuración en datos evita ciclos de despliegue.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern lets the business configure an app without deployments?","options":["Constants changeable only via deployment packages","Logs","Configuration tables with an admin interface","Nothing"],"explanation":"Data-driven configuration avoids deployment cycles."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene un sitio de administración para la aplicación?","options":["Más seguridad para todos","Que los usuarios finales puedan modificar el código de la aplicación","Ninguna","Que los administradores de negocio gestionen datos de referencia"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Permite autonomía al negocio en datos de configuración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of an admin site for the app?","options":["More security for everyone","End users can modify the app's code","None","Business admins can manage reference data"],"explanation":"It gives the business autonomy over configuration data."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos tiene una interfaz con cientos de líneas sin componentes reutilizables? (Elige 2)","options":["Difícil de mantener","Más reutilizable","Más legible","Difícil de probar","Menos errores"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Las interfaces monolíticas son frágiles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks come from an interface with hundreds of lines and no reusable components? (Choose 2)","options":["Hard to maintain","More reusable","More readable","Hard to test","Fewer errors"],"explanation":"Monolithic interfaces are fragile."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica una regla de expresión sin descripción ni casos de prueba?","options":["Mayor rendimiento","Deuda técnica que dificulta su mantenimiento","Que la regla es tan simple que nunca fallará","Nada"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Descripciones y pruebas son parte de la calidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an expression rule with no description or test cases indicate?","options":["Better performance","Technical debt that hinders maintenance","The rule is so simple it'll never fail","Nothing"],"explanation":"Descriptions and tests are part of quality."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene incluir en la descripción de un objeto de Appian?","options":["Su propósito y cómo usarlo","Nada","Contraseñas","El nombre del desarrollador y su número de teléfono personal"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las descripciones ayudan a otros desarrolladores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should an Appian object's description include?","options":["Its purpose and how to use it","Nothing","Passwords","The developer's name and personal phone number"],"explanation":"Descriptions help other developers."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para mostrar u ocultar secciones según la respuesta del usuario?","options":["Recargar toda la página con otra interfaz distinta","Nada","showWhen basado en el valor de la variable","Un proceso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"showWhen hace la interfaz dinámica.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern shows or hides sections based on the user's answer?","options":["Reload the whole page with a different interface","Nothing","showWhen based on the variable's value","A process"],"explanation":"showWhen makes the interface dynamic."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay al usar showWhen con campos obligatorios?","options":["Que se borran sus datos","Los campos ocultos no se validan como obligatorios","Que los campos ocultos siguen bloqueando el envío del formulario","Ninguna"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los componentes ocultos no se evalúan para validación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration with showWhen on required fields?","options":["Their data is deleted","Hidden fields aren't validated as required","Hidden fields still block form submission","None"],"explanation":"Hidden components aren't evaluated for validation."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer con los datos de un campo que se oculta tras cambiar una opción?","options":["Ocultarlo dos veces","Decidir si limpiarlo en el saveInto que lo oculta","Nada, porque Appian lo borra siempre de la base de datos","Ignorarlo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Los valores ocultos pueden persistir si no se limpian.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done with a field's data when it's hidden after an option change?","options":["Hide it twice","Decide whether to clear it in the hiding saveInto","Nothing, Appian always deletes it from the DB","Ignore it"],"explanation":"Hidden values can persist unless cleared."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos formas tiene un desarrollador de dar formato numérico en una interfaz? (Elige 2)","options":["Ninguna","a!currency o formatos del componente","Concatenar ceros a mano siempre","Funciones como fixed o text","Cambiar el tipo de columna a texto"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Appian tiene funciones y componentes de formato.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two ways can a developer format numbers in an interface? (Choose 2)","options":["None","a!currency or component formats","Always pad zeros by hand","Functions like fixed or text","Change the column type to text"],"explanation":"Appian has formatting functions and components."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el componente a!richTextDisplayField?","options":["Nada","Mostrar texto con estilos, enlaces e iconos","Editar texto con formato enriquecido como un procesador de textos","Subir archivos"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Es de solo lectura con formato enriquecido.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a!richTextDisplayField allow?","options":["Nothing","Showing styled text, links and icons","Editing rich text like a word processor","Uploading files"],"explanation":"It's read-only rich formatting."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de gráfico conviene para mostrar evolución en el tiempo?","options":["Tabla de texto","Gráfico circular con una porción por fecha","Ninguno","Gráfico de líneas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las líneas muestran tendencias temporales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which chart suits showing change over time?","options":["Text table","Pie chart with one slice per date","None","Line chart"],"explanation":"Lines show time trends."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene configurar un gráfico directamente con datos de registro?","options":["Más código","Que el gráfico calcula los datos en el navegador con todas las filas","Ninguna","Agregación en servidor y enlace a registros"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los gráficos sobre registros agregan eficientemente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of configuring a chart directly on record data?","options":["More code","The chart computes in the browser with every row","None","Server-side aggregation and record linking"],"explanation":"Record-based charts aggregate efficiently."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones requiere una historia de \"exportar a Excel\" bien implementada? (Elige 2)","options":["Exportar todas las tablas de la BD","Exportar contraseñas","Ignorar filtros","Limitar el volumen exportado","Respetar la seguridad de los datos"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"La exportación debe ser segura y controlada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things does a well-implemented \"export to Excel\" story require? (Choose 2)","options":["Exporting every DB table","Exporting passwords","Ignoring filters","Limiting exported volume","Honoring data security"],"explanation":"Exports must be secure and controlled."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué funcionalidad permite exportar una grid de registros a Excel sin desarrollo adicional?","options":["Nada","La opción de exportación de la lista de registros","Un plug-in obligatorio para cada tipo de registro","Un correo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las listas de registros pueden permitir exportar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which feature exports a record grid to Excel without extra development?","options":["Nothing","The record list export option","A mandatory plug-in per record type","An email"],"explanation":"Record lists can allow export."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene para la navegación entre pasos de un asistente (wizard)?","options":["Un sitio por paso","Un proceso distinto con una tarea por cada paso del asistente","Variable local con el paso actual y botones Anterior/Siguiente","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Un wizard en una interfaz evita tareas innecesarias.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits navigating wizard steps?","options":["One site per step","A separate process with one task per wizard step","A local variable with the current step and Back/Next buttons","Nothing"],"explanation":"A single-interface wizard avoids needless tasks."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración hay con wizards basados en una sola interfaz?","options":["Los datos se envían al final, al completar el asistente","Que no se puede volver atrás","Que cada paso se guarda en la base de datos automáticamente","Ninguna"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Si se necesita guardar por pasos hay que diseñarlo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's a consideration with single-interface wizards?","options":["Data is submitted at the end on completion","You can't go back","Each step auto-saves to the database","None"],"explanation":"Step-wise saving must be designed explicitly."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos ayudan a que un proceso sea fácil de soportar en producción? (Elige 2)","options":["Variables y nodos bien nombrados","Lógica oculta en triggers","Ninguna alerta","Alertas a administradores ante errores","Nodos sin nombre"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"Alertas y nombres claros facilitan el soporte.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements make a process easy to support in production? (Choose 2)","options":["Well-named variables and nodes","Logic hidden in triggers","No alerts","Alerts to admins on errors","Unnamed nodes"],"explanation":"Alerts and clear names ease support."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se configura quién recibe las alertas de errores de un modelo de proceso?","options":["En la interfaz de inicio del proceso","En el log","En una constante de texto","En las propiedades de alertas del modelo de proceso"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los modelos permiten definir destinatarios de alertas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where is it configured who receives a process model's error alerts?","options":["In the process start interface","In the log","In a text constant","In the process model's alert settings"],"explanation":"Models let you set alert recipients."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que un nodo tenga marcado \"Delete previous instances\" o similar en su configuración?","options":["Que el nodo se ejecuta dos veces","Nada","Que el nodo borra datos de la base de datos","Controla cómo se gestionan instancias anteriores del nodo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las opciones de instancias afectan a la memoria y al historial.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a node setting like \"Delete previous instances\" indicate?","options":["The node runs twice","Nothing","The node deletes data from the database","It controls how prior node instances are handled"],"explanation":"Instance options affect memory and history."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para tareas que deben aparecer en el idioma del usuario?","options":["Solo inglés","Nada","Un modelo de proceso distinto por idioma","Nombres y textos de tarea traducibles"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las tareas pueden usar textos traducidos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for tasks shown in the user's language?","options":["English only","Nothing","A separate process model per language","Translatable task names and texts"],"explanation":"Tasks can use translated texts."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para que una tarea muestre a su destinatario por qué la recibe?","options":["Nombre y descripción de tarea con datos del caso","Un log","Nada","Una tarea con nombre genérico \"Tarea\" para todas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Nombres dinámicos dan contexto en la lista de tareas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern shows a task's recipient why they got it?","options":["Task name and description with case data","A log","Nothing","A generic \"Task\" name for all tasks"],"explanation":"Dynamic names give context in the task list."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos conviene definir en el diseño de seguridad de una aplicación nueva? (Elige 2)","options":["Acceso total para todos","Matriz de qué rol hace qué","Contraseñas compartidas","Seguridad solo en interfaz","Grupos por rol"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Una matriz de roles guía la configuración de seguridad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two elements should a new app's security design define? (Choose 2)","options":["Full access for all","A matrix of which role does what","Shared passwords","Interface-only security","Groups by role"],"explanation":"A role matrix guides security configuration."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué consideración de UX aplica a interfaces usadas en móvil?","options":["Diseño adaptable y componentes compatibles","Ventanas emergentes","Grids con muchas columnas y desplazamiento horizontal","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Appian adapta interfaces, pero el diseño debe considerarlo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which UX consideration applies to interfaces used on mobile?","options":["Responsive design and compatible components","Pop-ups","Grids with many columns and horizontal scrolling","Nothing"],"explanation":"Appian adapts interfaces, but design must account for it."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer cuando una tarea requiere datos que el usuario no tiene a mano?","options":["Nada","Cancelar el proceso","Obligar a completarla de una vez y perder los datos si sale","Permitir guardarla sin enviar y volver más tarde"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Guardar el progreso de la tarea evita perder trabajo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done when a task needs data the user doesn't have at hand?","options":["Nothing","Cancel the process","Force completing it in one go, losing data if they leave","Allow saving without submitting and returning later"],"explanation":"Saving task progress avoids lost work."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón conviene cuando una interfaz necesita datos de varias fuentes al cargar?","options":["Consultas eficientes en variables locales con refresco controlado","Consultas repetidas en cada componente que necesita el dato","Un correo","Nada"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Consultar una vez y reutilizar reduce carga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits an interface needing data from several sources on load?","options":["Efficient queries in locals with controlled refresh","Repeated queries in each component needing the data","An email","Nothing"],"explanation":"Querying once and reusing reduces load."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones forman parte de definir una buena interfaz de usuario? (Elige 2)","options":["Copiar sistemas antiguos tal cual","Añadir todos los campos posibles","Ignorar el feedback","Validar el diseño con usuarios","Seguir guías de diseño de Appian"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Validación y guías llevan a mejores interfaces.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions are part of defining a good UI? (Choose 2)","options":["Copying old systems as-is","Adding every possible field","Ignoring feedback","Validating the design with users","Following Appian design guidelines"],"explanation":"Validation and guidelines lead to better interfaces."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón se usa para cálculos que se repiten en varias reglas con distintas entradas?","options":["Nada","Una regla parametrizada reutilizable","Copiar el cálculo y cambiar los valores en cada copia","Una constante"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La parametrización evita duplicación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern suits calculations repeated across rules with different inputs?","options":["Nothing","A reusable parameterized rule","Copy the calculation and change values in each copy","A constant"],"explanation":"Parameterization avoids duplication."}}},{"domain":"D3","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene comprobar antes de marcar una historia como lista para pruebas?","options":["El color","Que el desarrollador cree que funciona sin haberlo probado","Que cumple los criterios y la DoD del equipo","Nada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"La DoD asegura calidad antes de pasar a pruebas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be checked before marking a story ready for testing?","options":["The color","The developer believes it works without testing","It meets the criteria and team DoD","Nothing"],"explanation":"The DoD ensures quality before testing."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipos de autenticación admite un connected system HTTP de Appian?","options":["Solo usuario y contraseña escritos en cada integración","Solo certificados","Ninguna","Básica, API key y OAuth 2.0, entre otras"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El HTTP connected system soporta varios métodos de autenticación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which auth types does an Appian HTTP connected system support?","options":["Only username and password typed in each integration","Only certificates","None","Basic, API key and OAuth 2.0, among others"],"explanation":"The HTTP connected system supports several auth methods."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué flujo OAuth 2.0 usar cuando Appian llama a una API en nombre de la aplicación, sin usuario?","options":["Authorization code, que pide a cada usuario iniciar sesión","Ninguno","Client credentials","Implicit"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Client credentials autentica la aplicación, no al usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which OAuth 2.0 flow fits Appian calling an API on the app's behalf, with no user?","options":["Authorization code, which asks each user to log in","None","Client credentials","Implicit"],"explanation":"Client credentials authenticates the app, not a user."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué flujo OAuth 2.0 usar cuando cada usuario debe autorizar el acceso a sus propios datos externos?","options":["Ninguno","Básica","Client credentials, con una única cuenta compartida","Authorization code grant"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El authorization code obtiene permisos por usuario.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which OAuth 2.0 flow fits when each user must authorize access to their own external data?","options":["None","Basic","Client credentials, with one shared account","Authorization code grant"],"explanation":"Authorization code obtains per-user consent."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene guardar la autenticación en el connected system y no en la integración?","options":["Ninguna","Que es más lento","Que cada integración puede usar credenciales distintas sin control","Se gestiona en un lugar y se ajusta por entorno"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Centralizar facilita mantenimiento y despliegues.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of storing auth in the connected system rather than the integration?","options":["None","It's slower","Each integration can use uncontrolled different credentials","It's managed in one place and set per environment"],"explanation":"Centralizing eases maintenance and deployments."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos elementos se configuran en un objeto de integración HTTP? (Elige 2)","options":["Método y ruta","Colores","Parámetros, cabeceras y cuerpo","Seguridad de filas de registros","Grupos del sitio"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"La integración define la petición concreta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two things are configured in an HTTP integration object? (Choose 2)","options":["Method and path","Colors","Parameters, headers and body","Record row security","Site groups"],"explanation":"The integration defines the specific request."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la opción de una integración \"modifica datos\" (Writes Data)?","options":["Que la integración solo puede leer datos de forma segura","Que se ejecuta al cargar la interfaz","Nada","Solo puede llamarse desde saveInto, procesos o Web APIs"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las integraciones que escriben no se ejecutan en evaluaciones normales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an integration's \"Writes Data\" option mean?","options":["The integration can only read data safely","It runs on interface load","Nothing","It can only be called from saveInto, processes or Web APIs"],"explanation":"Writing integrations don't run in normal evaluations."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Por qué una integración que crea datos no debe ejecutarse al cargar una interfaz?","options":["No hay problema","Podría ejecutarse varias veces creando duplicados","Porque Appian no permite llamadas HTTP desde interfaces en ningún caso","Porque es lenta"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las evaluaciones de interfaz pueden repetirse.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Why shouldn't a data-creating integration run on interface load?","options":["No problem","It could run several times creating duplicates","Appian never allows HTTP calls from interfaces","It's slow"],"explanation":"Interface evaluations may repeat."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nodo de proceso ejecuta un objeto de integración?","options":["Write Records","Send E-Mail","Call Integration","Script task con la URL escrita en una expresión"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Call Integration invoca la integración desde el proceso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which process node runs an integration object?","options":["Write Records","Send E-Mail","Call Integration","A script task with the URL in an expression"],"explanation":"Call Integration invokes the integration from a process."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene configurar para manejar errores de una integración en un proceso?","options":["Nada, porque Appian corrige los errores del sistema externo","Borrar el proceso","Comprobar la salida de error y ramificar el flujo","Un correo al cliente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las integraciones devuelven información de error para gestionarla.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be configured to handle integration errors in a process?","options":["Nothing, Appian fixes the external system's errors","Delete the process","Check the error output and branch the flow","An email to the customer"],"explanation":"Integrations return error info to handle."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos valores devuelve típicamente una integración al ejecutarse? (Elige 2)","options":["El resultado (respuesta)","Si hubo error y su detalle","La contraseña usada","El código de la interfaz","Nada"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Las integraciones devuelven result, success y error.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two values does an integration typically return? (Choose 2)","options":["The result (response)","Whether it errored and details","The password used","The interface code","Nothing"],"explanation":"Integrations return result, success and error."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función convierte una respuesta JSON en un diccionario de Appian?","options":["a!toJson, que transforma texto JSON en objetos","tostring","Ninguna","a!fromJson"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!fromJson parsea JSON; a!toJson lo genera.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function converts a JSON response into an Appian dictionary?","options":["a!toJson, which turns JSON text into objects","tostring","None","a!fromJson"],"explanation":"a!fromJson parses JSON; a!toJson generates it."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función convierte un valor de Appian en texto JSON para enviarlo en el cuerpo?","options":["Ninguna","tostring","a!fromJson, que serializa datos a JSON","a!toJson"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"a!toJson serializa valores a JSON.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function turns an Appian value into JSON text for a request body?","options":["None","tostring","a!fromJson, which serializes data to JSON","a!toJson"],"explanation":"a!toJson serializes values to JSON."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es una Web API en Appian?","options":["Una integración saliente hacia un sistema externo","Un grupo","Un endpoint HTTP que expone datos o acciones de Appian","Un plug-in"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las Web APIs reciben peticiones externas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Web API in Appian?","options":["An outbound integration to an external system","A group","An HTTP endpoint exposing Appian data or actions","A plug-in"],"explanation":"Web APIs receive external requests."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué métodos HTTP puede tener una Web API de Appian?","options":["Solo POST","Solo GET, porque las Web APIs son de solo lectura","Ninguno","GET, POST, PUT y DELETE"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las Web APIs admiten varios métodos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which HTTP methods can an Appian Web API have?","options":["Only POST","Only GET, since Web APIs are read-only","None","GET, POST, PUT and DELETE"],"explanation":"Web APIs support several methods."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se autentica normalmente un sistema externo que llama a una Web API de Appian?","options":["Con el usuario y contraseña de un administrador real","Por IP únicamente","Con una API key asociada a una cuenta de servicio","Sin autenticación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Las cuentas de servicio con API key son lo recomendado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How does an external system usually authenticate to an Appian Web API?","options":["With a real admin's username and password","By IP only","With an API key tied to a service account","No authentication"],"explanation":"Service accounts with API keys are recommended."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos aspectos de seguridad aplican a una Web API? (Elige 2)","options":["Color de la respuesta","Permisos de la cuenta de servicio","Nombre del navegador","Ninguno","Seguridad del objeto Web API"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Quién puede llamarla y con qué permisos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two security aspects apply to a Web API? (Choose 2)","options":["Response color","Service account permissions","Browser name","None","Web API object security"],"explanation":"Who can call it and with what permissions."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué función se usa en una Web API para devolver una respuesta HTTP?","options":["a!startProcess","a!queryEntity","a!httpResponse","a!save, que devuelve el cuerpo al cliente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"a!httpResponse define estado, cabeceras y cuerpo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which function returns an HTTP response from a Web API?","options":["a!startProcess","a!queryEntity","a!httpResponse","a!save, which returns the body to the client"],"explanation":"a!httpResponse sets status, headers and body."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"Una Web API POST debe crear un caso. ¿Cómo lo hace?","options":["Con a!queryRecordType, que inserta si el caso no existe","Llamando a a!startProcess o a!writeRecords desde la Web API","Enviando un correo","No puede"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Las Web APIs pueden iniciar procesos o escribir datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A POST Web API must create a case. How?","options":["With a!queryRecordType, which inserts if missing","Calling a!startProcess or a!writeRecords from it","Sending an email","It can't"],"explanation":"Web APIs can start processes or write data."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué código HTTP conviene devolver cuando la petición a una Web API tiene datos inválidos?","options":["200, con un mensaje de error en el cuerpo de la respuesta","500","400","302"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"400 indica error del cliente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which HTTP status should a Web API return when the request has invalid data?","options":["200, with an error message in the body","500","400","302"],"explanation":"400 indicates a client error."}}},{"domain":"D4","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un smart service en Appian?","options":["Un log","Una regla de expresión que solo puede leer datos","Un grupo","Un nodo que realiza una acción (escribir, enviar, generar)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los smart services ejecutan acciones en procesos.","i18n":{"en":{"s