 expect in Mule 4?","options":["Plain text","Free JSON","CSV","XML matching the WSDL schema"],"explanation":"Built with DataWeave to XML."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conector permite crear y consultar registros de Salesforce desde Mule?","options":["Database con JDBC a Salesforce","File","HTTP Request a la web de Salesforce sin autenticación","Salesforce Connector"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Ofrece operaciones como Query, Create, Upsert.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which connector creates and queries Salesforce records from Mule?","options":["Database via JDBC to Salesforce","File","HTTP Request to Salesforce site unauthenticated","Salesforce Connector"],"explanation":"It offers Query, Create, Upsert, etc."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué lenguaje se usa en la operación Query del Salesforce Connector?","options":["SOQL","DataWeave","GraphQL","SQL ANSI completo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Salesforce Object Query Language.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which language is used in the Salesforce Connector Query operation?","options":["SOQL","DataWeave","GraphQL","Full ANSI SQL"],"explanation":"Salesforce Object Query Language."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué estrategia permite a un conector reintentar la conexión si el sistema remoto cae?","options":["Un Transform Message","Un Logger con nivel ERROR","Estrategia de reconexión","Un ámbito Async"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"reconnection con frecuencia e intentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which strategy lets a connector retry connecting if the remote system goes down?","options":["A Transform Message","A Logger at ERROR","Reconnection strategy","An Async scope"],"explanation":"reconnection with frequency and attempts."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos conectores sirven para mensajería entre sistemas? (Elige 2)","options":["JMS","Logger","Anypoint MQ","File Read","Database Select"],"correct":[0,2],"explanation":"Colas y temas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two connectors serve messaging between systems? (Choose 2)","options":["JMS","Logger","Anypoint MQ","File Read","Database Select"],"explanation":"Queues and topics."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conector usar para comunicación por colas dentro de la misma aplicación Mule?","options":["File","HTTP","VM","JMS externo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"VM es intraaplicación (o dominio).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which connector for queue communication within the same Mule app?","options":["File","HTTP","VM","External JMS"],"explanation":"VM is intra-app (or domain)."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error DB:CONNECTIVITY?","options":["El SQL tiene un error de sintaxis","Que la consulta devolvió un payload JSON en lugar de filas","La consulta devolvió cero filas","No se pudo conectar con la base de datos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Error de conexión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does DB:CONNECTIVITY indicate?","options":["The SQL has a syntax error","The query returned a JSON payload instead of rows","The query returned zero rows","The database couldn't be reached"],"explanation":"A connection error."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error HTTP:NOT_FOUND en un HTTP Request?","options":["La red está caída","Falta la configuración global","El servicio remoto devolvió 404","El listener no encontró el flujo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los códigos de error remotos se mapean a tipos HTTP.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does HTTP:NOT_FOUND on an HTTP Request indicate?","options":["The network is down","The global config is missing","The remote service returned 404","The listener didn't find the flow"],"explanation":"Remote error codes map to HTTP types."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se evita que un HTTP Request lance error ante códigos 4xx concretos?","options":["Usando un Logger","Cambiando el puerto","Configurando el validador de respuesta con los códigos aceptados","Desactivando el conector"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"responseValidator con successStatusCodes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is an HTTP Request kept from failing on specific 4xx codes?","options":["Use a Logger","Change the port","Configure the response validator with accepted codes","Disable the connector"],"explanation":"responseValidator with successStatusCodes."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos operaciones ofrece el conector Database además de Select e Insert? (Elige 2)","options":["Listen HTTP","Publish","Read file","Update","Stored Procedure"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"También Delete, Bulk y DDL.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two operations does the Database connector offer besides Select and Insert? (Choose 2)","options":["Listen HTTP","Publish","Read file","Update","Stored Procedure"],"explanation":"Also Delete, Bulk and DDL."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se necesita en el proyecto para conectar a una base de datos MySQL?","options":["Un subflujo con la cadena de conexión escrita en un Set Variable","El driver JDBC como dependencia","Una política de API Manager","Un archivo RAML"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El driver se añade al pom.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's needed in the project to connect to MySQL?","options":["A subflow with the connection string in a Set Variable","The JDBC driver as a dependency","An API Manager policy","A RAML file"],"explanation":"The driver is added to the pom."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve el Salesforce Connector en una operación Create?","options":["Nada: la operación Create no devuelve información al flujo","El objeto completo de Salesforce siempre","Un CSV","Resultados por registro con id y éxito o errores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"SaveResult por registro.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Salesforce Connector return on Create?","options":["Nothing: Create returns no information to the flow","Always the full Salesforce object","A CSV","Per-record results with id and success or errors"],"explanation":"A SaveResult per record."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué origen del Salesforce Connector escucha cambios en registros?","options":["HTTP Listener con ruta /salesforce","File On New File apuntando al directorio de exportaciones de Salesforce","On New Object / On Modified Object o Replay Channel","Query programada con un Logger"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Sources de eventos y streaming.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Salesforce Connector source listens for record changes?","options":["HTTP Listener on /salesforce","File On New File pointed at the Salesforce export directory","On New Object / On Modified Object or Replay Channel","A Query scheduled with a Logger"],"explanation":"Event and streaming sources."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para conectar a un sistema sin conector disponible pero con API REST?","options":["Un conector Database","Un Logger que registre las peticiones para que otro equipo las envíe","Copiar archivos a mano","HTTP Request o REST Connect desde la especificación"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"HTTP Request o un conector generado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable for a system with no connector but a REST API?","options":["A Database connector","A Logger recording requests for another team to send","Copying files by hand","HTTP Request or REST Connect from the spec"],"explanation":"HTTP Request or a generated connector."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace la operación Write del conector File si el directorio no existe y createParentDirectories es true?","options":["Crea los directorios necesarios","Ignora la escritura y devuelve el payload sin cambios ni error","Lanza siempre un error","Escribe en el directorio raíz"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Por defecto crea directorios padre.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does File Write do if the directory doesn't exist and createParentDirectories is true?","options":["Creates the needed directories","It skips the write and returns the payload unchanged with no error","Always throws","Writes to the root"],"explanation":"It creates parent directories by default."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos atributos del archivo están disponibles tras On New or Updated File? (Elige 2)","options":["fileName","queryParams","method","lastModifiedTime","statusCode"],"correct":[0,3],"explanation":"FileAttributes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two file attributes are available after On New or Updated File? (Choose 2)","options":["fileName","queryParams","method","lastModifiedTime","statusCode"],"explanation":"FileAttributes."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene si un conector de base de datos tarda en responder y bloquea hilos?","options":["Aumentar los logs a DEBUG","Configurar timeouts y revisar el pool","Usar Flow Reference para llamar al conector desde otro flujo","Eliminar el manejo de errores"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Timeouts y dimensionamiento del pool.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What if a database connector is slow and blocks threads?","options":["Raise logs to DEBUG","Set timeouts and review the pool","Use Flow Reference to call the connector from another flow","Remove error handling"],"explanation":"Timeouts and pool sizing."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el parámetro fetchSize en una consulta Select?","options":["El tiempo de espera","Cuántas filas se traen por bloque al hacer streaming","El tamaño del pool","El número máximo de columnas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Ayuda al streaming de grandes resultados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does fetchSize indicate on a Select?","options":["Timeout","How many rows are fetched per chunk when streaming","Pool size","Max columns"],"explanation":"It helps stream large results."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conector publica y consume mensajes en Anypoint MQ?","options":["Database connector","VM connector","Web Service Consumer","Anypoint MQ connector"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Publish, Consume y Subscriber.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which connector publishes and consumes Anypoint MQ messages?","options":["Database connector","VM connector","Web Service Consumer","Anypoint MQ connector"],"explanation":"Publish, Consume and Subscriber."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene usar colas entre aplicaciones?","options":["Eliminar la necesidad de errores","Que el consumidor responde de forma síncrona","Desacoplar productor y consumidor","Compartir variables"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Resiliencia y desacoplamiento.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the advantage of queues between apps?","options":["No errors needed","The consumer replies synchronously","Decoupling producer and consumer","Sharing variables"],"explanation":"Resilience and decoupling."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de autenticación admite el HTTP Request?","options":["Solo API keys en la URL","Solo sin autenticación","Basic, Digest, NTLM y OAuth, entre otras","Solo certificados"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Varias opciones de autenticación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which authentication does HTTP Request support?","options":["Only API keys in the URL","Only none","Basic, Digest, NTLM and OAuth, among others","Only certificates"],"explanation":"Several auth options."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error FILE:ILLEGAL_PATH?","options":["Falta un permiso de red","La ruta indicada no es válida o no existe","El archivo está vacío","El archivo es muy grande"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Ruta inválida.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does FILE:ILLEGAL_PATH indicate?","options":["A network permission is missing","The given path is invalid or missing","The file is empty","The file is too big"],"explanation":"Invalid path."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda MuleSoft para credenciales de conectores?","options":["Pasarlas en variables desde el cliente","Publicarlas en Exchange para que los equipos las reutilicen","Propiedades seguras o gestor de secretos","Escribirlas en el XML"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Nunca en texto plano.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MuleSoft recommend for connector credentials?","options":["Passing them in variables from the client","Publish them to Exchange so teams can reuse them","Secure properties or a secrets manager","Writing them in the XML"],"explanation":"Never in plain text."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve la operación Update del conector Database?","options":["Un booleano siempre","Las filas actualizadas completas","El SQL ejecutado","El número de filas afectadas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"affectedRows.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Database Update operation return?","options":["Always a boolean","The full updated rows","The executed SQL","The number of affected rows"],"explanation":"affectedRows."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos opciones permiten llamar a un procedimiento almacenado con parámetros de salida? (Elige 2)","options":["File Write","Definir outputParameters","Operación Stored Procedure","VM Publish","Select con CALL dentro concatenado"],"correct":[1,2],"explanation":"Stored Procedure con in/out params.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two options call a stored procedure with output parameters? (Choose 2)","options":["File Write","Defining outputParameters","Stored Procedure operation","VM Publish","Select with a concatenated CALL"],"explanation":"Stored Procedure with in/out params."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la opción de conector \"Test Connection\" en Studio?","options":["Ejecuta la consulta en producción","Verifica que la configuración puede conectarse","Genera datos de prueba","Despliega la app"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Validación de configuración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a connector's Test Connection in Studio do?","options":["Runs the query in production","Verifies the config can connect","Generates test data","Deploys the app"],"explanation":"Config validation."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para leer un archivo muy grande sin cargarlo entero en memoria?","options":["Convertirlo a String primero","Duplicarlo y leer cada copia en un flujo distinto en paralelo","Leerlo entero en una variable","Usar streaming y procesarlo por partes"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Streaming y procesamiento por bloques.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable to read a huge file without loading it all into memory?","options":["Convert it to String first","Duplicate it and read each copy in a different flow in parallel","Read it all into a variable","Use streaming and process in parts"],"explanation":"Streaming and chunked processing."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un flujo debe llamar a un servicio REST externo que exige un token en la cabecera Authorization. ¿Dónde se añade?","options":["En el archivo pom.xml como propiedad de Maven del proyecto","En el HTTP Listener del flujo que recibe la petición del cliente","En el path del HTTP Request como parámetro adicional al final de la URL","En la sección Headers del HTTP Request"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Las cabeceras se definen en la operación de request.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A flow must call an external REST service needing a token in the Authorization header. Where is it added?","options":["In pom.xml as a project Maven property","In the flow's HTTP Listener that receives the client request","In the HTTP Request path as an extra parameter at the end of the URL","In the HTTP Request Headers section"],"explanation":"Headers are set on the request operation."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conector conviene para recoger cada noche un archivo CSV de un proveedor en un servidor FTP sin cifrar?","options":["Web Service Consumer apuntando al servidor de archivos","Database con un driver de ficheros planos","SFTP, aunque el servidor del proveedor no ofrezca SSH","FTP"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se usa el conector que coincide con el protocolo del servidor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which connector suits collecting a supplier's nightly CSV from an unencrypted FTP server?","options":["Web Service Consumer pointed at the file server","Database with a flat-file driver","SFTP, even though the supplier's server offers no SSH","FTP"],"explanation":"Use the connector matching the server protocol."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos riesgos evita usar parámetros de entrada en el conector Database? (Elige 2)","options":["Inyección SQL","Errores de formato al concatenar valores","Que el driver JDBC no se cargue al arrancar la aplicación","Que la consulta devuelva demasiadas columnas en el resultado","Que el pool de conexiones se quede sin hilos disponibles"],"correct":[0,1],"explanation":"Los parámetros escapan y tipan los valores.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two risks does using input parameters in the Database connector avoid? (Choose 2)","options":["SQL injection","Format errors from concatenating values","The JDBC driver not loading at startup","The query returning too many result columns","The connection pool running out of threads"],"explanation":"Parameters escape and type values."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"Un HTTP Request a un servicio lento supera el tiempo de espera. ¿Qué ajuste se revisa?","options":["El nivel del Logger configurado en log4j2.xml","El responseTimeout de la operación","El tipo MIME de la respuesta esperada","El número de workers de la aplicación en Runtime Manager"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"El timeout se configura en la petición o la configuración.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An HTTP Request to a slow service times out. Which setting is reviewed?","options":["The Logger level in log4j2.xml","The operation's responseTimeout","The expected response MIME type","The number of app workers in Runtime Manager"],"explanation":"Timeout is set on the request or config."}}},{"domain":"D6","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve la operación Consume de Anypoint MQ?","options":["Un error si la cola tiene más de un mensaje pendiente","El número de mensajes pendientes sin leer su contenido","Todos los mensajes de la cola de una vez y los borra al instante","Un mensaje de la cola, que luego se confirma (ACK)"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se confirma con ACK o se rechaza con NACK.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Anypoint MQ Consume operation return?","options":["An error if more than one message is pending","The pending message count without reading content","All queue messages at once, deleting them immediately","A message from the queue, later acknowledged (ACK)"],"explanation":"It's confirmed with ACK or rejected with NACK."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el ámbito For Each?","options":["Itera una colección y procesa cada elemento secuencialmente","Procesa todos los elementos en paralelo y agrega los resultados","Divide los registros en lotes persistentes con pasos y resumen final","Repite el flujo hasta que no haya errores"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"For Each es secuencial y síncrono.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the For Each scope do?","options":["Iterates a collection and processes each element sequentially","Processes all elements in parallel and aggregates results","Splits records into persistent batches with steps and a final summary","Repeats the flow until there are no errors"],"explanation":"For Each is sequential and synchronous."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cuál es el payload después de un For Each?","options":["Un array con los payloads producidos en cada iteración del bucle","Un array con los resultados de cada iteración","El payload original que había antes del For Each","El resultado de la última iteración"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"For Each no modifica el payload exterior.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is the payload after a For Each?","options":["An array of the payloads produced in each loop iteration","An array of each iteration's results","The original payload from before the For Each","The last iteration's result"],"explanation":"For Each doesn't modify the outer payload."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué variable contiene el número de iteración dentro de un For Each?","options":["vars.counter","attributes.iteration","vars.index, que empieza en cero","payload.counter"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"counter empieza en 1 por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which variable holds the iteration number inside a For Each?","options":["vars.counter","attributes.iteration","vars.index, which starts at zero","payload.counter"],"explanation":"counter starts at 1 by default."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué variable da acceso al mensaje completo original dentro de un For Each?","options":["payload.parent","attributes.root","vars.rootMessage","vars.originalPayload"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"rootMessage contiene el mensaje anterior al For Each.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which variable gives access to the original full message inside a For Each?","options":["payload.parent","attributes.root","vars.rootMessage","vars.originalPayload"],"explanation":"rootMessage holds the pre-For Each message."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con las variables modificadas dentro de un For Each?","options":["Solo persisten si son de tipo String","Se convierten en atributos del evento al salir del ámbito","Se descartan al terminar cada iteración","Los cambios persisten después del ámbito"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"A diferencia del payload, las variables se mantienen.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to variables modified inside a For Each?","options":["They persist only if String","They become event attributes when leaving the scope","They're discarded after each iteration","Changes persist after the scope"],"explanation":"Unlike the payload, variables persist."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el parámetro batchSize de For Each?","options":["Procesar en paralelo varios elementos","Limitar el número total de elementos","Agrupar varios elementos por iteración","Persistir los elementos en disco"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Cada iteración recibe un subarray.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does For Each's batchSize allow?","options":["Processing several elements in parallel","Limiting the total element count","Grouping several elements per iteration","Persisting elements to disk"],"explanation":"Each iteration gets a sub-array."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre por defecto si falla una iteración de For Each?","options":["Se reintenta indefinidamente","El error se propaga y se detiene el For Each","Se ignora sin registrar","Se salta el elemento y continúa con el siguiente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se puede envolver en Try para continuar.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens by default if a For Each iteration fails?","options":["It retries indefinitely","The error propagates and For Each stops","It's ignored unlogged","The element is skipped and the next continues"],"explanation":"Wrap in Try to continue."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ámbito procesa elementos de una colección en paralelo y devuelve los resultados?","options":["For Each con batchSize mayor que 1","Parallel For Each","Async dentro de un For Each","Cache"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Parallel For Each agrega resultados en orden.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which scope processes collection elements in parallel and returns results?","options":["For Each with batchSize over 1","Parallel For Each","Async inside a For Each","Cache"],"explanation":"Parallel For Each aggregates results in order."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué payload deja Parallel For Each al terminar?","options":["El payload original que había antes de entrar en el ámbito","El payload original","Solo el último resultado","Una colección con el resultado de cada ruta"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"A diferencia de For Each.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What payload does Parallel For Each leave when done?","options":["The original payload from before entering the scope","The original payload","Only the last result","A collection with each route's result"],"explanation":"Unlike For Each."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué está pensado un Batch Job?","options":["Atender peticiones HTTP síncronas de baja latencia","Procesar grandes volúmenes de registros de forma fiable y asíncrona","Enrutar mensajes por contenido hacia distintos sistemas en tiempo real","Transformar un único registro en tiempo real"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Batch persiste registros y procesa en bloques.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Batch Job designed for?","options":["Serving low-latency synchronous HTTP requests","Processing large record volumes reliably and asynchronously","Routing messages by content to different systems in real time","Transforming a single record in real time"],"explanation":"Batch persists records and processes in blocks."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tres fases tiene un Batch Job?","options":["Inicio, pausa y reanudación, controladas desde Runtime Manager","Validación, despliegue y monitorización","Carga y envío, procesamiento y finalización (On Complete)","Lectura, escritura y borrado"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Load and dispatch, process, on complete.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which three phases does a Batch Job have?","options":["Start, pause and resume, controlled from Runtime Manager","Validate, deploy and monitor","Load and dispatch, process, and On Complete","Read, write and delete"],"explanation":"Load and dispatch, process, on complete."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recibe la fase On Complete de un Batch Job como payload?","options":["El payload original de la entrada","El último registro","La lista completa de registros procesados","Un resumen con registros procesados, exitosos y fallidos"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"BatchJobResult con estadísticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Batch Job's On Complete phase receive as payload?","options":["The original input payload","The last record","The full list of processed records","A summary of processed, successful and failed records"],"explanation":"BatchJobResult with statistics."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un Batch Step?","options":["Una etapa por la que pasa cada registro","Un archivo de configuración del lote","Un tipo de origen de flujo","Un hilo del pool de procesamiento asignado a un registro concreto"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los registros pasan por los steps en orden.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a Batch Step?","options":["A stage each record passes through","A batch config file","A flow source type","A processing pool thread assigned to a specific record"],"explanation":"Records pass through steps in order."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué controla la política de aceptación (accept policy) de un Batch Step?","options":["El número de hilos del lote","El tamaño de bloque","Qué registros entran según su estado: no fallidos, solo fallidos o todos","El formato de salida"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"NO_FAILURES por defecto; ONLY_FAILURES; ALL.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Batch Step's accept policy control?","options":["Batch thread count","Block size","Which records enter by status: no failures, only failures or all","Output format"],"explanation":"NO_FAILURES by default; ONLY_FAILURES; ALL."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite la expresión de aceptación (accept expression) de un Batch Step?","options":["Filtrar registros por una condición","Reintentar registros fallidos","Cambiar el tamaño de bloque del lote según el contenido del registro","Cambiar el orden de los pasos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Solo procesa registros que cumplen la expresión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Batch Step accept expression allow?","options":["Filtering records by a condition","Retrying failed records","Changing the job's block size based on record content","Reordering steps"],"explanation":"Only matching records are processed."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el Batch Aggregator dentro de un Batch Step?","options":["Combina varios Batch Jobs en uno","Agrupa registros para procesarlos juntos, por ejemplo un bulk insert","Divide un registro en varios","Calcula estadísticas finales"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Aggregator con tamaño fijo o streaming.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Batch Aggregator do inside a Batch Step?","options":["Combines several Batch Jobs","Groups records to process together, e.g. a bulk insert","Splits one record into many","Computes final statistics"],"explanation":"Aggregator with fixed size or streaming."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tamaño de bloque (block size) usa un Batch Job por defecto?","options":["1.000 registros","1 registro","Todo el conjunto","100 registros"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Los registros se procesan en bloques de 100.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What block size does a Batch Job use by default?","options":["1,000 records","1 record","The whole set","100 records"],"explanation":"Records are processed in blocks of 100."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué controla maxFailedRecords en un Batch Job?","options":["El número de reintentos por registro","Cuántos registros pueden fallar antes de detener el lote","El tamaño de bloque","El número de steps que puede tener el lote como máximo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"0 detiene al primer fallo; -1 nunca.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does maxFailedRecords control in a Batch Job?","options":["Retries per record","How many records may fail before stopping the job","Block size","The maximum number of steps the job may have"],"explanation":"0 stops on first failure; -1 never."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué valor de maxFailedRecords permite que el lote continúe con cualquier número de fallos?","options":["100","-1","0","1"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"-1 = sin límite.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which maxFailedRecords value lets the job continue with any number of failures?","options":["100","-1","0","1"],"explanation":"-1 = unlimited."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con un registro que falla en un Batch Step?","options":["Se reintenta indefinidamente","Se marca como fallido y no pasa a los steps que solo aceptan no fallidos","Detiene siempre todo el lote inmediatamente","Se elimina del lote sin registrar el fallo en el resultado final"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Según maxFailedRecords y accept policy.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to a record that fails in a Batch Step?","options":["It retries indefinitely","It's marked failed and skips steps that only accept non-failed","It always stops the whole job immediately","It's dropped from the job without logging the failure in the result"],"explanation":"Per maxFailedRecords and accept policy."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué son las variables de registro en un Batch Job?","options":["Variables globales compartidas por todos los registros","Propiedades de configuración","Variables ligadas a cada registro que persisten entre steps","Atributos HTTP"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Cada registro conserva sus variables entre steps.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What are record variables in a Batch Job?","options":["Global variables shared by all records","Config properties","Variables tied to each record persisting across steps","HTTP attributes"],"explanation":"Each record keeps its variables across steps."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Es síncrono el Batch Job respecto al flujo que lo invoca?","options":["Solo si el lote tiene un step","Depende del tamaño de bloque: con bloques pequeños es síncrono","Sí, espera a que termine el último registro","No: el flujo continúa sin esperar el resultado del lote"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Batch es asíncrono.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Is the Batch Job synchronous relative to the invoking flow?","options":["Only with one step","Depends on block size: small blocks make it synchronous","Yes, it waits for the last record","No: the flow continues without waiting for the job"],"explanation":"Batch is asynchronous."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde persisten los registros durante un Batch Job?","options":["En la memoria del flujo invocante","En colas persistentes gestionadas por Mule","En el archivo pom.xml","En Exchange"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Permite recuperación ante reinicios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where do records persist during a Batch Job?","options":["In the invoking flow's memory","In persistent queues managed by Mule","In pom.xml","In Exchange"],"explanation":"It allows recovery on restart."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos casos de uso encajan con Batch? (Elige 2)","options":["Sincronizar cientos de miles de registros cada noche","Responder a una petición HTTP en milisegundos","Validar un único formulario web","Enrutar un mensaje por su tipo","Migrar datos entre sistemas"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Volumen y fiabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two use cases fit Batch? (Choose 2)","options":["Syncing hundreds of thousands of records nightly","Answering an HTTP request in milliseconds","Validating one web form","Routing a message by type","Migrating data between systems"],"explanation":"Volume and reliability."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué diferencia principal hay entre For Each y Batch Job?","options":["For Each solo funciona con XML","Batch no admite errores","For Each es síncrono y en memoria; Batch es asíncrono y persistente","For Each es asíncrono y Batch síncrono"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Elegir según volumen y fiabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the main difference between For Each and Batch Job?","options":["For Each only works with XML","Batch doesn't support errors","For Each is sync and in-memory; Batch is async and persistent","For Each is async and Batch sync"],"explanation":"Choose by volume and reliability."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué origen del conector Database facilita procesar solo filas nuevas automáticamente?","options":["Stored Procedure","On Table Row con watermark","Bulk Insert","Select dentro de un For Each"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Watermark automático.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Database source eases processing only new rows automatically?","options":["Stored Procedure","On Table Row with watermark","Bulk Insert","Select inside a For Each"],"explanation":"Automatic watermark."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se usa para guardar manualmente el último valor procesado entre ejecuciones?","options":["attributes","Object Store","Una variable de flujo","Un Logger"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Object Store persiste entre ejecuciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's used to manually store the last processed value between runs?","options":["attributes","Object Store","A flow variable","A Logger"],"explanation":"Object Store persists between runs."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué operaciones ofrece el conector Object Store?","options":["Select, Insert y Update","Read y Write de archivos","Store, Retrieve, Remove y Contains, entre otras","Publish y Consume"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Almacén clave-valor.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which operations does the Object Store connector offer?","options":["Select, Insert and Update","File Read and Write","Store, Retrieve, Remove and Contains, among others","Publish and Consume"],"explanation":"A key-value store."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica que un Object Store sea persistente?","options":["Que solo admite valores de tipo String y se borra al reiniciar","Que se replica en Exchange","Sus valores sobreviven a reinicios de la aplicación","Que se borra al terminar el flujo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"persistent=true.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a persistent Object Store mean?","options":["It only accepts String values and clears on restart","It's replicated in Exchange","Its values survive app restarts","It's cleared when the flow ends"],"explanation":"persistent=true."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace la operación Retrieve de Object Store si la clave no existe y hay valor por defecto?","options":["Crea la clave vacía","Lanza siempre un error","Devuelve todas las claves","Devuelve el valor por defecto"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"defaultValue evita OS:KEY_NOT_FOUND.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does Object Store Retrieve do if the key is missing but a default exists?","options":["Creates the key empty","Always throws","Returns all keys","Returns the default"],"explanation":"defaultValue avoids OS:KEY_NOT_FOUND."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué error lanza Retrieve si la clave no existe y no hay valor por defecto?","options":["OS:STORE_NOT_AVAILABLE","MULE:EXPRESSION","OS:KEY_NOT_FOUND","DB:QUERY_EXECUTION"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Error tipado del Object Store.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which error does Retrieve throw if the key is missing with no default?","options":["OS:STORE_NOT_AVAILABLE","MULE:EXPRESSION","OS:KEY_NOT_FOUND","DB:QUERY_EXECUTION"],"explanation":"Typed Object Store error."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón aplica el watermark manual con Object Store?","options":["Procesar toda la tabla en cada ejecución","Leer el último valor, consultar desde ahí y guardar el nuevo valor","Borrar todas las filas procesadas de la tabla origen","Guardar el payload completo en el Object Store"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Evita reprocesar datos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which pattern does manual watermarking with Object Store follow?","options":["Process the whole table each run","Read last value, query from there and store the new value","Delete all processed rows from the source table","Store the full payload in the Object Store"],"explanation":"It avoids reprocessing."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ámbitos procesan colecciones? (Elige 2)","options":["Choice","For Each","Try","Parallel For Each","Cache"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Iteración secuencial y paralela.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two scopes process collections? (Choose 2)","options":["Choice","For Each","Try","Parallel For Each","Cache"],"explanation":"Sequential and parallel iteration."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer en un Batch Step que inserta en base de datos para mejorar rendimiento?","options":["Insertar cada registro con un For Each dentro del step","Usar Flow Reference a un subflujo con Select","Usar un Batch Aggregator con Bulk Insert","Desactivar el pooling"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Agregar e insertar en bloque.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What improves performance in a Batch Step inserting into a database?","options":["Insert each record with a For Each in the step","Flow Reference to a Select subflow","Use a Batch Aggregator with Bulk Insert","Disable pooling"],"explanation":"Aggregate and bulk insert."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el parámetro maxConcurrency de un Batch Job?","options":["El tamaño del bloque","Cuántos steps puede tener el lote y en qué orden se ejecutan","Cuántos bloques se procesan en paralelo","Cuántos registros fallidos se admiten"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Controla el paralelismo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a Batch Job's maxConcurrency indicate?","options":["Block size","How many steps the job may have and their order","How many blocks process in parallel","How many failures are allowed"],"explanation":"It controls parallelism."}}},{"domain":"D7","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de entrada puede recibir un Batch Job?","options":["Solo un único objeto JSON","Solo un archivo XML","Solo un string con los registros separados por saltos de línea","Una colección iterable o un stream de registros"],"correct":[3]