 uno de respaldo?","options":["First Successful con ambas rutas","Choice sin condición","Round Robin, que alterna entre principal y respaldo","Scatter-Gather"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Fallback ordenado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What suits a primary service with a backup?","options":["First Successful with both routes","Choice with no condition","Round Robin, alternating primary and backup","Scatter-Gather"],"explanation":"Ordered fallback."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué expresión es válida en un when de Choice?","options":["{{country}}","${payload.country == \"ES\"}","payload.country = \"ES\"","#[payload.country == \"ES\"]"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Expresión DataWeave booleana.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which expression is valid in a Choice when?","options":["{{country}}","${payload.country == \"ES\"}","payload.country = \"ES\"","#[payload.country == \"ES\"]"],"explanation":"A boolean DataWeave expression."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve Choice como payload?","options":["Un booleano que indica qué condición se cumplió","El payload resultante de la ruta ejecutada","El payload original siempre","Un objeto con todas las rutas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"La ruta ejecutada define el resultado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does Choice return as payload?","options":["A boolean indicating which condition matched","The payload from the executed route","Always the original payload","An object with all routes"],"explanation":"The executed route defines the result."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error VALIDATION:NULL?","options":["Un email era incorrecto","Un servicio no respondió","Un valor era demasiado largo","Un valor esperado no nulo era nulo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Is not null falló.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does VALIDATION:NULL indicate?","options":["An email was invalid","A service didn't respond","A value was too long","A value expected non-null was null"],"explanation":"Is not null failed."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones mejoran el rendimiento de un Scatter-Gather con muchas rutas? (Elige 2)","options":["Añadir más rutas vacías","Configurar timeouts adecuados","Duplicar el payload","Limitar maxConcurrency","Usar Logger en cada ruta a DEBUG"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Control de concurrencia y tiempos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two actions improve a many-route Scatter-Gather's performance? (Choose 2)","options":["Add more empty routes","Set proper timeouts","Duplicate the payload","Limit maxConcurrency","Log at DEBUG in each route"],"explanation":"Concurrency and timeout control."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué router se usa para enviar el mismo mensaje a varios sistemas sin necesitar respuesta combinada, de forma asíncrona?","options":["Choice","Async o publicar en una cola","First Successful","Round Robin"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Fire-and-forget.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What sends the same message to several systems asynchronously without a combined response?","options":["Choice","Async or publishing to a queue","First Successful","Round Robin"],"explanation":"Fire-and-forget."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de validación es mejor hacer con APIkit que con el módulo Validation?","options":["Reglas de negocio complejas entre campos","Validación del contrato definido en la especificación","Comprobaciones contra la base de datos","Validaciones de estado en el CRM"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"APIkit valida contra el RAML; Validation para reglas de negocio.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which validation is better done with APIkit than with the Validation module?","options":["Complex cross-field business rules","Contract validation defined in the spec","Checks against the database","State checks in CRM"],"explanation":"APIkit validates against RAML; Validation for business rules."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el validador Matches regex?","options":["Comprobar que un texto cumple un patrón","Dividir un texto","Cifrar un texto con una clave definida en el patrón","Convertir texto a número"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Validación por expresión regular.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Matches regex validator allow?","options":["Checking text matches a pattern","Splitting text","Encrypting text with a key defined in the pattern","Converting text to number"],"explanation":"Regex validation."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si una ruta de First Successful falla y la siguiente también?","options":["Se reintenta la primera","Se ejecuta un Choice con las rutas restantes del router","Se lanza un error indicando que ninguna ruta tuvo éxito","Se devuelve el payload original sin error"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Error si todas fallan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if every First Successful route fails?","options":["The first retries","A Choice runs with the router's remaining routes","An error says no route succeeded","The original payload returns with no error"],"explanation":"Error if all fail."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para devolver un 400 al cliente cuando falla una validación de negocio?","options":["Usar Round Robin para enviar la petición a otro flujo sin validación","Dejar que se devuelva un 500 por defecto","Ignorar el error con un Logger","Mapear el error VALIDATION a un código 400 en el manejo de errores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Error handling con statusCode.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How to return a 400 when a business validation fails?","options":["Use Round Robin to send the request to an unvalidated flow","Let the default 500 return","Ignore it with a Logger","Map the VALIDATION error to 400 in error handling"],"explanation":"Error handling with statusCode."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué router ejecuta rutas según el contenido y admite una ruta por defecto?","options":["Choice","Scatter-Gather","Round Robin","Parallel For Each"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"otherwise es la ruta por defecto.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which router routes by content with a default route?","options":["Choice","Scatter-Gather","Round Robin","Parallel For Each"],"explanation":"otherwise is the default route."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos consideraciones hay al usar Scatter-Gather con servicios lentos? (Elige 2)","options":["No consume hilos","Solo admite dos rutas","Las rutas se ejecutan en serie","La respuesta total depende de la ruta más lenta","Conviene un timeout para no bloquear"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Espera a todas las rutas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two considerations apply to Scatter-Gather with slow services? (Choose 2)","options":["It uses no threads","It allows only two routes","Routes run serially","Total response depends on the slowest route","A timeout avoids blocking"],"explanation":"It waits for all routes."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un manejador On Error Propagate?","options":["Ignora el error sin ejecutar nada","Reintenta el procesador que falló","Ejecuta sus procesadores y vuelve a lanzar el error al llamador","Captura el error y el flujo termina con éxito"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El error se propaga hacia arriba.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an On Error Propagate handler do?","options":["Ignores the error running nothing","Retries the failing processor","Runs its processors and rethrows the error to the caller","Catches the error and the flow ends successfully"],"explanation":"The error propagates upward."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace un manejador On Error Continue?","options":["Detiene la aplicación","Reintenta el procesador","Relanza el error al flujo que llamó","Ejecuta sus procesadores y el flujo termina como si no hubiera error"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El resultado del handler se usa como respuesta.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an On Error Continue handler do?","options":["Stops the app","Retries the processor","Rethrows the error to the calling flow","Runs its processors and the flow ends as if no error"],"explanation":"The handler's result becomes the response."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Con un HTTP Listener, ¿qué código de estado se devuelve si el error termina en On Error Continue?","options":["400 siempre","200 (o el configurado en la respuesta normal)","404, porque el error indica que el recurso no se encontró","500 siempre"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se usa la respuesta normal, no la de error.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"With an HTTP Listener, which status returns if the error ends in On Error Continue?","options":["Always 400","200 (or the normal response config)","404, since the error says the resource wasn't found","Always 500"],"explanation":"The normal response is used, not the error one."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Con un HTTP Listener, ¿qué código se devuelve por defecto si el error se propaga sin manejar?","options":["200","500","302","204"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se usa la Error Response del listener.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"With an HTTP Listener, which code returns by default if the error propagates unhandled?","options":["200","500","302","204"],"explanation":"The listener's Error Response is used."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un flujo no tiene manejador de errores y ocurre un error?","options":["La aplicación se detiene","El error se ignora y el flujo continúa","Se usa el manejador por defecto, que registra y propaga","Se llama automáticamente al Scheduler de reintentos de la aplicación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El default error handler registra y relanza.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if a flow has no error handler and an error occurs?","options":["The app stops","The error is ignored and the flow continues","The default handler logs and propagates","The app's retry Scheduler is called automatically"],"explanation":"The default handler logs and rethrows."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un manejador de errores global (default error handler) de la aplicación?","options":["Una política de API Manager","Un error handler configurado para usarse en todos los flujos que no tengan uno","Un Logger global que registra todos los errores de la organización","Un flujo que se ejecuta al arrancar"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se configura en la configuración global con defaultErrorHandler.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an app's global default error handler?","options":["An API Manager policy","An error handler used by all flows lacking one","A global Logger recording every org error","A flow run at startup"],"explanation":"Set in global config with defaultErrorHandler."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué hace el ámbito Try?","options":["Reintenta los procesadores hasta que funcionen","Cachea los resultados de los procesadores para reutilizarlos","Permite manejar errores de un grupo de procesadores","Ejecuta en paralelo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Try tiene su propio error handling.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does the Try scope do?","options":["Retries processors until they work","Caches processor results for reuse","Handles errors for a group of processors","Runs in parallel"],"explanation":"Try has its own error handling."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Dentro de un Try con On Error Continue, ¿qué pasa tras manejar el error?","options":["El error se propaga al flujo padre","Se reintenta el Try completo hasta que termina sin errores","El flujo continúa con el siguiente procesador tras el Try","El flujo termina inmediatamente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El Try se considera exitoso.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Inside a Try with On Error Continue, what happens after handling?","options":["The error propagates to the parent","The whole Try retries until it ends without errors","The flow continues after the Try","The flow ends immediately"],"explanation":"The Try is treated as successful."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Dentro de un Try con On Error Propagate, ¿qué pasa tras manejar el error?","options":["Se reinicia la app","El error se ignora","El flujo continúa tras el Try","El error sale del Try hacia el manejo del flujo"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se relanza al nivel superior.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Inside a Try with On Error Propagate, what happens after handling?","options":["The app restarts","The error is ignored","The flow continues after the Try","The error leaves the Try to the flow's handling"],"explanation":"It's rethrown upward."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Cómo se filtra un On Error para un tipo concreto, como HTTP:NOT_FOUND?","options":["Con una propiedad del YAML","Con un Choice dentro del flujo","Con un Logger","Con el atributo type del manejador"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"type=\"HTTP:NOT_FOUND\" o when=expresión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How is an On Error filtered for a specific type like HTTP:NOT_FOUND?","options":["With a YAML property","With a Choice in the flow","With a Logger","With the handler's type attribute"],"explanation":"type=\"HTTP:NOT_FOUND\" or when=expression."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿En qué orden se evalúan varios On Error dentro de un Error Handler?","options":["El último primero","Al azar, para repartir la carga entre manejadores","En orden; se ejecuta el primero que coincide","Todos los que coinciden en paralelo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El orden importa: de específico a genérico.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"In what order are several On Errors evaluated in an Error Handler?","options":["The last first","Randomly, to spread load across handlers","In order; the first match runs","All matching in parallel"],"explanation":"Order matters: specific to generic."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué variable contiene información del error dentro de un manejador?","options":["exception","error","attributes.error","vars.error"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"error.description, error.errorType, error.cause.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which variable holds error info inside a handler?","options":["exception","error","attributes.error","vars.error"],"explanation":"error.description, error.errorType, error.cause."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve error.errorType.identifier para un error HTTP:NOT_FOUND?","options":["404","NOT_FOUND","HTTP:NOT_FOUND","HTTP"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"namespace = HTTP, identifier = NOT_FOUND.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does error.errorType.identifier return for HTTP:NOT_FOUND?","options":["404","NOT_FOUND","HTTP:NOT_FOUND","HTTP"],"explanation":"namespace = HTTP, identifier = NOT_FOUND."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite el mapeo de errores (error mapping) en un procesador?","options":["Reintentar el procesador","Ignorar todos los errores del procesador","Convertir un tipo de error en otro propio de la aplicación","Cambiar el payload"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"P. ej. HTTP:CONNECTIVITY → APP:BACKEND_DOWN.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does error mapping on a processor allow?","options":["Retrying the processor","Ignoring all the processor's errors","Converting an error type into an app-specific one","Changing the payload"],"explanation":"E.g. HTTP:CONNECTIVITY → APP:BACKEND_DOWN."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente lanza un error personalizado de forma explícita?","options":["Raise Error","Set Payload con texto de error","Logger con nivel ERROR","Choice"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Raise Error con type y description.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which component explicitly raises a custom error?","options":["Raise Error","Set Payload with error text","Logger at ERROR","Choice"],"explanation":"Raise Error with type and description."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error genérico captura cualquier error?","options":["HTTP:ANY","MULE:ALL","ERROR:*","ANY"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"ANY es el tipo raíz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which generic error type catches any error?","options":["HTTP:ANY","MULE:ALL","ERROR:*","ANY"],"explanation":"ANY is the root type."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ámbito reintenta un grupo de procesadores hasta que funcione o se agoten los intentos?","options":["Async","For Each","Until Successful","Try"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"maxRetries y millisBetweenRetries.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which scope retries processors until success or attempts run out?","options":["Async","For Each","Until Successful","Try"],"explanation":"maxRetries and millisBetweenRetries."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué error se lanza cuando Until Successful agota los reintentos?","options":["HTTP:TIMEOUT","MULE:RETRY_EXHAUSTED","MULE:EXPRESSION","ANY, porque Until Successful no tiene un tipo propio"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Indica fin de reintentos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which error is raised when Until Successful exhausts retries?","options":["HTTP:TIMEOUT","MULE:RETRY_EXHAUSTED","MULE:EXPRESSION","ANY, since Until Successful has no type of its own"],"explanation":"It signals retries are exhausted."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Un flujo A llama a B con Flow Reference. B tiene On Error Continue y falla. ¿Qué ve A?","options":["Un 500 automático","Una ejecución correcta con el payload del manejador de B","El error de B propagado","Nada: la ejecución de A queda en pausa sin respuesta"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"On Error Continue no propaga.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Flow A calls B via Flow Reference. B has On Error Continue and fails. What does A see?","options":["An automatic 500","A successful run with B's handler payload","B's error propagated","Nothing: A's execution hangs with no response"],"explanation":"On Error Continue doesn't propagate."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Un flujo A llama a B con Flow Reference. B tiene On Error Propagate. ¿Qué ocurre en A?","options":["A continúa como si nada","A se reinicia y vuelve a llamar a B automáticamente","A recibe un payload vacío","El error llega a A y se gestiona con su manejo de errores"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El error se propaga al llamador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Flow A calls B via Flow Reference. B has On Error Propagate. What happens in A?","options":["A continues as if nothing happened","A restarts and calls B again automatically","A gets an empty payload","The error reaches A and is handled by A's error handling"],"explanation":"The error propagates to the caller."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos datos se suelen devolver al cliente en una respuesta de error bien diseñada? (Elige 2)","options":["El SQL ejecutado","Un mensaje descriptivo","Credenciales internas","La traza de pila completa","Un código o identificador de error"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"Información útil sin exponer internos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two items does a well-designed error response return? (Choose 2)","options":["The executed SQL","A descriptive message","Internal credentials","The full stack trace","An error code or identifier"],"explanation":"Useful info without exposing internals."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se configura el código de estado HTTP para respuestas de error del listener?","options":["En Exchange, dentro de la documentación de la API","En el Logger","En el pom.xml","En la sección Error Response del HTTP Listener"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se suele usar una variable httpStatus.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where is the HTTP status for listener error responses configured?","options":["In Exchange, within the API documentation","In the Logger","In pom.xml","In the HTTP Listener's Error Response section"],"explanation":"Often an httpStatus variable is used."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué patrón es común para fijar el código de error de la respuesta HTTP?","options":["Guardar el código en una variable y usarla en la respuesta del listener","Es