rowing?","options":["Turn the error into success","Just delete the payload","Restart the app to clear the error state","Log the error or clean up resources"],"explanation":"Logging and compensation."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos ámbitos o componentes ayudan a gestionar fallos transitorios? (Elige 2)","options":["Logger","Set Variable","Until Successful","Choice","Estrategia de reconexión del conector"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Reintentos y reconexión.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two scopes/components help handle transient failures? (Choose 2)","options":["Logger","Set Variable","Until Successful","Choice","Connector reconnection strategy"],"explanation":"Retries and reconnection."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué expresión filtra un On Error por el código HTTP devuelto por un servicio remoto?","options":["type=\"404\"","when=\"${statusCode}\"","type=\"HTTP:404\"","when=\"#[error.muleMessage.attributes.statusCode == 404]\""],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Se puede inspeccionar el mensaje del error.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which expression filters an On Error by the remote HTTP status?","options":["type=\"404\"","when=\"${statusCode}\"","type=\"HTTP:404\"","when=\"#[error.muleMessage.attributes.statusCode == 404]\""],"explanation":"The error's message can be inspected."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error de APIkit se suele mapear a 405?","options":["APIKIT:NOT_ACCEPTABLE","APIKIT:BAD_REQUEST","APIKIT:NOT_FOUND","APIKIT:METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Method not allowed.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which APIkit error is usually mapped to 405?","options":["APIKIT:NOT_ACCEPTABLE","APIKIT:BAD_REQUEST","APIKIT:NOT_FOUND","APIKIT:METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED"],"explanation":"Method not allowed."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para no exponer detalles internos en errores 500?","options":["Devolver error.description completo siempre","Devolver el XML de configuración","Devolver la traza de Java","Devolver un mensaje genérico y registrar el detalle internamente"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Seguridad de la información.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What avoids exposing internals in 500 errors?","options":["Always return the full error.description","Return the config XML","Return the Java stack trace","Return a generic message and log details internally"],"explanation":"Information security."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error lanza Raise Error si se define type=\"APP:INVALID_ORDER\"?","options":["VALIDATION:INVALID_ORDER","APP:INVALID_ORDER","HTTP:BAD_REQUEST","MULE:ANY"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Namespace propio de la app.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which error does Raise Error throw with type=\"APP:INVALID_ORDER\"?","options":["VALIDATION:INVALID_ORDER","APP:INVALID_ORDER","HTTP:BAD_REQUEST","MULE:ANY"],"explanation":"An app-specific namespace."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con las transacciones si se produce un error en un Try transaccional con On Error Propagate?","options":["Se revierte la transacción","Se duplica","Se ignora","Se confirma la transacción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Propagate provoca rollback.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to transactions if a transactional Try errors with On Error Propagate?","options":["The transaction rolls back","It duplicates","It's ignored","The transaction commits"],"explanation":"Propagate triggers rollback."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre con la transacción en un Try transaccional con On Error Continue?","options":["Se reintenta","Se confirma (commit)","Se pausa","Se revierte"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Continue se trata como éxito.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens to the transaction in a transactional Try with On Error Continue?","options":["It retries","It commits","It pauses","It rolls back"],"explanation":"Continue counts as success."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos jerarquías de tipos de error son ciertas? (Elige 2)","options":["MULE:EXPRESSION incluye a ANY","ANY incluye a todos los tipos","DB incluye a APIKIT","VALIDATION incluye a HTTP","HTTP:NOT_FOUND es un tipo de error HTTP"],"correct":[1,4],"explanation":"ANY es la raíz.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two error type hierarchies are true? (Choose 2)","options":["MULE:EXPRESSION includes ANY","ANY includes all types","DB includes APIKIT","VALIDATION includes HTTP","HTTP:NOT_FOUND is an HTTP error type"],"explanation":"ANY is the root."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para tratar de forma distinta errores de conexión y de validación en el mismo flujo?","options":["Ignorar los de validación","Usar Round Robin","Varios On Error con tipos distintos","Un único On Error ANY con un Choice dentro obligatoriamente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Handlers específicos por tipo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"How to treat connection and validation errors differently in one flow?","options":["Ignore validation ones","Use Round Robin","Several On Errors with different types","Mandatorily one On Error ANY with a Choice inside"],"explanation":"Type-specific handlers."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si un error se produce dentro de un On Error?","options":["Se ejecuta el siguiente On Error","Se reintenta el On Error","Se propaga el nuevo error","Se ignora"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Los errores en handlers se propagan.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if an error occurs inside an On Error?","options":["The next On Error runs","The On Error retries","The new error propagates","It's ignored"],"explanation":"Errors in handlers propagate."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica error.description?","options":["El payload","El tipo del error","El texto descriptivo del error","El nombre del flujo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Mensaje legible.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does error.description hold?","options":["The payload","The error type","The error's descriptive text","The flow name"],"explanation":"A readable message."}}},{"domain":"D8","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué devuelve payload groupBy $.country sobre un array de clientes?","options":["Un array ordenado alfabéticamente por el nombre del país de cada cliente","El número de clientes distintos que hay en cada país de la lista","Un array de arrays con un cliente en cada posición","Un objeto cuyas claves son países"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"groupBy devuelve objeto clave → array.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does payload groupBy $.country return on a customer array?","options":["An array sorted alphabetically by each customer's country name","The number of distinct customers per country in the list","An array of arrays with one customer each","An object keyed by country"],"explanation":"groupBy returns key → array object."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para que una API rechace pedidos con cantidad negativa antes de procesarlos?","options":["Un Round Robin entre dos implementaciones del flujo","Un validador al inicio del flujo","Un Scatter-Gather que envíe el pedido a todos los sistemas a la vez","Un Logger que registre la cantidad negativa y continúe con el proceso"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Validación temprana.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What makes an API reject orders with negative quantity before processing?","options":["A Round Robin between two flow implementations","A validator at flow start","A Scatter-Gather sending the order to every system at once","A Logger recording the negative quantity and continuing"],"explanation":"Early validation."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué router conviene para llamar a un CRM y a un ERP a la vez y devolver ambos datos combinados?","options":["Round Robin, que alterna entre CRM y ERP en cada petición","Scatter-Gather","First Successful, que llama a ambos y combina las respuestas","Choice, que ejecuta todas las rutas cuya condición se cumple a la vez"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Ejecución paralela con agregación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which router calls a CRM and an ERP at once and returns both combined?","options":["Round Robin, alternating CRM and ERP per request","Scatter-Gather","First Successful, which calls both and merges responses","Choice, which runs every matching route at once"],"explanation":"Parallel execution with aggregation."}}},{"domain":"D9","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de error conviene mapear cuando un validador de negocio falla y la API debe responder 422?","options":["Un Choice tras el validador que compruebe si hubo error","El error VALIDATION a un On Error que fije 422","Un Raise Error de tipo HTTP:INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR","Un On Error Continue genérico que devuelva siempre 200 al cliente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Mapear el tipo al código adecuado.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which mapping fits when a business validator fails and the API must answer 422?","options":["A Choice after the validator checking for errors","The VALIDATION error to an On Error setting 422","A Raise Error of type HTTP:INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR","A generic On Error Continue always returning 200"],"explanation":"Map the type to the right code."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"Un HTTP Request falla de forma intermitente por la red. ¿Qué solución es más adecuada?","options":["Aumentar el nivel de log a DEBUG para que el error deje de ocurrir","Un On Error Continue que oculte el fallo y devuelva una respuesta vacía al cliente","Until Successful o reconexión","Sustituir el HTTP Request por un Logger"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Reintentos para fallos transitorios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An HTTP Request fails intermittently due to the network. Which solution fits best?","options":["Raising the log level to DEBUG so the error stops","An On Error Continue hiding the failure and returning an empty response","Until Successful or reconnection","Replacing the HTTP Request with a Logger"],"explanation":"Retries for transient failures."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre si dos On Error del mismo handler coinciden con el error?","options":["Solo se ejecuta el primero","Se ejecutan los dos en el orden en que aparecen en el manejador","Se ejecuta el último porque sobrescribe al anterior","Se lanza un error de configuración al desplegar"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Se ejecuta el primero que coincide.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens if two On Errors in the same handler match the error?","options":["Only the first runs","Both run in the order they appear in the handler","The last runs since it overrides the first","A config error is raised at deploy"],"explanation":"The first match runs."}}},{"domain":"D10","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos variables del error son útiles para registrar un fallo? (Elige 2)","options":["payload del flujo de otra aplicación","vars.counter del último For Each ejecutado","attributes.queryParams de la petición de salida","error.errorType","error.description"],"correct":[3,4],"explanation":"Tipo y descripción.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two error variables are useful for logging a failure? (Choose 2)","options":["Another app's flow payload","vars.counter from the last For Each","attributes.queryParams of the outbound request","error.errorType","error.description"],"explanation":"Type and description."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta de Anypoint Studio permite detener la ejecución en un procesador e inspeccionar el evento?","options":["El editor de la especificación RAML con el servicio de simulación","El portal de Exchange","El depurador con puntos de interrupción","Runtime Manager con la vista de alertas de la aplicación"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Breakpoints en el Mule Debugger.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which Studio tool pauses execution at a processor to inspect the event?","options":["The RAML spec editor with the mocking service","The Exchange portal","The debugger with breakpoints","Runtime Manager's app alerts view"],"explanation":"Breakpoints in the Mule Debugger."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué se puede evaluar en el depurador de Studio mientras la ejecución está detenida?","options":["Las políticas de API Manager","La configuración de red del sistema operativo","El código fuente de los conectores instalados desde Exchange","Expresiones DataWeave sobre el evento"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Evaluate expression.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What can be evaluated in Studio's debugger while paused?","options":["API Manager policies","The OS network configuration","Source code of connectors installed from Exchange","DataWeave expressions on the event"],"explanation":"Evaluate expression."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Dónde se ven los logs de una aplicación desplegada en CloudHub?","options":["En Design Center, en la pestaña de la especificación de la API","En Runtime Manager","En el portal público de Exchange","En el archivo pom.xml del proyecto"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Runtime Manager muestra logs de la app.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Where are a CloudHub app's logs viewed?","options":["In Design Center, on the API spec tab","In Runtime Manager","On the public Exchange portal","In the project's pom.xml"],"explanation":"Runtime Manager shows app logs."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué archivo configura los niveles de log de una aplicación Mule?","options":["log4j2.xml","pom.xml en la sección de plugins de Maven","mule-artifact.json, en la sección de dependencias del proyecto","config.yaml"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Log4j 2 controla categorías y niveles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which file configures a Mule app's log levels?","options":["log4j2.xml","pom.xml in the Maven plugins section","mule-artifact.json, in the project dependencies section","config.yaml"],"explanation":"Log4j 2 controls categories and levels."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nivel de log muestra más detalle?","options":["ERROR, porque registra la información completa de cada evento procesado","TRACE","INFO","WARN"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"TRACE > DEBUG > INFO > WARN > ERROR.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which log level shows the most detail?","options":["ERROR, since it records full info for each processed event","TRACE","INFO","WARN"],"explanation":"TRACE > DEBUG > INFO > WARN > ERROR."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué herramienta permite escribir pruebas unitarias de flujos Mule?","options":["Postman","Runtime Manager","JUnit sin ninguna integración con el runtime de Mule ni con los flujos","MUnit"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"MUnit prueba flujos con mocks y aserciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which tool writes unit tests for Mule flows?","options":["Postman","Runtime Manager","JUnit with no integration with the Mule runtime or flows","MUnit"],"explanation":"MUnit tests flows with mocks and assertions."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Para qué sirve Mock When en MUnit?","options":["Simular la respuesta de un procesador","Desplegar la app","Ejecutar el procesador real contra el sistema de producción durante la prueba","Registrar el resultado en el log de Runtime Manager"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Evita llamar a sistemas reales.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is MUnit Mock When for?","options":["Simulating a processor's response","Deploying the app","Running the real processor against production during the test","Logging the result in Runtime Manager"],"explanation":"It avoids calling real systems."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué componente de MUnit comprueba el valor de una expresión?","options":["Mock When, que también compara el payload esperado con el real","Set Event, que verifica el resultado del flujo","Assert That (o Assert Equals)","Spy"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Aserciones con matchers.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which MUnit component checks an expression's value?","options":["Mock When, which also compares expected and actual payload","Set Event, which verifies the flow result","Assert That (or Assert Equals)","Spy"],"explanation":"Assertions with matchers."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica la cobertura de MUnit?","options":["El número de usuarios que han ejecutado la API en producción","El tiempo medio de respuesta de la aplicación desplegada","El tamaño del JAR","El porcentaje de procesadores ejecutados por las pruebas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Puede exigirse un mínimo en el build.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MUnit coverage indicate?","options":["The number of users who ran the API in production","The deployed app's average response time","The JAR size","The share of processors executed by tests"],"explanation":"A minimum can be enforced in the build."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"Una app devuelve datos incorrectos tras una transformación. ¿Qué es lo más rápido para diagnosticarlo en local?","options":["Desplegar en producción y revisar las quejas de los clientes al día siguiente","Reinstalar Anypoint Studio y volver a importar el proyecto","Depurar y revisar el payload antes y después","Borrar el Transform"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Breakpoints alrededor de la transformación.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An app returns wrong data after a transformation. What's fastest to diagnose locally?","options":["Deploy to production and review customer complaints next day","Reinstall Anypoint Studio and reimport the project","Debug and check the payload before and after","Delete the Transform"],"explanation":"Breakpoints around the transformation."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene registrar para seguir una petición entre varias APIs?","options":["La contraseña del usuario de integración","Nada","Un identificador de correlación","El payload completo con todos los datos personales del cliente en cada paso"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"correlationId permite trazabilidad.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be logged to trace a request across several APIs?","option