 attached to production","Restarting Studio","Editing XML on the worker"],"explanation":"Logs and monitoring."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene evitar en los logs de producción?","options":["Mensajes de nivel INFO con el identificador de correlación de cada petición","Datos sensibles","El nombre del flujo que procesa la petición","Marcas de tiempo"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"No registrar PII ni secretos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be avoided in production logs?","options":["INFO messages with each request's correlation ID","Sensitive data","The name of the flow processing the request","Timestamps"],"explanation":"Don't log PII or secrets."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite la herramienta Spy de MUnit?","options":["Inspeccionar el evento antes y después de un procesador","Simular la respuesta de un sistema externo con datos de ejemplo","Cambiar la configuración","Desplegar la aplicación en un entorno de pruebas aislado"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Spy añade verificaciones alrededor de un procesador.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MUnit Spy allow?","options":["Inspecting the event before and after a processor","Simulating an external system response with sample data","Changing config","Deploying the app to an isolated test environment"],"explanation":"Spy adds checks around a processor."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica Verify Call en MUnit?","options":["Cuántas veces se llamó a un procesador","La cobertura","El valor exacto del payload al final de la prueba ejecutada","El tiempo de respuesta máximo permitido para el flujo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Verifica invocaciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MUnit Verify Call check?","options":["How many times a processor was called","Coverage","The exact payload value at the end of the test","The flow's max allowed response time"],"explanation":"It verifies invocations."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene si un flujo funciona en local pero falla en CloudHub con error de conexión a la base de datos?","options":["Revisar red, propiedades del entorno y acceso del worker","Borrar los tests de MUnit del proyecto","Cambiar el Logger a TRACE en local","Reinstalar Anypoint Studio en el equipo del desarrollador"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Diferencias de entorno y red.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What if a flow works locally but fails on CloudHub with a DB connection error?","options":["Check network, environment properties and worker access","Delete the project's MUnit tests","Set the Logger to TRACE locally","Reinstall Anypoint Studio on the developer's machine"],"explanation":"Environment and network differences."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué categoría de log conviene subir a DEBUG para ver el tráfico HTTP?","options":["La del conector HTTP","La de MUnit","La de Exchange","La raíz de toda la aplicación de forma permanente en producción"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Ajustar categorías concretas temporalmente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which log category should be raised to DEBUG to see HTTP traffic?","options":["The HTTP connector's","MUnit's","Exchange's","The whole app's root permanently in production"],"explanation":"Tune specific categories temporarily."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite Set Event en MUnit?","options":["Preparar el evento de entrada de la prueba","Simular un procesador","Registrar en el log los resultados de cada aserción","Desplegar la app"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Define payload, atributos y variables de entrada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MUnit Set Event allow?","options":["Preparing the test's input event","Mocking a processor","Logging each assertion's results","Deploying the app"],"explanation":"It sets input payload, attributes and vars."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ventaja tiene ejecutar MUnit en el pipeline de CI?","options":["Que la app se ejecuta más rápido","Que no hace falta Runtime Manager","Detectar regresiones antes de desplegar","Ninguna: MUnit solo puede ejecutarse desde Anypoint Studio"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Calidad automatizada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's the benefit of running MUnit in CI?","options":["The app runs faster","No Runtime Manager needed","Catching regressions before deploying","None: MUnit can only run from Anypoint Studio"],"explanation":"Automated quality."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene comprobar si una API devuelve 404 para todas las rutas tras desplegar?","options":["La contraseña de la base de datos","La versión de Java del equipo local","La ruta base del listener y la configuración de APIkit","El nivel de log"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Path y router.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What to check if an API returns 404 on every path after deploying?","options":["Database password","Local Java version","Listener base path and APIkit config","Log level"],"explanation":"Path and router."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el error MULE:EXPRESSION en el log?","options":["Falta un permiso de Access Management","El puerto está ocupado","Una expresión DataWeave falló al evaluarse","El servidor remoto no respondió"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Revisar la expresión y los datos de entrada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MULE:EXPRESSION in the log indicate?","options":["An Access Management permission is missing","The port is taken","A DataWeave expression failed to evaluate","The remote server didn't respond"],"explanation":"Review the expression and input data."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos acciones son buenas prácticas de logging? (Elige 2)","options":["Usar niveles adecuados","Desactivar todos los logs","Registrar contraseñas para depurar","Registrar todo a TRACE en producción","Registrar entrada y salida de flujos clave"],"correct":[0,4],"explanation":"Logs útiles y proporcionados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two are logging best practices? (Choose 2)","options":["Use proper levels","Disable all logs","Log passwords to debug","Log everything at TRACE in production","Log entry and exit of key flows"],"explanation":"Useful, proportionate logs."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es CloudHub?","options":["Un editor web de especificaciones RAML y OpenAPI","La plataforma gestionada de MuleSoft para ejecutar aplicaciones en la nube","Un repositorio de código fuente para proyectos Mule compartidos entre equipos","Un servicio de colas"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"iPaaS gestionado (CloudHub y CloudHub 2.0).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is CloudHub?","options":["A web editor for RAML and OpenAPI specs","MuleSoft's managed platform for running apps in the cloud","A source repository for Mule projects shared across teams","A queue service"],"explanation":"Managed iPaaS (CloudHub and CloudHub 2.0)."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un worker en CloudHub 1.0?","options":["Una instancia dedicada que ejecuta la aplicación","Una política","Un usuario de Anypoint Platform con permisos de despliegue en el entorno","Un flujo de la aplicación que procesa peticiones en paralelo"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Se elige tamaño (vCores) y número.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is a worker in CloudHub 1.0?","options":["A dedicated instance running the app","A policy","An Anypoint user with deploy permissions in the environment","An app flow processing requests in parallel"],"explanation":"You choose size (vCores) and count."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué aporta desplegar una aplicación en dos workers?","options":["Menos coste","Que cada worker ejecuta un flujo distinto de la aplicación","Alta disponibilidad y más capacidad","Que se comparten las variables entre ambos workers automáticamente"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Escalado horizontal.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does deploying an app on two workers give?","options":["Lower cost","Each worker runs a different app flow","High availability and more capacity","Variables auto-shared between both workers"],"explanation":"Horizontal scaling."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué nombre debe tener una aplicación en CloudHub 1.0?","options":["Cualquiera","Igual al nombre del proyecto en Anypoint Studio obligatoriamente","Único solo dentro de la unidad de negocio y del entorno seleccionado","Único en todo CloudHub"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Forma parte del dominio cloudhub.io.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What name must a CloudHub 1.0 app have?","options":["Any","Mandatorily equal to the Studio project name","Unique only within the business group and selected environment","Unique across CloudHub"],"explanation":"It's part of the cloudhub.io domain."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es un proxy de API en API Manager?","options":["Una copia de seguridad de la implementación de la API","Un servidor DNS que resuelve el dominio de la API","Un conector que replica la API en otra región de CloudHub","Una app que intercepta peticiones para aplicar políticas"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Útil para APIs no Mule o despliegues separados.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is an API proxy in API Manager?","options":["A backup of the API implementation","A DNS server resolving the API domain","A connector replicating the API in another CloudHub region","An app intercepting requests to apply policies"],"explanation":"Useful for non-Mule APIs or separate deployments."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es API Autodiscovery?","options":["Un tipo de log","Vincular una app desplegada con su instancia en API Manager","Descubrir automáticamente APIs públicas de terceros en internet","Generar especificaciones RAML a partir del código de la aplicación"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Se configura con el API ID.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is API Autodiscovery?","options":["A log type","Linking a deployed app to its API Manager instance","Auto-discovering third-party public APIs on the internet","Generating RAML specs from app code"],"explanation":"Configured with the API ID."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué necesita Autodiscovery además del API ID?","options":["Una política de rate limiting ya aplicada","Credenciales de la organización en el runtime","Un archivo RAML local","El código fuente de los consumidores de la API"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Client ID/secret de la organización o entorno.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does Autodiscovery need besides the API ID?","options":["A rate-limiting policy already applied","Org credentials on the runtime","A local RAML file","The API consumers' source code"],"explanation":"Org or environment client ID/secret."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política limita el número de peticiones por periodo para toda la API?","options":["Rate Limiting","Client ID Enforcement, que también limita el número de peticiones","IP Allowlist","CORS"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Rate limiting global.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy limits requests per period for the whole API?","options":["Rate Limiting","Client ID Enforcement, which also limits request counts","IP Allowlist","CORS"],"explanation":"Global rate limiting."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política limita peticiones por consumidor según su nivel de SLA?","options":["Spike Control aplicado a toda la API sin distinguir consumidores","Header Injection","Basic Authentication","Rate Limiting - SLA Based"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Requiere SLA tiers y contratos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy limits requests per consumer by SLA tier?","options":["Spike Control applied API-wide without distinguishing consumers","Header Injection","Basic Authentication","Rate Limiting - SLA Based"],"explanation":"Needs SLA tiers and contracts."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política exige que los consumidores envíen client_id y client_secret?","options":["Spike Control","JSON Threat Protection","Client ID Enforcement","Rate Limiting sin contratos de cliente registrados"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Valida credenciales de aplicaciones cliente.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy requires consumers to send client_id and client_secret?","options":["Spike Control","JSON Threat Protection","Client ID Enforcement","Rate Limiting with no registered client contracts"],"explanation":"It validates client app credentials."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política suaviza picos de tráfico encolando o rechazando peticiones?","options":["Client ID Enforcement","CORS","Spike Control","Message Logging"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Protege el backend de ráfagas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy smooths traffic spikes by queuing or rejecting requests?","options":["Client ID Enforcement","CORS","Spike Control","Message Logging"],"explanation":"It protects the backend from bursts."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué código HTTP devuelve una política de rate limiting cuando se supera el límite?","options":["404 Not Found","401 Unauthorized, porque el cliente ha perdido sus credenciales","503 siempre","429 Too Many Requests"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"429.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which HTTP code does a rate-limiting policy return when exceeded?","options":["404 Not Found","401 Unauthorized, since the client lost its credentials","Always 503","429 Too Many Requests"],"explanation":"429."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos pasos hacen falta para que un consumidor use una API con SLA tiers? (Elige 2)","options":["Desplegar la API en su propio worker","Descargar el código fuente de la API","Solicitar acceso a un nivel de SLA","Registrar una aplicación cliente","Editar la política en API Manager"],"correct":[2,3],"explanation":"Contrato con un tier.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two steps let a consumer use an API with SLA tiers? (Choose 2)","options":["Deploy the API on their own worker","Download the API source","Request access to an SLA tier","Register a client application","Edit the policy in API Manager"],"explanation":"A contract with a tier."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué tipo de despliegue usa servidores gestionados por el cliente con Runtime Manager?","options":["CloudHub 2.0 compartido en regiones de MuleSoft","Runtime Fabric en la nube de MuleSoft únicamente","Híbrido (servidores on-premises registrados)","Exchange"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"El runtime se registra en Runtime Manager.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which deployment uses customer-managed servers with Runtime Manager?","options":["Shared CloudHub 2.0 in MuleSoft regions","Runtime Fabric only in MuleSoft's cloud","Hybrid (registered on-prem servers)","Exchange"],"explanation":"The runtime registers with Runtime Manager."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es Runtime Fabric?","options":["Un tejido de red entre los workers de CloudHub 1.0 en la misma región","Una plataforma de contenedores para ejecutar Mule en infraestructura del cliente","Un conector para ejecutar flujos en máquinas virtuales de Azure","Una política de seguridad de API Manager"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"Basado en Kubernetes.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Runtime Fabric?","options":["A network fabric between CloudHub 1.0 workers in one region","A container platform to run Mule on customer infrastructure","A connector to run flows on Azure virtual machines","An API Manager security policy"],"explanation":"Kubernetes-based."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué propiedad conviene marcar como segura en Runtime Manager para ocultarla?","options":["El nombre de la aplicación y su versión publicada en Exchange","La región","Contraseñas y secretos","El número de workers asignados en el entorno"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"secureProperties en mule-artifact.json.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which property should be marked secure in Runtime Manager to hide it?","options":["The app name and version published to Exchange","The region","Passwords and secrets","The number of workers assigned in the environment"],"explanation":"secureProperties in mule-artifact.json."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene usar para desplegar Mule automáticamente desde un pipeline?","options":["Copiar el proyecto por correo al equipo de operaciones","Exchange","El Mule Maven plugin o la CLI de Anypoint","Subir el JAR a mano en Runtime Manager en cada versión publicada"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Automatización CI/CD.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What deploys Mule automatically from a pipeline?","options":["Emailing the project to operations","Exchange","The Mule Maven plugin or Anypoint CLI","Uploading the JAR by hand in Runtime Manager each release"],"explanation":"CI/CD automation."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política restringe el acceso a ciertas IP?","options":["CORS","Rate Limiting por dirección IP del cliente","Message Logging","IP Allowlist"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Lista de IPs permitidas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy restricts access to certain IPs?","options":["CORS","Rate Limiting by client IP","Message Logging","IP Allowlist"],"explanation":"A list of allowed IPs."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política valida tokens OAuth 2.0?","options":["Spike Control","Una política de validación de tokens OAuth o JWT","Client ID Enforcement","Basic Authentication sobre las credenciales del cliente"],"correct":[1],"explanation":"JWT Validation u OAuth token enforcement.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy validates OAuth 2.0 tokens?","options":["Spike Control","An OAuth or JWT token validation policy","Client ID Enforcement","Basic Authentication on client credentials"],"explanation":"JWT Validation or OAuth token enforcement."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué ocurre al aplicar una política en API Manager a una API con Autodiscovery?","options":["Hay que redesplegar la aplicación para que la política tenga efecto","Se borra la API","La política solo afecta a la documentación de Exchange","Se aplica sin redesplegar la aplicación"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"El runtime descarga las políticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What happens when a policy is applied in API Manager to an API with Autodiscovery?","options":["The app must be redeployed for it to take effect","The API is deleted","It only affects Exchange docs","It applies without redeploying"],"explanation":"The runtime downloads policies."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica el estado \"Active\" de una instancia en API Manager?","options":["Nada relevante: es el estado inicial de cualquier instancia creada","Que la especificación está publicada en Exchange","Que la aplicación tiene más de un worker","El runtime se ha vinculado mediante Autodiscovery"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Unregistered si no hay vínculo.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does an Active instance status in API Manager indicate?","options":["Nothing relevant: it's any new instance's initial state","The spec is published to Exchange","The app has more than one worker","The runtime linked via Autodiscovery"],"explanation":"Unregistered if no link."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene para promover una API de Sandbox a Producción en API Manager?","options":["Promover la instancia con sus políticas y desplegar la app en producción","Copiar el JAR por correo","Crear todo de nuevo a mano","Nada: las APIs de Sandbox pasan solas a producción al publicarlas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"API Manager permite promover configuraciones.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What's advisable to promote an API from Sandbox to Production in API Manager?","options":["Promote the instance with its policies and deploy the app to production","Email the JAR","Recreate everything by hand","Nothing: Sandbox APIs move to production on publish"],"explanation":"API Manager can promote configurations."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos opciones permiten escalar una app en CloudHub? (Elige 2)","options":["Usar Choice","Añadir más flujos privados","Aumentar el número de workers","Cambiar el nivel de log","Aumentar el tamaño del worker"],"correct":[2,4],"explanation":"Vertical y horizontal.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two options scale an app on CloudHub? (Choose 2)","options":["Use Choice","Add more private flows","Increase worker count","Change log level","Increase worker size"],"explanation":"Vertical and horizontal."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es el Object Store v2 en CloudHub?","options":["Un almacén clave-valor gestionado y persistente","Un repositorio de JARs","Una base de datos relacional","Un registro de logs de las aplicaciones desplegadas"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Persistencia entre workers y reinicios.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Object Store v2 on CloudHub?","options":["A managed persistent key-value store","A JAR repository","A relational database","A log store for deployed apps"],"explanation":"Persistence across workers and restarts."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política registra peticiones y respuestas para auditoría?","options":["Message Logging","IP Blocklist","Rate Limiting","CORS"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Con cuidado de no registrar datos sensibles.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy logs requests and responses for audit?","options":["Message Logging","IP Blocklist","Rate Limiting","CORS"],"explanation":"Mind not logging sensitive data."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué política permite que navegadores de otros dominios llamen a la API?","options":["CORS","Header Removal","Spike Control","Client ID Enforcement"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Cross-Origin Resource Sharing.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which policy lets browsers from other domains call the API?","options":["CORS","Header Removal","Spike Control","Client ID Enforcement"],"explanation":"Cross-Origin Resource Sharing."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué recomienda MuleSoft para APIs expuestas a internet?","options":["Exponerlas sin políticas para mejorar el rendimiento","Usar solo IP Allowlist","Combinar autenticación, límites de tráfico y protección de amenazas","Nada: CloudHub protege automáticamente cualquier API pública"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Defensa en capas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does MuleSoft recommend for internet-facing APIs?","options":["Expose them with no policies for performance","Use only IP Allowlist","Combine authentication, traffic limits and threat protection","Nothing: CloudHub automatically protects any public API"],"explanation":"Layered defense."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué indica CloudHub 2.0 frente a CloudHub 1.0?","options":["Es un editor de RAML","No admite APIs","Ejecuta apps solo en servidores del cliente","Ejecuta apps en contenedores con réplicas y espacios privados"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Réplicas en lugar de workers; Private Spaces.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does CloudHub 2.0 mean versus 1.0?","options":["It's a RAML editor","Doesn't support APIs","Runs apps only on customer servers","Runs apps in containers with replicas and private spaces"],"explanation":"Replicas instead of workers; Private Spaces."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué permite una VPC o Private Space en CloudHub?","options":["Crear usuarios de Anypoint con acceso a la red privada","Cambiar el lenguaje DataWeave","Conectar apps de forma privada con la red corporativa","Publicar APIs en Exchange"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Conectividad privada (VPN, peering).","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What does a VPC or Private Space in CloudHub allow?","options":["Creating Anypoint users with private network access","Changing DataWeave","Privately connecting apps to the corporate network","Publishing APIs to Exchange"],"explanation":"Private connectivity (VPN, peering)."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué dos políticas protegen frente a cargas maliciosas? (Elige 2)","options":["Message Logging","JSON Threat Protection","Header Injection","XML Threat Protection","CORS"],"correct":[1,3],"explanation":"Limitan tamaño y profundidad de payloads.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"Which two policies protect against malicious payloads? (Choose 2)","options":["Message Logging","JSON Threat Protection","Header Injection","XML Threat Protection","CORS"],"explanation":"They limit payload size and depth."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene configurar para recibir avisos si una app en CloudHub se detiene?","options":["Un Scheduler","Una política CORS","Alertas en Runtime Manager","Un Logger en cada flujo"],"correct":[2],"explanation":"Alertas por estado, CPU, memoria.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be set up to get notified if a CloudHub app stops?","options":["A Scheduler","A CORS policy","Runtime Manager alerts","A Logger in each flow"],"explanation":"Alerts on status, CPU, memory."}}},{"domain":"D11","source":"bank","stem":"Un test de MUnit falla porque el flujo llama a un servicio externo que no está disponible en el pipeline. ¿Qué se hace?","options":["Simular la llamada con Mock When","Desactivar el test hasta que el servicio externo vuelva a estar disponible en CI","Apuntar el test al entorno de producción del servicio externo","Subir el timeout del HTTP Request a varios minutos"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Las pruebas unitarias no deben depender de sistemas externos.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"An MUnit test fails because the flow calls an external service unavailable in the pipeline. What's done?","options":["Mock the call with Mock When","Disable the test until the external service is back in CI","Point the test at the external service's production","Raise the HTTP Request timeout to several minutes"],"explanation":"Unit tests shouldn't depend on external systems."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"Un socio externo debe consumir la API con un máximo de 100 peticiones por minuto, y otro con 1.000. ¿Qué se configura?","options":["Niveles de SLA con la política SLA Based","Una política de Rate Limiting global de 1.000 peticiones para toda la API","Dos aplicaciones Mule distintas, una para cada socio","Una política CORS por socio"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Los tiers asignan límites por contrato.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"One partner must consume the API at max 100 req/min and another at 1,000. What's configured?","options":["SLA tiers with the SLA Based policy","A global 1,000-request Rate Limiting policy for the whole API","Two separate Mule apps, one per partner","A CORS policy per partner"],"explanation":"Tiers assign limits per contract."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"Una API implementada en Java fuera de Mule debe gobernarse con políticas de API Manager. ¿Qué opción encaja?","options":["Desplegar un proxy de API delante de ella","Publicar la especificación en Exchange, que aplica las políticas","Configurar un Scheduler en Runtime Manager","Usar Autodiscovery dentro del código Java sin ningún runtime de Mule"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"El proxy (o Flex Gateway) aplica políticas.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"A Java API outside Mule must be governed with API Manager policies. Which option fits?","options":["Deploy an API proxy in front of it","Publish the spec to Exchange, which applies policies","Configure a Scheduler in Runtime Manager","Use Autodiscovery inside the Java code with no Mule runtime"],"explanation":"A proxy (or Flex Gateway) applies policies."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué es Anypoint Flex Gateway?","options":["Un gateway ligero para gestionar APIs en cualquier entorno","Un editor de flujos Mule en el navegador para equipos de negocio","Una herramienta de pruebas MUnit","Un conector de bases de datos NoSQL"],"correct":[0],"explanation":"Aplica políticas a APIs Mule y no Mule.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What is Anypoint Flex Gateway?","options":["A lightweight gateway to manage APIs anywhere","A browser Mule flow editor for business teams","An MUnit testing tool","A NoSQL database connector"],"explanation":"It applies policies to Mule and non-Mule APIs."}}},{"domain":"D12","source":"bank","stem":"¿Qué conviene hacer antes de retirar la versión v1 de una API con consumidores activos?","options":["Bajar su rate limit a cero sin comunicarlo","Cambiar su contrato para que coincida con v2 sin avisar","Borrar la instancia de API Manager y la app de golpe para forzar la migración","Marcarla como obsoleta y avisar con antelación"],"correct":[3],"explanation":"Deprecación gestionada.","i18n":{"en":{"stem":"What should be done before retiring an API's v1 with active consumers?","options":["Drop its rate limit to zero silently","Change its contract to match v2 without notice","Delete the API Manager instance and app at once to force migration","Mark it deprecated and give advance notice"],"explanation":"Managed deprecation."}}}]}$exam$::jsonb);

